{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_10","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The title \"A Cry Too Far\" was selected from the crypto index.\n\nThe dev folder and HTML file are named with the selected title plus a timestamp. The next steps are to unzip the kit, download hub files, and study the engine APIs and hub README.\n\nThe game architecture will prioritize compact, testable code over perfect art asset fidelity. The acceptance criteria require a title, HTML, exit-interview, PROGRESS file, and about/credits page. The survival systems need a 1280x1280 basin with first-person movement and driving controls including walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade.\n\nThe survival systems are now fully detailed. Guns degrade, jam, and break at zero wear. Locker weapons stay clean while ground weapons accumulate wear. Combat uses a five-meter fire grid with wind affecting head speed and flanks. Burned ground cannot burn again. Scars appear on the map. Fever clears via held tablet; ignoring collapses removes stones. Low-health field surgery is available. Living buddies can rescue downed allies. Downed buddies need a syrette or a finish-it command. Paper maps and GPS remain active during walking and driving without pausing the world. Clean storage music volume is set to 0.1. Voices use code gibberish.\n\nThe story will use invented names such as Sorrel, Concord, and Harvest. Missions run from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal to a choice about who gets the minefield sheet, ending with both cards. Story scars appear even if the player burned something else. A ledger tracks hectares burned, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets cannot kill civilians. Every mission is startable from setup and finishable with real actions.\n\nBoth endings must appear, including one where a buddy is already dead. The §26 never-cut list is complete and all items remain intact.\n\nThe HUD renders in art pixels rather than DOM elements. Prompts follow the last device used: PS default, Xbox setting, or kbm. Mouse hover moves focus and click activates. Pad, keyboard, and mouse share identical menus. Pause sets timeScale to zero. Touch-only mode shows an exact notice requiring a controller or keyboard, offers one Settings control, and allows attract mode.\n\nAttract mode triggers after ten seconds on the title or main menu. It loops with a demo tag and any input returns without saving.\n\nDev mode is hidden in the hub. It exposes live balance sliders and restores defaults on reset.\n\nThe session runs Cash Run for one to four players for about six minutes. Players carry stone cases to an extraction truck. Friendly fire is enabled. Downed allies can be revived or looted. Solo play uses hired-gun AI without the hub.\n\nA normal boot without a session reaches the title. The boot sequence connects to the hub, starts a headless server on a timer instead of a render loop, and signals readiness before any key press. Card answers use Enter and M from window keydown.\n\nFour harness scenarios pass. The same-computer two-window link is preserved unless cut.\n\nThe implementation will be a complete simulation using engine views where practical. Art will use essential models rather than hundreds of unique detailed assets, but no stubs are allowed and every included feature must work. The strategy is a cohesive, non-over-engineered module structure with many files for designer extensibility.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0067f6ef-011d-4b4c-baab-ddf91fdc6d6c-9","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"STEM='A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917'\nROOT='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work'\nDEV=\"$ROOT/$STEM\"\nSCRATCH='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer'\nmkdir -p \"$DEV\"\nunzip -q -o \"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine.zip\" -d \"$DEV/..\"\n# zip extracts to pixel-engine/ — move contents into dev folder\nif [ -d \"$ROOT/pixel-engine\" ]; then\n  # move kit files into DEV without clobbering if rerun\n  shopt -s dotglob\n  mv \"$ROOT/pixel-engine/\"* \"$DEV/\"\n  rmdir \"$ROOT/pixel-engine\" 2>/dev/null || true\nfi\nmkdir -p \"$DEV/vendor/hub\" \"$DEV/src\" \"$DEV/tests\" \"$DEV/tools\"\n# keep zip for byte compare\ncp \"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine.zip\" \"$DEV/vendor/pixel-engine.zip\"\n# hub client + harness\ncd \"$DEV/vendor\"\ncurl -fsSL -o session.js \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\"\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/README.md \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\"\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/harness.html \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\"\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/bridge.js \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\"\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/round.js \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\"\n# arena example if present\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/arena.html \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/examples/arena.html\" || echo \"no arena\"\n# list hub dir from github api\ncurl -fsSL \"https://api.github.com/repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub\" | node -e 'let s=\"\";process.stdin.on(\"data\",d=>s+=d);process.stdin.on(\"end\",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(s); for (const f of j) console.log(f.type, f.name, f.size);})'\necho \"---- kit top ----\"\nls -la \"$DEV\" | head -40\necho \"---- version ----\"\nnode -e '\nconst fs=require(\"fs\");\nconst t=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1],\"utf8\");\nconst m=t.match(/version[\"\\s:]+([0-9.]+)/i);\nconsole.log(\"changelog head:\");\n' \"$DEV/CHANGELOG.md\"\nhead -40 \"$DEV/CHANGELOG.md\"\necho \"---- pixel bytes ----\"\n# extract zip pixel-engine.js and cmp\nunzip -p \"$DEV/vendor/pixel-engine.zip\" pixel-engine/pixel-engine.js > \"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine-from-zip.js\"\ncmp \"$DEV/pixel-engine.js\" \"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine-from-zip.js\" && echo BYTE_IDENTICAL\nwc -c \"$DEV/pixel-engine.js\" \"$DEV/vendor/session.js\"","description":"Unzip kit, vendor hub, verify engine bytes"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4716,"output_tokens":1905,"cache_read_input_tokens":58880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"1dca36ed-472e-49df-a96b-64072172b8ec"}
