5,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,32,67,114,121,32,84,111,111,32,70,97,114,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,47,118,101,110,100,111,114,47,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,46,106,115,10,52,56,56,48,57,51,53,32,116,111,116,97,108,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\ncurl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 404\\nno arena\\nfile README.md 17587\\nfile bridge.js 13624\\ndir examples 0\\nfile harness.html 27469\\nfile retrofit.md 3718\\nfile round.js 20248\\nfile session.js 16707\\n(node:210565) Warning: The 'NO_COLOR' env is ignored due to the 'FORCE_COLOR' env being set.\\n(Use `node --trace-warnings ...` to show where the warning was created)\\n---- kit top ----\\ntotal 5888\\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  248164 Dec 31  1979 API.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   15883 Dec 31  1979 ASSETS.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   57520 Dec 31  1979 CHANGELOG.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   41812 Dec 31  1979 CREDITS.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   60159 Dec 31  1979 GUIDE.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  176448 Dec 31  1979 LIBRARY.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    1071 Dec 31  1979 LICENSE\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    3151 Dec 31  1979 README.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   30347 Dec 31  1979 check.mjs\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 examples\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    4526 Dec 31  1979 game.js\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     506 Dec 31  1979 index.html\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  431976 Dec 31  1979 library.json\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   18064 Dec 31  1979 manifest.json\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 packs\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     226 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.d.ts\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 4864228 Dec 31  1979 pixel-engine.js\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 src\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 tests\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 tools\\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 types\\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha    4096 Nov  5 01:43 vendor\\n---- version ----\\nchangelog head:\\n# Changelog\\n\\nWhat changed in Pixel Engine for a game built on it, newest first. The version is\\n`package.json`'s; a game reads it as `ENGINE_VERSION`, `Engine.version` or\\n`engine.state().version`. The engine kit (`npm run bundle`, docs/GUIDE.md) ships this file.\\n\\nWhen a change alters the public API (`src/bundle.ts` exports) or something a game can see,\\nbump the version (minor while it is 0.x) and add its section here; `npm test` fails when\\n`package.json`'s version has no section.\\n\\n## 0.46.0\\n\\n- **No more handoff page**: the engine's site is gone, so `manifest.json` has no `handoff` and the\\n  kit's `README.md` no longer names a page for agents. Newer kits are where they were:\\n  `latest` (the newest release's zip), `releases` and `source`.\\n\\n## 0.45.0\\n\\n- **The kit runs in Node**: `Engine.headless(game, { assets })` from `pixel-engine.js` alone, with\\n  no `node_modules`. In Node, Rapier's wasm comes from the data URL the kit inlines, and a reader\\n  (`assets`, `setAssetReader`) no longer sees the files the kit embeds (`__PIXEL_ASSETS__`: the\\n  built-in models load as they do in a page).\\n- **`node check.mjs --headless game.js`**: plays a game module in Node, no browser. It makes the game\\n  with the module's `createGame()` export, plays the `--keys` frames, replays the recording in a\\n  fresh game and writes `report.json` (`state()`, errors, the fingerprint). Exit 1 on an error or a\\n  replay that ends elsewhere, 2 for a page or a module without `createGame()`.\\n- **The starter `game.js` exports `createGame()`** and starts the engine only where there is a\\n  `document`, so it imports in Node. GUIDE.md section 8, *Play it in Node*, shows a test of your own.\\n\\n## 0.44.0\\n\\n- **Removed from the texture library: its equipment icons**: `sword-icon`, `axe-icon`,\\n  `mace-icon`, `dagger-icon`, `bow-icon`, `staff-icon`, `wand-icon`, `shield-icon`,\\n  `round-shield-icon`, `quiver-icon`, `helmet-icon`, `armor-icon`, `gloves-icon`, `boots-icon`,\\n  `belt-icon`, `ring` and `amulet`. They were a second way to draw an item next to Riftlight's own\\n  icons, which fill any item footprint (a one-cell item's box is 7 px wide), and nothing used them. A game that wants one makes its own\\n  `TextureDef` (docs/GUIDE-ASSETS.md) and adds it with `TEXTURE_LIBRARY.add(def)`. The library\\n  keeps the items Riftlight has no class for (potions, key, scroll, map, book, bomb, torch...),\\n  `gem-icon`, `gold-icon`, the skill and UI icons and the creatures.\\n\\n---- pixel bytes ----\\nBYTE_IDENTICAL\\n4864228 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.js\\n  16707 /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/session.js\\n4880935 total\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"STEM='A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917'\\nROOT='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work'\\nDEV=\\\"$ROOT/$STEM\\\"\\nSCRATCH='/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer'\\nmkdir -p \\\"$DEV\\\"\\nunzip -q -o \\\"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine.zip\\\" -d \\\"$DEV/..\\\"\\n# zip extracts to pixel-engine/ — move contents into dev folder\\nif [ -d \\\"$ROOT/pixel-engine\\\" ]; then\\n  # move kit files into DEV without clobbering if rerun\\n  shopt -s dotglob\\n  mv \\\"$ROOT/pixel-engine/\\\"* \\\"$DEV/\\\"\\n  rmdir \\\"$ROOT/pixel-engine\\\" 2>/dev/null || true\\nfi\\nmkdir -p \\\"$DEV/vendor/hub\\\" \\\"$DEV/src\\\" \\\"$DEV/tests\\\" \\\"$DEV/tools\\\"\\n# keep zip for byte compare\\ncp \\\"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine.zip\\\" \\\"$DEV/vendor/pixel-engine.zip\\\"\\n# hub client + harness\\ncd \\\"$DEV/vendor\\\"\\ncurl -fsSL -o session.js \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\\\"\\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/README.md \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\\\"\\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/harness.html \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\\"\\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/bridge.js \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\\\"\\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/round.js \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\\\"\\n# arena example if present\\ncurl -fsSL -o hub/arena.html \\\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/examples/arena.html\\\" || echo \\\"no arena\\\"\\n# list hub dir from github api\\ncurl -fsSL \\\"https://api.github.com/repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub\\\" | node -e 'let s=\\\"\\\";process.stdin.on(\\\"data\\\",d=>s+=d);process.stdin.on(\\\"end\\\",()=>{const j=JSON.parse(s); for (const f of j) console.log(f.type, f.name, f.size);})'\\necho \\\"---- kit top ----\\\"\\nls -la \\\"$DEV\\\" | head -40\\necho \\\"---- version ----\\\"\\nnode -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nconst t=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1],\\\"utf8\\\");\\nconst m=t.match(/version[\\\"\\\\s:]+([0-9.]+)/i);\\nconsole.log(\\\"changelog head:\\\");\\n' \\\"$DEV/CHANGELOG.md\\\"\\nhead -40 \\\"$DEV/CHANGELOG.md\\\"\\necho \\\"---- pixel bytes ----\\\"\\n# extract zip pixel-engine.js and cmp\\nunzip -p \\\"$DEV/vendor/pixel-engine.zip\\\" pixel-engine/pixel-engine.js > \\\"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine-from-zip.js\\\"\\ncmp \\\"$DEV/pixel-engine.js\\\" \\\"$SCRATCH/pixel-engine-from-zip.js\\\" && echo BYTE_IDENTICAL\\nwc -c \\\"$DEV/pixel-engine.js\\\" \\\"$DEV/vendor/session.js\\\"\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Unzip kit, vendor hub, verify engine bytes\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-0067f6ef-011d-4b4c-baab-ddf91fdc6d6c-9.log\",\"total_bytes\":4645}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"42af1955-b01f-493f-9b34-c5b6ce434f8c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_11","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The kit version is 0.46.0.\n\nI am reading the engine API documentation to understand game creation, headless mode, HUD, audio, and key types. The simulation must be real and testable. I will keep visuals lightweight for headless performance. A 512x512 terrain grid is acceptable. Grass may be too heavy.\n\nGrass mesh building will be skipped or deferred for headless tests. I will read the starter game and key APIs next, then examine engine hooks and hub protocol before writing code systematically across multiple focused files.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/game.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/index.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-12","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^## |^### |createGame|fixedUpdate|headless|CharacterController|export (function|class|const)","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/GUIDE.md","head_limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-13","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/hub/README.md","limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-14","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3678,"output_tokens":765,"cache_read_input_tokens":63488,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"6e6dfee3-65e5-4af5-afbb-6f4eff38bdf1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n50→    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n60→    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n70→    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n80→    ctx.hud.clear();\\n    ctx.hud.text(6, 6, `COINS ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`, { color: 'sand' });\\n    if (this.won) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'YOU WIN!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\\n  }\\n\\n  cameraTarget() {\\n    const p = this.model?.position ?? this.target.set(0, 0, 4);\\n    return this.target.set(p.x, p.y + 0.9, p.z);\\n  }\\n\\n90→  onCameraChange(ctx) {\\n    this.hero.setLockDepth(ctx.camera.lockDepth); // side view: stay on the lane\\n    this.model.visible = !ctx.camera.hidesTarget; // first person: no body in the way\\n  }\\n\\n  status() {\\n    return `coins ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n100→/** A fresh game: the page starts one, and `node check.mjs --headless` plays one in Node (section 8). */\\nexport const createGame = () => new CoinGarden();\\n\\nif (typeof document !== 'undefined') await Engine.start(createGame(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso' } }));\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n10→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n20→  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n30→        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n40→      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n50→    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n60→    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n70→    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n80→    ctx.hud.clear();\\n    ctx.hud.text(6, 6, `COINS ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`, { color: 'sand' });\\n    if (this.won) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'YOU WIN!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\\n  }\\n\\n  cameraTarget() {\\n    const p = this.model?.position ?? this.target.set(0, 0, 4);\\n    return this.target.set(p.x, p.y + 0.9, p.z);\\n  }\\n\\n90→  onCameraChange(ctx) {\\n    this.hero.setLockDepth(ctx.camera.lockDepth); // side view: stay on the lane\\n    this.model.visible = !ctx.camera.hidesTarget; // first person: no body in the way\\n  }\\n\\n  status() {\\n    return `coins ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n100→/** A fresh game: the page starts one, and `node check.mjs --headless` plays one in Node (section 8). */\\nexport const createGame = () => new CoinGarden();\\n\\nif (typeof document !== 'undefined') await Engine.start(createGame(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso' } }));\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/game.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\\n\\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\\n\\n/** A box you can see (toon material, palette colour) and stand on (a static collider). */\\nfunction block(ctx, [x, y, z], [w, h, d], color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nclass CoinGarden {\\n  name = 'Coin Garden';\\n  assets = [HERO_MODEL, 'assets/coin.glb']; // start downloading before setup runs\\n  coins = [];\\n  collected = 0;\\n  won = false;\\n  target = new Vector3();\\n  ground = new Vector3();\\n\\n  async setup(ctx) {\\n    const { scene, physics, palette } = ctx;\\n    // Level: static geometry merged into one draw call per material; one collider per block.\\n    scene.add(\\n      ...mergeStaticMeshes([\\n        block(ctx, [0, -0.5, 0], [24, 1, 24], palette.green),\\n        block(ctx, [4, 0.5, -2], [3, 1, 3], palette.slate),\\n        block(ctx, [7, 1.25, -2], [3, 2.5, 3], palette.teal),\\n        block(ctx, [-5, 0.75, 4], [2, 1.5, 2], palette.orange),\\n      ]),\\n    );\\n    // Coins: a model, spinning; a trigger volume collects it when the hero walks in.\\n    const coin = await ctx.loadModel('assets/coin.glb', { castShadow: false });\\n    for (const [x, y, z] of [[4, 1.4, -2], [7, 2.9, -2], [-5, 1.9, 4], [-2, 0.4, -5]]) {\\n      const mesh = coin.scene.clone(true);\\n      mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n      setLookLayer(mesh, 'actors'); // characters & objects can get their own look\\n      scene.add(mesh);\\n      const item = { mesh, taken: false };\\n      physics.trigger({ cylinder: { halfHeight: 0.6, radius: 0.5 } }, [x, y, z], { tag: 'character', once: true, onEnter: () => this.collect(ctx, item) });\\n      this.coins.push(item);\\n    }\\n    // The hero: the bundled model and clips on a Mario-64-style controller.\\n    const hero = await ctx.loadModel(HERO_MODEL, { castShadow: false });\\n    this.model = hero.scene;\\n    setLookLayer(this.model, 'actors');\\n    this.shadow = new ContactShadow(0.42);\\n    scene.add(this.model, this.shadow);\\n    this.hero = new PlatformerCharacter(physics, { position: [0, 0, 4], lockDepth: ctx.camera.lockDepth });\\n    this.hero.attachModel(this.model, compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, HERO_RIG, this.model), HERO_RIG);\\n  }\\n\\n  collect(ctx, item) {\\n    item.taken = true;\\n    item.mesh.visible = false;\\n    this.collected++;\\n    ctx.audio.play('coin');\\n    ctx.particles.burst('sparkle', item.mesh.position);\\n  }\\n\\n  fixedUpdate(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.input = readMoveInput(ctx, this.hero, this.input); // filled in place after the first step\\n    this.hero.fixedUpdate(dt, this.input); // movement and forces: fixed 60 Hz step\\n  }\\n\\n  update(ctx, dt) {\\n    this.hero.updateVisual(this.model, dt, ctx.physics.alpha); // pose and interpolate\\n    const feet = this.model.position;\\n    const ground = ctx.physics.groundBelow(this.ground.set(feet.x, feet.y + 0.1, feet.z), 20, this.hero.body);\\n    if (ground) this.shadow.place(feet.x, ground.y, feet.z, feet.y - ground.y);\\n    for (const c of this.coins) if (!c.taken) c.mesh.rotation.y += dt * 3;\\n    if (!this.won && this.collected === this.coins.length) {\\n      this.won = true;\\n      this.hero.celebrate();\\n      ctx.audio.play('fanfare');\\n    }\\n    ctx.hud.clear();\\n    ctx.hud.text(6, 6, `COINS ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`, { color: 'sand' });\\n    if (this.won) ctx.hud.text(0, 0, 'YOU WIN!', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2, shadow: 'navy' });\\n  }\\n\\n  cameraTarget() {\\n    const p = this.model?.position ?? this.target.set(0, 0, 4);\\n    return this.target.set(p.x, p.y + 0.9, p.z);\\n  }\\n\\n  onCameraChange(ctx) {\\n    this.hero.setLockDepth(ctx.camera.lockDepth); // side view: stay on the lane\\n    this.model.visible = !ctx.camera.hidesTarget; // first person: no body in the way\\n  }\\n\\n  status() {\\n    return `coins ${this.collected}/${this.coins.length}`;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n/** A fresh game: the page starts one, and `node check.mjs --headless` plays one in Node (section 8). */\\nexport const createGame = () => new CoinGarden();\\n\\nif (typeof document !== 'undefined') await Engine.start(createGame(), withUrlOptions({ container: document.getElementById('app'), camera: { preset: 'iso' } }));\\n\",\"total_lines\":103}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f8532d80-486e-4998-b1b5-a359bb1a0912-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\\n  </head>\\n10→  <body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n    <script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"./game.js\\\"></script>\\n  </body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n  <head>\\n    <meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\" />\\n    <meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\\\" />\\n    <link rel=\\\"icon\\\" href=\\\"data:,\\\" />\\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\\n  </head>\\n10→  <body>\\n    <div id=\\\"app\\\"></div