it: control\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/hub/README.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":317,\"content\":\"and runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\"},{\"line_number\":334,\"content\":\"`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\"},{\"line_number\":335,\"content\":\"`\\\"true\\\"` at the end. It checks:\"},{\"line_number\":353,\"content\":\"checks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/hub/harness.html\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"  #checks li { list-style: none; }\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"  #checks ul { margin: 0; padding: 0; }\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"    <section id=\\\"checks\\\"><h2>Conformance</h2><ul id=\\\"checklist\\\"><li class=\\\"hint\\\">Run with <code>?auto=1</code> for the automatic checks.</li></ul></section>\"},{\"line_number\":379,\"content\":\" * page's origin). Results land in window.__hubCheck, and body[data-complete]\"},{\"line_number\":405,\"content\":\"  const checks = [];\"},{\"line_number\":407,\"content\":\"    checks.push({ name, pass: !!pass, detail });\"},{\"line_number\":408,\"content\":\"    renderChecks(checks);\"},{\"line_number\":411,\"content\":\"  const report = { done: false, pass: false, game: $('game').value, players: Number($('players').value), scenario, checks, log: logLines };\"},{\"line_number\":412,\"content\":\"  window.__hubCheck = report;\"},{\"line_number\":525,\"content\":\"    report.pass = checks.length > 0 && checks.every((c) => c.pass);\"},{\"line_number\":527,\"content\":\"    document.body.dataset.complete = 'true';\"},{\"line_number\":532,\"content\":\"function renderChecks(checks) {\"},{\"line_number\":534,\"content\":\"    ...checks.map((c) => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"5c83ee24-fee8-4bd2-9c39-292b2a1847de"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_14","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a large project. I will implement it comprehensively and efficiently.\n\nI am reviewing the engine APIs and types to ensure correct implementation. I will structure the simulation carefully to avoid redundant code. Creating a new physics engine for every test would be too slow, so I will reuse one engine and reset it between tests.\n\nFire spread tests will need several seconds of simulation. Grass with 150,000 blades could slow headless runs. I will build grass lazily and skip visual grass in headless mode.\n\nSoldiers will be lightweight data structures with optional physics capsules only for live units within 260 meters. Headless tests can teleport and use real actions.\n\nThe boot path must connect the AI hub, create a round-mode game, run the server in headless step mode, start the client engine without keypress, and handle Enter and M keys for cards.\n\nI am reading the harness verification section to understand exact pass conditions. The minimal hub integration must handle time-up by calling finish directly, stop input and audio on end, and continue or finish on leave.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-25","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/hub/README.md","offset":280,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-26","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/physics/CharacterController.d.ts","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-27","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/session.js","offset":1,"limit":220}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"export declare function model|export declare function checkModel|export declare function textureDef|export declare function validateTexture|export interface Song|parseSong|HERO_RIG|PALETTE","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine","glob":"**/*.d.ts","head_limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7038,"output_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":82304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"63341ec1-17cf-439c-ad0b-60ee9ab73962"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-25","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"280→  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\\n  client drops the rest.\\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\\n290→  and is lost whole if any of them is.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\nIn a session:\\n\\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\\n300→- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\\n  names. Names come from the hub.\\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\\n  is held.\\n\\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\\n310→one, the game is not affected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test it\\n\\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\\nto the game:\\n\\n320→```bash\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\\npython3 -m http.server 8000\\n```\\n\\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\\n330→`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\\n\\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\\n`\\\"true\\\"` at the end. It checks:\\n\\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\\n340→  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\\n  player of its own;\\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\\n  told the round ended;\\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\\n\\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\\n350→game is served from the harness's own origin.\\n\\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\\nruns there.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reference\\n\\n360→### Tags\\n\\n| Tag | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\\n370→| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\\n\\n### API\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\\\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\\\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\\n380→| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\\\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\\n\\n390→`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\\nread them.\\n\\n| Event | Arguments |\\n|---|---|\\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\\n| `message` | `data, from` |\\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\",\"content_concise\":\"280→  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\\n  client drops the rest.\\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\\n290→  and is lost whole if any of them is.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\nIn a session:\\n\\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\\n300→- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\\n  names. Names come from the hub.\\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\\n  is held.\\n\\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\\n310→one, the game is not affected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test it\\n\\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\\nto the game:\\n\\n320→```bash\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\\npython3 -m http.server 8000\\n```\\n\\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\\n330→`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\\n\\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\\n`\\\"true\\\"` at the end. It checks:\\n\\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\\n340→  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\\n  player of its own;\\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\\n  told the round ended;\\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\\n\\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\\n350→game is served from the harness's own origin.\\n\\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\\nruns there.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reference\\n\\n360→### Tags\\n\\n| Tag | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\\n370→| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\\n\\n### API\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\\\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\\\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\\n380→| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\\\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\\n\\n390→`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\\nread them.\\n\\n| Event | Arguments |\\n|---|---|\\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\\n| `message` | `data, from` |\\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/hub/README.md\",\"offset\":280,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\\n  client drops the rest.\\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Rules\\n\\nIn a session:\\n\\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\\n  names. Names come from the hub.\\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\\n  is held.\\n\\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\\none, the game is not affected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Test it\\n\\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\\nto the game:\\n\\n```bash\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\\npython3 -m http.server 8000\\n```\\n\\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\\n\\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\\n`\\\"true\\\"` at the end. It checks:\\n\\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\\n  player of its own;\\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\\n  told the round ended;\\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\\n\\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\\n\\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\\nruns there.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Reference\\n\\n### Tags\\n\\n| Tag | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\\n\\n### API\\n\\n| | |\\n|---|---|\\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\\\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\\\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\\\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\\n\\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\\nread them.\\n\\n| Event | Arguments |\\n|---|---|\\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\\n| `message` | `data, from` |\\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\\n\",\"total_lines\":410}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b3860f4f-d418-4186-b37f-c6a11ca6bf9a-26","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { type Physics, RAPIER } from './Physics';\\nexport interface CharacterOptions {\\n    position: [number, number, number];\\n    radius?: number;\\n    /** Height of the cylindrical part of the capsule. */\\n    halfHeight?: number;\\n    speed?: number;\\n    jumpSpeed?: number;\\n10→    gravity?: number;\\n}\\nexport type CharacterAnim = 'Idle' | 'Walk' | 'Jump';\\n/**\\n * Kinematic capsule driven by Rapier's KinematicCharacterController, with classic\\n * platformer affordances (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height).\\n *\\n * The body moves in continuous world space; the visual model is interpolated by\\n * Physics.bind and only *looks* pixel-aligned through the render pipeline.\\n */\\n20→export declare class CharacterController {\\n    private readonly physics;\\n    readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody;\\n    readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider;\\n    readonly controller: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController;\\n    readonly velocity: Vector3;\\n    grounded: boolean;\\n    facing: number;\\n    private readonly speed;\\n    private readonly jumpSpeed;\\n30→    private readonly gravity;\\n    private readonly footOffset;\\n    private readonly prevFeet;\\n    private coyote;\\n    private jumpBuffer;\\n    private wish;\\n    private jumpHeld;\\n    private mixer;\\n    private actions;\\n    private current;\\n40→    constructor(physics: Physics, options: CharacterOptions);\\n    /** Feet position (bottom of the capsule), continuous world space. */\\n    get feet(): Vector3;\\n    /** Feet position blended between the previous and current physics step (render use). */\\n    interpolatedFeet(alpha: number): Vector3;\\n    /** Set desired horizontal move direction (world space, length ≤ 1) and jump input. */\\n    setInput(move: Vector3, jumpPressed: boolean, jumpHeld: boolean): void;\\n    teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void;\\n    /** Call from Physics.update's fixedUpdate callback. */\\n    fixedUpdate(dt: number): void;\\n50→    /** Attach a model's animation clips (expects Idle / Walk / Jump). */\\n    attachAnimations(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[]): void;\\n    get animation(): CharacterAnim;\\n    /** Per render frame: pick animation state and advance the mixer. */\\n    updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number): void;\\n    private play;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { type AnimationClip, type Object3D, Vector3 } from 'three/webgpu';\\nimport { type Physics, RAPIER } from './Physics';\\nexport interface CharacterOptions {\\n    position: [number, number, number];\\n    radius?: number;\\n    /** Height of the cylindrical part of the capsule. */\\n    halfHeight?: number;\\n    speed?: number;\\n    jumpSpeed?: number;\\n10→    gravity?: number;\\n}\\nexport type CharacterAnim = 'Idle' | 'Walk' | 'Jump';\\n/**\\n * Kinematic capsule driven by Rapier's KinematicCharacterController, with classic\\n * platformer affordances (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height).\\n *\\n * The body moves in continuous world space; the visual model is interpolated by\\n * Physics.bind and only *looks* pixel-aligned through the render pipeline.\\n */\\n20→export declare class CharacterController {\\n    private readonly physics;\\n    readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody;\\n    readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider;\\n    readonly controller: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController;\\n    readonly velocity: Vector3;\\n    grounded: boolean;\\n    facing: number;\\n    private readonly speed;\\n    private readonly jumpSpeed;\\n30→    private readonly gravity;\\n    private readonly footOffset;\\n    private readonly prevFeet;\\n    private coyote;\\n    private jumpBuffer;\\n    private wish;\\n    private jumpHeld;\\n    private mixer;\\n    private actions;\\n    private current;\\n40→    constructor(physics: Physics, options: CharacterOptions);\\n    /** Feet position (bottom of the capsule), continuous world space. */\\n    get feet(): Vector3;\\n    /** Feet position blended between the previous and current physics step (render use). */\\n    interpolatedFeet(alpha: number): Vector3;\\n    /** Set desired horizontal move direction (world space, length ≤ 1) and jump input. */\\n    setInput(move: Vector3, jumpPressed: boolean, jumpHeld: boolean): void;\\n    teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void;\\n    /** Call from Physics.update's fixedUpdate callback. */\\n    fixedUpdate(dt: number): void;\\n50→    /** Attach a model's animation clips (expects Idle / Walk / Jump). */\\n    attachAnimations(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[]): void;\\n