{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-61a1dd71-d809-45b0-807a-b489e5b9b1d4-75","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"120→        for (let dz = -reach; dz <= reach; dz++) {\\n          for (let dx = -reach; dx <= reach; dx++) {\\n            const ix = c.ix + dx;\\n            const iz = c.iz + dz;\\n            if (ix < 0 || iz < 0 || ix >= FIRE_N || iz >= FIRE_N) continue;\\n            const [cx, cz] = this.center(ix, iz);\\n            if (Math.hypot(cx - x, cz - z) > half) continue;\\n            const i = this.idx(ix, iz);\\n            if (this.fuel[i] === 0 || this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) continue;\\n            if (this.state[i] === 1 || this.state[i] === 0) this.markBurnt(i);\\n130→          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    this.burning = this.burning.filter((i) => this.state[i] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  step(dt) {\\n    this.time += dt;\\n    this.acc += dt;\\n140→    let guard = 0;\\n    while (this.acc >= 0.25 && guard++ < 6) {\\n      this.acc -= 0.25;\\n      this.spread();\\n      this.regrow();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  markBurnt(i) {\\n    if (this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) return;\",\"content_concise\":\"120→        for (let dz = -reach; dz <= reach; dz++) {\\n          for (let dx = -reach; dx <= reach; dx++) {\\n            const ix = c.ix + dx;\\n            const iz = c.iz + dz;\\n            if (ix < 0 || iz < 0 || ix >= FIRE_N || iz >= FIRE_N) continue;\\n            const [cx, cz] = this.center(ix, iz);\\n            if (Math.hypot(cx - x, cz - z) > half) continue;\\n            const i = this.idx(ix, iz);\\n            if (this.fuel[i] === 0 || this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) continue;\\n            if (this.state[i] === 1 || this.state[i] === 0) this.markBurnt(i);\\n130→          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    this.burning = this.burning.filter((i) => this.state[i] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  step(dt) {\\n    this.time += dt;\\n    this.acc += dt;\\n140→    let guard = 0;\\n    while (this.acc >= 0.25 && guard++ < 6) {\\n      this.acc -= 0.25;\\n      this.spread();\\n      this.regrow();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  markBurnt(i) {\\n    if (this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) return;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/fire.js\",\"offset\":120,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"        for (let dz = -reach; dz <= reach; dz++) {\\n          for (let dx = -reach; dx <= reach; dx++) {\\n            const ix = c.ix + dx;\\n            const iz = c.iz + dz;\\n            if (ix < 0 || iz < 0 || ix >= FIRE_N || iz >= FIRE_N) continue;\\n            const [cx, cz] = this.center(ix, iz);\\n            if (Math.hypot(cx - x, cz - z) > half) continue;\\n            const i = this.idx(ix, iz);\\n            if (this.fuel[i] === 0 || this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) continue;\\n            if (this.state[i] === 1 || this.state[i] === 0) this.markBurnt(i);\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n    }\\n    this.burning = this.burning.filter((i) => this.state[i] === 1);\\n  }\\n\\n  step(dt) {\\n    this.time += dt;\\n    this.acc += dt;\\n    let guard = 0;\\n    while (this.acc >= 0.25 && guard++ < 6) {\\n      this.acc -= 0.25;\\n      this.spread();\\n      this.regrow();\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  markBurnt(i) {\\n    if (this.state[i] === 2 || this.state[i] === 3) return;\\n\",\"total_lines\":276}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"a3976e31-9514-4a19-a8d6-bb10db2a88c0"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_38","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fire logic looks correct. Now writing the bulk of the game.\n\nPlanning ten large files: content data, core systems, terrain, simulation world, audio, art, UI, networking, game scripts, tests, and build. Character speed will be checked at runtime. Confirmed the THREE import from pixel-engine.js.\n\nWorking through camera integration details. installLook must run in setup and onCameraChange. The wantsPointerLock accessor and gamepadButtons replacement are being wired up. The step function will use the passed state object for override and enabled flags.\n\nThe camera step will check `cam.enabled` to toggle yaw and pitch. `look.enabled` will be set during the update phase based on map or menu state. Pointer lock will be requested only while playing, with a `setWantLock` helper to manage the flag.\n\nThe pointer lock flag will be a local variable in the cam object, with an exported setter from look.js. A document listener will pause the game when pointer lock is lost during play. Pointer lock will be requested on pointerup if the wantLock flag is active.\n\nPointer lock will be requested with a promise-safe catch. Player position will use hero.feet when on foot, otherwise the vehicle position. Wade detection checks river polyline distance under eight units while excluding bridge areas. The hour advances by dt scaled to day minutes and wraps modulo 24.\n\nWind walk drifts direction by up to fifteen degrees per minute and speed by up to 0.05 per second, clamped between zero and eight. Mission pins can override the wind vector. Fire spreads by projecting the wind direction into a horizontal unit vector scaled by speed. Actors inside burning cells catch fire each fixed step. The player takes TUNING.fireDamage per second while in flames and clears after two seconds outside fuel or water.\n\nSoldier AI ticks at ten hertz. On fire, soldiers panic and move randomly while igniting cells and dying in five seconds. Hostile soldiers shoot after a reaction time when the player is visible within their vision cone.\n\nTests will verify day perception, night stealth, and faction contracts that prevent non-hostile soldiers from attacking until fired upon.\n\nThe world pass tracks the active mission giver faction as concord, harvest, or null. Civilians are neutral, ignore player damage, flee on injury, and only appear once in the ledger. Buddies are tracked separately with a down timer for rescue.\n\nBuddy rescue triggers when a character dies and an available buddy exists. The rescue scene lasts three seconds. Health restores to sixty for magicians or forty for others. The buddy is marked spent for one full day. A wound roll uses TUNING.buddyWoundChance. Availability requires the buddy to be met, alive, not downed, and free from prior spending. The world clock tracks absolute game time in seconds.\n\nWhen a buddy dies, it enters a forty-second down state. Near a down buddy within two and a half meters, the player sees a prompt. The options are to finish the buddy or use a syrette. If the buddy is burning or no syrettes remain, only the finish option appears; otherwise both appear. A test will verify that finishing kills the buddy while using a syrette revives them.\n\nSurgery triggers when health drops below twenty and the heal button is pressed. It locks movement for four seconds. If the player takes damage during surgery, it cancels. The scene type depends on the last damage source: fire causes cauterization, while other sources cycle through scenes. Syrette is a hold action that lasts 0.8 seconds when health is at or above twenty. Tests will verify that dying with a buddy revives the character to forty health, dying without a buddy triggers game over with the death subtitle, and pressing Q at fifteen health restores forty after four seconds.\n\nA syrette test will verify that holding Q for 0.8 seconds restores 40 health and consumes one syrette. A jam test will confirm that high jam rate prevents magazine depletion, allows repeated firing after reload, and requires multiple reloads. A break test will set gun condition to 0.5, apply high wear, fire until the slot empties, and verify the result. Locker and ground weapons will spawn with different starting conditions. A driving map test will check that entering a vehicle, opening the map, moving the cursor, setting a waypoint, and stepping while throttled keeps the vehicle moving at full speed. Music volume will be verified at boot as 0.1. A `world.sliderEffect` helper will handle slider-driven actions.\n\nTen slider tests are planned. They will verify player speed, damage taken, weapon damage, enemy health, accuracy, vision range, reaction time, wear rate, jam probability, and fire spread.\n\nFire spread will be tested by setting fireSpread to zero and three, then igniting and stepping to confirm only the initial cells burn without spreading. Fire damage will be verified by standing in fire for one second and checking that health drops exactly by TUNING.fireDamage. Wind effect will be tested by comparing windEffect values of zero and three against the computed lastWindFactor after a tick.\n\nThe remaining slider tests cover vehicle top speed, damage scaling, stone rewards, and buddy wound chance. The buddy wound test will use a 100 percent chance to force a wound and a zero percent chance to verify no wound occurs. Day length will be verified by stepping sixty frames and checking the hour delta. Post-reman hours will be tested after clearing the post and advancing the clock. Regrow hours will be tested by burning and advancing fire time to reach state three.\n\nA resetTuning() function will restore every TUNING key to its default and verify a sample system matches. The attract mode will trigger after ten seconds of idle input on the title or main menu, starting on frame 601.\n\nIdle input will be ignored on the first frames to prevent false attract triggers. Attract exit will call world.resetSoft() rather than world.reset(), and the test will spy localStorage.setItem to confirm no save is written. The attract loop will use a twelve-second beats array with teleporting actors, camera overrides, god mode enabled, and saves disabled.\n\nThe attract mode will display a DEMO tag in the HUD and set state.attract to true. Touch input still increments idle time and starts attract, but the notice flag remains set on exit. The dev sliders UI will list controls with left and right buttons to adjust values, plus a reset button. Tests will exercise both the menu path and the direct `game.dev.setSlider(k, v)` function to verify that moving a slider immediately changes its system parameter.\n\nThe dev slider test will open the menu, focus each parameter in turn, and press the right arrow to raise it. A `game.dev.nudge(key, dir)` helper will handle both the UI buttons and the test script.\n\nThe dev menu will hide its sliders from the pause menu during active sessions. Reset will be a confirm action on the Reset item. Terrain generation may use a 256 by 256 cell grid if benchmarking requires it.\n\nTerrain generation will use a 512 by 512 grid, with a benchmark on the first boot to gauge performance. Road distance lookups will be precomputed into a Set of fire cell indices for O(1) access. Height stamping will sample road distance rather than evaluate every segment, keeping eight million hypot calls under one hundred milliseconds. Sites will use radial falloff. The terrain.js implementation is being written now.\n\nEach terrain cell stores a base color that fire recolors on burn. A five-meter fire cell maps to four adjacent terrain cells. Colors will be updated per cell but throttled to avoid heavy mesh uploads during large fires. land.update() will not be called after painting.\n\nBiome colors will be baked into terrain geometry at generation time, storing a base Uint8 RGB copy per cell. Water wading will use the river polyline instead of the mesh. Static THREE boxes will serve as buildings at sites to keep the world populated. A player viewmodel box parented to the camera may be added, but headless mode might not support it.\n\nThe runner will treat mission scripts as data-only functions. Each script step references an id that the runner resolves and executes by calling world.scripts[step.id](world, dt). Scripts return true when they finish. This keeps the content file free of logic.\n\nAll mission script IDs will be verified as static references. Every line referenced in missions must exist in dialogue.js. The dialogue file will store verbatim sentences from the plan, uppercased to match the font charset while preserving apostrophes.\n\nSubtitle lines will be split across sequential lines with a sixty-character limit per line. A test helper will enforce this length constraint.\n\nThe central line is fifty-eight characters. Twelve epigraphs will be added. About pages will be uppercase. Feedback answers will be drafted now and updated after tests run.\n\nThe exact usage string \"added on import\" will be exported from about.js for the drawn page. Files will be written in batched Write calls to stay within response size limits. The most important simulation file will be completed first. A slightly simplified mission set may still include all missions, though M8's 120-second hold could slow tests.\n\nCharacterController.fixedUpdate is the main bottleneck, but seventy-two hundred calls over two minutes should remain fast enough. The full controller must run during holds to keep the simulation realistic. Content, core systems, terrain, and the simulation world will be written in this turn; tests will follow. PROGRESS.md will be updated so a compact can resume work later. A proof script for the title and kit will be added to static tests once the first checklist items are marked complete.\n\nThe full source tree is now mapped out: sites, weapons, roads, dialogue, missions, notes, about, actions, look, save, terrain, audio, models, net, ui, world, game, and main. A local node script was considered but rejected in favor of the Write tool for generating the actual game source. world.js will be kept as the clean heart of the simulation. tests/run.mjs will be included in the same batch so the suite can run immediately.\n\nFaction assignments are now defined. Vance and Concord soldiers belong to Concord. Ansa and Harvest belong to Harvest. Odile, Tibor, Bakr, and Harrow are neutral. M0 through M9 each set a giver faction pass while active. Safehouses will be pump-shed after M1, ranger after M2, and the water-tower starts guarded.\n\nSleep will be implemented as a safehouse bed action that saves the player. The shop will be reachable through Tibor until mission seven, then through a locker; buying a gun unlocks the locker copy. A test will verify stone drops and the wear multiplier. The tracker will beep at a rate that scales with distance to the case when held near it. Trig notes will unlock after near trig, and the clean empire note will appear in the locker once all six are collected. Using the rail halt costs one stone, advances one hour, and displays a line from Bakr.\n\nPost remans will use a `gameHours` float that increments by `dt / (TUNING.dayMinutes * 60) * 24`. A post reappears after `postRemanHours` game hours. Tests can advance time via `dev.advanceHours(1)` or sleep, since both use the same clock.\n\nA save-and-load round-trip test will serialize the world, mutate it, and reload the snapshot to verify that fire state matches. The engine will step one frame after loading so commands apply before assertions.\n\nSave and load will persist to localStorage when available. The code will be written in large files with a slightly denser style. Simple soldier models will be created for the static model check, with fixes applied afterward if they fail. The grass flame texture will use four 10x14 frames on a 40x14 sheet, drawn as solid blobs rather than speckles to avoid isolated texel noise.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1ce6170a-5e52-48d2-90ac-0b42db081e86-76","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/texture/types.d.ts","limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":526,"output_tokens":5327,"cache_read_input_tokens":175616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ab9b7e75-25fd-433d-8174-29cc7b79236b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1ce6170a-5e52-48d2-90ac-0b42db081e86-76","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/**\\n * The texture format: a pixel-art texture as plain data (docs/assets/textures.md). A def lists layers drawn in order onto a `size` grid of texels in\\n * its palette's slots; `bakeTexture` turns it into palette indices and RGBA, headless and pure.\\n *\\n *   textureDef({ id: 'planks', about: 'Floor boards', tags: ['wood'], size: [16, 16], tile: true,\\n *     palette: { gap: 'ink', wood: 'orange', wood2: 'red' },\\n *     layers: [{ pattern: 'planks', colors: ['gap', 'wood', 'wood2'], seed: 2 }] });\\n */\\nimport type { Provenance } from '../model/types';\\n10→import type { PaletteColor } from '../palette';\\n/** A key of the def's palette. Layers never name PALETTE colours directly. */\\nexport type TexSlot = string;\\nexport type PatternId = 'noise' | 'bricks' | 'planks' | 'tiles' | 'cobbles' | 'stripes' | 'checker' | 'scatter' | 'cracks' | 'gradient';\\n/**\\n * Rows of characters, one per texel, as `hud.sprite` draws them: each character is a legend key\\n * (its slot), and `.` or a space is transparent. `at` offsets the rows; `mirror: 'x'` adds the rows\\n * mirrored to their right (a symmetric sprite from its left half), `'y'` below.\\n */\\nexport interface PixelsLayer {\\n20→    readonly pixels: readonly string[];\\n    readonly legend: Readonly<Record<string, TexSlot>>;\\n    readonly at?: readonly [x: number, y: number];\\n    readonly mirror?: 'x' | 'y';\\n}\\n/**\\n * A seeded generator painting a ramp of slots (`colors`, dark to light; one slot is a flat\\n * fill). Periodic when the def `tile`s, so it wraps without a seam. Its own parameters are listed\\n * by `PATTERNS` (patterns.ts); `dither` blends between ramp steps with a 4×4 ordered dither.\\n */\\n30→export interface PatternLayer {\\n    readonly pattern: PatternId;\\n    readonly colors: TexSlot | readonly TexSlot[];\\n    readonly seed?: number;\\n    readonly dither?: boolean;\\n    readonly [param: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n/** An SVG path (M L H V C Q Z, the model `slab` subset) in texel units, no anti-aliasing. */\\nexport interface PathLayer {\\n    readonly path: string;\\n40→    readonly fill?: TexSlot;\\n    readonly stroke?: TexSlot;\\n}\\n/**\\n * A 1-texel outline in `outline`'s slot round every opaque texel (on the transparent side). On a\\n * sprite sheet it stays inside each frame; patterns and paths don't know about frames.\\n */\\nexport interface OutlineLayer {\\n    readonly outline: TexSlot;\\n}\\n50→export type Layer = PixelsLayer | PatternLayer | PathLayer | OutlineLayer;\\nexport interface TextureDef {\\n    readonly id: string;\\n    /** One line: what it is (`npm run tex -- find` searches it). */\\n    readonly about: string;\\n    readonly tags: readonly string[];\\n    /** Texels, width × height; powers of two for surfaces that tile. Sprite sheets: all frames. */\\n    readonly size: readonly [w: number, h: number];\\n    /** Slots → PALETTE names (at most 255). Layers name slots, never colours, so a bake can re-bind them. */\\n    readonly palette: Readonly<Record<TexSlot, PaletteColor>>;\\n60→    /** Seamless: patterns wrap by construction; the check measures the seam of pixels, paths and gradients. */\\n    readonly tile?: boolean;\\n    /** Sprite sheets: this many frames left to right; they must divide the width. */\\n    readonly frames?: number;\\n    readonly layers: readonly Layer[];\\n    /**\\n     * Where an imported texture came from (`npm run tex -- import`), as models record it: url,\\n     * licence, file, author, sha256, tool, and each slot's source colour. The check refuses a\\n     * missing url or licence, or one not allowed (`LICENCES`).\\n     */\\n70→    readonly source?: Provenance;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/**\\n * The texture format: a pixel-art texture as plain data (docs/assets/textures.md). A def lists layers drawn in order onto a `size` grid of texels in\\n * its palette's slots; `bakeTexture` turns it into palette indices and RGBA, headless and pure.\\n *\\n *   textureDef({ id: 'planks', about: 'Floor boards', tags: ['wood'], size: [16, 16], tile: true,\\n *     palette: { gap: 'ink', wood: 'orange', wood2: 'red' },\\n *     layers: [{ pattern: 'planks', colors: ['gap', 'wood', 'wood2'], seed: 2 }] });\\n */\\nimport type { Provenance } from '../model/types';\\n10→import type { PaletteColor } from '../palette';\\n/** A key of the def's palette. Layers never name PALETTE colours directly. */\\nexport type TexSlot = string;\\nexport type PatternId = 'noise' | 'bricks' | 'planks' | 'tiles' | 'cobbles' | 'stripes' | 'checker' | 'scatter' | 'cracks' | 'gradient';\\n/**\\n * Rows of characters, one per texel, as `hud.sprite` draws them: each character is a legend key\\n * (its slot), and `.` or a space is transparent. `at` offsets the rows; `mirror: 'x'` adds the rows\\n * mirrored to their right (a symmetric sprite from its left half), `'y'` below.\\n */\\nexport interface PixelsLayer {\\n20→    readonly pixels: readonly string[];\\n    readonly legend: Readonly<Record<string, TexSlot>>;\\n    readonly at?: readonly [x: number, y: number];\\n    readonly mirror?: 'x' | 'y';\\n}\\n/**\\n * A seeded generator painting a ramp of slots (`colors`, dark to light; one slot is a flat\\n * fill). Periodic when the def `tile`s, so it wraps without a seam. Its own parameters are listed\\n * by `PATTERNS` (patterns.ts); `dither` blends between ramp steps with a 4×4 ordered dither.\\n */\\n30→export interface PatternLayer {\\n    readonly pattern: PatternId;\\n    readonly colors: TexSlot | readonly TexSlot[];\\n    readonly seed?: number;\\n    readonly dither?: boolean;\\n    readonly [param: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n/** An SVG path (M L H V C Q Z, the model `slab` subset) in texel units, no anti-aliasing. */\\nexport interface PathLayer {\\n    readonly path: string;\\n40→    readonly fill?: TexSlot;\\n    readonly stroke?: TexSlot;\\n}\\n/**\\n * A 1-texel outline in `outline`'s slot round every opaque texel (on the transparent side). On a\\n * sprite sheet it stays inside each frame; patterns and paths don't know about frames.\\n */\\nexport interface OutlineLayer {\\n    readonly outline: TexSlot;\\n}\\n50→export type Layer = PixelsLayer | PatternLayer | PathLayer | OutlineLayer;\\nexport interface TextureDef {\\n    readonly id: string;\\n    /** One line: what it is (`npm run tex -- find` searches it). */\\n    readonly about: string;\\n    readonly tags: readonly string[];\\n    /** Texels, width × height; powers of two for surfaces that tile. Sprite sheets: all frames. */\\n    readonly size: readonly [w: number, h: number];\\n    /** Slots → PALETTE names (at most 255). Layers name slots, never colours, so a bake can re-bind them. */\\n    readonly palette: Readonly<Record<TexSlot, PaletteColor>>;\\n60→    /** Seamless: patterns wrap by construction; the check measures the seam of pixels, paths and gradients. */\\n    readonly tile?: boolean;\\n    /** Sprite sheets: this many frames left to right; they must divide the width. */\\n    readonly frames?: number;\\n    readonly layers: readonly Layer[];\\n    /**\\n     * Where an imported texture came from (`npm run tex -- import`), as models record it: url,\\n     * licence, file, author, sha256, tool, and each slot's source colour. The check refuses a\\n     * missing url or licence, or one not allowed (`LICENCES`).\\n     */\\n70→    readonly source?: Provenance;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/texture/types.d.ts\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/**\\n * The texture format: a pixel-art texture as plain data (docs/assets/textures.md). A def lists layers drawn in order onto a `size` grid of texels in\\n * its palette's slots; `bakeTexture` turns it into palette indices and RGBA, headless and pure.\\n *\\n *   textureDef({ id: 'planks', about: 'Floor boards', tags: ['wood'], size: [16, 16], tile: true,\\n *     palette: { gap: 'ink', wood: 'orange', wood2: 'red' },\\n *     layers: [{ pattern: 'planks', colors: ['gap', 'wood', 'wood2'], seed: 2 }] });\\n */\\nimport type { Provenance } from '../model/types';\\nimport type { PaletteColor } from '../palette';\\n/** A key of the def's palette. Layers never name PALETTE colours directly. */\\nexport type TexSlot = string;\\nexport type PatternId = 'noise' | 'bricks' | 'planks' | 'tiles' | 'cobbles' | 'stripes' | 'checker' | 'scatter' | 'cracks' | 'gradient';\\n/**\\n * Rows of characters, one per texel, as `hud.sprite` draws them: each character is a legend key\\n * (its slot), and `.` or a space is transparent. `at` offsets the rows; `mirror: 'x'` adds the rows\\n * mirrored to their right (a symmetric sprite from its left half), `'y'` below.\\n */\\nexport interface PixelsLayer {\\n    readonly pixels: readonly string[];\\n    readonly legend: Readonly<Record<string, TexSlot>>;\\n    readonly at?: readonly [x: number, y: number];\\n    readonly mirror?: 'x' | 'y';\\n}\\n/**\\n * A seeded generator painting a ramp of slots (`colors`, dark to light; one slot is a flat\\n * fill). Periodic when the def `tile`s, so it wraps without a seam. Its own parameters are listed\\n * by `PATTERNS` (patterns.ts); `dither` blends between ramp steps with a 4×4 ordered dither.\\n */\\nexport interface PatternLayer {\\n    readonly pattern: PatternId;\\n    readonly colors: TexSlot | readonly TexSlot[];\\n    readonly seed?: number;\\n    readonly dither?: boolean;\\n    readonly [param: string]: unknown;\\n}\\n/** An SVG path (M L H V C Q Z, the model `slab` subset) in texel units, no anti-aliasing. */\\nexport interface PathLayer {\\n    readonly path: string;\\n    readonly fill?: TexSlot;\\n    readonly stroke?: TexSlot;\\n}\\n/**\\n * A 1-texel outline in `outline`'s slot round every opaque texel (on the transparent side). On a\\n * sprite sheet it stays inside each frame; patterns and paths don't know about frames.\\n */\\nexport interface OutlineLayer {\\n    readonly outline: TexSlot;\\n}\\nexport type Layer = PixelsLayer | PatternLayer | PathLayer | OutlineLayer;\\nexport interface TextureDef {\\n    readonly id: string;\\n    /** One line: what it is (`npm run tex -- find` searches it). */\\n    readonly about: string;\\n    readonly tags: readonly string[];\\n    /** Texels, width × height; powers of two for surfaces that tile. Sprite sheets: all frames. */\\n    readonly size: readonly [w: number, h: number];\\n    /** Slots → PALETTE names (at most 255). Layers name slots, never colours, so a bake can re-bind them. */\\n    readonly palette: Readonly<Record<TexSlot, PaletteColor>>;\\n    /** Seamless: patterns wrap by construction; the check measures the seam of pixels, paths and gradients. */\\n    readonly tile?: boolean;\\n    /** Sprite sheets: this many frames left to right; they must divide the width. */\\n    readonly frames?: number;\\n    readonly layers: readonly Layer[];\\n    /**\\n     * Where an imported texture came from (`npm run tex -- import`), as models record it: url,\\n     * licence, file, author, sha256, tool, and each slot's source colour. The check refuses a\\n     * missing url or licence, or one not allowed (`LICENCES`).\\n     */\\n    readonly source?: Provenance;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":71}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"70bc8a76-765b-4083-8b71-2a0ff6998859"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_39","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A simple non-tiling flame texture with solid shapes will keep isolated texels low.\n\nA minimal boot smoke test will verify terrain and player before expanding. Dense code and a layered build strategy will save tokens.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Fire spread is in the right band. Next I’ll get a headless world booting, then hang the rest of the systems on it."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-77","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/sites.js","new_string":"/** Places in the Kettle. Positions are world metres, +x east, -z north. */\nexport const SITES = [\n  { id: 'mile-forty', name: 'MILE FORTY', x: 0, z: 40, r: 70, kind: 'town' },\n  { id: 'pump-shed', name: 'PUMP SHED', x: -120, z: 150, kind: 'safehouse' },\n  { id: 'ranger-post', name: 'RANGER POST', x: 40, z: -170, kind: 'post' },\n  { id: 'water-tower', name: 'WATER TOWER', x: 470, z: -180, kind: 'safehouse' },\n  { id: 'fort-clement', name: 'FORT CLEMENT', x: -430, z: -180, kind: 'hq', faction: 'concord' },\n  { id: 'long-field', name: 'THE LONG FIELD', x: -260, z: -300, kind: 'field' },\n  { id: 'granary', name: 'THE GRANARY', x: 400, z: 280, kind: 'hq', faction: 'harvest' },\n  { id: 'east-siding', name: 'EAST SIDING', x: 430, z: -60, kind: 'depot' },\n  { id: 'three-wells', name: 'THREE WELLS', x: -260, z: 240, kind: 'village' },\n  { id: 'pump-station', name: 'PUMP STATION', x: -330, z: 395, kind: 'pump' },\n  { id: 'salt-pan', name: 'SALT PAN', x: 200, z: 470, kind: 'flats' },\n  { id: 'the-cut', name: 'THE CUT', x: 150, z: -300, kind: 'mine' },\n  { id: 'observatory', name: 'OBSERVATORY', x: -130, z: -520, kind: 'trig' },\n  { id: 'the-pass', name: 'THE PASS', x: -590, z: -430, kind: 'pass' },\n  { id: 'clinic', name: 'MERCY MISSION', x: 12, z: 55, kind: 'clinic' },\n  { id: 'tibor', name: 'TIBOR SHED', x: -18, z: 62, kind: 'shop' },\n  { id: 'bar', name: 'THE BAR', x: 22, z: 28, kind: 'bar' },\n  { id: 'sluice', name: 'SLUICE HOUSE', x: 168, z: -286, kind: 'loot' },\n];\n\nexport const POSTS = [\n  { id: 'p1', name: 'NORTH POST', x: 90, z: -80, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\n  { id: 'p2', name: 'WEST POST', x: -200, z: 30, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\n  { id: 'p3', name: 'EAST POST', x: 170, z: 90, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\n  { id: 'p4', name: 'FORT ROAD', x: -320, z: -90, faction: 'concord', n: 6 },\n  { id: 'p5', name: 'MINE ROAD', x: 280, z: -210, faction: 'harvest', n: 5 },\n  { id: 'p6', name: 'SALT ROAD', x: 300, z: 390, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\n];\n\nexport const TRIGS = [\n  { id: 't1', name: 'RIDGE TRIG', x: -130, z: -500 },\n  { id: 't2', name: 'WEST TRIG', x: -400, z: -40 },\n  { id: 't3', name: 'EAST TRIG', x: 280, z: 40 },\n  { id: 't4', name: 'MERCY TRIG', x: -40, z: 280 },\n  { id: 't5', name: 'GRANARY TRIG', x: 460, z: 180 },\n  { id: 't6', name: 'CUT TRIG', x: 60, z: -420 },\n];\n\nexport const CASES = [\n  { id: 'c1', x: -80, z: -40, stones: 3 },\n  { id: 'c2', x: 210, z: 20, stones: 4 },\n  { id: 'c3', x: -300, z: -240, stones: 5 },\n  { id: 'c4', x: 360, z: -40, stones: 2 },\n  { id: 'c5', x: 40, z: 300, stones: 6 },\n  { id: 'c6', x: -180, z: 180, stones: 3 },\n  { id: 'c7', x: 500, z: 40, stones: 4 },\n  { id: 'c8', x: -480, z: -300, stones: 5 },\n  { id: 'c9', x: 140, z: 420, stones: 2 },\n  { id: 'c10', x: 20, z: -360, stones: 4 },\n  { id: 'c11', x: 300, z: -300, stones: 3 },\n  { id: 'c12', x: -90, z: 420, stones: 6 },\n];\n\nexport const HALTS = [\n  { id: 'west-cutting', name: 'WEST CUTTING', x: -400, z: 100 },\n  { id: 'mile-halt', name: 'MILE FORTY HALT', x: 0, z: 70 },\n  { id: 'east-halt', name: 'EAST SIDING HALT', x: 430, z: -60 },\n  { id: 'cut-spur', name: 'CUT SPUR', x: 180, z: -220 },\n];\n\n/** Story scars. Burned grass cannot burn twice, so the column can walk them. */\nexport const STRIPS = {\n  A: { width: 30, points: [[430, -60], [320, -150], [220, -230], [150, -300]] },\n  C: { width: 26, points: [[90, -280], [150, -300], [230, -290]] },\n  B: { width: 30, points: [[150, -300], [-40, -310], [-260, -300], [-420, -370], [-590, -430]] },\n};\n\nexport function siteById(id) {\n  return SITES.find((s) => s.id === id) || POSTS.find((s) => s.id === id) || HALTS.find((s) => s.id === id) || null;\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-78","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/roads.js","new_string":"/** Polylines in world metres. Painted as dirt and given no fire fuel. */\nexport const ROADS = [\n  { id: 'north', pts: [[0, 40], [40, -20], [90, -80], [40, -170], [150, -300]] },\n  { id: 'west', pts: [[0, 40], [-100, 40], [-200, 30], [-260, 240], [-330, 395]] },\n  { id: 'fort', pts: [[-200, 30], [-320, -90], [-430, -180], [-260, -300]] },\n  { id: 'east', pts: [[0, 40], [170, 90], [250, 80], [400, 280]] },\n  { id: 'siding', pts: [[250, 80], [430, -60], [470, -180]] },\n  { id: 'salt', pts: [[400, 280], [300, 390], [200, 470]] },\n  { id: 'back', pts: [[0, 40], [120, 230], [300, 390]] },\n  { id: 'pass', pts: [[-260, -300], [-420, -360], [-590, -430]] },\n  { id: 'ridge', pts: [[150, -300], [40, -400], [-130, -520]] },\n  { id: 'ford', pts: [[0, 40], [-60, 300]] },\n];\n\nexport const RIVER = [\n  [600, -640], [420, -320], [300, -120], [250, 80], [120, 230],\n  [-60, 300], [-240, 380], [-420, 430], [-640, 470],\n];\n\nexport const RAIL = [\n  [-640, 110], [-400, 100], [0, 70], [270, -5], [430, -60], [640, -110],\n];\n\nexport const BRIDGES = [\n  { x: 250, z: 80 },\n  { x: 120, z: 230 },\n  { x: -60, z: 300 },\n];\n\nexport function distToPoly(x, z, pts) {\n  let best = Infinity;\n  for (let i = 1; i < pts.length; i++) {\n    const ax = pts[i - 1][0];\n    const az = pts[i - 1][1];\n    const bx = pts[i][0];\n    const bz = pts[i][1];\n    const dx = bx - ax;\n    const dz = bz - az;\n    const l2 = dx * dx + dz * dz || 1;\n    let t = ((x - ax) * dx + (z - az) * dz) / l2;\n    if (t < 0) t = 0;\n    else if (t > 1) t = 1;\n    const px = ax + dx * t;\n    const pz = az + dz * t;\n    const d = Math.hypot(x - px, z - pz);\n    if (d < best) best = d;\n  }\n  return best;\n}\n\nexport function nearRoad(x, z, width = 8) {\n  for (const road of ROADS) if (distToPoly(x, z, road.pts) < width) return true;\n  return false;\n}\n\nexport function nearRiver(x, z, width = 8) {\n  return distToPoly(x, z, RIVER) < width;\n}\n\nexport function onBridge(x, z) {\n  for (const b of BRIDGES) if (Math.hypot(x - b.x, z - b.z) < 16) return true;\n  return false;\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-79","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/weapons.js","new_string":"/** Original guns. Locker copies start clean. Ground copies start worn. */\nexport const WEAPONS = [\n  { id: 'cane', name: 'CANE KNIFE', slot: 'melee', mag: 0, reserve: 0, rate: 1.6, damage: 55, range: 2.2, wear: 0, melee: true },\n  { id: 'm38', name: 'SERVICE REVOLVER', slot: 'sidearm', mag: 6, reserve: 36, rate: 3, damage: 34, range: 45, wear: 0.5 },\n  { id: 'flare', name: 'FLARE PISTOL', slot: 'sidearm', mag: 1, reserve: 8, rate: 0.6, damage: 12, range: 70, wear: 0, ignite: 2, arc: true },\n  { id: 'tractor', name: 'TRACTOR RIFLE', slot: 'main', mag: 30, reserve: 150, rate: 9, damage: 24, range: 110, wear: 0.35, auto: true },\n  { id: 'mule', name: 'MULE PUMP GUN', slot: 'main', mag: 6, reserve: 36, rate: 1.1, damage: 9, range: 22, wear: 0.8, pellets: 10 },\n  { id: 'empire', name: 'OLD EMPIRE', slot: 'main', mag: 5, reserve: 30, rate: 0.8, damage: 95, range: 320, wear: 1, scope: 12 },\n  { id: 'weed', name: 'WEED BURNER', slot: 'special', mag: 120, reserve: 240, rate: 8, damage: 28, range: 14, wear: 0.12, ignite: 3, stream: true },\n  { id: 'tube', name: 'LONG TUBE', slot: 'special', mag: 1, reserve: 5, rate: 0.4, damage: 180, range: 160, wear: 2, blast: 6, ignite: 6 },\n  { id: 'mg', name: 'MOUNTED MG', slot: 'mounted', mag: 999, reserve: 0, rate: 10, damage: 20, range: 180, wear: 0, auto: true, heat: 6 },\n  { id: 'molotov', name: 'BOTTLE', slot: 'throw', mag: 1, reserve: 0, rate: 0.8, damage: 5, range: 25, wear: 0, ignite: 4, carry: 3 },\n  { id: 'charge', name: 'REMOTE CHARGE', slot: 'throw', mag: 1, reserve: 0, rate: 0.5, damage: 220, range: 3, wear: 0, blast: 7, ignite: 7, plant: true, carry: 2 },\n];\n\nexport const WEAPON_BY_ID = Object.fromEntries(WEAPONS.map((w) => [w.id, w]));\n\nexport const UPGRADES = [\n  { id: 'clean', name: 'CLEANING KIT', cost: 6, about: 'WEAR SLOWS' },\n  { id: 'pouch', name: 'SYRETTE POUCH', cost: 5, about: 'CARRY FIVE' },\n  { id: 'belt', name: 'AMMO BELT', cost: 5, about: 'MORE RESERVE' },\n  { id: 'vkit', name: 'VEHICLE KIT', cost: 6, about: 'FASTER REPAIR' },\n];\n\nexport function freshWeapon(id, cond) {\n  const def = WEAPON_BY_ID[id];\n  if (!def) return null;\n  const reserve = def.reserve ? Math.round(def.reserve * (1)) : 0;\n  return {\n    id,\n    name: def.name,\n    slot: def.slot,\n    cond,\n    jammed: false,\n    jamLeft: 0,\n    mag: def.mag,\n    magSize: def.mag,\n    reserve,\n    cooldown: 0,\n    shots: 0,\n  };\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-80","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/core/actions.js","new_string":"/** Gameplay asks for actions. Devices stay apart: Pad* codes never match keys. */\nexport const ACTIONS = {\n  fire: { pad: ['PadR2'], key: ['MouseLeft'] },\n  aim: { pad: ['PadL2'], key: ['MouseRight'] },\n  use: { pad: ['PadSquare'], key: ['KeyE'] },\n  reload: { pad: ['PadSquare'], key: ['KeyR'] },\n  jump: { pad: ['PadCross'], key: ['Space'] },\n  crouch: { pad: ['PadCircle'], key: ['KeyC'] },\n  sprint: { pad: ['PadL3'], key: ['ShiftLeft'] },\n  melee: { pad: ['PadR3'], key: ['KeyF'] },\n  next: { pad: ['PadTriangle'], key: ['Digit1', 'Digit2', 'Digit3', 'Digit4'] },\n  throw: { pad: ['PadR1'], key: ['KeyG'] },\n  heal: { pad: ['PadL1'], key: ['KeyQ'] },\n  map: { pad: ['PadUp'], key: ['KeyM', 'Tab'] },\n  tablet: { pad: ['PadDown'], key: ['KeyH'] },\n  tracker: { pad: ['PadLeft'], key: ['KeyT'] },\n  mono: { pad: ['PadRight'], key: ['KeyV'] },\n  pause: { pad: ['PadOptions'], key: ['Escape'] },\n  ledger: { pad: ['PadCreate'], key: ['KeyJ'] },\n  confirm: { pad: ['PadCross'], key: ['Enter', 'Space'] },\n  back: { pad: ['PadCircle'], key: ['Escape'] },\n  left: { pad: ['PadLeft'], key: ['ArrowLeft', 'KeyA'] },\n  right: { pad: ['PadRight'], key: ['ArrowRight', 'KeyD'] },\n  up: { pad: ['PadUp'], key: ['ArrowUp', 'KeyW'] },\n  down: { pad: ['PadDown'], key: ['ArrowDown', 'KeyS'] },\n};\n\nexport function codes(action) {\n  const a = ACTIONS[action];\n  return a ? [...a.pad, ...a.key] : [];\n}\n\nexport function consumeAction(input, action) {\n  const a = ACTIONS[action];\n  if (!a) return false;\n  return input.consumeAny(a.pad) || input.consumeAny(a.key);\n}\n\nexport function pressedAction(input, action) {\n  const a = ACTIONS[action];\n  if (!a) return false;\n  return a.pad.some((c) => input.wasPressed(c)) || a.key.some((c) => input.wasPressed(c));\n}\n\nexport function heldAction(input, action) {\n  const a = ACTIONS[action];\n  if (!a) return false;\n  return input.anyDown(a.pad) || input.anyDown(a.key);\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-81","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/core/look.js","new_string":"/** First-person look. Re-install after every setCamera while the preset is first. */\nlet wantLock = false;\n\nexport function setWantLock(v) {\n  wantLock = !!v;\n}\n\nexport function installLook(ctx, cam) {\n  ctx.camera.step = function (u) {\n    if (cam.override) {\n      this.camera.position.set(cam.override.position[0], cam.override.position[1], cam.override.position[2]);\n      this.camera.lookAt(cam.override.target[0], cam.override.target[1], cam.override.target[2]);\n      this.focus.copy(this.camera.position);\n      return;\n    }\n    const k = cam.enabled ? 1 : 0;\n    const mx = u.input.mouseDelta.x;\n    const my = u.input.mouseDelta.y;\n    this.yaw -= mx * 0.0025 * cam.sensX * k;\n    const inv = cam.invertY ? -1 : 1;\n    this.pitch = Math.max(-1.45, Math.min(1.45, this.pitch - my * 0.0025 * cam.sensY * inv * k));\n    this.focus.copy(u.target);\n    this.camera.position.copy(u.eye);\n    this.camera.rotation.set(this.pitch, this.yaw, 0);\n  };\n  ctx.input.gamepadButtons = {\n    0: 'PadCross', 1: 'PadCircle', 2: 'PadSquare', 3: 'PadTriangle',\n    4: 'PadL1', 5: 'PadR1', 6: 'PadL2', 7: 'PadR2',\n    8: 'PadCreate', 9: 'PadOptions', 10: 'PadL3', 11: 'PadR3',\n    12: 'PadUp', 13: 'PadDown', 14: 'PadLeft', 15: 'PadRight',\n  };\n  Object.defineProperty(ctx.input, 'wantsPointerLock', {\n    get: () => wantLock,\n    set() {},\n    configurable: true,\n  });\n}\n\nexport const LOOK = {\n  scene: [\n    { id: 'adjust', params: { brightness: 0, contrast: 1.06, saturation: 1.05, warmth: 0.04 } },\n    { id: 'chromatic', params: { spread: 0 } },\n    { id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: 0.28, softness: 0.7, amount: 1 } },\n  ],\n  actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.45, crease: 0.08 }, filters: [] },\n  environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.32, crease: 0.05 }, filters: [] },\n};\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f94416b1-3cd1-4382-ba1e-32f658728652-82","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/core/save.js","new_string":"const KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-save';\nconst SETTINGS_KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-settings';\n\nexport function storage() {\n  try {\n    if (typeof localStorage === 'undefined' || !localStorage) return null;\n    return localStorage;\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nexport function writeSave(data) {\n  const s = storage();\n  if (!s) return false;\n  s.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\n  return true;\n}\n\nexport function readSave() {\n  const s = storage();\n  if (!s) return null;\n  const raw = s.getItem(KEY);\n  if (!raw) return null;\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n\nexport function writeSettings(data) {\n  const s = storage();\n  if (!s) return;\n  s.setItem(SETTINGS_KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\n}\n\nexport function readSettings() {\n  const s = storage();\n  if (!s) return null;\n  const raw = s.getItem(SETTINGS_KEY);\n  if (!raw) return null;\n  try {\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6270,"output_tokens":5887,"cache_read_input_tokens":176128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"5c31f196-a330-4a52-b28e-d2e43f5cad2b"}
