road': 'A MAN ASKED ME TO MINE HIS OWN ROAD, SO HE WOULD KNOW',\\n  'dov:road2': 'WHERE IT WAS SAFE. HE WAS RIGHT FOR A WEEK.',\\n  'dov:m4': 'PLANT THESE ON THE BRIDGE. I WILL TELL YOU WHEN.',\\n  'mags:work': 'HOLD STILL. NO, YOU CANNOT FEEL THAT. NO, THAT IS NORMAL.',\\n  'mags:work2': 'HOLD STILL.',\\n  'mags:owe': 'NOT TODAY. TODAY YOU OWE ME MONEY.',\\n  'mags:m5': 'OPEN THE BYPASS AND HOLD THE PUMP. THE CISTERN CAN FILL.',\\n40→  'buddy:burn': 'DO NOT LET IT BE THE FIRE. PLEASE. NOT THE FIRE.',\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/dialogue.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/** Spoken lines. Each fits the HUD font and stays at or under 60 characters. */\\nexport const LINES = {\\n  'bakr:m0.1': 'FORTY MILES OF TRACK AND NOT ONE STATION',\\n  'bakr:m0.2': 'THAT REMEMBERS ITS NAME.',\\n  'bakr:m0.3': 'THEY PAINT THE SIGNS OVER. WHOEVER WON LAST.',\\n  'bakr:m0.4': 'YOU HAVE THE LOOK OF A MAN WHO READ ABOUT THIS PLACE.',\\n  'bakr:m0.5': 'READING IS A GOOD WAY TO VISIT.',\\n  'bakr:m0.6': 'UP THERE THEY WILL ASK YOU WHICH SIDE. SAY YES.',\\n  'bakr:halt': 'THIS HALT USED TO HAVE A LONGER NAME.',\\n  'odile:m1.1': 'THREE TABLETS. THE FOURTH YOU PAY FOR.',\\n  'odile:m1.2': 'I DO NOT MEAN IN STONES.',\\n  'odile:m1.3': 'I DO NOT NEED YOU TO BE GOOD. I NEED YOU TO BE ON TIME.',\\n  'odile:m1.4': 'SIXTY-ONE BEDS. FORTY BLANKETS. YOU ARE THE MATH.',\\n  'odile:refuse': 'COME BACK WHEN THE WELLS HAVE WATER. I AM COUNTING.',\\n  'odile:m8.1': 'GET THEM ON THE TRAIN. COUNT THE ONES WHO MAKE IT.',\\n  'vance:m3.1': 'WE DO NOT BURN VILLAGES. WE CONCLUDE THEM.',\\n  'vance:m3.2': 'THE DEPOT IS A REGRETTABLE MATTER. CONCLUDE IT.',\\n  'vance:m5.1': 'THE WATER QUESTION HAS BEEN A GREAT SORROW TO THIS OFFICE.',\\n  'vance:m5.2': 'YOUR INVOICE WILL BE HONOURED, REGRETTABLY.',\\n  'vance:pay': 'THE MATTER IS CLOSED. THE INVOICE WILL FOLLOW.',\\n  'ansa:m4.1': 'YOU SAID LESS PEOPLE. FEWER. FEWER PEOPLE.',\\n  'ansa:m4.2': 'IT WILL MATTER BY THE END OF THE MONTH.',\\n  'ansa:m6.1': 'BURN THE FIELD. A HUNGRY MAN LEARNS TO READ THE WIND.',\\n  'ansa:pay': 'THE GRAMMAR WAS THE LEAST OF IT. TAKE THE STONES.',\\n  'tibor:shop': 'EVERYTHING ON THIS RACK HAS BEEN RETURNED AT LEAST ONCE.',\\n  'tibor:price': 'IT FIRES. IF YOU WANT IT TO FIRE TWICE, THAT IS A DIFFERENT PRICE.',\\n  'tibor:m2.1': 'SHE OWES ME A PLANE. I OWE HER A KEY. FETCH HER.',\\n  'ines:meet': 'I FLEW FOR BOTH OF THEM. NEITHER PAID. GET IN.',\\n  'ines:owe': 'YOU OWE ME A TRUCK. YOU OWE ME SEVERAL TRUCKS.',\\n  'ines:m3': 'TAKE THE TANKER AT THE EAST POST AND DRIVE IT IN.',\\n  'dov:meet': 'TWO FINGERS I LEFT IN THIS COUNTRY.',\\n  'dov:meet2': 'I CAME BACK TO SEE WHAT THEY ARE DOING.',\\n  'dov:road': 'A MAN ASKED ME TO MINE HIS OWN ROAD, SO HE WOULD KNOW',\\n  'dov:road2': 'WHERE IT WAS SAFE. HE WAS RIGHT FOR A WEEK.',\\n  'dov:m4': 'PLANT THESE ON THE BRIDGE. I WILL TELL YOU WHEN.',\\n  'mags:work': 'HOLD STILL. NO, YOU CANNOT FEEL THAT. NO, THAT IS NORMAL.',\\n  'mags:work2': 'HOLD STILL.',\\n  'mags:owe': 'NOT TODAY. TODAY YOU OWE ME MONEY.',\\n  'mags:m5': 'OPEN THE BYPASS AND HOLD THE PUMP. THE CISTERN CAN FILL.',\\n  'buddy:burn': 'DO NOT LET IT BE THE FIRE. PLEASE. NOT THE FIRE.',\\n\",\"total_lines\":99}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5734068f-5833-414c-8158-afdaef0ad736-49","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Places in the Kettle. Positions are world metres, +x east, -z north. */\\nexport const SITES = [\\n  { id: 'mile-forty', name: 'MILE FORTY', x: 0, z: 40, r: 70, kind: 'town' },\\n  { id: 'pump-shed', name: 'PUMP SHED', x: -120, z: 150, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'ranger-post', name: 'RANGER POST', x: 40, z: -170, kind: 'post' },\\n  { id: 'water-tower', name: 'WATER TOWER', x: 470, z: -180, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'fort-clement', name: 'FORT CLEMENT', x: -430, z: -180, kind: 'hq', faction: 'concord' },\\n  { id: 'long-field', name: 'THE LONG FIELD', x: -260, z: -300, kind: 'field' },\\n  { id: 'granary', name: 'THE GRANARY', x: 400, z: 280, kind: 'hq', faction: 'harvest' },\\n10→  { id: 'east-siding', name: 'EAST SIDING', x: 430, z: -60, kind: 'depot' },\\n  { id: 'three-wells', name: 'THREE WELLS', x: -260, z: 240, kind: 'village' },\\n  { id: 'pump-station', name: 'PUMP STATION', x: -330, z: 395, kind: 'pump' },\\n  { id: 'salt-pan', name: 'SALT PAN', x: 200, z: 470, kind: 'flats' },\\n  { id: 'the-cut', name: 'THE CUT', x: 150, z: -300, kind: 'mine' },\\n  { id: 'observatory', name: 'OBSERVATORY', x: -130, z: -520, kind: 'trig' },\\n  { id: 'the-pass', name: 'THE PASS', x: -590, z: -430, kind: 'pass' },\\n  { id: 'clinic', name: 'MERCY MISSION', x: 12, z: 55, kind: 'clinic' },\\n  { id: 'tibor', name: 'TIBOR SHED', x: -18, z: 62, kind: 'shop' },\\n  { id: 'bar', name: 'THE BAR', x: 22, z: 28, kind: 'bar' },\\n20→  { id: 'sluice', name: 'SLUICE HOUSE', x: 168, z: -286, kind: 'loot' },\\n];\\n\\nexport const POSTS = [\\n  { id: 'p1', name: 'NORTH POST', x: 90, z: -80, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p2', name: 'WEST POST', x: -200, z: 30, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p3', name: 'EAST POST', x: 170, z: 90, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n  { id: 'p4', name: 'FORT ROAD', x: -320, z: -90, faction: 'concord', n: 6 },\\n  { id: 'p5', name: 'MINE ROAD', x: 280, z: -210, faction: 'harvest', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p6', name: 'SALT ROAD', x: 300, z: 390, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n30→];\\n\\nexport const TRIGS = [\\n  { id: 't1', name: 'RIDGE TRIG', x: -130, z: -500 },\\n  { id: 't2', name: 'WEST TRIG', x: -400, z: -40 },\\n  { id: 't3', name: 'EAST TRIG', x: 280, z: 40 },\\n  { id: 't4', name: 'MERCY TRIG', x: -40, z: 280 },\\n  { id: 't5', name: 'GRANARY TRIG', x: 460, z: 180 },\\n  { id: 't6', name: 'CUT TRIG', x: 60, z: -420 },\\n];\\n40→\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Places in the Kettle. Positions are world metres, +x east, -z north. */\\nexport const SITES = [\\n  { id: 'mile-forty', name: 'MILE FORTY', x: 0, z: 40, r: 70, kind: 'town' },\\n  { id: 'pump-shed', name: 'PUMP SHED', x: -120, z: 150, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'ranger-post', name: 'RANGER POST', x: 40, z: -170, kind: 'post' },\\n  { id: 'water-tower', name: 'WATER TOWER', x: 470, z: -180, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'fort-clement', name: 'FORT CLEMENT', x: -430, z: -180, kind: 'hq', faction: 'concord' },\\n  { id: 'long-field', name: 'THE LONG FIELD', x: -260, z: -300, kind: 'field' },\\n  { id: 'granary', name: 'THE GRANARY', x: 400, z: 280, kind: 'hq', faction: 'harvest' },\\n10→  { id: 'east-siding', name: 'EAST SIDING', x: 430, z: -60, kind: 'depot' },\\n  { id: 'three-wells', name: 'THREE WELLS', x: -260, z: 240, kind: 'village' },\\n  { id: 'pump-station', name: 'PUMP STATION', x: -330, z: 395, kind: 'pump' },\\n  { id: 'salt-pan', name: 'SALT PAN', x: 200, z: 470, kind: 'flats' },\\n  { id: 'the-cut', name: 'THE CUT', x: 150, z: -300, kind: 'mine' },\\n  { id: 'observatory', name: 'OBSERVATORY', x: -130, z: -520, kind: 'trig' },\\n  { id: 'the-pass', name: 'THE PASS', x: -590, z: -430, kind: 'pass' },\\n  { id: 'clinic', name: 'MERCY MISSION', x: 12, z: 55, kind: 'clinic' },\\n  { id: 'tibor', name: 'TIBOR SHED', x: -18, z: 62, kind: 'shop' },\\n  { id: 'bar', name: 'THE BAR', x: 22, z: 28, kind: 'bar' },\\n20→  { id: 'sluice', name: 'SLUICE HOUSE', x: 168, z: -286, kind: 'loot' },\\n];\\n\\nexport const POSTS = [\\n  { id: 'p1', name: 'NORTH POST', x: 90, z: -80, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p2', name: 'WEST POST', x: -200, z: 30, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p3', name: 'EAST POST', x: 170, z: 90, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n  { id: 'p4', name: 'FORT ROAD', x: -320, z: -90, faction: 'concord', n: 6 },\\n  { id: 'p5', name: 'MINE ROAD', x: 280, z: -210, faction: 'harvest', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p6', name: 'SALT ROAD', x: 300, z: 390, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n30→];\\n\\nexport const TRIGS = [\\n  { id: 't1', name: 'RIDGE TRIG', x: -130, z: -500 },\\n  { id: 't2', name: 'WEST TRIG', x: -400, z: -40 },\\n  { id: 't3', name: 'EAST TRIG', x: 280, z: 40 },\\n  { id: 't4', name: 'MERCY TRIG', x: -40, z: 280 },\\n  { id: 't5', name: 'GRANARY TRIG', x: 460, z: 180 },\\n  { id: 't6', name: 'CUT TRIG', x: 60, z: -420 },\\n];\\n40→\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/sites.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"/** Places in the Kettle. Positions are world metres, +x east, -z north. */\\nexport const SITES = [\\n  { id: 'mile-forty', name: 'MILE FORTY', x: 0, z: 40, r: 70, kind: 'town' },\\n  { id: 'pump-shed', name: 'PUMP SHED', x: -120, z: 150, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'ranger-post', name: 'RANGER POST', x: 40, z: -170, kind: 'post' },\\n  { id: 'water-tower', name: 'WATER TOWER', x: 470, z: -180, kind: 'safehouse' },\\n  { id: 'fort-clement', name: 'FORT CLEMENT', x: -430, z: -180, kind: 'hq', faction: 'concord' },\\n  { id: 'long-field', name: 'THE LONG FIELD', x: -260, z: -300, kind: 'field' },\\n  { id: 'granary', name: 'THE GRANARY', x: 400, z: 280, kind: 'hq', faction: 'harvest' },\\n  { id: 'east-siding', name: 'EAST SIDING', x: 430, z: -60, kind: 'depot' },\\n  { id: 'three-wells', name: 'THREE WELLS', x: -260, z: 240, kind: 'village' },\\n  { id: 'pump-station', name: 'PUMP STATION', x: -330, z: 395, kind: 'pump' },\\n  { id: 'salt-pan', name: 'SALT PAN', x: 200, z: 470, kind: 'flats' },\\n  { id: 'the-cut', name: 'THE CUT', x: 150, z: -300, kind: 'mine' },\\n  { id: 'observatory', name: 'OBSERVATORY', x: -130, z: -520, kind: 'trig' },\\n  { id: 'the-pass', name: 'THE PASS', x: -590, z: -430, kind: 'pass' },\\n  { id: 'clinic', name: 'MERCY MISSION', x: 12, z: 55, kind: 'clinic' },\\n  { id: 'tibor', name: 'TIBOR SHED', x: -18, z: 62, kind: 'shop' },\\n  { id: 'bar', name: 'THE BAR', x: 22, z: 28, kind: 'bar' },\\n  { id: 'sluice', name: 'SLUICE HOUSE', x: 168, z: -286, kind: 'loot' },\\n];\\n\\nexport const POSTS = [\\n  { id: 'p1', name: 'NORTH POST', x: 90, z: -80, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p2', name: 'WEST POST', x: -200, z: 30, faction: 'concord', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p3', name: 'EAST POST', x: 170, z: 90, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n  { id: 'p4', name: 'FORT ROAD', x: -320, z: -90, faction: 'concord', n: 6 },\\n  { id: 'p5', name: 'MINE ROAD', x: 280, z: -210, faction: 'harvest', n: 5 },\\n  { id: 'p6', name: 'SALT ROAD', x: 300, z: 390, faction: 'harvest', n: 4 },\\n];\\n\\nexport const TRIGS = [\\n  { id: 't1', name: 'RIDGE TRIG', x: -130, z: -500 },\\n  { id: 't2', name: 'WEST TRIG', x: -400, z: -40 },\\n  { id: 't3', name: 'EAST TRIG', x: 280, z: 40 },\\n  { id: 't4', name: 'MERCY TRIG', x: -40, z: 280 },\\n  { id: 't5', name: 'GRANARY TRIG', x: 460, z: 180 },\\n  { id: 't6', name: 'CUT TRIG', x: 60, z: -420 },\\n];\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":72}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"62a4268c-ff97-4e9d-88fa-3077cfbb6b64"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_61","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"lastWindFactor is only set when dx equals 1 and dz equals 0.\n\nWindEffect tests will verify lastWindFactor changes with wind along +x. A fireSpread of 0 means no spread. The world.js patch plan includes importing PALETTE, tracking deadBuddies, filtering dead buddies in applySetup, adding a downBuddy method, and updating knockBuddy to burn.\n\ntickPlayer will map cursor input, handle tryUse and reload, draw lines, process choice menus, and finish the step. announceStep spawns a cage guard. A report flag is added. tryUse will trigger finishing. Choice menus must precede the early return so left and right movement still work. blocksSim skips player input during menus, pause, and title screens but still ticks fire. Attract mode does not block simulation.\n\nPause sets timeScale to zero so fixedUpdate does not run. Menus execute in update rather than fixedUpdate. Headless tests step the engine via update, and attract mode counts frames by calling e.step(1, 1/60) repeatedly. The idleTime check runs at the start of update before adding delta time.\n\nIdleTime accumulates delta time each frame. After 600 steps it reaches exactly 10, so attract starts on the 601st frame and no extra delta is added. Title mode keeps timeScale at 1 to prevent idleTime from stalling. Any input—keyboard, mouse, or stick—exits attract without writing a save.\n\nTouch-only mode enables the notice set while keeping settings menus open. Attract still starts. The device type defaults to pad; keyboard and mouse map to kbm, and analog sticks above 0.35 map to pad. Settings glyphs default to PlayStation but include an Xbox option. Music volume initializes at 0.1 on clean storage before playback begins. Save and load methods will serialize the world state. Playthrough performance is estimated at roughly fifteen seconds on an M1 drive versus one hundred eighty seconds on an M8.\n\nTwo full playthroughs total roughly five hundred simulated seconds. At sixty milliseconds per simulated second, that equals about thirty wall-clock seconds. The fire grid is the main cost, but spread only iterates burning cells so it should remain fast enough.\n\nOn M0 fever-fall, tablets and fever time are zero, so fever starts immediately and ignores the twenty-five-second collapse delay. Lines still require confirmation and the map needs its key.\n\nTest bots can hold keys via setKey and teleport between distant locations with dev.teleport.\n\nThe playthrough bot will perform real actions for every objective. It enters the truck, points yaw, and holds W to drive. For goto objectives it teleports near the target and walks the final meters in.\n\nHold and ride objectives are handled by standing still for the required duration. The dead buddy run begins with dov already dead before m6 knocks ines. If all buddies are dead at that point, knockBuddy completes the step immediately. The finish-it test is separate from the buddy-down system.\n\nA dead buddy persists across sequential missions. If m6 kills ines, she stays dead when m7 begins. Isolated starts reset via applySetup, so a test must finish m6 before starting m7 to keep the dead state.\n\nThe test bot will run missions in isolation, passing a dead list into each startMission and asserting the onDone state after every finish. A full sequential chain is also possible, but isolated runs are sufficient to verify both endings and the dead-buddy scenario.\n\nThe end mission setup defaults to the sheet give ending, so isolated runs must pass an opts.sheet override to select the walk ending. showEnding will set the game.endingCard text. Ledger assertions will run after every mission. damageProp is being simplified so destroy works: kill when hp reaches zero, or when a destroy step matches the tag and any hit occurs.\n\nChecking ending dialogue for characters outside the font charset. The world patch will be applied in several search_replace calls, and new files will be written. CharacterController speed is declared private readonly in TypeScript, so external assignment might fail silently in strict mode.\n\nA smoke test will verify whether the player speed multiplier actually changes movement. If the engine treats speed as a private field, assigning it externally creates a new property that the controller ignores, so movement stays locked to the constructor default. The controller clamps input to length one and multiplies by its internal speed, meaning the slider cannot affect motion unless the value is truly mutable.\n\nThe speed multiplier will be verified at runtime, trusting the plan that it is a plain field. Vehicle topSpeed and Game cameraTarget will also be checked at runtime. Headless mode will use Engine.headless(game) to avoid GPU requirements. GrassField will only initialize in the browser when a document exists, skipping it in headless for performance.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-601b5377-73d0-4347-8b79-e1a5dc4f2d48-50","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/input.d.ts","offset":100,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-601b5377-73d0-4347-8b79-e1a5dc4f2d48-51","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/dialogue.js","offset":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4354,"output_tokens":2259,"cache_read_input_tokens":112256,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"dc388207-b275-4a84-86f9-ed0f73ad2372"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-601b5377-73d0-4347-8b79-e1a5dc4f2d48-50","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→ *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\",\"content_concise\":\"100→ *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n110→    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n120→        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n130→        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n140→    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n150→        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n160→    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n170→     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/input.d.ts\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\" *   locked), wheel delta per frame, optional pointer lock (first-person). Mouse buttons on\\n *   the canvas are keys too (`MOUSE_BUTTONS`: `MouseLeft`, `MouseRight`, `MouseMiddle`), and a\\n *   finger is `Touch` (`TOUCH_KEY`), held and pressed like any other, so a click shorter than\\n *   a frame is not lost.\\n * - Commands (`send`): data from outside the canvas, delivered to the game at the next frame\\n *   and recorded with it.\\n * - `dispose()` removes every listener it added.\\n */\\nexport declare class Input {\\n    private readonly target;\\n    private readonly held;\\n    private readonly pressed;\\n    /** Queued presses → the game time they happened at. */\\n    private readonly queued;\\n    /** Keys held through gamepad buttons (merged into isDown). */\\n    private readonly padHeld;\\n    private readonly listeners;\\n    /** Pointer movement this frame, in CSS pixels (drag or pointer lock). */\\n    readonly mouseDelta: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Where the pointer last was over the canvas, in normalised device coordinates (−1..1, y up:\\n     * `camera.rayAt(pointer.x, pointer.y, …)` turns it into a ray), and whether it is over it now.\\n     * Under pointer lock it is the screen's centre (the crosshair).\\n     */\\n    readonly pointer: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n        over: boolean;\\n        touch: boolean;\\n    };\\n    /** Wheel ticks this frame (+1 = scroll down / zoom out). */\\n    wheel: number;\\n    /** This frame's button presses and releases, in order (`buttonEvents`). */\\n    private _buttonEvents;\\n    /** Commands sent since the last frame began, and this frame's (`send`, `commands`). */\\n    private outbox;\\n    private _commands;\\n    private lockTarget;\\n    /** When true, clicking the canvas requests pointer lock (first-person / free camera). */\\n    wantsPointerLock: boolean;\\n    /** Touch joystick, -1..1 per axis; overrides keys when active. */\\n    readonly analog: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Gamepad left stick after the deadzone, -1..1 (y = forward). */\\n    readonly padAxis: {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** True while any gamepad is connected. */\\n    gamepadConnected: boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Extra key codes whose browser default is blocked (arrows and Space always are): a game's\\n     * own F1 / F2 / Tab panels, so the browser's help page or focus change doesn't fire.\\n     */\\n    readonly preventKeys: Set<string>;\\n    /** Gamepad button index → key code (defaults: GAMEPAD_BUTTONS). */\\n    gamepadButtons: Record<number, string>;\\n    /** Stick deadzone (radial, 0..1). */\\n    gamepadDeadzone: number;\\n    /** Right stick look speed: pointer pixels per second at full tilt. */\\n    gamepadLookSpeed: number;\\n    /** Game time (s) of the current frame; set by the engine through `beginFrame`. */\\n    now: number;\\n    /**\\n     * True while a replay drives input (`engine.replay()`): keyboard, pointer and wheel events,\\n     * `setKey` / `setPointer` / `setButtons` / `addPointer` (touch buttons, scripts) and `send`\\n     * are ignored, and `playBefore` / `playAfter` set everything.\\n     */\\n    get playing(): boolean;\\n    set playing(on: boolean);\\n    private _playing;\\n    private playedPad;\\n    /** Queued presses older than this many seconds of game time are dropped. */\\n    pressWindow: number;\\n    /** `target`: where keys are heard (the page's window); null listens to nothing (`Engine.headless`: input comes from `setKey`, `send`, a replay). */\\n\",\"total_lines\":278}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-601b5377-73d0-4347-8b79-e1a5dc4f2d48-51","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  'buddy:burn': 'DO NOT LET IT BE THE FIRE. PLEASE. NOT THE FIRE.',\\n  'buddy:rescue': 'GET UP. I DID NOT CARRY YOU FOR THE VIEW.',\\n  'harrow:m9.1': 'YOU ARE LATE. I SAID YOU WOULD BE. SIT DOWN.',\\n  'harrow:m9.2': 'IT WILL NOT TAKE LONG. NEITHER OF US HAS LONG.',\\n  'harrow:m9.3': 'I DREW THE LINES THAT STARTED THIS.',\\n  'harrow:m9.4': 'I WOULD LIKE TO DRAW ONE MORE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.5': 'YOU HAVE BEEN DRAWING FOR ME. LOOK AT IT.',\\n  'harrow:m9.6': 'BURNED GRASS CANNOT BURN TWICE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.7': 'IT IS THE ONLY SAFE ROAD IN THE COUNTRY,',\\n  'harrow:m9.8': 'AND YOU BUILT IT FOR WAGES.',\\n50→  'harrow:sheet': 'WHO GETS THE HONEST MAP OF THE MINEFIELD?',\\n  'bark:spot': 'THERE! IN THE GRASS!',\\n  'bark:fire': 'WHO LIT THAT?',\\n  'bark:jam': 'IT IS STUCK! IT IS STUCK AGAIN!',\\n  'bark:down': 'LEAVE HIM, HE IS ALREADY GONE.',\\n  'end:walk1': 'YOU REACHED THE BORDER WITH A CASE OF STONES',\\n  'end:walk2': 'AND A MAP NOBODY ELSE WILL EVER USE.',\\n  'end:walk3': 'THE GUARD ASKS YOUR TRADE. YOU TELL HIM: SURVEYOR.',\\n  'end:give1': 'THEY CROSSED AT FIRST LIGHT, WALKING ON ASH.',\\n  'end:give2': 'NOBODY HAS ASKED WHO LIT IT.',\\n60→  'end:give3': 'THE FEVER IS NOT FINISHED WITH YOU,',\\n  'end:give4': 'AND YOU ARE OUT OF TABLETS. IT IS A GOOD VIEW.',\\n  'death': 'YOU DIED IN THE SORREL. THE PAPERWORK WILL TAKE LONGER.',\\n  'fever': 'THE FEVER.',\\n  'note:0': 'MIND THE FEVER. YOU ARE LATE ALREADY. E.H.',\\n};\\n\\nexport const NOTES = [\\n  'A MAP IS A PROMISE MADE BY SOMEONE WHO HAS ALREADY LEFT.',\\n  'I DREW THE RIVER WHERE THE COMPANY WANTED IT.',\\n70→  'THE RIVER WAS SLOW TO COMPLY, BUT IT CAME ROUND.',\\n  'BOTH ARMIES BUY FROM ME. THE CONCORD PAYS ON TIME.',\\n  'THE HARVEST PAYS IN GRAIN AND TEARS.',\\n  'I HAVE EATEN BETTER ON THE TEARS.',\\n  'YOU WILL HAVE NOTICED THAT YOU FOLLOW ROADS.',\\n  'I DREW THOSE TOO.',\\n  'GRASS IS THE ONLY HONEST BORDER.',\\n  'IT GOES WHERE THE WIND TELLS IT, AND IT KEEPS A RECORD.',\\n  'BY NOW YOU HAVE BURNED WHAT I MARKED.',\\n  'LOOK AT IT FROM THE RIDGE. TELL ME THAT IS NOT A LINE.',\\n80→];\\n\\nexport const EPIGRAPHS = [\\n  'A ROAD IS A RUMOR THAT LEARNED TO LIE STILL.',\\n  'I WAS PAID TWICE FOR THE SAME BORDER.',\\n  'THE GRASS KEEPS THE ONLY MINUTES THAT MATTER.',\\n  'THEY ASKED FOR A MAP. I SOLD THEM A DELAY.',\\n  'WATER GOES WHERE IT IS PUSHED, THEN PRETENDS IT CHOSE.',\\n  'A SAFE HOUSE IS A ROOM THAT HAS NOT BURNED YET.',\\n  'COUNT THE LIVING. THE DEAD ARE BAD AT ARITHMETIC.',\\n90→  'I MARKED THE MINEFIELD WRONG ON PURPOSE, ONCE.',\\n  'NIGHT IS JUST THE PLATEAU WITH THE LAMP BLOWN OUT.',\\n  'EVERY INVOICE IN THIS COUNTRY IS A THREAT.',\\n  'ASH IS A KIND OF ROAD, IF YOU ARE HONEST ABOUT IT.',\\n  'LEAVE BEFORE THE GREEN COMES BACK. IT COMES BACK FASTER.',\\n];\\n\\nexport function line(id) {\\n  return LINES[id] || '';\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  'buddy:burn': 'DO NOT LET IT BE THE FIRE. PLEASE. NOT THE FIRE.',\\n  'buddy:rescue': 'GET UP. I DID NOT CARRY YOU FOR THE VIEW.',\\n  'harrow:m9.1': 'YOU ARE LATE. I SAID YOU WOULD BE. SIT DOWN.',\\n  'harrow:m9.2': 'IT WILL NOT TAKE LONG. NEITHER OF US HAS LONG.',\\n  'harrow:m9.3': 'I DREW THE LINES THAT STARTED THIS.',\\n  'harrow:m9.4': 'I WOULD LIKE TO DRAW ONE MORE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.5': 'YOU HAVE BEEN DRAWING FOR ME. LOOK AT IT.',\\n  'harrow:m9.6': 'BURNED GRASS CANNOT BURN TWICE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.7': 'IT IS THE ONLY SAFE ROAD IN THE COUNTRY,',\\n  'harrow:m9.8': 'AND YOU BUILT IT FOR WAGES.',\\n50→  'harrow:sheet': 'WHO GETS THE HONEST MAP OF THE MINEFIELD?',\\n  'bark:spot': 'THERE! IN THE GRASS!',\\n  'bark:fire': 'WHO LIT THAT?',\\n  'bark:jam': 'IT IS STUCK! IT IS STUCK AGAIN!',\\n  'bark:down': 'LEAVE HIM, HE IS ALREADY GONE.',\\n  'end:walk1': 'YOU REACHED THE BORDER WITH A CASE OF STONES',\\n  'end:walk2': 'AND A MAP NOBODY ELSE WILL EVER USE.',\\n  'end:walk3': 'THE GUARD ASKS YOUR TRADE. YOU TELL HIM: SURVEYOR.',\\n  'end:give1': 'THEY CROSSED AT FIRST LIGHT, WALKING ON ASH.',\\n  'end:give2': 'NOBODY HAS ASKED WHO LIT IT.',\\n60→  'end:give3': 'THE FEVER IS NOT FINISHED WITH YOU,',\\n  'end:give4': 'AND YOU ARE OUT OF TABLETS. IT IS A GOOD VIEW.',\\n  'death': 'YOU DIED IN THE SORREL. THE PAPERWORK WILL TAKE LONGER.',\\n  'fever': 'THE FEVER.',\\n  'note:0': 'MIND THE FEVER. YOU ARE LATE ALREADY. E.H.',\\n};\\n\\nexport const NOTES = [\\n  'A MAP IS A PROMISE MADE BY SOMEONE WHO HAS ALREADY LEFT.',\\n  'I DREW THE RIVER WHERE THE COMPANY WANTED IT.',\\n70→  'THE RIVER WAS SLOW TO COMPLY, BUT IT CAME ROUND.',\\n  'BOTH ARMIES BUY FROM ME. THE CONCORD PAYS ON TIME.',\\n  'THE HARVEST PAYS IN GRAIN AND TEARS.',\\n  'I HAVE EATEN BETTER ON THE TEARS.',\\n  'YOU WILL HAVE NOTICED THAT YOU FOLLOW ROADS.',\\n  'I DREW THOSE TOO.',\\n  'GRASS IS THE ONLY HONEST BORDER.',\\n  'IT GOES WHERE THE WIND TELLS IT, AND IT KEEPS A RECORD.',\\n  'BY NOW YOU HAVE BURNED WHAT I MARKED.',\\n  'LOOK AT IT FROM THE RIDGE. TELL ME THAT IS NOT A LINE.',\\n80→];\\n\\nexport const EPIGRAPHS = [\\n  'A ROAD IS A RUMOR THAT LEARNED TO LIE STILL.',\\n  'I WAS PAID TWICE FOR THE SAME BORDER.',\\n  'THE GRASS KEEPS THE ONLY MINUTES THAT MATTER.',\\n  'THEY ASKED FOR A MAP. I SOLD THEM A DELAY.',\\n  'WATER GOES WHERE IT IS PUSHED, THEN PRETENDS IT CHOSE.',\\n  'A SAFE HOUSE IS A ROOM THAT HAS NOT BURNED YET.',\\n  'COUNT THE LIVING. THE DEAD ARE BAD AT ARITHMETIC.',\\n90→  'I MARKED THE MINEFIELD WRONG ON PURPOSE, ONCE.',\\n  'NIGHT IS JUST THE PLATEAU WITH THE LAMP BLOWN OUT.',\\n  'EVERY INVOICE IN THIS COUNTRY IS A THREAT.',\\n  'ASH IS A KIND OF ROAD, IF YOU ARE HONEST ABOUT IT.',\\n  'LEAVE BEFORE THE GREEN COMES BACK. IT COMES BACK FASTER.',\\n];\\n\\nexport function line(id) {\\n  return LINES[id] || '';\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/dialogue.js\",\"offset\":40,\"raw_output\":\"  'buddy:burn': 'DO NOT LET IT BE THE FIRE. PLEASE. NOT THE FIRE.',\\n  'buddy:rescue': 'GET UP. I DID NOT CARRY YOU FOR THE VIEW.',\\n  'harrow:m9.1': 'YOU ARE LATE. I SAID YOU WOULD BE. SIT DOWN.',\\n  'harrow:m9.2': 'IT WILL NOT TAKE LONG. NEITHER OF US HAS LONG.',\\n  'harrow:m9.3': 'I DREW THE LINES THAT STARTED THIS.',\\n  'harrow:m9.4': 'I WOULD LIKE TO DRAW ONE MORE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.5': 'YOU HAVE BEEN DRAWING FOR ME. LOOK AT IT.',\\n  'harrow:m9.6': 'BURNED GRASS CANNOT BURN TWICE.',\\n  'harrow:m9.7': 'IT IS THE ONLY SAFE ROAD IN THE COUNTRY,',\\n  'harrow:m9.8': 'AND YOU BUILT IT FOR WAGES.',\\n  'harrow:sheet': 'WHO GETS THE HONEST MAP OF THE MINEFIELD?',\\n  'bark:spot': 'THERE! IN THE GRASS!',\\n  'bark:fire': 'WHO LIT THAT?',\\n  'bark:jam': 'IT IS STUCK! IT IS STUCK AGAIN!',\\n  'bark:down': 'LEAVE HIM, HE IS ALREADY GONE.',\\n  'end:walk1': 'YOU REACHED THE BORDER WITH A CASE OF STONES',\\n  'end:walk2': 'AND A MAP NOBODY ELSE WILL EVER USE.',\\n  'end:walk3': 'THE GUARD ASKS YOUR TRADE. YOU TELL HIM: SURVEYOR.',\\n  'end:give1': 'THEY CROSSED AT FIRST LIGHT, WALKING ON ASH.',\\n  'end:give2': 'NOBODY HAS ASKED WHO LIT IT.',\\n  'end:give3': 'THE FEVER IS NOT FINISHED WITH YOU,',\\n  'end:give4': 'AND YOU ARE OUT OF TABLETS. IT IS A GOOD VIEW.',\\n  'death': 'YOU DIED IN THE SORREL. THE PAPERWORK WILL TAKE LONGER.',\\n  'fever': 'THE FEVER.',\\n  'note:0': 'MIND THE FEVER. YOU ARE LATE ALREADY. E.H.',\\n};\\n\\nexport const NOTES = [\\n  'A MAP IS A PROMISE MADE BY SOMEONE WHO HAS ALREADY LEFT.',\\n  'I DREW THE RIVER WHERE THE COMPANY WANTED IT.',\\n  'THE RIVER WAS SLOW TO COMPLY, BUT IT CAME ROUND.',\\n  'BOTH ARMIES BUY FROM ME. THE CONCORD PAYS ON TIME.',\\n  'THE HARVEST PAYS IN GRAIN AND TEARS.',\\n  'I HAVE EATEN BETTER ON THE TEARS.',\\n  'YOU WILL HAVE NOTICED THAT YOU FOLLOW ROADS.',\\n  'I DREW THOSE TOO.',\\n  'GRASS IS THE ONLY HONEST BORDER.',\\n  'IT GOES WHERE THE WIND TELLS IT, AND IT KEEPS A RECORD.',\\n  'BY NOW YOU HAVE BURNED WHAT I MARKED.',\\n  'LOOK AT IT FROM THE RIDGE. TELL ME THAT IS NOT A LINE.',\\n];\\n\\nexport const EPIGRAPHS = [\\n  'A ROAD IS A RUMOR THAT LEARNED TO LIE STILL.',\\n  'I WAS PAID TWICE FOR THE SAME BORDER.',\\n  'THE GRASS KEEPS THE ONLY MINUTES THAT MATTER.',\\n  'THEY ASKED FOR A MAP. I SOLD THEM A DELAY.',\\n  'WATER GOES WHERE IT IS PUSHED, THEN PRETENDS IT CHOSE.',\\n  'A SAFE HOUSE IS A ROOM THAT HAS NOT BURNED YET.',\\n  'COUNT THE LIVING. THE DEAD ARE BAD AT ARITHMETIC.',\\n  'I MARKED THE MINEFIELD WRONG ON PURPOSE, ONCE.',\\n  'NIGHT IS JUST THE PLATEAU WITH THE LAMP BLOWN OUT.',\\n  'EVERY INVOICE IN THIS COUNTRY IS A THREAT.',\\n  'ASH IS A KIND OF ROAD, IF YOU ARE HONEST ABOUT IT.',\\n  'LEAVE BEFORE THE GREEN COMES BACK. IT COMES BACK FASTER.',\\n];\\n\\nexport function line(id) {\\n  return LINES[id] || '';\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":99}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c7ab7262-6a1a-4785-9f0a-3e8c784a2af9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_62","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed the text \"HONOURED\" contains only ASCII characters.\n\nBeginning implementation. World.js patches will be applied first, followed by game.js as the orchestrator.\n\nRound cash mechanics are planned: round start triggers world.setupRound(players), spawning at road ends and cases near the cut, with a truck at extraction. Solo mode uses AI mercenaries, while the host simulates all clients and inputs are interpolated on the client side.\n\nFor the hub test, the focus is on verifying ready states, card entry, bidirectional messaging, time-up finish with all present players, and error-free operation.\n\nA host leave will not crash the hub; it simply voids the session.\n\nSolo tests need a real but simple round so players can bank, drop, revive, and time-up. A `soloSession` helper is being defined with a local host, four players, and stubbed methods for time, RNG, messaging, ready, answer, and finish.\n\nThe soloSession helper now includes `fail()` and `emit()` stubs.\n\nTest scenarios are being defined. Time-up will be driven by emitting a session event with a grace period, then asserting that finish was called for all players. The bank flow moves a player to a case, uses it, returns to the truck, and banks. The down-and-revive flow hurts a player to zero, drops the case, and revives them; in solo mode this will rely on the hired gun AI or a second merc controlled by the test.\n\nMercenaries will revive downed players within four meters before chasing cases. The test will teleport a merc beside the fallen player and step for three seconds to trigger the revive. Round players will be modeled as 'merc' actors with IDs, allowing friendly fire between players. The World round state design is now being drafted.\n\nThe round state will be a `this.round` object containing active status, end time, per-seat data for position, health, stones, carried items, downed status, bleed timer, respawn cooldown, kills, revives, lighting, name, and AI flag, plus local player index and truck position. Stones banked on a seat will be tracked there. The local player will keep using the hero actor while other players become separate actors. Round start and tick logic will live in new `startRound` and `tickRound` methods. A minimal hub round that simply sends state is sufficient if solo tests reuse the same code.\n\nMercenaries will move at 3 m/s with a reaction delay, so they do not grab all six distant cases immediately. The test will teleport the human player.\n\nNetwork snapshots will let clients and the host exchange state. The host applies client positions for their heroes. The harness accepts any JSON send, but the server will send real state.\n\nThe server has no local hero input. It builds terrain and starts rounds using only remote players from the session.\n\nA dedicated `Round` class will be extracted from world.js to keep the implementation manageable. Seats remain idle at spawn until their remote `me` messages arrive, and the host simulates fire, soldiers, and applies client positions. The network traffic pattern is confirmed: clients send position updates while the host broadcasts full state. A menu key press bug was also spotted: `tryUse` receives a delta time from the fixed update loop, but `consumeAction` should instead call `consumePress` during the fixed step.\n\nMenu keys will be smoke tested next. The engine docs confirm that `wasPressed` works correctly because `step` begins each frame. `blocksSim` will prevent player movement during menus, attract mode, and round play. Pause will freeze time by setting `timeScale` to zero; resume will restore it to one. Dev mode will default the freeze toggle to on.\n\nThe hub session will only show Resume and Settings in its pause menu, with no Dev option. Attract mode is excluded from the hub.\n\nA `window.__GAME__` reference will be attached during initialization. The `state()` payload will carry mode, screen, focus, device, glyph set, notice, attract, mission, step, health, stones, tablets, syrettes, weapon status, fever, position, yaw, vehicle, hour, wind, fire state, prompts, subtitle, buddies, ledger, title, waypoint, and ending.\n\nPrompts will be arrays of objects with an action, text, and glyph, such as `{ id: 'use', text: 'GET IN', glyph: 'SQUARE' }`, so tests can verify glyph changes.\n\nPrompt glyphs will vary by input device: E or LMB for keyboard and mouse, X for Xbox use. The full mapping covers use, fire, confirm, map, and pause across platforms. A `menu` array of `{id, label}` objects will be added to state so tests can verify Settings appears in the pause menu.\n\nAttract mode will be tracked by an `attract` boolean in state, and the previous screen will be restored afterward. Save operations will be disabled during attract via a guard in game.js. The m2 clear step will spawn a soldier with the 'cage-guard' post at the ranger post when it begins. Fuel tanks are already present for the destroy step. After the convoy is destroyed, the payroll case will appear and the collect step will complete upon picking it up.\n\nThe collect step will now complete when the player uses the payroll case near the destroyed convoy. The report step will finish immediately if the player is within sixteen meters of the target site and presses use, removing the need for a separate _reported flag.\n\nThe report step will be completed entirely inside `tryUse`, so the auto-complete logic in `tickMission` is being removed to avoid double-completing. The jamming mechanic requires five shots before the weapon jams, then reloads for two to four seconds; tests will hold fire and reload. The syrette step will reduce health to seventy and hold heal for 0.8 seconds. Repair will require zero vehicle health, with use held for three seconds near the truck.\n\nThe announce step will ensure the truck is present, and the player will be outside with low vehicle health so repair is required. The tablet step holds H for one second. The map step presses M. In fever mode, tablets are zero so the collapse step completes the fall. Choice menus will use left and right to focus options and confirm to select; tickPlayer will consume those actions before movement so arrow keys do not move the player during selection.\n\nDuring dialogue lines, the player will consume confirm and fire actions to advance text while remaining stationary. The buddy finish step will kill a downed buddy when the player presses use while the buddy is burning or syrettes are exhausted.\n\nThe buddy-down step will increment the friend ledger and complete when the player presses use. Syrette healing takes priority over finishing a downed buddy; the finish action is only offered when syrettes are exhausted.\n\nThe buddy-down step will use KeyE or use to syrette a healthy buddy, or KeyF or melee to finish it. A new `downBuddy(id)` helper creates a downed buddy when the ID is absent from the list. The `knockBuddy` helper marks buddies as burning for fire-related story events. A persistent `deadBuddies` Set will survive setup and be populated from saved dead IDs.\n\nBuddies are filtered against the dead set during setup, and dead IDs are pushed into the dead list when a buddy dies in play. `startMission` accepts a `dead` option to pre-dead buddies. `newGame()` clears the dead set for fresh worlds, while isolated missions keep existing deaths. A `sheet` override is added to `startMission`.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2f08572d-91d7-4dae-97b3-567705d5f4c2-52","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/terrain.js","offset":90}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4124,"output_tokens":3314,"cache_read_input_tokens":116608,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"36ecb002-bcca-4db0-9558-5290211de5f6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-2f08572d-91d7-4dae-97b3-567705d5f4c2-52","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"90→      const bi = (ix + iz * nx) * 3;\\n      base[bi] = Math.round(c.r * 255);\\n      base[bi + 1] = Math.round(c.g * 255);\\n      base[bi + 2] = Math.round(c.b * 255);\\n      const vi = 6 * (ix + iz * nx);\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n  land.userData = { base };\\n100→  return base;\\n}\\n\\nexport function paintScar(land, ix, iz) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const x = FIRE_ORIGIN + (ix + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const z = FIRE_ORIGIN + (iz + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const [cw, ch] = land.cell;\\n  const x0 = land.pointX(0);\\n110→  const z0 = land.pointZ(0);\\n  const tx0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((x - FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((z - FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const tx1 = Math.min(nx - 1, Math.ceil((x + FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz1 = Math.min(land.nz - 1, Math.ceil((z + FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const ink = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n  const slate = new Color(PALETTE.slate);\\n  for (let tz = tz0; tz <= tz1; tz++) {\\n    for (let tx = tx0; tx <= tx1; tx++) {\\n      const vi = 6 * (tx + tz * nx);\\n120→      const c = ((tx + tz) & 1) ? ink : slate;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fuelAt(x, z, heights) {\\n  if (nearRiver(x, z, 9)) return 0;\\n  if (nearRoad(x, z, 7)) return 0;\\n130→  if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 130) return 0;\\n  const h = heights(x, z);\\n  if (h > 68) return 0;\\n  if (Math.hypot(x - 150, z + 300) < 40) return 0;\\n  if (x > 180 && z > -160 && z < 80) return 2;\\n  return 1;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fillFuel(fire, heights) {\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < FIRE_N; iz++) {\\n140→    for (let ix = 0; ix < FIRE_N; ix++) {\\n      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      fire.fuel[fire.idx(ix, iz)] = fuelAt(x, z, heights);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function addBlock(ctx, x, y, z, w, h, d, color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n150→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  ctx.scene.add(mesh);\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nvoid PALETTE;\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"90→      const bi = (ix + iz * nx) * 3;\\n      base[bi] = Math.round(c.r * 255);\\n      base[bi + 1] = Math.round(c.g * 255);\\n      base[bi + 2] = Math.round(c.b * 255);\\n      const vi = 6 * (ix + iz * nx);\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n  land.userData = { base };\\n100→  return base;\\n}\\n\\nexport function paintScar(land, ix, iz) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const x = FIRE_ORIGIN + (ix + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const z = FIRE_ORIGIN + (iz + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const [cw, ch] = land.cell;\\n  const x0 = land.pointX(0);\\n110→  const z0 = land.pointZ(0);\\n  const tx0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((x - FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((z - FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const tx1 = Math.min(nx - 1, Math.ceil((x + FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz1 = Math.min(land.nz - 1, Math.ceil((z + FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const ink = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n  const slate = new Color(PALETTE.slate);\\n  for (let tz = tz0; tz <= tz1; tz++) {\\n    for (let tx = tx0; tx <= tx1; tx++) {\\n      const vi = 6 * (tx + tz * nx);\\n120→      const c = ((tx + tz) & 1) ? ink : slate;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fuelAt(x, z, heights) {\\n  if (nearRiver(x, z, 9)) return 0;\\n  if (nearRoad(x, z, 7)) return 0;\\n130→  if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 130) return 0;\\n  const h = heights(x, z);\\n  if (h > 68) return 0;\\n  if (Math.hypot(x - 150, z + 300) < 40) return 0;\\n  if (x > 180 && z > -160 && z < 80) return 2;\\n  return 1;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fillFuel(fire, heights) {\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < FIRE_N; iz++) {\\n140→    for (let ix = 0; ix < FIRE_N; ix++) {\\n      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      fire.fuel[fire.idx(ix, iz)] = fuelAt(x, z, heights);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function addBlock(ctx, x, y, z, w, h, d, color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n150→  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  ctx.scene.add(mesh);\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nvoid PALETTE;\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/terrain.js\",\"offset\":90,\"raw_output\":\"      const bi = (ix + iz * nx) * 3;\\n      base[bi] = Math.round(c.r * 255);\\n      base[bi + 1] = Math.round(c.g * 255);\\n      base[bi + 2] = Math.round(c.b * 255);\\n      const vi = 6 * (ix + iz * nx);\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n  land.userData = { base };\\n  return base;\\n}\\n\\nexport function paintScar(land, ix, iz) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const x = FIRE_ORIGIN + (ix + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const z = FIRE_ORIGIN + (iz + 0.5) * FIRE_CELL;\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const [cw, ch] = land.cell;\\n  const x0 = land.pointX(0);\\n  const z0 = land.pointZ(0);\\n  const tx0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((x - FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz0 = Math.max(0, Math.floor((z - FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const tx1 = Math.min(nx - 1, Math.ceil((x + FIRE_CELL - x0) / cw));\\n  const tz1 = Math.min(land.nz - 1, Math.ceil((z + FIRE_CELL - z0) / ch));\\n  const ink = new Color(PALETTE.ink);\\n  const slate = new Color(PALETTE.slate);\\n  for (let tz = tz0; tz <= tz1; tz++) {\\n    for (let tx = tx0; tx <= tx1; tx++) {\\n      const vi = 6 * (tx + tz * nx);\\n      const c = ((tx + tz) & 1) ? ink : slate;\\n      for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) col.setXYZ(vi + k, c.r, c.g, c.b);\\n    }\\n  }\\n  col.needsUpdate = true;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fuelAt(x, z, heights) {\\n  if (nearRiver(x, z, 9)) return 0;\\n  if (nearRoad(x, z, 7)) return 0;\\n  if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 130) return 0;\\n  const h = heights(x, z);\\n  if (h > 68) return 0;\\n  if (Math.hypot(x - 150, z + 300) < 40) return 0;\\n  if (x > 180 && z > -160 && z < 80) return 2;\\n  return 1;\\n}\\n\\nexport function fillFuel(fire, heights) {\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < FIRE_N; iz++) {\\n    for (let ix = 0; ix < FIRE_N; ix++) {\\n      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      fire.fuel[fire.idx(ix, iz)] = fuelAt(x, z, heights);\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function addBlock(ctx, x, y, z, w, h, d, color) {\\n  ctx.physics.addStaticBox({ position: [x, y, z], halfExtents: [w / 2, h / 2, d / 2] });\\n  const mesh = new Mesh(new BoxGeometry(w, h, d), toonMaterial(color));\\n  mesh.position.set(x, y, z);\\n  mesh.castShadow = mesh.receiveShadow = true;\\n  ctx.scene.add(mesh);\\n  return mesh;\\n}\\n\\nvoid PALETTE;\\n\",\"total_lines\":156}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e2acc20b-dfdc-4ac5-ab23-d31570df43cb"}
