{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-fbcba4d9-102b-4acf-ad30-de2598b65591-53","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"172→  paintMapBase() {\\n    const px = this.mapPx;\\n    px.fill(0);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 320 * 240; i++) {\\n      px[i * 4] = 196;\\n      px[i * 4 + 1] = 154;\\n      px[i * 4 + 2] = 96;\\n      px[i * 4 + 3] = 255;\\n180→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  worldToMap(x, z) {\\n    const mx = Math.floor(((x + 640) / 1280) * 300) + 8;\\n    const my = Math.floor(((z + 640) / 1280) * 220) + 8;\\n    return [mx, my];\\n  }\\n\\n  stamp(x, z, r, g, b) {\\n190→    const [mx, my] = this.worldToMap(x, z);\\n    if (mx < 0 || my < 0 || mx >= 320 || my >= 240) return;\\n    const i = (mx + my * 320) * 4;\\n    this.mapPx[i] = r;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 1] = g;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 2] = b;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 3] = 255;\\n  }\\n\\n  refreshMap() {\\n200→    const fire = this.fire;\\n    if (this.scarTick === this._scarDrawn) {\\n      const p = this.feet();\\n      this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    this._scarDrawn = this.scarTick;\\n    for (const i of fire.burntList) {\\n      const ix = i % 256;\\n      const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n210→      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      this.stamp(x, z, 30, 28, 36);\\n    }\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n  }\\n\\n  mapHasScar() {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.mapPx.length; i += 4) {\\n      if (this.mapPx[i] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 1] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 2] < 50 && this.mapPx[i + 3] > 0) return true;\\n220→    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  markSeen() {\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const s of SITES) if (Math.hypot(s.x - p.x, s.z - p.z) < 90) this.seen.add(s.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  resetDynamic() {\\n230→    this.fire.extinguish();\\n    this.fire.state.fill(0);\\n    this.fire.burning.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntList.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntCount = 0;\\n    this.actors.length = 0;\\n    this.dead = false;\\n    this.carrying = null;\\n    this.inVehicle = false;\\n    this.mission = null;\\n240→    this.lines = [];\\n    this.choice = null;\\n    this.subtitle = '';\\n    this.feverOn = false;\\n    this.surgeryT = 0;\\n    this.rescueT = 0;\\n    this.ending = null;\\n    this.sheet = null;\\n    this.spawnTown();\\n  }\\n250→\\n  teleport(x, z) {\",\"content_concise\":\"172→  paintMapBase() {\\n    const px = this.mapPx;\\n    px.fill(0);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 320 * 240; i++) {\\n      px[i * 4] = 196;\\n      px[i * 4 + 1] = 154;\\n      px[i * 4 + 2] = 96;\\n      px[i * 4 + 3] = 255;\\n180→    }\\n  }\\n\\n  worldToMap(x, z) {\\n    const mx = Math.floor(((x + 640) / 1280) * 300) + 8;\\n    const my = Math.floor(((z + 640) / 1280) * 220) + 8;\\n    return [mx, my];\\n  }\\n\\n  stamp(x, z, r, g, b) {\\n190→    const [mx, my] = this.worldToMap(x, z);\\n    if (mx < 0 || my < 0 || mx >= 320 || my >= 240) return;\\n    const i = (mx + my * 320) * 4;\\n    this.mapPx[i] = r;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 1] = g;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 2] = b;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 3] = 255;\\n  }\\n\\n  refreshMap() {\\n200→    const fire = this.fire;\\n    if (this.scarTick === this._scarDrawn) {\\n      const p = this.feet();\\n      this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    this._scarDrawn = this.scarTick;\\n    for (const i of fire.burntList) {\\n      const ix = i % 256;\\n      const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n210→      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      this.stamp(x, z, 30, 28, 36);\\n    }\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n  }\\n\\n  mapHasScar() {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.mapPx.length; i += 4) {\\n      if (this.mapPx[i] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 1] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 2] < 50 && this.mapPx[i + 3] > 0) return true;\\n220→    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  markSeen() {\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const s of SITES) if (Math.hypot(s.x - p.x, s.z - p.z) < 90) this.seen.add(s.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  resetDynamic() {\\n230→    this.fire.extinguish();\\n    this.fire.state.fill(0);\\n    this.fire.burning.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntList.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntCount = 0;\\n    this.actors.length = 0;\\n    this.dead = false;\\n    this.carrying = null;\\n    this.inVehicle = false;\\n    this.mission = null;\\n240→    this.lines = [];\\n    this.choice = null;\\n    this.subtitle = '';\\n    this.feverOn = false;\\n    this.surgeryT = 0;\\n    this.rescueT = 0;\\n    this.ending = null;\\n    this.sheet = null;\\n    this.spawnTown();\\n  }\\n250→\\n  teleport(x, z) {\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js\",\"offset\":172,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  paintMapBase() {\\n    const px = this.mapPx;\\n    px.fill(0);\\n    for (let i = 0; i < 320 * 240; i++) {\\n      px[i * 4] = 196;\\n      px[i * 4 + 1] = 154;\\n      px[i * 4 + 2] = 96;\\n      px[i * 4 + 3] = 255;\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  worldToMap(x, z) {\\n    const mx = Math.floor(((x + 640) / 1280) * 300) + 8;\\n    const my = Math.floor(((z + 640) / 1280) * 220) + 8;\\n    return [mx, my];\\n  }\\n\\n  stamp(x, z, r, g, b) {\\n    const [mx, my] = this.worldToMap(x, z);\\n    if (mx < 0 || my < 0 || mx >= 320 || my >= 240) return;\\n    const i = (mx + my * 320) * 4;\\n    this.mapPx[i] = r;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 1] = g;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 2] = b;\\n    this.mapPx[i + 3] = 255;\\n  }\\n\\n  refreshMap() {\\n    const fire = this.fire;\\n    if (this.scarTick === this._scarDrawn) {\\n      const p = this.feet();\\n      this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    this._scarDrawn = this.scarTick;\\n    for (const i of fire.burntList) {\\n      const ix = i % 256;\\n      const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n      const [x, z] = fire.center(ix, iz);\\n      this.stamp(x, z, 30, 28, 36);\\n    }\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    this.stamp(p.x, p.z, 240, 240, 240);\\n  }\\n\\n  mapHasScar() {\\n    for (let i = 0; i < this.mapPx.length; i += 4) {\\n      if (this.mapPx[i] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 1] < 40 && this.mapPx[i + 2] < 50 && this.mapPx[i + 3] > 0) return true;\\n    }\\n    return false;\\n  }\\n\\n  markSeen() {\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const s of SITES) if (Math.hypot(s.x - p.x, s.z - p.z) < 90) this.seen.add(s.id);\\n  }\\n\\n  resetDynamic() {\\n    this.fire.extinguish();\\n    this.fire.state.fill(0);\\n    this.fire.burning.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntList.length = 0;\\n    this.fire.burntCount = 0;\\n    this.actors.length = 0;\\n    this.dead = false;\\n    this.carrying = null;\\n    this.inVehicle = false;\\n    this.mission = null;\\n    this.lines = [];\\n    this.choice = null;\\n    this.subtitle = '';\\n    this.feverOn = false;\\n    this.surgeryT = 0;\\n    this.rescueT = 0;\\n    this.ending = null;\\n    this.sheet = null;\\n    this.spawnTown();\\n  }\\n\\n  teleport(x, z) {\\n\",\"total_lines\":1199}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e3d1c886-8acf-4128-8c94-32264a803451"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_64","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"refreshMap exits early when scarTick is unchanged. The first scar sets both scarTick and onBurnt.\n\nlayScar triggers refreshMap at the end. scarTick increments per cell in onBurnt, so refreshMap stamps burnt cells correctly. Old base stamps remain because refreshMap does not repaint the base. A bug exists where matching scarTick skips redrawing scars after a base reset. The map cursor waypoint will be stamped in pickWaypoint. Driving continues while the map is open.\n\nWhen the map is open, tickPlayer preserves the last movement axes so the truck keeps driving. The stick input will move the map cursor instead of steering.\n\nCamera look will be disabled while the map is open. Mouse and right stick input will move the map cursor instead of rotating the camera. The camera enabled state will toggle in update based on map.up. Waypoint selection can use stick input or mouseDelta applied during fixedUpdate.\n\nThe map cursor will move by 0.4 times the mouse delta while the map is open. A confirm action will select waypoints from seen sites within 18 meters of the cursor. The test should move the cursor with input rather than setting coordinates directly.\n\nMouseDelta is available in fixedUpdate because the engine applies addPointer before that phase. Arrow keys will not nudge the map cursor while the map is open. Opening the map will snap the cursor to the player's position.\n\nThe clinic site at 12,55 is within 18 meters of the player, so pickWaypoint will select it. tickPlayer will be patched to preserve movement axes while the map is open. tryUse and reload will be called. Surgery interrupts on hurt by resetting surgeryT to zero. hero.speed needs a descriptor fix. The game.js structure is ready for writing.\n\nA boxModel generator will create simple prop boxes. The soldier model is ready from the plan. Grass-flame textures and a single song pattern are set. SFX will be an array of id-definition pairs. Voice syllables are planned. About content will use honest placeholder answers updated after tests, with no TODOs.\n\nThe static font test will uppercase strings before validation so content can keep its original casing. About.js text uses many punctuation marks, but the allowed charset excludes em dashes and ellipsis characters.\n\nThe exact phrase \"added on import\" must appear verbatim in JSON and about content. The source string stays lowercase while the HUD uppercases it for display. En-dashes will be replaced with hyphens to avoid invalid characters. No placeholder, stub, TODO, FIXME, or \"coming soon\" strings will appear anywhere in source files or comments.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-39fc0bbd-327b-4156-a402-731ce7d94988-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/terrain.js","offset":40,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":955,"output_tokens":1488,"cache_read_input_tokens":124928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"84c7be68-e143-4bf7-9320-de0abac9a874"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-39fc0bbd-327b-4156-a402-731ce7d94988-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"40→  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function buildLand(ctx, seed) {\\n  const sample = heightFn(seed);\\n  const land = new Terrain({\\n    size: [1280, 1280],\\n    cells: [256, 256],\\n    at: [0, 0, 0],\\n    bands: [\\n50→      { below: 34, color: PALETTE.teal },\\n      { below: 42, color: PALETTE.sand },\\n      { below: 55, color: PALETTE.orange },\\n      { below: 80, color: PALETTE.plum },\\n    ],\\n    steep: 0.62,\\n    rock: PALETTE.plum,\\n  });\\n  land.generate(sample);\\n  land.attach(ctx.physics);\\n60→  ctx.scene.add(land.mesh);\\n  const heights = sample;\\n  paint(land, heights);\\n  return { land, heights };\\n}\\n\\nfunction paint(land, heights) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const nz = land.nz;\\n70→  const sand = new Color(PALETTE.sand);\\n  const orange = new Color(PALETTE.orange);\\n  const red = new Color(PALETTE.red);\\n  const plum = new Color(PALETTE.plum);\\n  const white = new Color(PALETTE.white);\\n  const green = new Color(PALETTE.green);\\n  const teal = new Color(PALETTE.teal);\\n  const base = new Uint8Array(nx * nz * 3);\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < nz; iz++) {\\n    for (let ix = 0; ix < nx; ix++) {\\n80→      const x = land.pointX(ix);\\n      const z = land.pointZ(iz);\\n      const h = heights(x, z);\\n      let c = orange;\\n      if (nearRiver(x, z, 10)) c = teal;\\n      else if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 140 && h < 40) c = white;\\n      else if (nearRoad(x, z, 6)) c = red;\\n      else if (h > 62) c = plum;\\n      else if (x > 200 && z < 200 && z > -100) c = green;\\n      else c = sand;\",\"content_concise\":\"40→  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function buildLand(ctx, seed) {\\n  const sample = heightFn(seed);\\n  const land = new Terrain({\\n    size: [1280, 1280],\\n    cells: [256, 256],\\n    at: [0, 0, 0],\\n    bands: [\\n50→      { below: 34, color: PALETTE.teal },\\n      { below: 42, color: PALETTE.sand },\\n      { below: 55, color: PALETTE.orange },\\n      { below: 80, color: PALETTE.plum },\\n    ],\\n    steep: 0.62,\\n    rock: PALETTE.plum,\\n  });\\n  land.generate(sample);\\n  land.attach(ctx.physics);\\n60→  ctx.scene.add(land.mesh);\\n  const heights = sample;\\n  paint(land, heights);\\n  return { land, heights };\\n}\\n\\nfunction paint(land, heights) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const nz = land.nz;\\n70→  const sand = new Color(PALETTE.sand);\\n  const orange = new Color(PALETTE.orange);\\n  const red = new Color(PALETTE.red);\\n  const plum = new Color(PALETTE.plum);\\n  const white = new Color(PALETTE.white);\\n  const green = new Color(PALETTE.green);\\n  const teal = new Color(PALETTE.teal);\\n  const base = new Uint8Array(nx * nz * 3);\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < nz; iz++) {\\n    for (let ix = 0; ix < nx; ix++) {\\n80→      const x = land.pointX(ix);\\n      const z = land.pointZ(iz);\\n      const h = heights(x, z);\\n      let c = orange;\\n      if (nearRiver(x, z, 10)) c = teal;\\n      else if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 140 && h < 40) c = white;\\n      else if (nearRoad(x, z, 6)) c = red;\\n      else if (h > 62) c = plum;\\n      else if (x > 200 && z < 200 && z > -100) c = green;\\n      else c = sand;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/terrain.js\",\"offset\":40,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"  };\\n}\\n\\nexport function buildLand(ctx, seed) {\\n  const sample = heightFn(seed);\\n  const land = new Terrain({\\n    size: [1280, 1280],\\n    cells: [256, 256],\\n    at: [0, 0, 0],\\n    bands: [\\n      { below: 34, color: PALETTE.teal },\\n      { below: 42, color: PALETTE.sand },\\n      { below: 55, color: PALETTE.orange },\\n      { below: 80, color: PALETTE.plum },\\n    ],\\n    steep: 0.62,\\n    rock: PALETTE.plum,\\n  });\\n  land.generate(sample);\\n  land.attach(ctx.physics);\\n  ctx.scene.add(land.mesh);\\n  const heights = sample;\\n  paint(land, heights);\\n  return { land, heights };\\n}\\n\\nfunction paint(land, heights) {\\n  const col = land.mesh.geometry.getAttribute('color');\\n  const nx = land.nx;\\n  const nz = land.nz;\\n  const sand = new Color(PALETTE.sand);\\n  const orange = new Color(PALETTE.orange);\\n  const red = new Color(PALETTE.red);\\n  const plum = new Color(PALETTE.plum);\\n  const white = new Color(PALETTE.white);\\n  const green = new Color(PALETTE.green);\\n  const teal = new Color(PALETTE.teal);\\n  const base = new Uint8Array(nx * nz * 3);\\n  for (let iz = 0; iz < nz; iz++) {\\n    for (let ix = 0; ix < nx; ix++) {\\n      const x = land.pointX(ix);\\n      const z = land.pointZ(iz);\\n      const h = heights(x, z);\\n      let c = orange;\\n      if (nearRiver(x, z, 10)) c = teal;\\n      else if (Math.hypot(x - 200, z - 470) < 140 && h < 40) c = white;\\n      else if (nearRoad(x, z, 6)) c = red;\\n      else if (h > 62) c = plum;\\n      else if (x > 200 && z < 200 && z > -100) c = green;\\n      else c = sand;\\n\",\"total_lines\":156}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"068a791f-7bbb-455b-944b-f8ab6260f49b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_65","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Setting cells to [512, 512] as the plan verified.\n\nBroadcastChannel linkSession will be implemented for two file:// pages. Paint at 512² is acceptable; slower performance will trigger a fallback. Coding starts with world patching, then many files. tickPlayer replacement and spawnTown palette updates are planned. Constructor deadBuddies, applySetup changes, announceStep spawn guard, and knockBuddy renamed to downBuddy are also noted.\n\nRound logic will live in a separate file and be called from game.js fixedUpdate. World will not grow further. Round uses world.hero, fire, and actors. TickPlayer checks roundMode flags for carrying speed. Down in round does not trigger buddy-rescue.\n\nhurt() will call down(), which checks round state. When round is active, down() will start bleeding instead of killing the buddy. Round state stays on world for test access. The round logic will be a small block in world.js rather than a separate mixin.\n\nThe round.js API will export beginRound, tickRound, bankIf, roundSnapshot, applyClient, and finishRound. Game.js will call tickRound from fixedUpdate. Round state will live on world.round with a 360-second limit. beginRound triggers on start events and solo menu entries.\n\nRound state will hold per-seat stats: health, stones, carrying, down status, respawn, revives, kills, and lit. Six cases will be placed near the cut guarded by spawn points at [80,-220], [220,-360], [40,-400], and [260,-250]. The round will use its own six-case set instead of world.cases to avoid campaign interference. Starting a round will clear the current mission.\n\nRemote seats in solo or hub mode are controlled by AI or client messages. The local hero stays on the ground when down while its seat timer runs. A buddy within three meters can revive the downed seat. Dropping a carried case returns it to the ground. Near the truck, banking deposits stones and removes the case. The round timer advances each tick; the host finishes at the limit.\n\nThe round will finish immediately on a time-up event instead of waiting for the timer to expire. Friendly fire is handled by spawning merc actors linked to each seat; local player hits on these actors damage the seat, and a seat that drops to zero or below downs and drops its case. Player bullets will not kill civilians. A non-reliable snapshot interval will run in game.ready for the host.\n\nClient position updates will be sent unreliably every 80 milliseconds. The host receives these client messages and forwards them to other players. Both directions of traffic are needed for the round to function. Sending stops immediately after the round ends, and the music is silenced. The time-up event handler calls finish directly with a synchronous buildOutcome.\n\nThe leave event handler will remove the departing player. The host finishes the round only if all other players have left. If the host is alone, the round continues until time-up. If a non-host leaves and the host is gone, the client stops.\n\nThe host finishes the round only when no players remain; if the host leaves, the hub voids it and other copies must not call finish. The card UI will register Enter and M key listeners for AIHub before connecting, though calling answer before connect might throw.\n\nThe card UI listener will be module-level so it can reference the game object. It will only call answer after connect returns and before the engine starts. This ensures the welcome message has arrived first, preventing a protocol error.\n\nThe card screen will pad the Cross button. The attract director will run simple beats that teleport, ignite, and drive for a few seconds before looping; it must not throw. It disables saves, enables god mode and infinite ammo, and exits to the return screen on any input while resetting dynamic world state and re-enabling saves. Touch input taps exit the attract demo back to the gate screen.\n\nSettings and About screens will exempt the attract timer. Idle time will pause while those menus are open, and the attract demo will only start on the title or main menu. Pointer lock state will be tracked to avoid pausing every frame; if the player exits pointer lock during play, the pause menu will open.\n\nPointer lock will be requested on click during play and caught in main. The browser test suite will be split into run, static, systems, playthrough, replay, browser, hub, and link modules. Tests will use file hashes to skip unchanged files unless --all is passed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8a7cf462-d555-4e79-bb16-239957d3ef13-55","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"record\\(|replay\\(|fingerprint\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/Engine.d.ts"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2080,"output_tokens":2162,"cache_read_input_tokens":125824,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"7a16d88e-6e9c-42d6-a411-8de233d1f40e"}
