{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_67","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Recording a short mission segment by stepping with input to get the engine.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f843cd70-d7b5-4b04-ba23-b4f17c8f3e8f-57","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/Engine.d.ts","offset":470,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1391,"output_tokens":196,"cache_read_input_tokens":130304,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"68f6ee15-5b89-442c-8e0d-34c9b1e6fb62"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f843cd70-d7b5-4b04-ba23-b4f17c8f3e8f-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"470→            right: number;\\n            top: number;\\n            bottom: number;\\n        } | null;\\n        filters: string[];\\n        /** The look preset in use, or `custom`; `split` when layers render as two passes. */\\n        look: string;\\n        split: boolean;\\n        status: string;\\n    };\\n480→    /**\\n     * Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation,\\n     * animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n     */\\n    step(n?: number, dt?: number): void;\\n    /**\\n     * One manual frame (`step()`), its input live or from a recorded frame (`replay()`). A game\\n     * hook's exception finishes the frame first, then is thrown to the caller of `step()`; in a\\n     * replay it is reported and the replay goes on, as in live play (`tick()`).\\n     */\\n490→    private frameStep;\\n    /** The end of every frame: input's per-frame state goes, and a marker notes when promise callbacks run. */\\n    private endFrame;\\n    /**\\n     * Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas,\\n     * camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n     *\\n     * Safe to call from anywhere, including a game's own hooks (a level door in `update`,\\n     * `fixedUpdate` or a trigger's `onEnter`): the swap waits for the current frame to end.\\n     * Loads run one at a time, and only the latest one wins: a newer `loadGame()` (or\\n500→     * `dispose()`) makes an older one stop after its `setup()`, and the newer one unloads\\n     * whatever it built. The returned promise resolves when the level runs (or was superseded).\\n     *\\n     * Unloading calls the old game's `dispose(ctx)`, removes every scene object that is not\\n     * engine-owned and frees its GPU resources, clears physics (bodies, colliders, joints,\\n     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n510→     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\",\"content_concise\":\"470→            right: number;\\n            top: number;\\n            bottom: number;\\n        } | null;\\n        filters: string[];\\n        /** The look preset in use, or `custom`; `split` when layers render as two passes. */\\n        look: string;\\n        split: boolean;\\n        status: string;\\n    };\\n480→    /**\\n     * Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation,\\n     * animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n     */\\n    step(n?: number, dt?: number): void;\\n    /**\\n     * One manual frame (`step()`), its input live or from a recorded frame (`replay()`). A game\\n     * hook's exception finishes the frame first, then is thrown to the caller of `step()`; in a\\n     * replay it is reported and the replay goes on, as in live play (`tick()`).\\n     */\\n490→    private frameStep;\\n    /** The end of every frame: input's per-frame state goes, and a marker notes when promise callbacks run. */\\n    private endFrame;\\n    /**\\n     * Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas,\\n     * camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n     *\\n     * Safe to call from anywhere, including a game's own hooks (a level door in `update`,\\n     * `fixedUpdate` or a trigger's `onEnter`): the swap waits for the current frame to end.\\n     * Loads run one at a time, and only the latest one wins: a newer `loadGame()` (or\\n500→     * `dispose()`) makes an older one stop after its `setup()`, and the newer one unloads\\n     * whatever it built. The returned promise resolves when the level runs (or was superseded).\\n     *\\n     * Unloading calls the old game's `dispose(ctx)`, removes every scene object that is not\\n     * engine-owned and frees its GPU resources, clears physics (bodies, colliders, joints,\\n     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n510→     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/Engine.d.ts\",\"offset\":470,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"            right: number;\\n            top: number;\\n            bottom: number;\\n        } | null;\\n        filters: string[];\\n        /** The look preset in use, or `custom`; `split` when layers render as two passes. */\\n        look: string;\\n        split: boolean;\\n        status: string;\\n    };\\n    /**\\n     * Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation,\\n     * animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n     */\\n    step(n?: number, dt?: number): void;\\n    /**\\n     * One manual frame (`step()`), its input live or from a recorded frame (`replay()`). A game\\n     * hook's exception finishes the frame first, then is thrown to the caller of `step()`; in a\\n     * replay it is reported and the replay goes on, as in live play (`tick()`).\\n     */\\n    private frameStep;\\n    /** The end of every frame: input's per-frame state goes, and a marker notes when promise callbacks run. */\\n    private endFrame;\\n    /**\\n     * Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas,\\n     * camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n     *\\n     * Safe to call from anywhere, including a game's own hooks (a level door in `update`,\\n     * `fixedUpdate` or a trigger's `onEnter`): the swap waits for the current frame to end.\\n     * Loads run one at a time, and only the latest one wins: a newer `loadGame()` (or\\n     * `dispose()`) makes an older one stop after its `setup()`, and the newer one unloads\\n     * whatever it built. The returned promise resolves when the level runs (or was superseded).\\n     *\\n     * Unloading calls the old game's `dispose(ctx)`, removes every scene object that is not\\n     * engine-owned and frees its GPU resources, clears physics (bodies, colliders, joints,\\n     * controllers, triggers, tags, movers, force fields, belts; gravity and the solver back to\\n     * their defaults), particles, HUD and music, and resets the scene background, fog and the\\n     * sun / ambient light to the engine defaults. Filters, render\\n     * mode, resolution, quality, volumes and the camera rig carry over; pass `camera` to\\n     * switch the preset (applied before `setup()`, so `ctx.camera` is already the new one).\\n     * Nothing advances while loading, and input made while loading is dropped (data sent with\\n     * `ctx.input.send` waits for the first frame that runs).\\n     */\\n    loadGame(game: Game, options?: {\\n        camera?: CameraConfig;\\n    }): Promise<void>;\\n    /**\\n     * Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM,\\n     * GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its\\n     * `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n\",\"total_lines\":613}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"dfd7c149-0198-4d35-9b44-7247dfe4bb60"}
