   * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n\",\"total_lines\":144}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e7b8888c-e663-4f4a-960b-116049643a49"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_70","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"setVolume persists to storage by default.\n\nThe engine settings panel will be hidden and its localStorage key disabled. Audio persistence will be turned off so the engine does not save its own copy. Music volume will be controlled through custom settings storage instead.\n\nConfirmed the volume fix works across clean storage and default engine values. Now patching world.js with eight changes: importing PALETTE, adding deadBuddies to the constructor, fixing spawnTown colors, applying a buddy filter in applySetup, rounding down() values, passing opts.sheet in startMission, and routing knockBuddy through downBuddy.\n\nThe patch list now has twelve items. The tickPlayer movement and input section will be replaced. tryUse will be updated for finish, report, and collect. announceStep spawn logic will be adjusted. The void PALETTE declaration in terrain will be removed and cells set to 512. New files are next.\n\nThe tickPlayer replacement will run before readNeeds. It checks lines and confirms first. Then it handles choices and map cursor movement. It always reads the move axis. It runs tryUse and reload. Combat fires for player and bot. A new handleContext method will be added at the end of tickPlayer. readNeeds will initialize the map cursor when opening.\n\nThe handleContext method will advance dialogue on confirm, then run tryUse when a prompt exists. Reload and use actions are handled separately so they do not conflict.\n\nThe reload and use input logic is being refined to avoid double-consumption. A boolean flag will track the reload key press so tryReload only runs once. If a prompt exists, tryUse handles the action first; otherwise tryReload handles use or reload. PadSquare input is consumed by tryUse when a prompt is active.\n\nThe reload and use input logic is being refined to avoid double-consumption. A boolean flag will track the reload key press so tryReload only runs once. If a prompt exists, tryUse handles the action first; otherwise tryReload handles use or reload. PadSquare input is consumed by tryUse when a prompt is active.\n\nuseContext will return prompts for buddy down, map up, truck near, step actions, and case near. JAMMED prompts will not block reload. The tablet uses KeyH instead of use. tryUse will also handle report when near a report step.\n\ntryUse will collect payroll. Syrettes take priority over finishing when both are available. A melee action in tickPlayer will trigger finishBuddy on the down buddy.\n\nannounceStep will spawn a concord soldier at the ranger-post for clear steps tagged as cage-guard. The soldier will have 30 health, which is enough to survive one or two tractor shots. A lower health value was considered so a single flare could kill it. The bot will aim by yaw, and the soldier will be placed at the player's feet.\n\nSoldiers will spawn 8 meters ahead of the player based on yaw. The test flow teleports the player to the ranger post, then clears spawns a soldier at that exact site so the player stands directly on top of it; the ray still hits because along distance is zero and lateral distance is within range. Tank destruction targets are placed at east-siding coordinates.\n\nAim will be set by adjusting camera.yaw toward each tank before firing. During destroy steps, any damage kills the target immediately, so one aimed shot per tank is sufficient. The bot will enter the truck with KeyE, hold KeyW, and aim at the target.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The simulation parses, but it has never been booted. I'll fix the palette crash, then start a headless world and correct whatever the engine actually does."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3335b5fb-bf22-49a8-a5a7-e8e8c29c67d3-60","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","old_string":"import { CharacterController, THREE, Vehicle } from '../../pixel-engine.js';","new_string":"import { CharacterController, PALETTE, THREE, Vehicle } from '../../pixel-engine.js';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3335b5fb-bf22-49a8-a5a7-e8e8c29c67d3-61","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","old_string":"    addBlock(this.ctx, 12, y + 1.2, 55, 6, 2.4, 4, this.ctx.palette.white);\n    addBlock(this.ctx, -18, this.ground(-18, 62) + 1.1, 62, 5, 2.2, 4, this.ctx.palette.orange);\n    addBlock(this.ctx, 0, this.ground(0, 70) + 0.4, 70, 14, 0.4, 4, this.ctx.palette.slate);","new_string":"    addBlock(this.ctx, 12, y + 1.2, 55, 6, 2.4, 4, PALETTE.white);\n    addBlock(this.ctx, -18, this.ground(-18, 62) + 1.1, 62, 5, 2.2, 4, PALETTE.orange);\n    addBlock(this.ctx, 0, this.ground(0, 70) + 0.4, 70, 14, 0.4, 4, PALETTE.slate);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3335b5fb-bf22-49a8-a5a7-e8e8c29c67d3-62","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","old_string":"      addBlock(this.ctx, x, this.ground(x, z) + 1.5, z, 2.2, 3, 2.2, this.ctx.palette.slate);","new_string":"      addBlock(this.ctx, x, this.ground(x, z) + 1.5, z, 2.2, 3, 2.2, PALETTE.slate);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3335b5fb-bf22-49a8-a5a7-e8e8c29c67d3-63","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/world/terrain.js","old_string":"    cells: [256, 256],","new_string":"    cells: [512, 512],"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3335b5fb-bf22-49a8-a5a7-e8e8c29c67d3-64","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"