plied\":{\"old_string\":\"      const y = 78 + i * 16;\",\"new_string\":\"      const y = 86 + i * 16;\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"      const y = 78 + i * 16;\",\"old_line\":598,\"new_string\":\"      const y = 86 + i * 16;\",\"new_line\":598,\"context_before\":\"    const px = (input.pointer.x + 1) / 2 * width;\\n    const py = (1 - input.pointer.y) / 2 * height;\\n    items.forEach((item, i) => {\\n\",\"context_after\":\"      if (px > 36 && px < width - 36 && py > y - 2 && py < y + 14) this.focus = i;\\n    });\\n    for (const ev of input.buttonEvents) {\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"1fe1be2e-1c53-4d82-a228-8a66cc495311"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_94","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Delay is not a PlayOptions field.\n\nPitch is semitones, not a multiplier. Passing ~0.85 semitones is valid and produces minimal shift. Raw SoundDef objects can be played directly. Now writing main.js, index, and a boot test.\n\nmain.js configures the engine with a first-person camera and custom look. It registers Enter and M keys to trigger ready and more callbacks via window.__cardAnswer. A canvas lock mechanism is also being added.\n\nThe pointer lock listener now only triggers when the game is in play or round mode. The boot function checks for an active AIHub before proceeding.\n\nAIHub connects in shared-world mode with seats 1 and 4 and card support. On success, the boot function creates a network session and wires window.__cardAnswer to its answer method. It then launches createGame with that session. If the response includes a server field, it initializes a headless engine with the provided seed and steps it at 60 fps.\n\nThe boot function now checks for WebGPU support and fails if it is missing. It then starts the engine with the game, a DOM container, and the seed from the AIHub session. If no session exists, it falls back to creating a local game and starting the engine without a seed.\n\nStatic import of hubSession avoids a redundant dynamic import. The headless server path calls AIHub.ready idempotently. Both the engine step interval and the network interval will run. Engine.start failures are caught and reported to AIHub. Tests import game.js directly rather than main.js.\n\nA dev index.html is being created with a vendor session script and a module entry point. File:// protocol will not load the module, so bundling is the intended delivery method. A build.mjs script will be added per the plan. Pointer lock will be enabled via setWantLock(true) when the game enters play mode.\n\nThe engine checks wantsPointerLock. The click handler requests pointer lock when that flag is set. The pointerup listener remains in place.\n\nwithUrlOptions is confirmed as a named export from the index file.\n\nThe boot test will create a headless game, step it five times, verify the title state, and check music volume to catch setup errors.\n\nGrass rendering and sky application are skipped in Node.js. Audio.setVolume may throw without audio hardware but that is acceptable for now.\n\nWorld generation takes about 1.8 seconds.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d77fa886-56de-49ab-9319-65f173c2cca4-122","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/main.js","old_string":"","new_string":"import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\n\nconst OPTIONS = {\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\n  look: LOOK,\n  touch: false,\n  debugKeys: false,\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\n};\n\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\n    if (!answer) return;\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\n  });\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\n  });\n}\n\nasync function boot() {\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\n  let info = null;\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\n    try {\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n    } catch (err) {\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\n      return;\n    }\n  }\n  if (info) {\n    const session = hubSession(info);\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\n    const game = createGame({ session });\n    if (info.server) {\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\n      return;\n    }\n    try {\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\n    } catch (err) {\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\n    }\n    return;\n  }\n  const game = createGame();\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\n}\n\nboot();\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d77fa886-56de-49ab-9319-65f173c2cca4-123","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/index.html","old_string":"","new_string":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script src=\"vendor/session.js\"></script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>A Cry Too Far</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"app\"></div>\n<script type=\"module\" src=\"src/main.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1226,"output_tokens":2245,"cache_read_input_tokens":202368,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"18808a48-c26a-4849-9713-faad6e924fff"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-d77fa886-56de-49ab-9319-65f173c2cca4-122","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!navi