\"line_number\":555,\"content\":\"     * (`step()`), waiting for promise callbacks wherever the recorded run did. `frames` stops\"},{\"line_number\":557,\"content\":\"     * game is deterministic) and stays in manual time: `step()` plays on from there, live, and\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5a3e731a-2b12-49b6-b6bc-1df68081565c-20","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"100→    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n110→     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n120→     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n130→    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n140→    private bufferFor;\\n    private toBuffer;\\n    private decode;\\n    private applyVolumes;\\n}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"100→    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n110→     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n120→     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n130→    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n140→    private bufferFor;\\n    private toBuffer;\\n    private decode;\\n    private applyVolumes;\\n}\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/audio/AudioManager.d.ts\",\"offset\":100,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"    register(name: string, def: SoundDef): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Play a sound effect by name (built-in SFX, `register`ed or `load`ed) or directly from a\\n     * SoundDef. Returns false when nothing could be heard (locked, muted, no Web Audio).\\n     */\\n    play(sound: string | SoundDef, options?: PlayOptions): boolean;\\n    /**\\n     * Start a sound looping, as a voice you steer while it plays (volume, pan, muffle, pitch:\\n     * with `spatialize` it sits at a place in the world). Before the first user input, or with\\n     * no Web Audio, the voice keeps its settings silently and starts once audio unlocks.\\n     * Stop it when you are done (a level's `dispose`).\\n     */\\n    loop(sound: string | SoundDef, settings?: VoiceSettings): Voice;\\n    /** Voices playing or waiting to (tooling and tests). */\\n    get loops(): readonly Voice[];\\n    /** Stop every looping voice (the engine does this when a level unloads). */\\n    stopLoops(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Load an audio file (wav/ogg/mp3…) under `name`; `play(name)` then plays it. Works\\n     * before the first user input too: the file is decoded once audio unlocks.\\n     */\\n    load(name: string, url: string): Promise<void>;\\n    /** Start a song (looping by default), replacing the current one. `null` stops music. */\\n    playMusic(song: Song | null, name?: string): void;\\n    stopMusic(): void;\\n    /**\\n     * Volume changes are written to storage. The engine turns this off while a replay plays: the\\n     * recording sets the volumes it set, nothing is written, and the player's come back after.\\n     */\\n    persist: boolean;\\n    setVolume(channel: VolumeChannel, value: number): void;\\n    setMuted(muted: boolean): void;\\n    toggleMute(): boolean;\\n    /** The default volumes, sound on (the settings panel's Reset). */\\n    resetVolumes(): void;\\n    /** Engine: once per rendered frame. Schedules the next notes of the song. */\\n    update(): void;\\n    /** Stop everything and close the AudioContext. */\\n    dispose(): void;\\n    private start;\\n    private bufferFor;\\n    private toBuffer;\\n    private decode;\\n    private applyVolumes;\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":144}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"168a38f2-2504-4cf1-9a27-34dc10b3aa63"}
