{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_148","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I will extract from the engine at runtime.\n\nI'll inspect the HUD glyphs map after boot. I'll log its internal keys and verify text rendering without crashing. I'll skip detailed charset measurement and instead scan for characters outside a safe set, including spaces, letters, digits, punctuation, and symbols. If the test is too strict, I'll adjust the strings.\n\nI'll assume the font includes common punctuation like periods, commas, colons, hyphens, apostrophes, quotes, slashes, and parentheses. If semicolons are missing, I'll replace them with periods.\n\nI'm now implementing seven fixes: preventing giveGun from replacing other weapons, adding digit weapon selection in readNeeds, rounding wantsUse and tryUse, removing hub autofinish, setting m1 feverIn to zero, and skipping the round revive dt change. I'll write tests next and iterate.\n\nThe round check in tryUse must come before the buddy syrette logic. Otherwise the campaign truck pickup blocks case pickups during rounds. wantsUse also returns early near the campaign truck, which skips the round check.\n\nSolo rounds from the title screen won't spawn a campaign truck, so the player can't interact with one. The weapon selection logic will go at the start of readNeeds.\n\nThe digit weapon selection logic will consume presses for keys 1 through 4 and the numpad triangle key to cycle slots. The giveGun method now replaces an existing weapon by ID or appends a new one, then updates the active slot. I also set m1 feverIn to zero in setup and began removing the hub autofinish.\n\nSolo tests will finish at 360 seconds. The hub session link already auto-finishes at that limit. Revive ticks add one frame per call while the button is held. The wantsUse distance check keeps the downed player in revive state during that hold.\n\nPickup triggers on the first held frame, so a single tap still works. Bank also fires on the first held frame and returns true, though subsequent frames may pick up another case if the player is still near the truck. I will now implement these fixes and write tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71ae5afc-ead9-4afd-9b44-abccbdb61b5c-101","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"resetDynamic\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-71ae5afc-ead9-4afd-9b44-abccbdb61b5c-102","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","offset":200,"limit":60}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":581,"output_tokens":1229,"cache_read_input_tokens":157568,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f70cef52-d395-4fbf-a71c-1daa843c84b6"}
