"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/missions.js has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/missions.js\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"      x: 12, z: 55, hour: 8, tablets: 1, syrettes: 2, stones: 0,\",\"old_line\":18,\"new_string\":\"      x: 12, z: 55, hour: 8, tablets: 1, syrettes: 2, stones: 0, feverIn: 0,\",\"new_line\":18,\"context_before\":\"    id: 'm1', title: 'MERCY RUN', giver: 'odile', pay: 5, hour: 8, requires: ['m0'],\\n    faction: null,\\n    setup: {\\n\",\"context_after\":\"      guns: [{ id: 'cane', cond: 100 }, { id: 'm38', cond: 100 }, { id: 'tractor', cond: 45 }],\\n      buddies: [], flags: ['m0'], truck: true,\\n    },\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"74b4ac7f-1906-4ddb-850f-05623ddf5afc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_150","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A duplicate round.tryUse may have been left behind.\n\nThe duplicate tryUse is gone. The new call sits at the start of the function. PadTriangle consume in readNeeds won't interfere with choice input. Card mode correctly skips tickPlayer. Now writing tests.\n\nA single engine will run all tests to avoid rebuilding terrain. Tests will run in this order: static checks, boot, grid systems, locomotion, combat, missions, round, and attract last. Fire test can use title mode since fire.step happens before blocksSim.\n\nTitle mode blocks player input but fire still steps. Wind must be pinned for the test and cleared afterward. Igniting during title lets fire spread before startMission extinguishes it. The test suite will use assert helpers that collect failures and continue. Model checks will run during drafting, with warnings treated as non-fatal. A press helper is being designed to simulate inputs across frames.\n\nThe press and hold helpers are now defined. They toggle keys, step the engine, and release. A face helper rotates the camera toward a target. A seek helper drives the player toward coordinates with a distance limit.\n\nThe seek helper now steers vehicles by comparing camera yaw to car yaw and applying left or right input. It drives forward for eight frames per loop iteration. A timeout error is thrown if the target is not reached. The direction of positive steer will be verified during playtesting.\n\nThe engine will step 30 frames at a time for speed. The m8 hold lasts 7200 steps, about eleven seconds, which is safely shorter than the twelve-minute fever duration. The ride sequence needs 3600 steps. For line-based text, the test will press Enter repeatedly while the do flag is 'lines', then guard for twenty frames. Choice selection will press ArrowRight to reach index one and then Enter, since the default focus starts at zero.\n\nArrowRight is chosen over KeyD for choice navigation to avoid unwanted movement. The shoot choice will be tested with both options, and a single shot will confirm ledger.killed increments. An arm helper is being drafted to select weapons by ID.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-7a742e28-7f95-46e9-8114-db7bd02847a9-111","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/types/engine/input.d.ts","offset":210,"limit":50}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3304,"output_tokens":1411,"cache_read_input_tokens":160000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"41f961c0-d210-49f3-a169-f38c9b5e0a41"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-7a742e28-7f95-46e9-8114-db7bd02847a9-111","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n220→    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\\n    /**\\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick or a gamepad's left\\n     * stick (whichever is tilted further), else WASD / arrow keys / d-pad.\\n     */\\n    moveAxis(): {\\n        x: number;\\n        y: number;\\n    };\\n    /** Call at the end of each rendered frame. */\\n230→    endFrame(): void;\\n    /** Test hook: simulate a key being held (true) or released (false). */\\n    setKey(code: string, down: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: put the pointer at (x, y) in normalised device coordinates, pressed or not. */\\n    setPointer(x: number, y: number, down?: boolean): void;\\n    /** Test hook: hold mouse buttons (`PointerEvent.buttons` bits: 1 left, 2 right, 4 middle) as the canvas would. */\\n    setButtons(bits: number): void;\\n    /** Buttons held, as `PointerEvent.buttons` bits (1 left, 2 right, 4 middle; a finger is left): the same keys as `isDown('MouseLeft')`. */\\n    get mouseButtons(): number;\\n    /** A pointer button (a key code) goes down (pressed, unless held already) or up, where the pointer is. */\\n240→    private button;\\n    /**\\n     * This frame's pointer button presses and releases, in order, each with where the pointer\\n     * was: a drag shorter than a frame (a script's) still starts where it started and ends where\\n     * it ended. Recorded with the frame. UI that acts on clicks reads these; play reads `isDown`.\\n     */\\n    get buttonEvents(): readonly ButtonEvent[];\\n    /**\\n     * Hand the game data from outside the canvas: a DOM widget's value, a file the player picked,\\n     * a save read from storage, anything a game would otherwise take straight from the page. It\\n250→     * arrives in `commands` at the next frame the game runs, and the recording keeps it there, so\\n     * a replay delivers the same data at the same frame (and ignores what is sent live). It goes\\n     * through JSON first: live play reads exactly what a replay will.\\n     */\\n    send(command: unknown): void;\\n    /**\\n     * This frame's commands (`send`), oldest first; empty on most frames. They last one rendered\\n     * frame: read them in `update` (`fixedUpdate` runs zero or more times a frame).\\n     */\\n    get commands(): readonly unknown[];\",\"content_concise\":\"210→    consumePress(...codes: string[]): boolean;\\n    /** `consumePress` for a list of codes, without building a rest-argument array. */\\n    consumeAny(codes: readonly string[]): boolean;\\n    /** Held keys, queued presses and the pointer as data (`engine.snapshot()`), between frames. */\\n    state(): InputState;\\n    /** Back to `state()` at game time `now` (a restore): held keys are those the snapshot held, live ones let go. */\\n    setState(s: InputState, now: number): void;\\n    /** Presses waiting to be consumed (tooling / tests). */\\n    get queuedPresses(): string[];\\n    /** Drop queued presses (e.g. when a menu or mode swallows input). */\\n220→    clearQueued(...codes: string[]): void;\\n    /**\\n     * -1..1 on each axis (x = right, y = forward): the touch joystick