THING ON THIS RACK HAS BEEN RETURNED AT LEAST ONCE.',\\n  'tibor:price': 'IT FIRES. IF YOU WANT IT TO FIRE TWICE, THAT IS A DIFFERENT PRICE.',\\n  'tibor:m2.1': 'SHE OWES ME A PLANE. I OWE HER A KEY. FETCH HER.',\\n  'ines:meet': 'I FLEW FOR BOTH OF THEM. NEITHER PAID. GET IN.',\\n  'ines:owe': 'YOU OWE ME A TRUCK. YOU OWE ME SEVERAL TRUCKS.',\\n  'ines:m3': 'TAKE THE TANKER AT THE EAST POST AND DRIVE IT IN.',\\n\",\"total_lines\":99}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"9878f78f-3fe5-4301-a76a-849639f778c8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_158","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking for apostrophes and punctuation.\n\nWriting the test file now. It will include a charset check to ensure every character in the lines and about pages is present in the font. Also fixing round.tryUse revive to use a stored dt.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-460cb9f0-c4e1-4cf9-83a8-0568fd0d118a-121","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/core/save.js","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2448,"output_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":179968,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"4b34b0b2-5d0f-4969-8a80-c1e9511c78cd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-460cb9f0-c4e1-4cf9-83a8-0568fd0d118a-121","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→const KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-save';\\nconst SETTINGS_KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-settings';\\n\\nexport function storage() {\\n  try {\\n    if (typeof localStorage === 'undefined' || !localStorage) return null;\\n    return localStorage;\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n10→  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return false;\\n  s.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function readSave() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return null;\\n  const raw = s.getItem(KEY);\\n  if (!raw) return null;\\n  try {\\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n30→}\\n\\nexport function writeSettings(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return;\\n  s.setItem(SETTINGS_KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSettings() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n40→  if (!s) return null;\",\"content_concise\":\"1→const KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-save';\\nconst SETTINGS_KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-settings';\\n\\nexport function storage() {\\n  try {\\n    if (typeof localStorage === 'undefined' || !localStorage) return null;\\n    return localStorage;\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n10→  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return false;\\n  s.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\n20→export function readSave() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return null;\\n  const raw = s.getItem(KEY);\\n  if (!raw) return null;\\n  try {\\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n30→}\\n\\nexport function writeSettings(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return;\\n  s.setItem(SETTINGS_KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSettings() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n40→  if (!s) return null;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/core/save.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"const KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-save';\\nconst SETTINGS_KEY = 'a-cry-too-far-settings';\\n\\nexport function storage() {\\n  try {\\n    if (typeof localStorage === 'undefined' || !localStorage) return null;\\n    return localStorage;\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSave(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return false;\\n  s.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n  return true;\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSave() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return null;\\n  const raw = s.getItem(KEY);\\n  if (!raw) return null;\\n  try {\\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\\n  } catch {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport function writeSettings(data) {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return;\\n  s.setItem(SETTINGS_KEY, JSON.stringify(data));\\n}\\n\\nexport function readSettings() {\\n  const s = storage();\\n  if (!s) return null;\\n\",\"total_lines\":48}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"16280cb0-e16c-4a3f-b616-c639634d66b4"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_159","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Writing the test now. Adding a memory of keys to release.\n\nScanning for a 20-cell vertical strip of fuel to light. Wind is set to direction 0, speed 5, and the simulation steps 5 frames first so wind applies before measuring spread.\n\nDefining head and flank speed formulas from cell positions. Writing the test file now. Also fixing a potential bug in the m1 tablet step where feverOn and feverT interact.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8d5e1201-2e1b-40a5-b26b-b57d446c7631-122","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","offset":660,"limit":70}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":643,"output_tokens":617,"cache_read_input_tokens":182400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ea727ea9-16b8-4bac-b7b2-a020eec8713e"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8d5e1201-2e1b-40a5-b26b-b57d446c7631-122","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"660→\\n  tickActors(dt) {\\n    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n670→        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n680→        }\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n690→          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n700→\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n710→    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n720→  }\\n\\n  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\",\"content_concise\":\"660→\\n  tickActors(dt) {\\n    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n670→        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n680→        }\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n690→          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n700→\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n710→    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n720→  }\\n\\n  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js\",\"offset\":660,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"\\n  tickActors(dt) {\\n    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n        }\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\\n\",\"total_lines\":1347}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"4c7b3bbe-252c-494f-bf1e-11734c84c9a7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_160","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"m8 is at mile forty (0, 70), which falls within the town boundary.\n\nThe truce flag is false on m8. Soldiers can shoot. No soldiers are near the hold point at (0, 70). The ranger post is far away. The player is safe unless they wander.\n\nThe ranger is roughly 240 meters away, well past the 90-meter range. m8 is at hour 17, so it is not night. Player health regenerates normally during the hold. I will write the test script and run it with a filtered --only flag. I will also create ISSUES.md in the dev folder. The test runner must change to the project root because it lives in the dev subfolder.\n\nThe test script will import game modules and assets using relative paths from the dev subfolder. It will also load TUNING, missions, sites, songs, models, textures, and about. A `release` helper is being drafted to clear all input keys at once.\n\nThe test script now includes `tap`, `holdKey`, and `holdFire` helpers to simulate input actions across engine frames.\n\nA `goTo` helper is being drafted to walk the player toward a target position within a radius. The fire input will use `setButtons(1)` followed by `setButtons(0)` to simulate a tap, since the engine checks `wasPressed` for the left mouse button.\n\nThe `goTo` helper now calculates yaw to face the target. It steers the player forward with `KeyW`. When in a vehicle, it adjusts `KeyA` and `KeyD` to correct yaw error. The loop steps six frames per iteration.\n\nThe `goTo` helper now throws an error if it fails to reach the target. The 8000-spin timeout was reduced to 2500 spins to limit wall-clock time at roughly 250 seconds. An `arm()` helper is being drafted to select a gun by ID.\n\nThe `arm()` helper now taps the correct digit key and verifies the weapon is actually selected. A `shootUntil` helper is being drafted to hold fire for up to 90 frames until a predicate becomes true. The next step is a function to destroy all props matching a given tag.\n\nThe `destroyTag` helper is now drafted. It repeatedly locates alive props with the target tag, teleports the player to their position, arms the tractor gun if available or the current weapon, and fires until the prop dies or the destroy step ends. A guard loop limits this to eight attempts; failure throws an error.\n\nIf the player is in a vehicle during a destroy attempt, teleporting moves the car rather than the hero. Shots still originate from the car position, so this is acceptable. Combat does not check for inVehicle status, so weapons work while driving. The Burn helper is next.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The mission actions are wired. Next I’ll add the headless suite that drives the shipped game and fix whatever it fails."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c54daea7-0488-4a67-9616-0648453fedbe-123","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","new_string":"/** Headless acceptance. Run from the dev folder: node tests/run.mjs --all */\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport { Engine, checkModel, parseSong, validateTexture } from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { aboutPages } from '../src/content/about.js';\nimport { LINES } from '../src/content/dialogue.js';\nimport { SONGS } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\nimport { TEXTURES } from '../src/art/textures.js';\nimport { siteById } from '../src/content/sites.js';\nimport { TUNING_DEFAULTS, TUNING_RANGES, SLIDER_KEYS } from '../src/content/tuning-defaults.js';\nimport { TUNING } from '../src/core/tuning.js';\nimport { createGame } from '../src/game.js';\n\nconst root = dirname(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)));\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst only = args.find((a) => a.startsWith('--only='))?.slice(7)\n  || (args.includes('--only') ? args[args.indexOf('--only') + 1] : '');\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\nconst tests = [];\nconst test = (name, fn) => tests.push({ name, fn });\n\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\n}\n\nlet engine;\nlet game;\n\nasync function boot() {\n  if (engine) return;\n  game = createGame();\n  engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: 1 });\n}\n\nfunction release() {\n  for (const code of ['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'KeyE', 'KeyR', 'KeyQ', 'KeyM', 'KeyH', 'KeyF', 'KeyC', 'KeyJ', 'ShiftLeft', 'Space', 'Enter', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Digit1', 'Digit2', 'Digit3', 'Digit4']) {\n    engine.input.setKey(code, false);\n  }\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\n}\n\nfunction tap(code) {\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n}\n\nfunction holdKey(code, frames) {\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n}\n\nfunction tapFire() {\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\n  engine.step(2, DT);\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n}\n\nfunction holdFire(frames) {\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n}\n\nfunction arm(id) {\n  const w = game.world;\n  const i = w.guns.findIndex((g) => g.id === id);\n  if (i < 0) throw new Error('no gun ' + id);\n  tap('Digit' + (i + 1));\n  if (w.weapon?.id !== id) throw new Error('selected ' + w.weapon?.id + ' instead of ' + id);\n}\n\nfunction goTo(x, z, r) {\n  const w = game.world;\n  release();\n  for (let spins = 0; spins < 2500; spins++) {\n    const p = w.feet();\n    if (Math.hypot(x - p.x, z - p.z) <= r) {\n      release();\n      engine.step(1, DT);\n      return;\n    }\n    const yaw = Math.atan2(-(x - p.x), -(z - p.z));\n    game.ctx.camera.yaw = yaw;\n    if (w.inVehicle && w.car) {\n      let err = yaw - w.car.yaw;\n      while (err > Math.PI) err -= Math.PI * 2;\n      while (err < -Math.PI) err += Math.PI * 2;\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyA', err > 0.2);\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyD', err < -0.2);\n    }\n    engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\n    engine.step(6, DT);\n  }\n  const p = w.feet();\n  throw new Error('goto stuck at ' + p.x.toFixed(1) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(1) + ' wanting ' + x + ',' + z);\n}\n\nfunction placeFacing(x, z) {\n  const w = game.world;\n  if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\n  w.teleport(x, z + 4);\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n}\n\nfunction playMission(id, opts = {}) {\n  const w = game.world;\n  assert(w.startMission(id, opts), 'missing ' + id);\n  let choiceI = 0;\n  for (let guard = 0; guard < 80 && w.mission && !w.mission.done; guard++) {\n    const step = w.currentStep();\n    if (!step) break;\n    const before = w.mission.index;\n    if (step.do === 'lines') {\n      for (let n = 0; n < 8 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'lines'; n++) tap('Enter');\n    } else if (step.do === 'map') {\n      tap('KeyM');\n    } else if (step.do === 'fever-fall') {\n      engine.step(Math.ceil(26 * 60), DT);\n    } else if (step.do === 'tablet') {\n      holdKey('KeyH', 90);\n    } else if (step.do === 'goto' || step.do === 'drive' || step.do === 'leave') {\n      const site = step.site ? siteById(step.site) : null;\n      const x = site ? site.x : step.x;\n      const z = site ? site.z : step.z;\n      const radius = step.r || (step.do === 'leave' ? 40 : 20);\n      if (step.do === 'leave') {\n        goTo(x + radius + 30, z, 8);\n      } else goTo(x, z, Math.max(4, radius - 2));\n    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\n      arm('tractor');\n      holdFire(80);\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');\n    } else if (step.do === 'repair') {\n      holdKey('KeyE', 220);\n    } else if (step.do === 'syrette') {\n      holdKey('KeyQ', 70);\n    } else if (step.do === 'destroy') {\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'destroy'; n++) {\n        const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.alive !== false && p.tag === step.tag);\n        if (!prop) break;\n        placeFacing(prop.x, prop.z);\n        if (w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'tractor')) arm('tractor');\n        holdFire(50);\n      }\n    } else if (step.do === 'burn') {\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\n      w.teleport(step.x, step.z + 18);\n      game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\n      arm('flare');\n      tapFire();\n      engine.step(20, DT);\n    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\n      arm('tractor');\n      holdFire(80);\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\n      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\n      engine.step(1, DT);\n      tap('KeyE');\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\n      tap('KeyE');\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\n      release();\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\n      engine.step(frames, DT);\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\n      choiceI += 1;\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\n      tap('Enter');\n    } else {\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\n    }\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\n      const p = w.feet();\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\n    }\n  }\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\n  release();\n}\n\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\n    const path = join(dir, name);\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\n  }\n}\n\ntest('static files', () => {\n  const files = [];\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\n  const blob = files.join('\\n');\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\n  }\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\n');\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry]);\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\n  }\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\n    const check = checkModel(model);\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\n  }\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\n  }\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\'-/()%+#&');\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\n  for (const line of shown) {\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\n    }\n  }\n});\n\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const state = game.state();\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\n  engine.step(30, DT);\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\n  engine.step(5, DT);\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\n});\n\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\n  let column = null;\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\n    let ok = 0;\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\n  }\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\n  const iz0 = 70;\n  const iz1 = 99;\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\n  let maxX = column;\n  let minZ = iz1;\n  let maxZ = iz0;\n  let burnt = null;\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\n    const ix = i % 256;\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\n  }\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\n  game.world.refreshMap();\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\n  game.world.windPin = null;\n});\n\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const w = game.world;\n  w.startMission('m2');\n  release();\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\n  tap('KeyC');\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\n  tap('KeyC');\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\n  tap('Space');\n  engine.step(8, DT);\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\n  engine.step(5, DT);\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\n});\n\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const w = game.world;\n  w.startMission('m2');\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\n  arm('m38');\n  const before = w.guns.length;\n  tapFire();\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\n  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\n  arm('tractor');\n  w.jamScript = 5;\n  w.noJam = false;\n  holdFire(40);\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\n  holdFire(20);\n  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\n  const hp = civil.hp;\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\n  arm('tractor');\n  holdFire(20);\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\n  w.tablets = 1;\n  w.stones = 50;\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\n  w.feverOn = false;\n  engine.step(5, DT);\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\n  w.feverOn = true;\n  w.feverClear = 0;\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\n  w.tablets = 0;\n  w.stones = 50;\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\n  w.hp = 15;\n  tap('KeyQ');\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\n  w.startMission('m3');\n  w.hp = 1;\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT === 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp);\n  w.syrettes = 1;\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\n  tap('KeyE');\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\n  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\n  w.syrettes = 0;\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\n  tap('KeyE');\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\n});\n\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const w = game.world;\n  w.startMission('m1');\n  engine.step(2, DT);\n  tap('KeyE');\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\n  engine.step(20, DT);\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\n  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.2, 0.2, false);\n  engine.step(2, DT);\n  engine.input.setPointer(-0.4, -0.2, false);\n  engine.step(2, DT);\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\n  tap('KeyE');\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\n  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\n    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\n  }\n  game.resetSliders();\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\n});\n\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\n  playMission('m7');\n  playMission('m8');\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\n});\n\ntest('solo round', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  game.toTitle();\n  game.startSolo();\n  const round = game.world.round;\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\n  const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'merc' && a.seat === merc.id);\n  placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\n  arm('tractor');\n  holdFire(30);\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing');\n  if (!merc.down) {\n    holdFire(80);\n  }\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop');\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n  tap('KeyE');\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\n});\n\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\n  await boot();\n  game.toTitle();\n  game.idle = 0;\n  game.attract = false;\n  game.mode = 'title';\n  game.screen = 'title';\n  const saves = game.saves;\n  engine.step(600, DT);\n  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\n  engine.step(1, DT);\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\n  tap('KeyE');\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\n  game.screen = 'settings';\n  game.mode = 'menu';\n  game.idle = 0;\n  engine.step(700, DT);\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\n  game.toTitle();\n  tap('Enter');\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\n  game.screen = 'cash';\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\n  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\n  game.screen = 'menu';\n  game.mode = 'menu';\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\n  tap('Enter');\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\n  tap('Enter');\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\n  tap('Escape');\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\n  engine.step(30, DT);\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\n  tap('Enter');\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\n  const flat = aboutPages().flat().join('\\n');\n  for (const bit of ['2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Far Cry 2', 'PLAN.md', 'added on import', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated']) {\n    assert(flat.includes(bit), 'about missing ' + bit);\n  }\n});\n\nconst touch = test;\ntouch('touch gate', async () => {\n  const g = createGame({ touchOnly: true });\n  const e = await Engine.headless(g, { seed: 2 });\n  assert(g.notice === 'Controller or keyboard required', g.notice);\n  assert(g.items().length === 1 && g.items()[0].id === 'settings', 'touch menu');\n  e.step(601, DT);\n  assert(g.attract, 'touch blocked attract');\n  g.exitAttract();\n  g.focus = 0;\n  e.input.setPointer(0, 1 - (86 / 270) * 2, true);\n  e.input.setButtons(1);\n  e.step(1, DT);\n  e.input.setButtons(0);\n  e.step(1, DT);\n  assert(g.screen === 'settings', 'tap did not open settings ' + g.screen);\n});\n\nconst picked = tests.filter((t) => !only || t.name.includes(only));\nlet failed = 0;\nfor (const t of picked) {\n  try {\n    await t.fn();\n  } catch (err) {\n    failed += 1;\n    const msg = String(err && err.stack || err).split('\\n').filter((line) => line.length < 240).slice(0, 8).join('\\n');\n    console.log('FAIL ' + t.name + '\\n' + msg);\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('passed ' + (picked.length - failed) + ' failed ' + failed);\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1447,"output_tokens":9616,"cache_read_input_tokens":183040,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3f5a5bb4-9733-4fbf-86d3-91fe52735ac2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-c54daea7-0488-4a67-9616-0648453fedbe-123","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"\",\"new_string\":\"/** Headless acceptance. Run from the dev folder: node tests/run.mjs --all */\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { Engine, checkModel, parseSong, validateTexture } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { aboutPages } from '../src/content/about.js';\\nimport { LINES } from '../src/content/dialogue.js';\\nimport { SONGS } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { TEXTURES } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { siteById } from '../src/content/sites.js';\\nimport { TUNING_DEFAULTS, TUNING_RANGES, SLIDER_KEYS } from '../src/content/tuning-defaults.js';\\nimport { TUNING } from '../src/core/tuning.js';\\nimport { createGame } from '../src/game.js';\\n\\nconst root = dirname(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)));\\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\\nconst only = args.find((a) => a.startsWith('--only='))?.slice(7)\\n  || (args.includes('--only') ? args[args.indexOf('--only') + 1] : '');\\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\\nconst tests = [];\\nconst test = (name, fn) => tests.push({ name, fn });\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\nlet engine;\\nlet game;\\n\\nasync function boot() {\\n  if (engine) return;\\n  game = createGame();\\n  engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: 1 });\\n}\\n\\nfunction release() {\\n  for (const code of ['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'KeyE', 'KeyR', 'KeyQ', 'KeyM', 'KeyH', 'KeyF', 'KeyC', 'KeyJ', 'ShiftLeft', 'Space', 'Enter', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Digit1', 'Digit2', 'Digit3', 'Digit4']) {\\n    engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  }\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n}\\n\\nfunction tap(code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction holdKey(code, frames) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction tapFire() {\\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction holdFire(frames) {\\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction arm(id) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  const i = w.guns.findIndex((g) => g.id === id);\\n  if (i < 0) throw new Error('no gun ' + id);\\n  tap('Digit' + (i + 1));\\n  if (w.weapon?.id !== id) throw new Error('selected ' + w.weapon?.id + ' instead of ' + id);\\n}\\n\\nfunction goTo(x, z, r) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  release();\\n  for (let spins = 0; spins < 2500; spins++) {\\n    const p = w.feet();\\n    if (Math.hypot(x - p.x, z - p.z) <= r) {\\n      release();\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const yaw = Math.atan2(-(x - p.x), -(z - p.z));\\n    game.ctx.camera.yaw = yaw;\\n    if (w.inVehicle && w.car) {\\n      let err = yaw - w.car.yaw;\\n      while (err > Math.PI) err -= Math.PI * 2;\\n      while (err < -Math.PI) err += Math.PI * 2;\\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyA', err > 0.2);\\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyD', err < -0.2);\\n    }\\n    engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n    engine.step(6, DT);\\n  }\\n  const p = w.feet();\\n  throw new Error('goto stuck at ' + p.x.toFixed(1) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(1) + ' wanting ' + x + ',' + z);\\n}\\n\\nfunction placeFacing(x, z) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n  w.teleport(x, z + 4);\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction playMission(id, opts = {}) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  assert(w.startMission(id, opts), 'missing ' + id);\\n  let choiceI = 0;\\n  for (let guard = 0; guard < 80 && w.mission && !w.mission.done; guard++) {\\n    const step = w.currentStep();\\n    if (!step) break;\\n    const before = w.mission.index;\\n    if (step.do === 'lines') {\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 8 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'lines'; n++) tap('Enter');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'map') {\\n      tap('KeyM');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'fever-fall') {\\n      engine.step(Math.ceil(26 * 60), DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'tablet') {\\n      holdKey('KeyH', 90);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'goto' || step.do === 'drive' || step.do === 'leave') {\\n      const site = step.site ? siteById(step.site) : null;\\n      const x = site ? site.x : step.x;\\n      const z = site ? site.z : step.z;\\n      const radius = step.r || (step.do === 'leave' ? 40 : 20);\\n      if (step.do === 'leave') {\\n        goTo(x + radius + 30, z, 8);\\n      } else goTo(x, z, Math.max(4, radius - 2));\\n    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'repair') {\\n      holdKey('KeyE', 220);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'syrette') {\\n      holdKey('KeyQ', 70);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'destroy') {\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'destroy'; n++) {\\n        const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.alive !== false && p.tag === step.tag);\\n        if (!prop) break;\\n        placeFacing(prop.x, prop.z);\\n        if (w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'tractor')) arm('tractor');\\n        holdFire(50);\\n      }\\n    } else if (step.do === 'burn') {\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(step.x, step.z + 18);\\n      game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n      arm('flare');\\n      tapFire();\\n      engine.step(20, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\\n      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\\n      release();\\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\\n      engine.step(frames, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\\n      choiceI += 1;\\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\\n    }\\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\\n      const p = w.feet();\\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\\n  release();\\n}\\n\\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    const path = join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\ntest('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry]);\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\\n  arm('m38');\\n  const before = w.guns.length;\\n  tapFire();\\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\\n  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  w.jamScript = 5;\\n  w.noJam = false;\\n  holdFire(40);\\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\\n  const hp = civil.hp;\\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\\n  w.tablets = 1;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\\n  w.feverOn = false;\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\\n  w.feverOn = true;\\n  w.feverClear = 0;\\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\\n  w.tablets = 0;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\\n  w.hp = 15;\\n  tap('KeyQ');\\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\\n  w.startMission('m3');\\n  w.hp = 1;\\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT === 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp);\\n  w.syrettes = 1;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\\n  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\\n  w.syrettes = 0;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\\n});\\n\\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m1');\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\\n  engine.step(20, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\\n  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.2, 0.2, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  engine.input.setPointer(-0.4, -0.2, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\\n  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\\n    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\\n  }\\n  game.resetSliders();\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\\n});\\n\\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\\n  playMission('m7');\\n  playMission('m8');\\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\\n});\\n\\ntest('solo round', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.startSolo();\\n  const round = game.world.round;\\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\\n  const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'merc' && a.seat === merc.id);\\n  placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(30);\\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing');\\n  if (!merc.down) {\\n    holdFire(80);\\n  }\\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop');\\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\\n});\\n\\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  game.attract = false;\\n  game.mode = 'title';\\n  game.screen = 'title';\\n  const saves = game.saves;\\n  engine.step(600, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.screen = 'settings';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  engine.step(700, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\\n  game.screen = 'cash';\\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\\n  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\\n  game.screen = 'menu';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\\n  tap('Escape');\\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\\n  const flat = aboutPages().flat().join('\\\\n');\\n  for (const bit of ['2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Far Cry 2', 'PLAN.md', 'added on import', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated']) {\\n    assert(flat.includes(bit), 'about missing ' + bit);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nconst touch = test;\\ntouch('touch gate', async () => {\\n  const g = createGame({ touchOnly: true });\\n  const e = await Engine.headless(g, { seed: 2 });\\n  assert(g.notice === 'Controller or keyboard required', g.notice);\\n  assert(g.items().length === 1 && g.items()[0].id === 'settings', 'touch menu');\\n  e.step(601, DT);\\n  assert(g.attract, 'touch blocked attract');\\n  g.exitAttract();\\n  g.focus = 0;\\n  e.input.setPointer(0, 1 - (86 / 270) * 2, true);\\n  e.input.setButtons(1);\\n  e.step(1, DT);\\n  e.input.setButtons(0);\\n  e.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(g.screen === 'settings', 'tap did not open settings ' + g.screen);\\n});\\n\\nconst picked = tests.filter((t) => !only || t.name.includes(only));\\nlet failed = 0;\\nfor (const t of picked) {\\n  try {\\n    await t.fn();\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    failed += 1;\\n    const msg = String(err && err.stack || err).split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.length < 240).slice(0, 8).join('\\\\n');\\n    console.log('FAIL ' + t.name + '\\\\n' + msg);\\n  }\\n}\\nconsole.log('passed ' + (picked.length - failed) + ' failed ' + failed);\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"/** Headless acceptance. Run from the dev folder: node tests/run.mjs --all */\\nimport { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\\nimport { readdirSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { dirname, join } from 'node:path';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\\nimport { Engine, checkModel, parseSong, validateTexture } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { aboutPages } from '../src/content/about.js';\\nimport { LINES } from '../src/content/dialogue.js';\\nimport { SONGS } from '../src/audio/songs.js';\\nimport { MODELS } from '../src/art/models.js';\\nimport { TEXTURES } from '../src/art/textures.js';\\nimport { siteById } from '../src/content/sites.js';\\nimport { TUNING_DEFAULTS, TUNING_RANGES, SLIDER_KEYS } from '../src/content/tuning-defaults.js';\\nimport { TUNING } from '../src/core/tuning.js';\\nimport { createGame } from '../src/game.js';\\n\\nconst root = dirname(dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)));\\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\\nconst only = args.find((a) => a.startsWith('--only='))?.slice(7)\\n  || (args.includes('--only') ? args[args.indexOf('--only') + 1] : '');\\nconst DT = 1 / 60;\\nconst tests = [];\\nconst test = (name, fn) => tests.push({ name, fn });\\n\\nfunction assert(cond, msg) {\\n  if (!cond) throw new Error(msg || 'assertion failed');\\n}\\n\\nlet engine;\\nlet game;\\n\\nasync function boot() {\\n  if (engine) return;\\n  game = createGame();\\n  engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: 1 });\\n}\\n\\nfunction release() {\\n  for (const code of ['KeyW', 'KeyA', 'KeyS', 'KeyD', 'KeyE', 'KeyR', 'KeyQ', 'KeyM', 'KeyH', 'KeyF', 'KeyC', 'KeyJ', 'ShiftLeft', 'Space', 'Enter', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Digit1', 'Digit2', 'Digit3', 'Digit4']) {\\n    engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  }\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n}\\n\\nfunction tap(code) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction holdKey(code, frames) {\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, true);\\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey(code, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction tapFire() {\\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction holdFire(frames) {\\n  engine.input.setButtons(1);\\n  engine.step(frames, DT);\\n  engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction arm(id) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  const i = w.guns.findIndex((g) => g.id === id);\\n  if (i < 0) throw new Error('no gun ' + id);\\n  tap('Digit' + (i + 1));\\n  if (w.weapon?.id !== id) throw new Error('selected ' + w.weapon?.id + ' instead of ' + id);\\n}\\n\\nfunction goTo(x, z, r) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  release();\\n  for (let spins = 0; spins < 2500; spins++) {\\n    const p = w.feet();\\n    if (Math.hypot(x - p.x, z - p.z) <= r) {\\n      release();\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    const yaw = Math.atan2(-(x - p.x), -(z - p.z));\\n    game.ctx.camera.yaw = yaw;\\n    if (w.inVehicle && w.car) {\\n      let err = yaw - w.car.yaw;\\n      while (err > Math.PI) err -= Math.PI * 2;\\n      while (err < -Math.PI) err += Math.PI * 2;\\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyA', err > 0.2);\\n      engine.input.setKey('KeyD', err < -0.2);\\n    }\\n    engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n    engine.step(6, DT);\\n  }\\n  const p = w.feet();\\n  throw new Error('goto stuck at ' + p.x.toFixed(1) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(1) + ' wanting ' + x + ',' + z);\\n}\\n\\nfunction placeFacing(x, z) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n  w.teleport(x, z + 4);\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n}\\n\\nfunction playMission(id, opts = {}) {\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  assert(w.startMission(id, opts), 'missing ' + id);\\n  let choiceI = 0;\\n  for (let guard = 0; guard < 80 && w.mission && !w.mission.done; guard++) {\\n    const step = w.currentStep();\\n    if (!step) break;\\n    const before = w.mission.index;\\n    if (step.do === 'lines') {\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 8 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'lines'; n++) tap('Enter');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'map') {\\n      tap('KeyM');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'fever-fall') {\\n      engine.step(Math.ceil(26 * 60), DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'tablet') {\\n      holdKey('KeyH', 90);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'goto' || step.do === 'drive' || step.do === 'leave') {\\n      const site = step.site ? siteById(step.site) : null;\\n      const x = site ? site.x : step.x;\\n      const z = site ? site.z : step.z;\\n      const radius = step.r || (step.do === 'leave' ? 40 : 20);\\n      if (step.do === 'leave') {\\n        goTo(x + radius + 30, z, 8);\\n      } else goTo(x, z, Math.max(4, radius - 2));\\n    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'repair') {\\n      holdKey('KeyE', 220);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'syrette') {\\n      holdKey('KeyQ', 70);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'destroy') {\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'destroy'; n++) {\\n        const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.alive !== false && p.tag === step.tag);\\n        if (!prop) break;\\n        placeFacing(prop.x, prop.z);\\n        if (w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'tractor')) arm('tractor');\\n        holdFire(50);\\n      }\\n    } else if (step.do === 'burn') {\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(step.x, step.z + 18);\\n      game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n      arm('flare');\\n      tapFire();\\n      engine.step(20, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\\n      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\\n      release();\\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\\n      engine.step(frames, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\\n      choiceI += 1;\\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\\n    }\\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\\n      const p = w.feet();\\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\\n  release();\\n}\\n\\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    const path = join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\ntest('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry]);\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\\n  arm('m38');\\n  const before = w.guns.length;\\n  tapFire();\\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\\n  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  w.jamScript = 5;\\n  w.noJam = false;\\n  holdFire(40);\\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\\n  const hp = civil.hp;\\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\\n  w.tablets = 1;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\\n  w.feverOn = false;\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\\n  w.feverOn = true;\\n  w.feverClear = 0;\\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\\n  w.tablets = 0;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\\n  w.hp = 15;\\n  tap('KeyQ');\\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\\n  w.startMission('m3');\\n  w.hp = 1;\\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT === 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp);\\n  w.syrettes = 1;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\\n  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\\n  w.syrettes = 0;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\\n});\\n\\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m1');\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\\n  engine.step(20, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\\n  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.2, 0.2, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  engine.input.setPointer(-0.4, -0.2, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\\n  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\\n    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\\n  }\\n  game.resetSliders();\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\\n});\\n\\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\\n  playMission('m7');\\n  playMission('m8');\\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\\n});\\n\\ntest('solo round', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.startSolo();\\n  const round = game.world.round;\\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\\n  const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'merc' && a.seat === merc.id);\\n  placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(30);\\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing');\\n  if (!merc.down) {\\n    holdFire(80);\\n  }\\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop');\\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\\n});\\n\\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  game.attract = false;\\n  game.mode = 'title';\\n  game.screen = 'title';\\n  const saves = game.saves;\\n  engine.step(600, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.screen = 'settings';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  engine.step(700, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\\n  game.screen = 'cash';\\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\\n  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\\n  game.screen = 'menu';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\\n  tap('Escape');\\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\\n  const flat = aboutPages().flat().join('\\\\n');\\n  for (const bit of ['2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Far Cry 2', 'PLAN.md', 'added on import', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated']) {\\n    assert(flat.includes(bit), 'about missing ' + bit);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\nconst touch = test;\\ntouch('touch gate', async () => {\\n  const g = createGame({ touchOnly: true });\\n  const e = await Engine.headless(g, { seed: 2 });\\n  assert(g.notice === 'Controller or keyboard required', g.notice);\\n  assert(g.items().length === 1 && g.items()[0].id === 'settings', 'touch menu');\\n  e.step(601, DT);\\n  assert(g.attract, 'touch blocked attract');\\n  g.exitAttract();\\n  g.focus = 0;\\n  e.input.setPointer(0, 1 - (86 / 270) * 2, true);\\n  e.input.setButtons(1);\\n  e.step(1, DT);\\n  e.input.setButtons(0);\\n  e.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(g.screen === 'settings', 'tap did not open settings ' + g.screen);\\n});\\n\\nconst picked = tests.filter((t) => !only || t.name.includes(only));\\nlet failed = 0;\\nfor (const t of picked) {\\n  try {\\n    await t.fn();\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    failed += 1;\\n    const msg = String(err && err.stack || err).split('\\\\n').filter((line) => line.length < 240).slice(0, 8).join('\\\\n');\\n    console.log('FAIL ' + t.name + '\\\\n' + msg);\\n  }\\n}\\nconsole.log('passed ' + (picked.length - failed) + ' failed ' + failed);\\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"06c71f40-2eb4-4336-9175-03a7173bdf16"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_161","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A test bug checks root menu labels for HOST, which is absent. This is acceptable because the assertion is false.\n\nTouch and menu tests are registered correctly. The shared engine means fire test state is cleared by locomotion startMission. Guns test sets deadBuddies after mission m2.\n\nA shared engine state bug breaks the story chain. The guns test leaves ines in deadBuddies. Story m3 lists her as a living buddy, but applySetup marks her dead. This prevents knockBuddy on m6 from working and breaks rescue tests that need a living buddy.\n\nThe shared engine state is less problematic than first thought. The guns test rescues ines before finish-it kills her, so story m3 sees her as dead. This still allows knockBuddy on m6 to auto-complete because dov is also marked dead. applySetup only increments ledger.friends for newly added IDs, preventing double-counting.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-b4a518c9-5f63-459a-a71f-c0b1774c414f-124","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\" && node tests/run.mjs --only static","description":"Run static acceptance checks"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9743,"output_tokens":646,"cache_read_input_tokens":184448,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"8a19e56d-38cf-4bb1-9919-a8332993eaea"}
