{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_201","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Fuel tanks have physics blocks.\n\nBullets pass through physics blocks. Convoy and tube weapons are properly configured. Charge plant and tractor destroy logic are correct. The cage guard spawn position is set.\n\nRanger post and fort clement spawn positions are outside town. m2 starts inside town but walks out. The clinic block at 12, 55 may trap the player inside geometry.\n\nm1 spawns inside the clinic block. The player capsule intersects the geometry and walking may fail. Driving works because the truck is outside the building. m2 spawns at the orange building. If goTo fails from inside a building, teleporting slightly outside before walking will be a test accommodation.\n\nThe player spawning inside solid geometry is a real bug. The clinic block at 12, 55 is 6 by 2.4 by 4, so the spawn center sits inside the mesh. Teleporting to 12, 58 would place the player just outside. The proper fix is moving spawn positions in missions rather than nudging during goTo.\n\nA small teleport offset in applySetup is a hack. The test can instead nudge the player six meters forward before goTo if the first spins fail to move. Rapier may resolve overlap automatically. A stuck detector inside goTo could exit the vehicle or teleport eight meters toward the target, but that feels cheat-y. Static boxes block the character controller, so starting inside geometry risks getting stuck.\n\nThe story test finished in 2.5 seconds total. That is far faster than a 400-meter walk should take. The m0 fever simulation alone consumed 26 seconds of simulation time. Travel must have been nearly instant or the steps were completed without much movement. This suggests goTo reached its targets very quickly.\n\nThe drive target is at -260, 240 while the spawn is at 12, 55. That distance is huge. A sprint would take roughly 0.4 seconds. The test finished in 2.5 seconds total. This suggests either the step runs far faster than 1.6 milliseconds, or the drive step completed instantly. The feet() function might be wrong.\n\nHeadless execution without rendering explains the 2.5-second total. The world steps very fast when idle, so m1 travel completed successfully and the player reached the clinic report. The only remaining failure is KeyE not reporting, which points to the map staying up. In m0, tapping KeyM sets map.up true and nothing closes it, so m1's KeyE branch correctly triggers.\n\nI will fix the test and proactively address the burn radius issue because the road has no fuel. The charge plant and tube are unnecessary if the tractor logic works. I need to verify that steering works after entering the truck, since goTo sets both camera yaw and car yaw. Repair resets vehicle health to zero and exits the vehicle, but only m1 has a drive step; the other missions use goto.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-1ece9386-dd36-424d-bdd2-14affec309f4-42","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"onDeath|blocksSim","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2129,"output_tokens":1629,"cache_read_input_tokens":90112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3e093b06-f2d9-498d-bec9-1381f033c16c"}
