{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4b1f5908-9088-4f4d-b67c-03ead1b298d3-70","content":"{\"type\":\"TaskOutput\",\"Result\":{\"task_id\":\"e88fe99a-e73c-4080-af03-dcbc4b4e0070\",\"command\":\"cd \\\"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\\\" && node tests/run.mjs --only \\\"story\\\"\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"exit_code\":1,\"started\":\"2026-11-05T09:55:31Z\",\"ended\":\"2026-11-05T09:55:33Z\",\"duration_secs\":2.294567142,\"output\":\"mission m0\\nmission m1\\nFAIL story both endings\\nError: m1 stuck on jam CLEAR THE JAM at -204,49\\n    at playMission (file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:229:13)\\n    at Object.fn (file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:492:27)\\n    at async file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:625:5\\npassed 0 failed 1\\n\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-28becd78-8186-4fd7-9d1f-89a3b0725ae8-69.log\",\"truncated\":false,\"truncation_hint\":\"[truncated - use read_file on output_file for full content]\",\"raw_output_bytes\":689}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3a6ba7ef-4b9e-4e06-a89e-d878bf35b850"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_224","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The goTo early exit broke m1.\n\nThe robot reached the goto target but jam failed. Previously jam worked at this location. The cause of the regression is unclear.\n\nThe jam handler requires five shots and a reload. The robot may be in town, which would prevent firing.\n\nThe robot is not in town. The weapon is not a tractor. Sprint may be sticky and blocking shots.\n\nSprint is not sticky. The jam script is set correctly. Six reload taps should clear the jam. The goTo early-exit bug is unlikely to be the cause.\n\nThe gun is fresh, so leftover shots from a previous mission are not the cause. The robot can shoot from the vehicle, and the goTo early exit logic appears correct.\n\nThe robot likely completed goto at the edge of the 20-meter radius. The jam position is still inside that boundary, so the early exit should not have caused the failure.\n\nThe error message confirms the tractor was selected and firing began. The jam step only completes once the weapon is fully unjammed and five shots have been fired. The reload taps failed to clear the jam condition.\n\nReload and use are separate keys, so the reload tap should register. Lines blocking is not the cause. The gun did not break from wear during holdFire; 12 shots produced only 4.2 wear on a condition of 40. The jam script triggers on shot five.\n\nA new theory is that the robot died during the early-exit goto. If it died, onDeath freezes the game with timeScale zero. The engine then skips fixedUpdate, so tryReload never runs and the jam step never completes. This would explain why the robot is stuck at the jam site.\n\nA new theory is that goTo captures the drive step object at the start. If the robot passes through the goto target's radius before reaching the drive target, the early exit would trigger on the wrong step.\n\nThe goTo early-exit theory was wrong. The robot correctly stops at the drive target, then proceeds to goto and jam. The jam failure must have a different cause.\n\nThe jam script logic was verified. The jam step sets `jamScript` to 5, and the gun fires handler checks `shots >= 5` before applying the jam condition. This confirms the jam should trigger on the fifth shot.\n\nThe robot is not sprinting during goTo. The jam position is not inside town. If the robot died during the walk, tickPlayer would return early and arm() would throw a weapon selection error instead of firing.\n\nThe robot may already be dead. If it died during the early-exit goto, its weapon slot would still hold the tractor from the previous giveGun call. arm() would succeed because the weapon is already selected, but holdFire and reloads would do nothing while the game is frozen. This explains the jam failure. The earlier version likely survived because the extra walking allowed the player to reach the center before dying.\n\nThe death theory was rejected because the robot previously completed this jam successfully. The early-exit logic is not the cause; release() clears keys and steps one frame correctly. A new devastating bug in goTo for drive steps was discovered.\n\nThe drive-to-goto transition was traced. The mission index changes correctly between the two steps, so the loop logic is sound.\n\nThe sprint theory was ruled out because release() clears the key on both success paths. A weapon slot reset to the cane would cause arm() to throw, so that is unlikely. Map visibility does not block firing; it only blocks waypoint use.\n\nKeyR is not consumed by any other input handler, so the reload key should register normally even with the map open. The map is already closed after mission zero.\n\nThe jam completion logic was verified: once reload clears the jam, the shot count remains at or above five, so the step should finish. The remaining puzzle is why the robot never fired five shots. An accidental entry into the vehicle via KeyE is now being considered as a possible cause.\n\nI will add temporary debug logging inside the jam handler to inspect weapon state, shot count, health, and mode. This should reveal why the robot never fired five shots.\n\nThe tractor's condition is 45, and the story uses a 0.35 wear rate. Firing 80 shots of holdFire at 9 per second should only reduce condition to about 41. The gun should not break from wear alone. The magazine holds 30 rounds, so an empty magazine is not the cause either.\n\nThe robot may be passing within the 20-meter goto radius while still driving toward the drive target. If goTo exits early on that proximity, the drive step would complete before the robot reaches the actual destination.\n\nThe goto target at (-200, 30) is about 140 meters from the drive path, so the early-exit theory was wrong. The robot reaches the jam position at (-204, 49) and fails there.\n\nA new theory is that `release()` does not clear the button state, so a leftover fire press from a previous test could block firing. This would prevent the robot from ever reaching the required five shots to clear the jam.\n\nrelease() does clear buttons, so a leftover fire press cannot block firing. The jam script is set to five only when the jam step begins, not before.\n\nThe jam step never calls goTo, so an early-return on the jam step is impossible. Sprint is not triggered by KeyW alone; shift is required. The tractor is fully automatic, so holdFire should fire continuously. I will add debug logging and re-read the combat and fireGun jam code to find the exact failure point.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-450843e0-04c3-46a3-93bb-36ec42063a13-71","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\n      arm('tractor');\n      holdFire(80);\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');","new_string":"    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\n      arm('tractor');\n      holdFire(80);\n      const g = w.weapon;\n      console.log('jam', JSON.stringify({ id: g?.id, shots: g?.shots, jammed: g?.jammed, jamLeft: g?.jamLeft, cond: g?.cond, mag: g?.mag, hp: w.hp, dead: w.dead, mode: game.mode, sprint: w.sprint, veh: w.inVehicle, town: w.inTown(w.feet().x, w.feet().z) }));\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":616,"output_tokens":4272,"cache_read_input_tokens":120832,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"0c15a9b6-dd2b-49b5-95ba-f4e5c668fbee"}
