{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_226","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Jammed state: 4 shots fired, jammed, 4 left.\n\nThe gun jammed at shot 4, not 5. This suggests a random jam triggered instead of the scripted one. After reloading, shots remain at 4 and the jam clears, so completion is impossible.\n\nThe test reloads six times after the log, which clears the jam but leaves shots at 4. Completion requires 5 shots, so the step never finishes. The jam probability formula is being checked to explain why it triggered at shot 4 instead of 5.\n\nThe jam probability at 45% condition is roughly 3.6% per shot, so an early jam was purely a random occurrence. The test must loop: fire until the gun jams or reaches five shots, reload to clear the jam, then repeat until completion.\n\nThe test script already loops through twelve reload attempts while the step remains 'jam'. Each reload tap only reduces jamLeft by one, so multiple presses are required to fully clear a jam.\n\nTwenty reload cycles are more than enough to clear the jam. After clearing, the gun still needs one more shot to reach five, and the random jam zeroed out the scripted jam timer, so another random jam is possible.\n\nThe completion check is trapped inside the reload branch. If a random jam clears the gun before five shots, the script fires the fifth shot unjammed and the step never finishes. This is a game bug.\n\nThe fix is to prevent random jams from consuming the scripted jam timer. Only the scripted jam should zero out jamScript, so the completion check can run after clearing a random jam.\n\nThe completion check should run after both firing and reloading. The step finishes when shots reach five and the gun is unjammed. If a random jam occurs first, the scripted jam at shot five must still trigger so the player can clear it.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-434918bb-542b-467b-affb-d95626fdb4bc-73","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","old_string":"    const script = this.jamScript && gun.shots >= this.jamScript;\n    if (script || this.rng.next() < jamP) {\n      gun.jammed = true;\n      gun.jamLeft = 2 + Math.floor(this.rng.next() * 3);\n      this.jamScript = 0;\n    }","new_string":"    const script = this.jamScript && gun.shots >= this.jamScript;\n    if (script || this.rng.next() < jamP) {\n      gun.jammed = true;\n      gun.jamLeft = 2 + Math.floor(this.rng.next() * 3);\n      if (script) this.jamScript = 0;\n    }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-434918bb-542b-467b-affb-d95626fdb4bc-74","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\n      arm('tractor');\n      holdFire(80);\n      const g = w.weapon;\n      console.log('jam', JSON.stringify({ id: g?.id, shots: g?.shots, jammed: g?.jammed, jamLeft: g?.jamLeft, cond: g?.cond, mag: g?.mag, hp: w.hp, dead: w.dead, mode: game.mode, sprint: w.sprint, veh: w.inVehicle, town: w.inTown(w.feet().x, w.feet().z) }));\n      for (let n = 0; n < 6 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) tap('KeyR');","new_string":"    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\n      arm('tractor');\n      for (let n = 0; n < 24 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) {\n        if (w.weapon?.jammed) tap('KeyR');\n        else holdFire(15);\n      }"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":573,"output_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":125696,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"61ecae60-cbd6-4a24-9d55-64d534d70fa5"}
