{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_238","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug is that showEnding sets the mode to 'ending' when the mission ends.\n\nThe mouse button from the flare click lingers into the next frame. hover() sees it as a button-down event and activates the quit menu item. toTitle() then clears the ending state, so the test's click dismisses the ending card immediately.\n\nThe test cannot simply release the mouse button before stepping. The mission completes during the same frame that fires the flare, so the button-down event is still present when hover runs.\n\nThe proper fix is in the game code. The ending card should not be dismissed by the same input that ended the mission. A latch could ignore menu activation for a short time after the screen appears.\n\nThe simplest fix is to ignore menu activation for the frame the ending appears and while a button is held from before the screen change. This prevents the lingering mouse click from instantly dismissing the ending card.\n\nThe fix is a `menuArm` timer set to 0.45 seconds in `showEnding`. It will be decremented each frame and checked in `menuInput` and `hover` to ignore menu activation while the ending screen is active. This prevents the lingering mouse click from instantly dismissing the card.\n\nThe `menuArm` timer is also set in `onDeath()` for gameover screens. `update()` decrements it each frame by `dt`. `menuInput()` only activates items when the timer is not active. The test's extra 20 frames after the flare fire fall within the 0.45-second lock, so the ending card will stay visible.\n\nThe 0.5-second lock is sufficient. The test's extra frames plus the release step total about 0.38 seconds, which fits comfortably inside the window. This keeps the ending state readable for the test while still preventing accidental dismissal. The burn loop in playMission also runs menuInput during its steps, so the lock will block those as well.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf7cceb4-c96c-4cce-81e1-2e54152acedb-88","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js","old_string":"    this.ending = which === 'walk' ? 'walk' : 'give';\n    this.mode = 'ending';\n    this.screen = 'ending';\n    this.world.subtitle = this.ending === 'walk' ? 'YOU WALKED OUT WITH THE SHEET.' : 'YOU GAVE THEM THE SHEET.';","new_string":"    this.ending = which === 'walk' ? 'walk' : 'give';\n    this.mode = 'ending';\n    this.screen = 'ending';\n    this.menuArm = 0.6;\n    this.world.subtitle = this.ending === 'walk' ? 'YOU WALKED OUT WITH THE SHEET.' : 'YOU GAVE THEM THE SHEET.';"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf7cceb4-c96c-4cce-81e1-2e54152acedb-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js","old_string":"  onDeath() {\n    this.mode = 'gameover';\n    this.screen = 'gameover';\n    if (this.ctx?.engine) this.ctx.engine.timeScale = 0;\n  }","new_string":"  onDeath() {\n    this.mode = 'gameover';\n    this.screen = 'gameover';\n    this.menuArm = 0.6;\n    if (this.ctx?.engine) this.ctx.engine.timeScale = 0;\n  }"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf7cceb4-c96c-4cce-81e1-2e54152acedb-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js","old_string":"    this.trackIdle(ctx, dt);","new_string":"    if (this.menuArm > 0) this.menuArm = Math.max(0, this.menuArm - dt);\n    this.trackIdle(ctx, dt);"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bf7cceb4-c96c-4cce-81e1-2e54152acedb-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__