,82,79,71,82,69,83,83,46,109,100,96,46,10,52,52,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,70,105,110,105,115,104,32,67,97,115,104,32,82,117,110,32,40,104,111,115,116,44,32,99,108,105,101,110,116,44,32,115,111,108,111,32,98,111,116,115,44,32,99,97,114,100,32,108,105,115,116,101,110,101,114,115,41,46,32,82,101,45,114,117,110,32,96,110,111,100,101,32,116,101,115,116,115,47,114,117,110,46,109,106,115,32,45,45,97,108,108,96,44,32,116,104,101,32,116,119,111,32,96,102,105,108,101,58,47,47,96,32,108,97,117,110,99,104,101,115,44,32,116,104,101,32,112,104,111,110,101,45,112,114,111,102,105,108,101,32,99,104,101,99,107,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,102,111,117,114,32,104,117,98,32,115,99,101,110,97,114,105,111,115,46,32,87,114,105,116,101,32,96,101,120,105,116,45,105,110,116,101,114,118,105,101,119,46,106,115,111,110,96,32,97,110,100,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,32,96,80,82,79,71,82,69,83,83,46,109,100,96,44,32,105,110,99,108,117,100,105,110,103,32,97,110,121,32,194,167,50,54,32,99,117,116,115,46,10,52,54,58,35,35,32,82,105,115,107,115,32,47,32,67,111,110,116,114,97,100,105,99,116,105,111,110,115,10,53,50,58,45,32,69,115,99,32,117,110,100,101,114,32,112,111,105,110,116,101,114,32,108,111,99,107,32,109,97,121,32,110,101,118,101,114,32,97,114,114,105,118,101,32,97,115,32,97,32,107,101,121,44,32,97,110,100,32,96,114,101,113,117,101,115,116,80,111,105,110,116,101,114,76,111,99,107,40,41,96,32,99,97,110,32,114,101,106,101,99,116,46,32,70,111,108,108,111,119,32,116,104,101,32,194,167,51,32,104,97,110,100,108,105,110,103,32,111,114,32,116,104,101,32,104,117,98,32,99,104,101,99,107,32,99,97,110,32,102,97,105,108,32,111,110,32,97,110,32,117,110,104,97,110,100,108,101,100,32,114,101,106,101,99,116,105,111,110,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":20,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/goal/plan.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"## Goal kind\"},{\"line_number\":6,\"content\":\"## Acceptance criteria\"},{\"line_number\":7,\"content\":\"1. Title and hand-in. Fifty playful riffs on \\\"Far Cry 2\\\" are listed and one is chosen with a real random-number generator (not by hand). That exact string is the on-screen title, the HTML `<title>`, and `aiHub.name`. The folder that contains `STAGE.md` holds (a) one HTML file whose filename stem is `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917`, runnable from `file://` with nothing else required beside it, (b) `exit-interview.json` beside that HTML, one object in TASK.md's exact shape, every value filled, `usage` exactly `added on import`, \\\"unknown\\\" only where a fact cannot be confirmed, and (c) `PROGRESS.md`. All dev files live in a subfolder with that same stem. The shipped `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the kit zip and is never edited. About/Credits, reachable from the main menu and from pause, shows every TASK.md Source Information field (Date `2026-11-05 01:39:17`, Source `Far Cry 2`, Plan `PLAN.md`, genre, perspective, tech, art, animation, audio, online, testing, [... truncated (1031 chars total)]\"},{\"line_number\":10,\"content\":\"4. 10-foot shell, attract, and dev mode. UI is drawn with the engine HUD in art pixels, not DOM. Prompts follow the last used device: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph setting, and keyboard/mouse glyphs. Mouse hover moves menu focus and a click activates; pad, keyboard, and mouse all operate the same menus. Pause sets time scale to 0. A touch-only device shows the exact notice `Controller or keyboard required` and one Settings control, with no on-screen touch controls, and attract is still allowed to start. With no input, attract starts only after 10 seconds on the title or main menu (not on Settings or About), loops without error, shows a demo tag, and any input returns to the screen it came from without writing a save. Pause opens Dev Mode (hidden in a hub session) with the live balance sliders in PLAN.md §17; moving a slider changes that system immediately; Reset restores every default.\"},{\"line_number\":11,\"content\":\"5. Session round. Cash Run is a round of 1 to 4 players, about 6 minutes: carry stone cases to an extraction truck, friendly fire on, downed players can be revived or looted. The same round runs with no hub as solo play against hired-gun AI, and a normal boot with no session still reaches the title. Boot follows PLAN.md §19: hub connect, a headless server advanced on a timer rather than the render loop, ready signaled with no key press, and the card answering Enter and M from a window keydown listener. All four harness scenarios in PLAN.md §24 pass on the built file. If shared-world cannot be made stable, ship ghost, then parallel, only after that, with session meta tags matching the mode actually shipped, and the four scenarios still pass. Same-computer two-window link is required unless it is the §26 cut.\"},{\"line_number\":13,\"content\":\"## Verification plan\"},{\"line_number\":17,\"content\":\"4. gating: Copy the built HTML beside the hub harness files, serve that directory with `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page title is the chosen game title, then run the four PLAN.md §24 scenarios one at a time. Pass only when each reaches `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. Capture `{SCRATCH}/hub.log`, including any failed `__hubCheck.checks`. Stop only that server, by its PID. If same-computer link was not cut, also drive two `file://` pages through one shared round to matching standings and a shared fire or case, logged in `{SCRATCH}/link.log`. If link was cut, that log must show the feature is absent (no menu entry).\"},{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"5. evidence: After the game has been rendering for at least 10 seconds, save the PLAN.md §24 screenshots under `{SCRATCH}/shots/`. Parse `exit-interview.json` and confirm the key shape. Screenshot absence or a blank WebGPU frame does not fail the goal once steps 1–4 hold.\"},{\"line_number\":20,\"content\":\"## Non-goals\"},{\"line_number\":27,\"content\":\"## Assumed scope\"},{\"line_number\":28,\"content\":\"- Work folder root (beside `STAGE.md`, `PLAN.md`, `TASK.md`): the single HTML deliverable, `exit-interview.json`, `PROGRESS.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":29,\"content\":\"- Dev subfolder `{GameTitle}-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917`: unzipped riftlight pixel-engine kit (latest release zip), unmodified AI Hub `session.js` plus the hub harness used only for tests, game sources, art and animation data, generated audio, `node tests/run.mjs`, and the esbuild single-file packager.\"},{\"line_number\":33,\"content\":\"## Implementation approach\"},{\"line_number\":34,\"content\":\"Follow PLAN.md §25 in order and §26 when cutting. Keep this as guidance, not a file-layout contract. Separate simulation data from meshes so headless tests never need a GPU. Put missions, weapons, sites, dialogue, tuning defaults, and model defs in plain data. Gameplay reads named actions, not raw keys. Simulate in the fixed step and draw in the frame update. Read tuning values at the moment of use. One game object owns the world; title, attract, campaign, and the round are modes, not a fresh terrain load. Guard every use of `window`, `document`, `navigator`, and `localStorage`. Randomness comes from the engine's seeded generator, forked by name. Build the single HTML the way PLAN.md §23 specifies (session script first, then hub meta tags, then the bundled module) so `file://` boots. Keep the four hub scenarios passing from the first bootable build. Log defects in the dev folder's issues note as tests catch them. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each step so a compacted context can resume.\"},{\"line_number\":36,\"content\":\"## Task checklist\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"- [ ] List 50 titles, pick one with a real RNG, record the list and the pick, create the dev subfolder, unzip the kit, vendor the hub client and harness, and prove `pixel-engine.js` matches the zip.\"},{\"line_number\":38,\"content\":\"- [ ] Scaffold the single-file build and a booting game so `file://` opens and all four hub scenarios pass. Start `PROGRESS.md`.\"},{\"line_number\":44,\"content\":\"- [ ] Finish Cash Run (host, client, solo bots, card listeners). Re-run `node tests/run.mjs --all`, the two `file://` launches, the phone-profile check, and the four hub scenarios. Write `exit-interview.json` and finish `PROGRESS.md`, including any §26 cuts.\"},{\"line_number\":46,\"content\":\"## Risks / Contradictions\"},{\"line_number\":52,\"content\":\"- Esc under pointer lock may never arrive as a key, and `requestPointerLock()` can reject. Follow the §3 handling or the hub check can fail on an unhandled rejection.\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f73a4be0-5e24-4899-ab3c-b4634bc1720a"}
