{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_260","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A timeScale of 0 causes clock.delta to return 0.\n\nframeStep passes 0 to advance, which calls physics.update with dt=0. The accumulator skips the fixed step, so the clock stays frozen during those 30 steps. The pause key press still advances the clock by DT on that frame because timeScale remains 1 during fixedUpdate. tap() also performs a second step when the key is released.\n\nThe test assertion was wrong. After the Escape press, the clock advances by one frame of DT. The next 30 steps with timeScale at zero add nothing. The corrected test checks that the clock stays unchanged after those 30 steps.\n\nAnother approach is to check for the Escape key at the start of fixed() before the clock advances. This would freeze the pause frame itself and prevent a bullet from firing on that frame. Input is already delivered by then, and playChrome lives in update rather than fixed.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-abc0bd70-1dc2-4655-8edb-ca00eac8af09-118","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"openPause\\(","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":610,"output_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":171264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"81e2ef2b-1eb8-4424-9a80-4f42c6ed198b"}
