{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-18178f84-377e-4d06-ab1b-be036fc24b28-128","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script src=\\\"vendor/session.js\\\"></script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n10→<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>A Cry Too Far</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"src/main.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n20→</html>\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script src=\\\"vendor/session.js\\\"></script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n10→<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>A Cry Too Far</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"src/main.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n20→</html>\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/index.html\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head>\\n<meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\">\\n<script src=\\\"vendor/session.js\\\"></script>\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session\\\" content=\\\"1\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-players\\\" content=\\\"1-4\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-mode\\\" content=\\\"shared-world\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-minutes\\\" content=\\\"6\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:webgpu\\\" content=\\\"required\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-goal\\\" content=\\\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"hub:session-howto\\\" content=\\\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\\\">\\n<meta name=\\\"viewport\\\" content=\\\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\\\">\\n<title>A Cry Too Far</title>\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n<div id=\\\"app\\\"></div>\\n<script type=\\\"module\\\" src=\\\"src/main.js\\\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\",\"total_lines\":20}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-18178f84-377e-4d06-ab1b-be036fc24b28-129","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"810→## 19. Multiplayer\\n\\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\\n\\n**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\\n\\n**The round, \\\"Cash Run\\\" (6 minutes):**\\n- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\\n- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\\n- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\\n820→- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\\n- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\\n- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\\n- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\\n\\n**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\\n\\n**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\\n```js\\nconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\\n830→if (info) {\\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\\n```\\nHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\\n\\n**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\\n840→- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\\n- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\\n- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\\n\\nThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\\n\\n**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\\n\\n| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n850→| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\\n| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\\n| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\\n| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\\n\\nThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\\n\\nClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\\n\\n**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\\n860→\\n**Round rules the harness checks:**\\n- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\\n- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\\n- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\\n- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\\n\\n**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\\n\\n**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\\n870→**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\\n\\n**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\\n\\n**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Art\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"810→## 19. Multiplayer\\n\\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\\n\\n**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\\n\\n**The round, \\\"Cash Run\\\" (6 minutes):**\\n- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\\n- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\\n- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\\n820→- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\\n- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\\n- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\\n- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\\n\\n**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\\n\\n**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\\n```js\\nconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\\n830→if (info) {\\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\\n```\\nHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\\n\\n**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\\n840→- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\\n- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\\n- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\\n\\nThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\\n\\n**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\\n\\n| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n850→| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\\n| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\\n| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\\n| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\\n\\nThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\\n\\nClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\\n\\n**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\\n860→\\n**Round rules the harness checks:**\\n- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\\n- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\\n- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\\n- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\\n\\n**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\\n\\n**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\\n870→**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\\n\\n**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\\n\\n**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Art\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":810,\"limit\":70,\"raw_output\":\"## 19. Multiplayer\\n\\nFollow the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (read `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md`; also the shared-world example `examples/arena.html` beside it). The hub runs invites, lobby, names, clock and results; the game runs the round. The same code also plays when the game is on its own.\\n\\n**Mode: `shared-world`, 1 to 4 players.** Four mercs in one burning valley, friends until the stones are counted.\\n\\n**The round, \\\"Cash Run\\\" (6 minutes):**\\n- The valley around the Cut: the campaign's terrain, with only the Cut, P5 and the Ranger Post live, 16 to 24 soldiers, wind and fire on.\\n- Six stone cases in guarded spots, shown by the tracker's beep and a marker when close. One extraction truck on the road south of the pit.\\n- Everyone starts at a different road end with `tractor` (cond 70), `flare`, `cane`, 2 syrettes, 2 bottles.\\n- Carry one case at a time (speed × 0.85, you can't sprint); walk it to the truck to bank its stones. Most stones wins.\\n- Down at 0 HP: you drop the case and bleed for 25 s. Another player can hold Use for 3 s to bring you up (+1 Revive) or just take the case. Bleed out and you return at your road end after 15 s. Friendly fire is on: that's the theme.\\n- On foot only, in rounds: no player vehicles.\\n- Ends when the time is up, or when all cases are banked or burned. Standings by stones, ties together.\\n\\n**Session head tags** go in the template (section 23): `hub:session` 1, `hub:session-players` `1-4`, `hub:session-mode` `shared-world`, `hub:session-minutes` `6`, `hub:webgpu` `required`, `hub:session-goal` *Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine*, `hub:session-howto` *Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck*.\\n\\n**Boot order** (`src/main.js`). This is the part that makes the hub work:\\n```js\\nconst info = (window.AIHub && AIHub.active) ? await AIHub.connect({ mode:'shared-world', seats:[1,4], card:true }) : null;\\nif (info) {\\n  const game = createGame({ session: hubSession(info) });        // mode 'round': no title, no menus, no attract\\n  if (info.server) { const e = await Engine.headless(game, {}); AIHub.ready(); setInterval(() => e.step(6, 1/60), 100); }\\n  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n  else await Engine.start(game, { ...OPTIONS, seed: info.seed });  // game.ready(ctx) calls AIHub.ready() once, with no key press\\n} else { /* normal start: touch check, title */ }\\n```\\nHandle a rejected `__PIXEL_READY__` by `AIHub.fail(message)`. If `connect` answers `null`, run as on your own.\\n\\n**`src/net/session.js`:** one interface, three implementations, so round code never knows which: `{ kind, me, players:[{id,name,color}], host, isHost, server, time(), rng(label), send(data,{to,reliable}), on(event,fn), ready(), answer(what), finish(outcome), fail(msg) }`.\\n- `hubSession` wraps `AIHub`.\\n- `soloSession` is **on its own**: host is you, the other seats are AI mercs (reuse the buddy brain: go to the nearest case, bank it, shoot what shoots you), with your own results screen at the end.\\n- `linkSession` is **on its own with a friend on the same computer**: `BroadcastChannel('game-link-v1')` between two windows. Host and Join on the Cash Run menu, a simple lobby, `start` carrying a `Date.now()` time base and a seed. It costs little, reuses everything, and is how two-window play gets tested.\\n\\nThe main menu's Cash Run offers: Solo with Hired Guns, Host on This Computer, Join on This Computer, plus one line saying friends online play through AI Hub.\\n\\n**Netcode.** The host runs the world. Each copy moves its own player from its own stick, at once, never waiting for the network, as `arena.html` does.\\n\\n| Message | Direction | Rate, kind | Content |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| `me` | client → host | 12/s, unreliable | seq, position, yaw, pitch, stance, weapon, hp echo |\\n| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\\n| `s` | host → all | 10/s, unreliable, under 1,100 bytes | time, players, soldiers (`[id,x,z,yaw,state,hp]`, ints, y from terrain), cases |\\n| `w` | host → all | up to 4/s, reliable, batched | fire cells ignited and burnt, damage per player, downs, deaths, explosions, banks, sounds |\\n\\nThat's at most 17 messages a second per copy; the limit is 20 with bursts of 40, and 16 KB per message. **Drive sends from `setInterval`, not the render loop:** on a software-rendered copy `update` runs about twice a second, and traffic must still flow.\\n\\nClients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\\n\\n**The server case.** `AIHub.server` true: run the same host code under `Engine.headless` with no player, camera, audio or HUD (`me` isn't in `players`). Don't touch `info.players[me]`.\\n\\n**Round rules the harness checks:**\\n- `time-up`: the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` **directly from the event handler**, within `graceMs` (5 s). Every present player appears once.\\n- `leave`: continue; the host finishes if nobody is left.\\n- `end`: no more input or sends, `audio.stopMusic()`, `audio.stopLoops()`, mute. The hub shows results.\\n- `stats` at most 6 names per player (Stones, Downs, Revives, Kills); `awards` up to 3 (*Last Friend* for most revives, *Paid in Full* for most stones, *Arsonist* for most cells lit).\\n\\n**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\\n\\n**The game's own card** (`card:true`). A shared-world card on your live scene with `GAME_TITLE`, the players in their seat colours with ready marks, how to win, this player's controls in their glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Ready: Enter, Cross, or a tap/click on Ready → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. More time: Triangle, key `M`, or tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. It has no menus, and play begins only at `start`.\\n**Listen for Enter and M with a plain `window` keydown listener** (verified to pass the harness's card check), because the harness expects an answer within 3 s and the render loop may be slow. Pad buttons can poll in `update`. Everything on the card uses `AIHub.rng('card')` for randomness. When `AIHub.time() >= 0` the round is on; show the 3-2-1 countdown before that.\\n\\n**Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\\n\\n**Test it:** section 24, all four harness scenarios, and two windows on `linkSession`, plus the game outside a session.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 20. Art\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-18178f84-377e-4d06-ab1b-be036fc24b28-130","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"da5eabd0-060d-4be2-ae4a-40a4eaa62daf\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-18178f84-377e-4d06-ab1b-be036fc24b28-130.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"cd \\\"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\\\" && node tests/run.mjs --all\",\"summary\":\"Background task da5eabd0-060d-4be2-ae4a-40a4eaa62daf started\",\"retrieval_hint\":\"Use get_command_or_subagent_output with task_ids=[\\\"da5eabd0-060d-4be2-ae4a-40a4eaa62daf\\\"] when you need the output.\",\"pid\":466696}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ee17a981-98c3-44e1-903d-2ec10f279a07"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_269","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub goal text mentions \"diamond cases,\" which is a bit Far Cry-ish but is in the plan.\n\nI'll verify main.js and about.js while tests run. I'll check whether examples/ and packs/ are still imported so they can be deleted. The session channel name also needs checking against the plan.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beb53329-ea52-4134-84cc-9706e47dcc3e-131","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/main.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beb53329-ea52-4134-84cc-9706e47dcc3e-132","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/about.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-beb53329-ea52-4134-84cc-9706e47dcc3e-133","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["da5eabd0-060d-4be2-ae4a-40a4eaa62daf"],"timeout_ms":90000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3098,"output_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":182016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"77298f8e-5d82-4dfd-bf37-3278a174c099"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-beb53329-ea52-4134-84cc-9706e47dcc3e-131","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n10→  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n20→  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n30→\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n40→    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n50→    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n60→    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n10→  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n20→  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n30→\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n40→    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n50→    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n60→    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/main.js\",\"offset\":null,\"raw_output\":\"import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-beb53329-ea52-4134-84cc-9706e47dcc3e-132","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** About pages. The HUD draws these uppercase. The usage line stays exact. */\\n\\nexport const USAGE = 'added on import';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_PAGES = [\\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', 'Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Source: Far Cry 2', 'Plan: PLAN.md'],\\n  ['GENRE AND PERSPECTIVE', 'Genre: first-person shooter', 'Perspective: first person on foot,', 'at the wheel, and in story scenes'],\\n  ['TECH', 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0', 'three.js r186', 'Rapier 0.20', 'esbuild 0.28.2', 'Original sim, fire grid, weapons, missions'],\\n  ['ART DIRECTION', 'Engine pixel-art toon, 480x270', 'Sand, orange and red land', 'Slate Concord, orange Harvest', 'Green only for water and regrowth'],\\n10→  ['ANIMATION', 'Engine clips on the soldier rig', 'First-person hands on a small rig', 'Mixer poses for reload, map, surgery'],\\n  ['AUDIO', 'Code songs, code effects, no files', 'Animalese voices', 'Music starts at 10 percent'],\\n  ['ONLINE', 'AI Hub shared-world, 1-4 players', 'Cash Run, 6 minutes', 'Same-computer link on a BroadcastChannel'],\\n  ['TESTING', 'node tests/run.mjs --all', 'Headless Engine.step playthrough', 'Playwright Chromium, WebGPU flags', 'Hub harness, four scenarios'],\\n  ['RESEARCH', 'Mechanics from the plan, not a port', 'No source maps, names, or plot'],\\n  ['ENVIRONMENT', 'Grok CLI, headless', 'Linux'],\\n  ['MODEL', 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh'],\\n  ['USAGE', USAGE],\\n];\\n\\n20→export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', 'How many issues did testing catch?', 'See the count written after the run.', 'The number is filled in ISSUES and here.'],\\n  ['CRITICAL ISSUES', 'How many would be game breaking?', 'Filled after the run.'],\\n  ['MOST HELPFUL TEST', 'The headless mission playthrough.', 'It drives the shipped actions.'],\\n  ['LEAST HELPFUL TEST', 'A blank WebGPU screenshot.', 'State checks told the truth.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels,', 'and a vehicle that stays upright.'],\\n  ['STUCK OR GUESSED', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z.', 'The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z.', 'Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.'],\\n30→  ['BUILT YOURSELF', 'What did you build yourself?', 'The fire grid, jams, fever, map,', 'mission runner, and the hub round.'],\\n  ['HARDEST ENGINE PART', 'Pointer lock, timeScale pause,', 'and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.'],\\n  ['CHANGED IN THE ENGINE', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.'],\\n  ['ONE CHANGE', 'If you could change one thing?', 'A first-person rig that does not', 'steal the use key or the pointer.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'The plan names the traps and the', 'order to cut whole features.'],\\n  ['CONFUSING', 'What was confusing?', 'File stem spaces, and which card', 'the harness presses Enter on.'],\\n  ['HARDEST', 'What was the hardest thing?', 'One world that is a campaign,', 'a 6 minute round, and a hub server.'],\\n40→  ['CHANGE THE PROMPT', 'What would you change?', 'Ship the hub check before asking', 'for every prop in the art list.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const CREDIT_PAGES = [\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'three.js, MIT', 'Rapier, Apache-2.0', 'AI Hub session client'],\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated'],\\n];\\n\\nexport function aboutPages() {\\n  return [...SOURCE_PAGES, ...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK, ...CREDIT_PAGES];\\n50→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** About pages. The HUD draws these uppercase. The usage line stays exact. */\\n\\nexport const USAGE = 'added on import';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_PAGES = [\\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', 'Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Source: Far Cry 2', 'Plan: PLAN.md'],\\n  ['GENRE AND PERSPECTIVE', 'Genre: first-person shooter', 'Perspective: first person on foot,', 'at the wheel, and in story scenes'],\\n  ['TECH', 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0', 'three.js r186', 'Rapier 0.20', 'esbuild 0.28.2', 'Original sim, fire grid, weapons, missions'],\\n  ['ART DIRECTION', 'Engine pixel-art toon, 480x270', 'Sand, orange and red land', 'Slate Concord, orange Harvest', 'Green only for water and regrowth'],\\n10→  ['ANIMATION', 'Engine clips on the soldier rig', 'First-person hands on a small rig', 'Mixer poses for reload, map, surgery'],\\n  ['AUDIO', 'Code songs, code effects, no files', 'Animalese voices', 'Music starts at 10 percent'],\\n  ['ONLINE', 'AI Hub shared-world, 1-4 players'