{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_270","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The full test suite shares one engine. Earlier tests leave the world in a bad state.\n\nThe runner reuses one engine via boot(), so later tests inherit leftover state. Locomotion fails with run distance 8.34 m, likely from an unreset playerSpeed slider. Map, story, solo, and menus also fail.\n\nThe 8.34 m run distance equals roughly 8.34 m/s, which exceeds both sprint and normal run speeds. This suggests the previous test may have left a speed buff active, or the player was stuck in a vehicle.\n\nThe locomotion test itself might be calling release(). The fire and title tests are unlikely to have altered player speed. The 8.34 m result may reflect a vehicle or pre-existing movement rather than a true run.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bfd22295-d1fd-4010-9a14-99fcc051e600-134","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":300,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3761,"output_tokens":597,"cache_read_input_tokens":185088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ca38d9c8-275b-489f-97aa-31d40a7689ef"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-bfd22295-d1fd-4010-9a14-99fcc051e600-134","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"300→  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n310→  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n320→    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n330→  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\n340→test('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n350→  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n360→  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n370→  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  w.lines = [];\",\"content_concise\":\"300→  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n310→  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n320→    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n330→  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\n340→test('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n350→  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n360→  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n370→  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  w.lines = [];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":300,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n\",\"total_lines\":634}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"0b4c1b71-e9af-4941-a72b-08e334025227"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_271","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Run 8.34 is faster than a 5.4 m/s walk.\n\nThe m7 start might leave the player in a vehicle from a prior state. The sprint test does not enter a vehicle. The world boots with inVehicle false unless something else set it. If the player is in a vehicle and KeyW drives, the car yaw may be PI. This would make the car drive along the -Z axis, matching the measurement direction.\n\nThe m7 setup never calls ensureTruck, so the player should not be in a vehicle. The 8.34 m/s speed is plausible for a truck starting to move. The remaining question is whether the boot or title state left the player in a vehicle, or if leftover velocity from the fire test carried over.\n\nStuck keys are unlikely because release() clears them at the start of locomotion. A stuck key would still only produce ~5.4 m/s, which is too slow for 8.34 m/s. The TUNING.playerSpeed value may have been mutated by a previous test; if it were 1.54, that would explain the higher speed.\n\nA steep downhill slope at the m7 spawn could explain the extra speed. The terrain there may be steep enough to let the controller slide, adding roughly 54% beyond normal walking. The fire test ran for 16 seconds before this run, which might have altered the terrain or physics state.\n\nThe fire test never presses keys, so it cannot leave stuck input. It also nulls the wind pin at the end, ruling out lingering wind effects. The 16-second run was purely idle standing. When this test runs alone, startMission originates from title mode; when it follows fire, it originates from play mode with accumulated state. applySetup resets health, weapons, and position, but the prior physics and controller state may still carry over.\n\napplySetup does not reset crouch, sprint, inVehicle, or hero velocity. The prior 16-second fire test is now suspected of leaving lingering physics state that inflates the speed measurement. The title test is also being examined for key presses or stepping that could affect the result.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-21ce9e54-3001-4681-b434-5bb24cc98b9f-135","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":245,"limit":55}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1694,"output_tokens":1495,"cache_read_input_tokens":188800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"8a0edfae-6286-4c90-9636-b1e496ec55fd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-21ce9e54-3001-4681-b434-5bb24cc98b9f-135","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"245→test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n250→  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n260→  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n270→    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n280→\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n290→  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\",\"content_concise\":\"245→test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n250→  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n260→  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n270→    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n280→\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n290→  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":245,\"limit\":55,\"raw_output\":\"test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n\",\"total_lines\":634}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"40609223-923d-495a-acaa-f358152893a1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_272","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The fire test runs for 16 seconds while the player is on the title screen.\n\nThe player stays still during the fire test because blocksSim returns before tickPlayer. The 8.34 meter movement in the first 60 frames of KeyW is unexplained; wading and fever are ruled out. I will add a settle, force on-foot mode, and more logging.\n\nA fresh engine per test would prevent cross-talk but costs roughly nine seconds. Reusing one engine and resetting state at the start of each test is preferable to avoid physics and WASM memory leaks.\n\nThe boot function now resets the game to title mode and clears dynamic world state. I am checking whether resetDynamic can be called twice without duplicating props.\n\nresetDynamic clears props before repopulating them, so duplicate props are avoided. Resetting the game at the start of every test is safe because later tests call startMission immediately after boot. The failures in later tests stem from earlier tests leaving stale state: mission data, vehicle status, map settings, sliders, timeScale, story mode, menu arms, dead buddies, and active rounds.\n\nThe attract menu fails because stale input lingers between tests. Keys or mouse buttons from earlier tests remain pressed, so freshInput stays true and resets the attract idle timer before it can start. release() is not called at the end of every test, and exceptions can leave inputs stuck.\n\nThe locomotion test releases its key before throwing, so stale input is not the cause of the shared-engine failure. The 8.34 meter run on a reused engine is still unexplained; it should be roughly 4–7 meters after a fresh boot. I will reproduce just the fire and locomotion tests to isolate the issue.\n\nThe 8.34 meter run may be caused by physics stepping the character during the fire test's 16 seconds of title simulation. The engine's physics.update calls fixedStep even when blocksSim returns early from fixed, so the character controller could still move despite tickPlayer being skipped.\n\nRapier simulates all bodies every physics step even when blocksSim skips tickPlayer. The hero may slide down a slope during the fire test and accumulate velocity. Teleport resets position but not velocity, so that residual speed persists into the next test and explains the 8.34 meter run.\n\nThe 8.34 meter run is caused by leftover velocity persisting after teleport. The engine's teleport function resets position but not the character's physics velocity, so the capsule keeps sliding. I will zero velocity after teleport to fix this and match correct gameplay behavior.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-32addbe2-179b-4521-8f74-4d34ea866449-136","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\" && node --input-type=module -e '\nimport { readFileSync } from \"fs\";\nconst s = readFileSync(\"pixel-engine.js\",\"utf8\");\nconst key = \"teleport(e)\";\nlet idx = 4500000, n = 0;\nwhile ((idx = s.indexOf(\"teleport(\", idx)) !== -1 && idx < 4800000 && n < 8) {\n  console.log(\"\\n\", idx, s.slice(idx, idx+350).replace(/\\n/g,\" \"));\n  idx += 9; n++;\n}\n'","description":"Find character teleport and velocity reset"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2341,"output_tokens":1393,"cache_read_input_tokens":190464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e6077faa-a26a-4994-bf1d-4dea6120fb2b"}
