{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_293","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The map test runs before the story and includes sliders for playerDamageTaken and fireDamage at maximum.\n\nChecking whether resetSliders properly restores defaults. The map test passed in the last run and calls resetSliders at the end, so leftover slider state is unlikely to be causing the story failure. TUNING is a shared mutable object, but that probably isn't the root cause either.\n\nChecking m0-m7 for dead players, zero timeScale, blocked lines, or open choices. A full diagnostic script is too much code. I'll add temporary console.log to the playMission hold branch and run --only story.\n\nThe hold step logic checks player distance and increments a timer. The hero is inside the radius, so the timer should tick. The focus is now on why dt might be zero.\n\nA stuck Escape key could be forcing timeScale to zero. release() does not clear Escape, so a previous test might have left it pressed. The pause test runs after the story, so it is not the source. I will grep for KeyEscape presses in earlier tests.\n\nRelease() clears KeyE at the start of the hold step, so a stuck Escape key is unlikely. The engine.timeScale setter appears correct. A new possibility is that fixedUpdate receives scaled dt, and the engine's fixed step accumulator might behave badly when simulating many frames in a single step.\n\nThe hold step simulates 7230 frames. A stuck blocksSim flag would prevent tickMission from running even with positive dt. Mode changes like gameover, ending, pause, or session end could trigger this. A leftover session from an earlier test is unlikely because solo runs after the story.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bdb73028-63b3-4b09-ad20-0154e3c1dbad-28","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"playChrome|openPause|Escape","glob":"**/{game.js,run.mjs}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__202611