{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_308","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The diagnosis is excellent. The m8 hold lasts 90 frames.\n\nThe hold only reached 4.77 seconds before death. The soldier's bullet damage is roughly 18 damage per second, which matches the expected rate of two shots per second at 9 damage each.\n\nThe m8 reached 82 HP after 1.5 seconds, then died at roughly 5.5 seconds. The buddy rescue logic should have triggered since Ines was alive, but the character died instead of being rescued.\n\nThe deadBuddies state from the guns test likely persists across setups. If Ines was killed there, she remains dead for m8 and cannot rescue. The m8 player then dies from soldier fire.\n\nThe guns test soldier is roughly 244 meters away, well beyond the 90-meter vision range, so it cannot see the player. The map test does not spawn soldiers either. The source of the shooting remains unclear unless the soldier moved closer or enemy vision was never reset.\n\nThe damage multiplier is at default, so enemy vision is not stuck at 200. The player is inside the town center radius of 70 meters, but m8 has truce disabled. Without a truce, inTown does not block hostility, meaning any enemy within 90 meters could attack.\n\nThe town center does not provide protection. The only soldier is the guns test ranger post unit, which is too far away to attack. Civilians are not hostile and cannot shoot. The next step is to check whether the guns test spawns additional soldiers that might have been teleported closer.\n\nThe placeFacing teleport might have moved the player rather than the soldier. The guns test only spawns soldiers through world and round functions, so no hidden units should exist. The ranger post soldier remains too far away to attack. The source of the shooting is still unknown.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-59d51f3e-0158-4d5a-96cc-386ef32a0422-47","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","offset":100,"limit":50}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-59d51f3e-0158-4d5a-96cc-386ef32a0422-48","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"do: 'clear'|spawnSoldier|posts","glob":"**/*.{js}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-59d51f3e-0158-4d5a-96cc-386ef32a0422-49","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":376,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":895,"output_tokens":1485,"cache_read_input_tokens":81792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"221a0f5b-b909-49be-ad25-c93e99942215"}
