120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,37,50,48,67,114,121,37,50,48,84,111,111,37,50,48,70,97,114,45,70,97,114,37,50,48,67,114,121,37,50,48,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,47,116,101,115,116,115,47,114,117,110,46,109,106,115,58,54,50,56,58,53,10,112,97,115,115,101,100,32,57,32,102,97,105,108,101,100,32,49,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 1\\nFAIL menus attract pause touch\\nError: attract did not start\\n    at assert (file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:27:20)\\n    at Object.fn (file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:562:3)\\n    at async file:///home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A%20Cry%20Too%20Far-Far%20Cry%202-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs:628:5\\npassed 9 failed 1\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"command\":\"cd \\\"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\\\" && node tests/run.mjs --all\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Re-run full headless acceptance suite\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-d33f02a2-14d4-415a-91d8-9672746cf0d8-63.log\",\"total_bytes\":648}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"063f92ca-8463-4c33-a61d-5ed16fefe647"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_316","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Story and solo tests passed. Menus attract failed.\n\nSolo leaves a session set. Menus attract fails because toTitle() clears it, but startSolo's session may re-bind or trackIdle may still see it.\n\nThe failure is \"attract did not start\". trackIdle should allow idle accumulation when session is null and screen is title. freshInput may be true every frame, keeping idle at zero.\n\nThe first assertion passes, so idle is stuck at zero. The solo test never calls release() at the end of playMission, leaving input held and freshInput always true.\n\nThe stuck input is likely KeyW from an earlier test. Story's goTo releases it on success, but solo never calls release(), so the key stays down and freshInput remains true.\n\nThe stuck input theory is being reconsidered. playMission ends with release(), so solo should not leave keys down. Headless mode does not update mouseDelta, but that alone would not explain the failure.\n\ntoTitle clears the session before the menus test begins. The test also explicitly sets mode and screen to title, so trackIdle should not return early for a missing screen.\n\nRuled out netTimer as the cause. startSolo does not call ready(), so no timer restarts the session after toTitle clears it. The real reason idle never reaches 10 is still unknown.\n\nA new theory emerged: toTitle resets session to null but leaves this.ended set to true from the prior session's onSessionEnd. trackIdle does not check the ended flag, so it may be blocking idle accumulation.\n\nThe ended flag theory was rejected because trackIdle still runs during update. The focus shifted to freshInput blocking idle accumulation. holdFire clears buttons, placeFacing does not hold keys, arm taps a digit, and release() clears ShiftLeft, so no obvious stuck input was found.\n\nA new theory emerged: the engine may not clear `buttonEvents` between frames. If a button-down event lingers after release, `freshInput` stays true every frame and idle never accumulates, which would explain why attract never starts.\n\nSolo calls startSolo() before the friendly-fire assertion, so it sets a session even when it fails. Previously, solo's early failure left that session behind, which broke attract. Now that solo passes, it leaves the same session intact, and toTitle may not be clearing it properly.\n\nThe third run actually passed menus, so the failure only appeared when solo completed successfully and left its session intact. Previously, solo failed before startSolo(), which is why the session was already cleared.\n\nSolo now succeeds by calling hurt(500) and time-up. This sets ended to true. toTitle resets timeScale but leaves ended as true. trackIdle does not check ended. The cause of the attract failure is still unknown.\n\nA new theory is that timeScale remains zero after onSessionEnd. If dt becomes zero, idle cannot accumulate and attract never starts. toTitle resets timeScale at the start of the next test, but its engine reference might be missing. I will read toTitle and onSessionEnd in the file.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-011059a7-6f85-4e4a-ad4e-0e9e6c22d825-64","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"this\\.ended|ended","glob":"**/game.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-011059a7-6f85-4e4a-ad4e-0e9e6c22d825-65","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js","offset":430,"limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-011059a7-6f85-4e4a-ad4e-0e9e6c22d825-66","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7