{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_322","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"After 601 steps, idle is 0.\n\nIdle accumulated to 0.45 on the title screen before the game froze at gameover with timeScale 0. The player died during that brief title-screen idle period. The simulation logic is being checked to see if world blocks still update while the mode is title.\n\nThe title-screen freeze is caused by tickBurn and tickActors running before the blocksSim check. Burn damage and soldier attacks still execute while mode is title. Cash-round soldiers and mercenaries are not removed when returning to title, so they continue attacking.\n\nThe mercs' attacks trigger hurt(), which calls down(). Because toTitle nullifies world.round and clears world.buddies, down() finds no buddy and the player dies. This kills the attract mode. The fix is to clear hostile actors in toTitle or block damage when not in play.\n\nThe blocksSim check should move earlier so combat and burn damage do not run off the play modes. Fire spread on the title is intentional, so fire.step must keep running.\n\nThe fix is to move the blocksSim check before tickBurn and tickActors, while keeping fire.step. This stops title-screen fire damage and soldier bullets without blocking fire spread. Need to check if attract mode still requires tickActors.\n\nAttract mode is not blocked by blocksSim, so tickActors must keep running there to let the bot shoot and show fire. Mercenaries are harmless in attract because god mode blocks their damage. applySetup filters them out when starting a mission, but toTitle does not remove them.\n\nThe fix is to filter actors in `toTitle()` so only civil kinds remain. This removes leftover mercenaries and soldiers from prior cash rounds before the player returns to the title screen.\n\nGuarding tickActors and tickBurn behind blocksSim is still needed to prevent the menu from dying. Clearing actors in toTitle is cleaner than relying solely on that guard, since leftover mercenaries could still attack the attract bot. The player may also be dead or down from the title-screen death.\n\nThe plan is to clear non-civil actors in `toTitle()` and revive the player, then guard `fixed()` so combat, burn, and fever skip when `blocksSim` is true while fire still spreads. Moving the `blocksSim` check earlier will also stop `tickFever` from running on the title screen, which is correct since no fever subtitle should appear during the menu.\n\nAttract mode is not blocked by blocksSim, so tickFever will keep running there. The attract beat 4 sets feverOn, and the player may collapse after 25 seconds of fever. This matches prior behavior and is acceptable because the test only checks for engine errors. Only title and other non-play modes will be protected from off-mode damage.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-9a72e1b8-5484-4b25-90d3-672878451e4d-74","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mode = 'dev'|screen = 'dev'","glob":"**/*.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":433,"output_tokens":1630,"cache_read_input_tokens":110464,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"5e733b2e-99e5-4301-9c88-a4880047550b"}
