,121,96,59,32,116,104,101,32,110,97,109,101,32,105,115,32,121,111,117,114,32,116,105,116,108,101,46,10,49,49,48,56,58,124,32,83,105,110,103,108,101,32,72,84,77,76,32,112,97,99,107,97,103,101,44,32,67,68,78,32,97,108,108,111,119,97,110,99,101,44,32,98,117,110,100,108,101,32,105,110,116,111,32,114,111,111,116,32,124,32,50,51,32,124,10,49,49,49,57,58,124,32,70,101,97,116,117,114,101,45,99,111,109,112,108,101,116,101,32,118,101,114,116,105,99,97,108,32,115,108,105,99,101,44,32,105,110,102,114,97,115,116,114,117,99,116,117,114,101,32,102,111,114,32,108,97,116,101,114,32,98,117,105,108,100,45,111,117,116,32,124,32,52,44,32,49,52,44,32,50,53,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":64,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/TASK.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"## This computer\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"- **Tools:** node 24.22.1, npm 11.19.1, python3 3.14.8, pip3 26.2.1, git 2.56.0, gh 2.46.0, curl 8.22.0, wget 1.25.0, jq 1.8.1, ffmpeg 9.0.2, ffprobe 9.0.2, sqlite3 3.53.4, zip 3.0, unzip 6.00, rustc 1.99.0, cargo 1.99.0, go 1.27.1, java 27, lighthouse 13.5.0, shot-scraper 1.12, xvfb-run, magick 7.1.2, esbuild 0.28.2, uv 0.12.23, tsc 7.0.2, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129.\"},{\"line_number\":66,\"content\":\"## Goal\"},{\"line_number\":82,\"content\":\"## UI & UX: 10-Foot Controller-First Philosophy\"},{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"## Done\"},{\"line_number\":92,\"content\":\"## Source Information\"},{\"line_number\":96,\"content\":\"- Plan: the file name of the plan you were given to build from, or none\"},{\"line_number\":109,\"content\":\"Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (the game's run record and the AI Hub catalogue), so write plain text, and check that the file parses as JSON.\"},{\"line_number\":141,\"content\":\"- What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?\"}]},{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":1,\"content\":\"# PLAN: an original first-person war-zone survival shooter, inspired by Far Cry 2\"},{\"line_number\":3,\"content\":\"You are building this game without me. This plan makes the decisions, so you can spend your effort on building. Your brief outranks this plan; this plan outranks the engine's docs on what to build, and the engine's docs outrank this plan on how an API behaves.\"},{\"line_number\":15,\"content\":\"## 1. The game\"},{\"line_number\":51,\"content\":\"## 2. Setting, cast, story\"},{\"line_number\":85,\"content\":\"## 3. Verified engine facts\"},{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"**Single file on `file://` works.** The kit says modules don't load from `file://`, but that only applies to separate files. An inline `<script type=\\\"module\\\">` holding the esbuild bundle of game plus engine boots on `file://`, with `__PIXEL_READY__` resolving in 2 to 3 s (software WebGPU, 1280 m terrain, 150k grass blades). See section 23.\"},{\"line_number\":160,\"content\":\"- A `model()` with nested `pivot:true` groups named as `HERO_RIG`'s joints works with the hero's clips: `compileClips(HERO_CLIPS, { ...HERO_RIG, spine: undefined }, build.object)`.\"},{\"line_number\":204,\"content\":\"- `spriteSheet`, `textureMap`, `buildModel` and the HUD all work in Node. Only `drawSheet` needs a canvas: don't use it.\"},{\"line_number\":222,\"content\":\"## 4. Architecture\"},{\"line_number\":231,\"content\":\"tools/build.mjs           esbuild + inline: writes the one HTML file your brief names\"},{\"line_number\":252,\"content\":\"- **One Game object, one Engine.** `createGame()` builds the world once. Title, attract, campaign and round are modes on it (`game.mode`). Don't use `engine.loadGame` between them: it would throw away the terrain. For New Game and Attract use `world.reset()`, which clears fire, sites and actors and repaints the base colours.\"},{\"line_number\":263,\"content\":\"**Working rules from your brief:** keep every file inside your own folder (not `/tmp`, not a parent). Don't read other agents' folders. Other agents share this machine, so keep to one or two browsers at once and close them. Don't run `playwright install`; use `npm install playwright@1.63.0` in your folder. `uv run --with pillow ...` is the way to get Python packages. Stop only processes you started, by PID, and never use `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`. \\\"Target closed\\\" or \\\"page crashed\\\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying. If you serve anything, confirm the page's title is your game before trusting a result.\"},{\"line_number\":267,\"content\":\"## 5. World\"},{\"line_number\":328,\"content\":\"**Grass:** `GrassField` chunks of 48 × 48 m with about 7,000 blades, `mask` from the fuel map, `ground` from `heightAt`. Build a chunk the first time it comes within 170 m of the camera, hide it beyond 200 m, dispose beyond 320 m. On build, consult the fire grid (burnt cells get no blades).\"},{\"line_number\":338,\"content\":\"## 6. Fire, wind, time, weather\"},{\"line_number\":342,\"content\":\"- 256 × 256 cells at 5 m (`src/world/fire.js`). Arrays: `fuel` (0 none, 1 grass, 2 scrub, 3 tree, 4 building), `state` (0 fresh, 1 burning, 2 burnt, 3 regrowing), `burnEnd` and `burntAt`. Road, water, rock, salt and dirt have no fuel.\"},{\"line_number\":346,\"content\":\"  - `slopeFactor` = 1.4 uphill, 0.7 downhill. `rainFactor` = 0.15 while raining. `fuelFactor`: grass 1, scrub 0.8, tree 0.6, building 0.4.\"},{\"line_number\":348,\"content\":\"- Burn time: grass 8 to 14 s, scrub 12 to 18 s, tree and building 30 to 40 s.\"},{\"line_number\":386,\"content\":\"**The look.** The engine's native pixel pipeline plus a light grade. Keep these filters always on and change only parameters, since parameters are free and adding a filter rebuilds the pipeline:\"},{\"line_number\":398,\"content\":\"## 7. Player\"},{\"line_number\":420,\"content\":\"## 8. Weapons and wear\"},{\"line_number\":452,\"content\":\"## 9. The body\"},{\"line_number\":474,\"content\":\"## 10. Soldiers and AI\"},{\"line_number\":498,\"content\":\"Pathing uses a global `NavGrid` at 2 m (slope, water, buildings closed), budgeted per section 3; off the grid or far away they walk straight.\"},{\"line_number\":508,\"content\":\"## 11. Vehicles\"},{\"line_number\":522,\"content\":\"## 12. Buddies\"},{\"line_number\":550,\"content\":\"## 13. Stones, safehouses, side content\"},{\"line_number\":590,\"content\":\"## 14. Missions\"},{\"line_number\":631,\"content\":\"## 15. Writing\"},{\"line_number\":663,\"content\":\"## 16. UI and UX\"},{\"line_number\":744,\"content\":\"## 17. Dev mode\"},{\"line_number\":787,\"content\":\"## 18. Attract mode\"},{\"line_number\":810,\"content\":\"## 19. Multiplayer\"},{\"line_number\":867,\"content\":\"**In a session:** no title, menus or prompts before the round. No dialogs (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), no `window.open`, no navigation, no network except the hub. Quit does nothing. Names come only from the hub (sanitize to the font's characters; HUD canvas, never HTML). No chat, emotes or custom names. **On a pad, ignore Options while Create is held** (Create + Options is the hub's). Sessions get an empty storage, so settings start at defaults, music at 10%.\"},{\"line_number\":878,\"content\":\"## 20. Art\"},{\"line_number\":880,\"content\":\"**Base style:** the engine's native 3D-as-pixel-art pipeline at 480×270, toon materials, palette colours only. Make new assets for what makes the game feel like its source. The library covers generic props (use it: `crate`, `barrel`, `sack`, `table`, `chair`, `bed`, `stool`, `boulders`, `rock`, `dead-tree`, `bush`, `reeds`, `stone-wall`, `battlement`, `signpost`, `notice-board`, `market-stall`, `well`, `lamp-post`, `campfire`, `rubble`, `mine-rail`, `shovel`). The library has **no guns, vehicles, acacias or modern buildings**: you write those.\"},{\"line_number\":898,\"content\":\"## 21. Animation\"},{\"line_number\":923,\"content\":\"## 22. Audio\"},{\"line_number\":957,\"content\":\"## 23. Packaging\"},{\"line_number\":959,\"content\":\"The deliverable is **one HTML file** at the place your brief names, beside the dev folder. Nothing else is needed at runtime; no CDN is used. It must run from `file://` and from any web server.\"},{\"line_number\":972,\"content\":\"`tools/build.mjs` (the steps I ran, with `</script` escaped; set `OUT` from your brief):\"},{\"line_number\":974,\"content\":\"const js = execFileSync('esbuild', ['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--target=esnext','--legal-comments=inline','--log-level=warning'], { maxBuffer: 1 << 29 }).toString();\"},{\"line_number\":979,\"content\":\"Use function replacers as above, because the engine contains `$` sequences. The bundle is about 5.3 MB before your game is added. Append the licence texts of the engine, three.js and Rapier from the kit's `CREDITS.md` as an HTML comment at the end of the file. esbuild bundles `pixel-engine.js` without you editing it; that satisfies \\\"keep the engine as it ships\\\".\"},{\"line_number\":989,\"content\":\"## 24. Testing\"},{\"line_number\":1040,\"content\":\"## 25. Build order\"},{\"line_number\":1042,\"content\":\"Each step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\"},{\"line_number\":1046,\"content\":\"| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\"},{\"line_number\":1056,\"content\":\"| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\"},{\"line_number\":1060,\"content\":\"## 26. Cut order\"},{\"line_number\":1078,\"content\":\"## 27. Done, reports, coverage\"},{\"line_number\":1082,\"content\":\"- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\"},{\"line_number\":1092,\"content\":\"- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\"},{\"line_number\":1098,\"content\":\"**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\"},{\"line_number\":1108,\"content\":\"| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\"},{\"line_number\":1119,\"content\":\"| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-1b552cbe-9629-449d-890a-11523179c08a-83","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,10