e name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \\\"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\\\".\\n\\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\\n\\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\\n\\n1100→**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\\n\\n| Brief item | Section |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1060,\"limit\":50,\"raw_output\":\"## 26. Cut order\\n\\nIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\\n\\n1. Fauna (vultures first).\\n2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\\n3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\\n4. Chase camera; dust weather.\\n5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\\n6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\\n7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\\n8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\\n9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\\n\\nNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 27. Done, reports, coverage\\n\\n**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\\n- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\\n- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\\n- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\\n- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\\n- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\\n- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\\n\\n**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\\n- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \\\"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\\\".\\n\\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\\n\\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\\n\\n**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\\n\\n| Brief item | Section |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f82e0dcd-85da-4448-889b-e599f1fd98fe-89","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n10→  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n20→  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n30→\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n40→    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n50→    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n60→    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n10→  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n20→  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n30→\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n40→    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n50→    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n60→    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/main.js\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"import { Engine, withUrlOptions } from '../pixel-engine.js';\\nimport { LOOK } from './core/look.js';\\nimport { createGame } from './game.js';\\nimport { hubSession } from './net/session.js';\\n\\nconst OPTIONS = {\\n  camera: { preset: 'first', fov: 62 },\\n  look: LOOK,\\n  touch: false,\\n  debugKeys: false,\\n  settings: { button: false, key: false },\\n};\\n\\nif (typeof window !== 'undefined') {\\n  window.addEventListener('keydown', (ev) => {\\n    const answer = window.__cardAnswer;\\n    if (!answer) return;\\n    if (ev.key === 'Enter') answer('ready');\\n    if (ev.key === 'm' || ev.key === 'M') answer('more');\\n  });\\n  window.addEventListener('pointerup', () => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    if (!game || (game.mode !== 'play' && game.mode !== 'round')) return;\\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\\n    if (!canvas || document.pointerLockElement) return;\\n    const pending = canvas.requestPointerLock?.();\\n    if (pending && typeof pending.catch === 'function') pending.catch(() => {});\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot() {\\n  const hub = typeof window !== 'undefined' ? window.AIHub : null;\\n  let info = null;\\n  if (hub && hub.active) {\\n    try {\\n      info = await hub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n      return;\\n    }\\n  }\\n  if (info) {\\n    const session = hubSession(info);\\n    window.__cardAnswer = (what) => session.answer(what);\\n    const game = createGame({ session });\\n    if (info.server) {\\n      const engine = await Engine.headless(game, { seed: info.seed });\\n      setInterval(() => engine.step(6, 1 / 60), 100);\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!navigator.gpu) {\\n      hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    try {\\n      await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app'), seed: info.seed }));\\n    } catch (err) {\\n      hub.fail(String(err && err.message || err));\\n    }\\n    return;\\n  }\\n  const game = createGame();\\n  await Engine.start(game, withUrlOptions({ ...OPTIONS, container: document.getElementById('app') }));\\n}\\n\\nboot();\\n\",\"total_lines\":66}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f82e0dcd-85da-4448-889b-e599f1fd98fe-90","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** About pages. The HUD draws these uppercase. The usage line stays exact. */\\n\\nexport const USAGE = 'added on import';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_PAGES = [\\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', 'Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Source: Far Cry 2', 'Plan: PLAN.md'],\\n  ['GENRE AND PERSPECTIVE', 'Genre: first-person shooter', 'Perspective: first person on foot,', 'at the wheel, and in story scenes'],\\n  ['TECH', 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0', 'three.js r186', 'Rapier 0.20', 'esbuild 0.28.2', 'Original sim, fire grid, weapons, missions'],\\n  ['ART DIRECTION', 'Engine pixel-art toon, 480x270', 'Sand, orange and red land', 'Slate Concord, orange Harvest', 'Green only for water and regrowth'],\\n10→  ['ANIMATION', 'Engine clips on the soldier rig', 'First-person hands on a small rig', 'Mixer poses for reload, map, surgery'],\\n  ['AUDIO', 'Code songs, code effects, no files', 'Animalese voices', 'Music starts at 10 percent'],\\n  ['ONLINE', 'AI Hub shared-world, 1-4 players', 'Cash Run, 6 minutes', 'Same-computer link on a BroadcastChannel'],\\n  ['TESTING', 'node tests/run.mjs --all', 'Headless Engine.step playthrough', 'Playwright Chromium, WebGPU flags', 'Hub harness, four scenarios'],\\n  ['RESEARCH', 'Mechanics from the plan, not a port', 'No source maps, names, or plot'],\\n  ['ENVIRONMENT', 'Grok CLI, headless', 'Linux'],\\n  ['MODEL', 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh'],\\n  ['USAGE', USAGE],\\n];\\n\\n20→export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', 'How many issues did testing catch?', 'See the count written after the run.', 'The number is filled in ISSUES and here.'],\\n  ['CRITICAL ISSUES', 'How many would be game breaking?', 'Filled after the run.'],\\n  ['MOST HELPFUL TEST', 'The headless mission playthrough.', 'It drives the shipped actions.'],\\n  ['LEAST HELPFUL TEST', 'A blank WebGPU screenshot.', 'State checks told the truth.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels,', 'and a vehicle that stays upright.'],\\n  ['STUCK OR GUESSED', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z.', 'The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z.', 'Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.'],\\n30→  ['BUILT YOURSELF', 'What did you build yourself?', 'The fire grid, jams, fever, map,', 'mission runner, and the hub round.'],\\n  ['HARDEST ENGINE PART', 'Pointer lock, timeScale pause,', 'and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.'],\\n  ['CHANGED IN THE ENGINE', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.'],\\n  ['ONE CHANGE', 'If you could change one thing?', 'A first-person rig that does not', 'steal the use key or the pointer.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'The plan names the traps and the', 'order to cut whole features.'],\\n  ['CONFUSING', 'What was confusing?', 'File stem spaces, and which card', 'the harness presses Enter on.'],\\n  ['HARDEST', 'What was the hardest thing?', 'One world that is a campaign,', 'a 6 minute round, and a hub server.'],\\n40→  ['CHANGE THE PROMPT', 'What would you change?', 'Ship the hub check before asking', 'for every prop in the art list.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const CREDIT_PAGES = [\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'three.js, MIT', 'Rapier, Apache-2.0', 'AI Hub session client'],\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated'],\\n];\\n\\nexport function aboutPages() {\\n  return [...SOURCE_PAGES, ...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK, ...CREDIT_PAGES];\\n50→}\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** About pages. The HUD draws these uppercase. The usage line stays exact. */\\n\\nexport const USAGE = 'added on import';\\n\\nexport const SOURCE_PAGES = [\\n  ['SOURCE INFORMATION', 'Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17', 'Source: Far Cry 2', 'Plan: PLAN.md'],\\n  ['GENRE AND PERSPECTIVE', 'Genre: first-person shooter', 'Perspective: first person on foot,', 'at the wheel, and in story scenes'],\\n  ['TECH', 'Pixel Engine 0.46.0', 'three.js r186', 'Rapier 0.20', 'esbuild 0.28.2', 'Original sim, fire grid, weapons, missions'],\\n  ['ART DIRECTION', 'Engine pixel-art toon, 480x270', 'Sand, orange and red land', 'Slate Concord, orange Harvest', 'Green only for water and regrowth'],\\n10→  ['ANIMATION', 'Engine clips on the soldier rig', 'First-person hands on a small rig', 'Mixer poses for reload, map, surgery'],\\n  ['AUDIO', 'Code songs, code effects, no files', 'Animalese voices', 'Music starts at 10 percent'],\\n  ['ONLINE', 'AI Hub shared-world, 1-4 players', 'Cash Run, 6 minutes', 'Same-computer link on a BroadcastChannel'],\\n  ['TESTING', 'node tests/run.mjs --all', 'Headless Engine.step playthrough', 'Playwright Chromium, WebGPU flags', 'Hub harness, four scenarios'],\\n  ['RESEARCH', 'Mechanics from the plan, not a port', 'No source maps, names, or plot'],\\n  ['ENVIRONMENT', 'Grok CLI, headless', 'Linux'],\\n  ['MODEL', 'xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh'],\\n  ['USAGE', USAGE],\\n];\\n\\n20→export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['TESTING FEEDBACK', 'How many issues did testing catch?', 'See the count written after the run.', 'The number is filled in ISSUES and here.'],\\n  ['CRITICAL ISSUES', 'How many would be game breaking?', 'Filled after the run.'],\\n  ['MOST HELPFUL TEST', 'The headless mission playthrough.', 'It drives the shipped actions.'],\\n  ['LEAST HELPFUL TEST', 'A blank WebGPU screenshot.', 'State checks told the truth.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels,', 'and a vehicle that stays upright.'],\\n  ['STUCK OR GUESSED', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z.', 'The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z.', 'Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.'],\\n30→  ['BUILT YOURSELF', 'What did you build yourself?', 'The fire grid, jams, fever, map,', 'mission runner, and the hub round.'],\\n  ['HARDEST ENGINE PART', 'Pointer lock, timeScale pause,', 'and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.'],\\n  ['CHANGED IN THE ENGINE', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.'],\\n  ['ONE CHANGE', 'If you could change one thing?', 'A first-person rig that does not', 'steal the use key or the pointer.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'The plan names the traps and the', 'order to cut whole features.'],\\n  ['CONFUSING', 'What was confusing?', 'File stem spaces, and which card', 'the harness presses Enter on.'],\\n  ['HARDEST', 'What was the hardest thing?', 'One world that is a campaign,', 'a 6 minute round, and a hub server.'],\\n40→  ['CHANGE THE PROMPT', 'What would you change?', 'Ship the hub check before asking', 'for every prop in the art list.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const CREDIT_PAGES = [\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'three.js, MIT', 'Rapier, Apache-2.0', 'AI Hub session client'],\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated'],\\n];\\n\\nexport function aboutPages() {\\n  return [...SOURCE_PAGES, ...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK, ...CREDIT_PAGE