e shipped actions.'],\\n  ['LEAST HELPFUL TEST', 'A blank WebGPU screenshot.', 'State checks told the truth.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['ENGINE FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels,', 'and a vehicle that stays upright.'],\\n  ['STUCK OR GUESSED', 'Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z.', 'The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z.', 'Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.'],\\n  ['BUILT YOURSELF', 'What did you build yourself?', 'The fire grid, jams, fever, map,', 'mission runner, and the hub round.'],\\n  ['HARDEST ENGINE PART', 'Pointer lock, timeScale pause,', 'and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.'],\\n  ['CHANGED IN THE ENGINE', 'What did you change in the engine, and why?', 'None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.'],\\n  ['ONE CHANGE', 'If you could change one thing?', 'A first-person rig that does not', 'steal the use key or the pointer.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\\n  ['PROMPT FEEDBACK', 'What did you like most?', 'The plan names the traps and the', 'order to cut whole features.'],\\n  ['CONFUSING', 'What was confusing?', 'File stem spaces, and which card', 'the harness presses Enter on.'],\\n  ['HARDEST', 'What was the hardest thing?', 'One world that is a campaign,', 'a 6 minute round, and a hub server.'],\\n  ['CHANGE THE PROMPT', 'What would you change?', 'Ship the hub check before asking', 'for every prop in the art list.'],\\n];\\n\\nexport const CREDIT_PAGES = [\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Pixel Engine, MIT', 'three.js, MIT', 'Rapier, Apache-2.0', 'AI Hub session client'],\\n  ['CREDITS', 'Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated'],\\n];\\n\\nexport function aboutPages() {\\n  return [...SOURCE_PAGES, ...TESTING_FEEDBACK, ...ENGINE_FEEDBACK, ...PROMPT_FEEDBACK, ...CREDIT_PAGES];\\n}\\n\",\"total_lines\":50}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-f82e0dcd-85da-4448-889b-e599f1fd98fe-91","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor/\\n  - hub/\\n    - bridge.js\\n    - harness.html\\n    - README.md\\n    - round.js\\n  - pixel-engine.zip\\n  - session.js\",\"absolute_root_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/vendor\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"53a5e698-9dcd-4c0e-88ce-afbdbcbfa2d6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_329","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking the font charset for about pages.\n\nThe allowed character set excludes em dashes and ellipses. I will write ISSUES.md with a real list and count issues. About pages must use only allowed characters when uppercased.\n\nISSUES.md will list only defects the tests actually caught that required game fixes. The first four player-facing bugs are unequal song step counts, KeyE consumed by the map, burn objectives failing on unburnable terrain, and hidden payroll stealing convoy bullets.\n\nMore player-facing bugs were found. Scripted jams were cleared by random rolls. Ending cards dismissed by the same mouse click that fired flares. Touch gates treated mouse clicks as controller input and skipped to the menu. Attract mode carried over god, vehicle, and map states into the next mission. Existing trucks were not moved to mission setup. Title returns left solo sessions attached so attract mode never started. Mission starts left earlier soldiers alive causing firing squads. Cash rounds began while players were dead so shots never fired.\n\nMore player-facing bugs were found. Title and menu screens still ran soldier damage, killing the player and freezing attract mode. The buddy rescue timer was a test assertion bug, not a game defect. giveGun replaced the wrong slot. choicePick was not cleared. Hub rounds finished at 360 even for hub kind. m1 fever timer did not zero so fever-fall never triggered. Ground gun condition range was wrong. Civilian bullets reduced health. Jams blocked until reload. cond 0 was broken. Driving yaw in the bot was a test bug.\n\nI will verify every defect listed in ISSUES.md against the current code to avoid inventing issues. The count will only include fixes I personally observed or can confirm remain in the shipped build.\n\nThe leftover soldier at 20,20 during the m8 hold is one confirmed game bug. The dead buddy leak is shared-engine test state, not a game defect. Cash rounds reviving the player is another confirmed game fix.\n\nMercenaries killing the player on the title screen prevented attract mode from starting. The game fix blocks combat during attract and clears actors and revives the player when returning to the title.\n\nThe realControl exclusion of MouseLeft was observed in code. applySetup now clears vehicle, map, and god states and repositions the truck. toTitle clears the session so attract mode can start.\n\nI will not inflate the issue count. Every defect in ISSUES.md must be verifiable from this conversation's evidence. I am beginning to organize them into a numbered list, starting with game-breaking issues that blocked required play paths or the acceptance suite.\n\nThe held map consuming the use key was likely a test bug, not a game defect. Burn objectives on roads could not ignite and still needs verification.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d584ea99-2416-49dd-9cef-33ffb7b3b1b9-92","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"menuArm|jamScript = 0|state\\[.*\\] === 1|pay\\.x = prop","glob":"**/{world.js,game.js}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d584ea99-2416-49dd-9cef-33ffb7b3b1b9-93","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"examples/|packs/","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs,html,md}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d584ea99-2416-49dd-9cef-33ffb7b3b1b9-94","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/CREDITS.md","limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d584ea99-2416-49dd-9cef-33ffb7b3b1b9-95","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function startLink|HOST ON THIS COMPUTER|link","glob":"**/game.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3968,"output_tokens":1824,"cache_read_input_tokens":127616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f85c08b6-1eb2-4743-8390-c1ebe6b0a9c3"}
