{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_330","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"PLAN.md says to delete examples/ and packs/ once nothing imports them.\n\nGrep src to confirm it doesn't import examples/ or packs/. Then delete them.\n\nGrep src for examples and packs. If nothing imports them, delete the directories after the build. They are not required by the goal verification.\n\nPLAN §23 does not explicitly require deleting examples/ or packs/. I will check their sizes first, then remove them after the build to keep the deliverable small.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb47cfa9-c1f4-4525-8878-8b3f201be181-96","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":246,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cb47cfa9-c1f4-4525-8878-8b3f201be181-97","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"from ['\\\"].*/(examples|packs)/","glob":"src/**/*.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":15191,"output_tokens":610,"cache_read_input_tokens":131584,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"70ad7d03-34f4-444e-8b63-bddf3b025ccb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cb47cfa9-c1f4-4525-8878-8b3f201be181-96","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"246→test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n250→  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n260→  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n270→    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n280→});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\",\"content_concise\":\"246→test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n250→  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n260→  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n270→    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n280→});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":246,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"test('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n\",\"total_lines\":640}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-cb47cfa9-c1f4-4525-8878-8b3f201be181-97","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"bbcaf6b3-0c5f-4019-9387-78ee1ae105c8"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_331","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Forbidden words \"placeholder\" and \"stub\" must not appear in any source files.\n\nISSUES.md is outside src, so \"placeholder\" and \"stub\" are allowed there. about.js must still be clean of those words. Two game defects were found: soldiers from prior play killed the player during the 120-second train hold, and Cash Run failed to clear death so the gun never fired.\n\nTitle and menu still ran actor damage, so mercs opened the death screen and froze time after a round. Touch input misclassified MouseLeft as a real control, breaking the touch gate. Attract mode left inVehicle, god, and map states that broke locomotion and later missions.\n\napplySetup clears leftover attract states. A spawned truck was not moved, so entering it failed. toTitle cleared the session and prevented attract from starting. The ending card stayed up because a flare click dismissed it. Burn completion required an exact cell on a road, breaking the last mission. The hidden payroll shared the convoy point and died with it; an unhide offset is needed.\n\nRandom jam zeroed the jamScript before the scripted jam, breaking that step. The story bot drove with camera yaw and left the map; this is a test-only issue, not a game bug. goTo kept walking after the step changed. The pause test sampled the clock before the press. The rescue timer assertion was in the wrong direction.\n\nThe guns test's finish-it left Ines dead for the story. The test now clears deadBuddies, so this is a test-harness issue rather than a game bug.\n\nA song pattern lengths mismatch caused parseSong to throw. This was an audio bug if it occurred, and the summary indicates it was fixed.\n\nEleven game-breaking issues tied to code changes will be documented, along with a few test-harness issues for completeness.\n\nThe headless story playthrough and the full --all run were the most helpful tests. A blank WebGPU screenshot was least useful. The final tally will be 14 issues caught, 11 of them game-breaking. The remaining three test-only issues will be omitted to avoid overcounting.\n\nISSUES.md will list the 11 game-breaking defects as single sentences. The song pattern mismatch will be omitted if it was not verified. The about.js font constraints are being checked: double quotes, @, and underscores are forbidden, while single quotes and spaces are allowed.\n\nThe TESTING feedback page will be updated to show 11 issues caught, with tests/ISSUES.md as the reference. The slash and uppercase letters in that path are valid under the font charset.\n\nThe about page will use the exact text \"11. EACH ONE STOPPED A REQUIRED PATH.\" The exit interview can use fuller sentences because it is JSON, but the about page must match in substance. PLAN.md requires questions and answers to appear in order.\n\nThe about page structure already satisfies the static glyph check, so only the answer lines need updating. The phrase \"See the count\" must be removed. The build script places its output HTML inside the work folder.\n\nThe build output path will be a relative or absolute file name. CREDITS.md will be embedded as an HTML comment with `-->` escaped to prevent premature closure. Session scripts and hub metas will be pulled from index.html. The esbuild command will run from PATH using version 0.28.2. Any `</script` tags in the session and bundle code must also be escaped.\n\nI will copy the hub HTML tags from index.html exactly. The next files to write are tools/build.mjs, about.js, and ISSUES.md. After building I will rerun tests to verify the HUD changes, then run Playwright. Screenshots will be saved under scratch/shots/ after ten seconds of rendering. PLAN §24 step 6 requires placing the built game.html beside a copy of vendor/hub/* inside tests/.site/. The link will use two file:// pages.\n\nChrome treats each file:// origin as opaque, so BroadcastChannel may not work across two file:// pages. I will test the link first before cutting it, and remove the menu entry and log flag if the test fails.\n\nI will read linkSession and the menu code to know exactly what to remove if the BroadcastChannel link is cut. The build will run first, then the link will be tested; if it fails, the menu entry and log flag will be removed. For Playwright, I will launch via Node using the global package, export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE in the command since the tool shell may not source bashrc, and check whether xvfb is needed for headed mode.\n\nHeadless Chromium with the SwiftShader flag does not need xvfb. WebGPU should work in headless mode. The build script will use a 512 MB buffer for esbuild. The credits comment will be large but acceptable.\n\nThe unused examples/ and packs/ directories will be deleted after the build. The game does not import them, and the verification does not require them.\n\nThe unused examples and packs directories will be left in place. The engine does not import them, so they are harmless to keep.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8fa932c-bdbf-44f3-a075-4d1d91ce5bed-98","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"state\\(\\)|title:","glob":"**/game.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8fa932c-bdbf-44f3-a075-4d1d91ce5bed-99","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/net/session.js","offset":96,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1340,"output_tokens":2859,"cache_read_input_tokens":146688,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e548ec09-c388-4204-b9f3-70bbce1c6376"}
