{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-b412b9d5-ba07-4a31-8c12-739741aaec87-114","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"25→}\\n\\nexport function touchGateActive() {\\n  if (typeof matchMedia !== 'function') return false;\\n  const coarse = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\\n30→  const fine = matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\\n  let pad = false;\\n  try {\\n    pad = [...(navigator.getGamepads?.() || [])].some(Boolean);\\n  } catch { /* no pad list */ }\\n  return coarse && !fine && !pad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createGame(options = {}) {\\n  return new BasinGame(options);\\n40→}\\n\\nexport class BasinGame {\\n  constructor(options = {}) {\\n    this.name = GAME_TITLE;\",\"content_concise\":\"25→}\\n\\nexport function touchGateActive() {\\n  if (typeof matchMedia !== 'function') return false;\\n  const coarse = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\\n30→  const fine = matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\\n  let pad = false;\\n  try {\\n    pad = [...(navigator.getGamepads?.() || [])].some(Boolean);\\n  } catch { /* no pad list */ }\\n  return coarse && !fine && !pad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createGame(options = {}) {\\n  return new BasinGame(options);\\n40→}\\n\\nexport class BasinGame {\\n  constructor(options = {}) {\\n    this.name = GAME_TITLE;\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js\",\"offset\":25,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"}\\n\\nexport function touchGateActive() {\\n  if (typeof matchMedia !== 'function') return false;\\n  const coarse = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches;\\n  const fine = matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\\n  let pad = false;\\n  try {\\n    pad = [...(navigator.getGamepads?.() || [])].some(Boolean);\\n  } catch { /* no pad list */ }\\n  return coarse && !fine && !pad;\\n}\\n\\nexport function createGame(options = {}) {\\n  return new BasinGame(options);\\n}\\n\\nexport class BasinGame {\\n  constructor(options = {}) {\\n    this.name = GAME_TITLE;\\n\",\"total_lines\":757}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"64dce623-879f-4e5c-879b-fb663a21cc05"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_342","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Playwright's iPhone 14 preset includes isMobile and hasTouch.\n\nThe headless test used touchOnly to force the gate. The browser test must detect pointer: coarse via matchMedia. If Chromium's iPhone profile omits this, the test fails and emulation or detection needs fixing.\n\nThe plan uses Playwright's iPhone 14 device descriptor with defaultBrowserType removed. The browser test will tap the Settings item via page.touchscreen.tap. The HUD is 480x270 scaled to the canvas, which may be the full viewport or a pixel-art canvas inside.\n\nThe engine maps pointer input to NDC coordinates. The headless test used setPointer with NDC values. For the browser test, I need to tap the visual position of the SETTINGS button. If the canvas fills the viewport, the tap should be at (width/2, 86/270 * height). The iPhone 14 viewport is 390x844.\n\nThe canvas may be letterboxed, so the tap coordinates should be calculated relative to the actual canvas bounding box after load. The test will wait 11 seconds for the attract screen to start and then check state().attract. Headless Playwright throttles requestAnimationFrame, but the engine's idle tracking uses real-time deltas, so 11 seconds of real time should reliably trigger the attract state.\n\nThe browser test will wait up to 20 seconds for the attract screen to start, since headless Chrome throttles requestAnimationFrame when the page is backgrounded. The sequence will mirror the headless test: first verify the notice shows exactly one settings item, then confirm attract begins within 15 seconds, exit attract, and finally tap the Settings button.\n\nA key press would clear the touch gate, so the browser test must exit attract via `page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.exitAttract())` before tapping.\n\nThe engine's update loop consumes fresh input as an attract exit rather than menu activation in the same frame. A single tap exits attract and returns to the title screen. A second tap then opens settings.\n\nThe notice screen will remain visible after attract exits because exitAttract restores it when the touch gate is active.\n\nTwo sequential scripts will run in one browser: one for the launch sequence and touch test, another for the hub. They will not run in parallel.\n\nA title screenshot will be saved after waiting ten seconds during launch-1. The plan requires several screenshots under scratch/shots/, including title, day fp, night fire, and map in truck. Missing or blank WebGPU frames do not count as failures.\n\nCalling engine.step from the page risks double-stepping because the browser loop already runs on requestAnimationFrame. I will instead teleport the game state via page.evaluate, such as starting mission m1, and wait briefly before taking screenshots.\n\nI will export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 and locate the Playwright module path. The launch script will be written to scratch and run with a 120-second timeout for two boots. Swiftshader first boot may take up to 90 seconds, so I will check engine.errors on the page and include them in the log.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-cf62f38a-ada9-4594-b6db-0ffe7325f870-115","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/launch.mjs","old_string":"","new_string":"/** Two file:// boots plus the Chromium iPhone 14 touch gate. One browser at a time. */\nimport { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { chromium, devices } from 'playwright';\n\nconst html = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html';\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\nconst url = pathToFileURL(html).href;\nconst flags = [\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\n];\n\nfunction listen(page, lines) {\n  page.on('console', (msg) => lines.push('console.' + msg.type() + ' ' + msg.text()));\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => lines.push('pageerror ' + (err && err.message)));\n  page.on('requestfailed', (req) => lines.push('requestfailed ' + req.url() + ' ' + (req.failure() && req.failure().errorText)));\n}\n\nasync function readState(page) {\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\n    const state = game && game.state ? game.state() : null;\n    return {\n      documentTitle: document.title,\n      aihubActive: typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' && !!AIHub.active,\n      title: state && state.title,\n      screen: state && state.screen,\n      mode: state && state.mode,\n      notice: state && state.notice,\n      menu: state && state.menu,\n      attract: state && state.attract,\n      errors: engine && engine.errors ? engine.errors.map(String) : [],\n    };\n  });\n}\n\nasync function boot(page) {\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 90000 });\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.state && window.__GAME__.state().title, null, { timeout: 90000 });\n}\n\nconst results = [];\nfor (const n of [1, 2]) {\n  const lines = [];\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\n  listen(page, lines);\n  let info = null;\n  let failed = null;\n  try {\n    await boot(page);\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\n    info = await readState(page);\n  } catch (err) {\n    failed = String(err && err.stack || err);\n  }\n  const errors = lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('console.error') || line.startsWith('pageerror') || line.startsWith('requestfailed'));\n  const text = [\n    'url ' + url,\n    'boot ' + (failed ? 'FAIL' : 'ok'),\n    failed || '',\n    'state ' + JSON.stringify(info),\n    'errorCount ' + errors.length,\n    ...errors,\n    '--- log ---',\n    ...lines,\n  ].filter(Boolean).join('\\n');\n  writeFileSync(scratch + '/launch-' + n + '.log', text);\n  results.push({ n, failed, info, errors: errors.length });\n  await browser.close();\n}\n\nconst phoneLines = [];\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\nconst phone = devices['iPhone 14'];\nconst context = await browser.newContext({\n  viewport: phone.viewport,\n  userAgent: phone.userAgent,\n  deviceScaleFactor: phone.deviceScaleFactor,\n  isMobile: phone.isMobile,\n  hasTouch: phone.hasTouch,\n});\nconst page = await context.newPage();\nlisten(page, phoneLines);\nlet touch = {};\ntry {\n  await boot(page);\n  touch.boot = await readState(page);\n  const started = Date.now();\n  let attract = false;\n  while (Date.now() - started < 20000) {\n    const now = await readState(page);\n    if (now.attract) { attract = true; touch.afterIdle = now; break; }\n    await page.waitForTimeout(500);\n  }\n  touch.attract = attract;\n  if (attract) await page.evaluate(() => window.__GAME__.exitAttract());\n  touch.afterExit = await readState(page);\n  const box = await page.evaluate(() => {\n    const canvas = document.querySelector('#app canvas');\n    if (!canvas) return null;\n    const r = canvas.getBoundingClientRect();\n    return { x: r.x, y: r.y, w: r.width, h: r.height };\n  });\n  touch.box = box;\n  if (box) {\n    await page.touchscreen.tap(box.x + box.w * 0.5, box.y + box.h * (86 / 270));\n    await page.waitForTimeout(400);\n  }\n  touch.afterTap = await readState(page);\n} catch (err) {\n  touch.failed = String(err && err.stack || err);\n}\nconst phoneErrors = phoneLines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('console.error') || line.startsWith('pageerror'));\nwriteFileSync(scratch + '/touch.log', JSON.stringify(touch, null, 2) + '\\n--- errors ' + phoneErrors.length + ' ---\\n' + phoneErrors.join('\\n') + '\\n--- log ---\\n' + phoneLines.join('\\n'));\nawait browser.close();\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ results, touch: { attract: touch.attract, notice: touch.boot && touch.boot.notice, menu: touch.boot && touch.boot.menu, screen: touch.afterTap && touch.afterTap.screen, failed: touch.failed || null } }, null, 2));\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":341,"output_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":166016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ce2d1a28-cbdb-41de-8f5d-5816eb9499ee"}
