{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_359","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The client does not apply snapshots.\n\nTesting BroadcastChannel between file:// pages to enable link-to-share fire. If it works, snapshots will be applied on the client to sync state. If not, the feature will be dropped. A quick probe script will verify this first.\n\nThe snapshot only stores a fire lit count, not the full grid. A shared fire would need ignition events or the full grid from the host. Applying a snapshot would sync case ownership and fire status, but standings require session.finish computed by the host.\n\nThe join handler only applies finish messages when isHost, so the client never receives the outcome. Snapshots will sync cases, seats, and time.\n\nThe client will handle finish messages to set the outcome and end state. For fire, the host can send a small list of burning cell indices instead of the full grid. The simplest shared proof is an ignition on the host that appears on the client.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-c619cea8-3926-4e23-b131-fc172a2aa21b-134","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"ignite\\(|burning","glob":"**/fire.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1594,"output_tokens":777,"cache_read_input_tokens":182656,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ca5623ba-1c45-43ab-8a15-465f07aebd35"}
