4,32,97,109,98,105,101,110,99,101,44,32,102,101,101,108,44,32,97,114,116,32,112,97,115,115,101,115,44,32,98,97,108,97,110,99,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,116,104,101,32,115,108,105,100,101,114,115,44,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,115,32,124,32,89,111,117,39,100,32,115,104,111,119,32,105,116,32,116,111,32,115,111,109,101,111,110,101,32,124,10,49,48,56,56,58,45,32,91,32,93,32,89,111,117,32,108,111,111,107,101,100,32,97,116,32,116,104,101,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,115,46,10,49,49,49,54,58,124,32,84,101,115,116,105,110,103,58,32,104,101,97,100,108,101,115,115,44,32,115,99,114,105,112,116,101,100,32,112,108,97,121,116,104,114,111,117,103,104,44,32,111,110,101,32,99,111,109,109,97,110,100,44,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,115,32,111,110,108,121,32,119,104,101,110,32,110,101,101,100,101,100,44,32,110,111,32,114,101,118,105,101,119,32,115,117,98,97,103,101,110,116,115,32,124,32,50,52,32,124,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":16,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":89,\"content\":\"**Single file on `file://` works.** The kit says modules don't load from `file://`, but that only applies to separate files. An inline `<script type=\\\"module\\\">` holding the esbuild bundle of game plus engine boots on `file://`, with `__PIXEL_READY__` resolving in 2 to 3 s (software WebGPU, 1280 m terrain, 150k grass blades). See section 23.\"},{\"line_number\":201,\"content\":\"- `Engine.headless(createGame(), { camera:{ preset:'first' }, viewport:{ width:1920, height:1080, dpr:1 } })` runs at far faster than real time (300 steps took about 60 ms on a bare scene).\"},{\"line_number\":218,\"content\":\"**Software rendering runs at about 1 fps here.** That is expected. Treat the performance budget as unlimited: add as much detail, enemies, effects, lights and shadows as a scene needs. FPS targets and optimization are out of scope and handled later. Never judge the game by real time in a headless browser. Drive tests with `e.step(n)` and read state. For a real picture, set `e.manual = false`, wait 10 s or more, and take a Playwright `page.screenshot`. That produced correct frames for me with the flags in section 24.\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"- **Sim and view apart.** A soldier is data plus an optional view; a fire cell is data plus sprites. In a round, a client's soldiers are puppets with no brain and no collider, driven by snapshots. Write them this way from the first day, because retrofitting it is the expensive part of section 19.\"},{\"line_number\":332,\"content\":\"**Fauna:** gazelle herds in open grass (a small quadruped on its own rig with a keyed run cycle, fleeing gunshots and fire) and vultures circling burnt or corpse-heavy sites (`Boids` with a tiny flapping model). They are atmosphere and can't hurt you.\"},{\"line_number\":665,\"content\":\"**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\"},{\"line_number\":833,\"content\":\"  else if (!navigator.gpu) AIHub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');\"},{\"line_number\":851,\"content\":\"| `ev` | client → host | up to 5/s, reliable, batched | shots since last batch (origin, dir, weapon), use, pick up, bank, revive, ignite |\"},{\"line_number\":857,\"content\":\"Clients render soldiers as puppets interpolated 150 ms behind; they run fire visuals only; health is host-authoritative. Local shots show muzzle flash and tracers at once, and the host decides hits. Older snapshots are dropped by `at`. In a shared world use `AIHub.rng(label)`, because `Math.random` isn't seeded there; the world is the same static terrain on all copies anyway.\"},{\"line_number\":1015,\"content\":\"5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\"},{\"line_number\":1018,\"content\":\"   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\"},{\"line_number\":1034,\"content\":\"**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\"},{\"line_number\":1036,\"content\":\"**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\"},{\"line_number\":1055,\"content\":\"| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\"},{\"line_number\":1088,\"content\":\"- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\"},{\"line_number\":1116,\"content\":\"| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-11a24429-198e-491e-8c51-87b997dd3d06-8","content":"{\"type\":\"ListDir\",\"Content\":{\"content\":\"- /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/\\n  - boot.err\\n  - boot.mjs\\n  - boot.out\\n  - drive.err\\n  - drive.mjs\\n  - drive.out\\n  - hub-readme.md\\n  - hub.log\\n  - hub.mjs\\n  - launch-1.log\\n  - launch-2.log\\n  - launch.mjs\\n  - link-probe.mjs\\n  - link.log\\n  - link.mjs\\n  - phone.mjs\\n  - pixel-engine-from-zip.js\\n  - pixel-engine.zip\\n  - pointer.mjs\\n  - steer.mjs\\n  - tests-all.log\\n  - touch-final.mjs\\n  - touch.log\",\"absolute_root_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"324e3afa-af44-4174-b3b2-ad437ab2d716"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_377","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Tests and build will run in parallel.\n\nChecking hub.mjs, launch.mjs, and touch-final.mjs for correct HTML references. Tests may take several minutes due to story bot simulation time.\n\nTests will run with a 3-minute timeout. Build is fast. Commands must target the stem folder. Tests will write to tests-all.log.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-9","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/launch.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-10","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/hub.mjs","limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-11","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":990,"limit":60}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-12","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\" && node tests/run.mjs --all > \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/tests-all.log\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$?; tail -n 30 \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/tests-all.log\"","description":"Re-run full headless suite into scratch log","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-13","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"cd \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\" && node tools/build.mjs && python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html\")\nt = p.read_text(errors=\"replace\")\nneed = [\n  \"13. Listed in tests/ISSUES.md.\",\n  \"13. Each one stopped a required path.\",\n  \"added on import\",\n  \"<title>A Cry Too Far</title>\",\n  \"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\",\n]\nfor s in need:\n    print((\"OK\" if s in t else \"MISSING\"), s)\nprint(\"chars\", len(t))\nPY","description":"Rebuild single-file HTML and confirm About text"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1821,"output_tokens":1177,"cache_read_input_tokens":43008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c2560bd3-357d-420d-9592-108d25dd1968"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-9","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Two file:// boots plus the Chromium iPhone 14 touch gate. One browser at a time. */\\nimport { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium, devices } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst html = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html';\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\n10→const url = pathToFileURL(html).href;\\nconst flags = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n];\\n\\nfunction listen(page, lines) {\\n20→  page.on('console', (msg) => lines.push('console.' + msg.type() + ' ' + msg.text()));\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => lines.push('pageerror ' + (err && err.message)));\\n  page.on('requestfailed', (req) => lines.push('requestfailed ' + req.url() + ' ' + (req.failure() && req.failure().errorText)));\\n}\\n\\nasync function readState(page) {\\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    const state = game && game.state ? game.state() : null;\\n30→    return {\\n      documentTitle: document.title,\\n      aihubActive: typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' && !!AIHub.active,\\n      title: state && state.title,\\n      screen: state && state.screen,\\n      mode: state && state.mode,\\n      notice: state && state.notice,\\n      menu: state && state.menu,\\n      attract: state && state.attract,\\n      errors: engine && engine.errors ? engine.errors.map(String) : [],\\n40→    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot(page) {\\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 90000 });\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.state && window.__GAME__.state().title, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n}\\n\\nconst results = [];\\n50→for (const n of [1, 2]) {\\n  const lines = [];\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n  listen(page, lines);\\n  let info = null;\\n  let failed = null;\\n  try {\\n    await boot(page);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n60→    info = await readState(page);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    failed = String(err && err.stack || err);\\n  }\\n  const errors = lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('console.error') || line.startsWith('pageerror') || line.startsWith('requestfailed'));\\n  const text = [\\n    'url ' + url,\\n    'boot ' + (failed ? 'FAIL' : 'ok'),\\n    failed || '',\\n    'state ' + JSON.stringify(info),\\n70→    'errorCount ' + errors.length,\\n    ...errors,\\n    '--- log ---',\\n    ...lines,\\n  ].filter(Boolean).join('\\\\n');\\n  writeFileSync(scratch + '/launch-' + n + '.log', text);\\n  results.push({ n, failed, info, errors: errors.length });\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\n80→const phoneLines = [];\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Two file:// boots plus the Chromium iPhone 14 touch gate. One browser at a time. */\\nimport { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium, devices } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst html = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html';\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\n10→const url = pathToFileURL(html).href;\\nconst flags = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n];\\n\\nfunction listen(page, lines) {\\n20→  page.on('console', (msg) => lines.push('console.' + msg.type() + ' ' + msg.text()));\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => lines.push('pageerror ' + (err && err.message)));\\n  page.on('requestfailed', (req) => lines.push('requestfailed ' + req.url() + ' ' + (req.failure() && req.failure().errorText)));\\n}\\n\\nasync function readState(page) {\\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    const state = game && game.state ? game.state() : null;\\n30→    return {\\n      documentTitle: document.title,\\n      aihubActive: typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' && !!AIHub.active,\\n      title: state && state.title,\\n      screen: state && state.screen,\\n      mode: state && state.mode,\\n      notice: state && state.notice,\\n      menu: state && state.menu,\\n      attract: state && state.attract,\\n      errors: engine && engine.errors ? engine.errors.map(String) : [],\\n40→    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot(page) {\\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 90000 });\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.state && window.__GAME__.state().title, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n}\\n\\nconst results = [];\\n50→for (const n of [1, 2]) {\\n  const lines = [];\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n  listen(page, lines);\\n  let info = null;\\n  let failed = null;\\n  try {\\n    await boot(page);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n60→    info = await readState(page);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    failed = String(err && err.stack || err);\\n  }\\n  const errors = lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('console.error') || line.startsWith('pageerror') || line.startsWith('requestfailed'));\\n  const text = [\\n    'url ' + url,\\n    'boot ' + (failed ? 'FAIL' : 'ok'),\\n    failed || '',\\n    'state ' + JSON.stringify(info),\\n70→    'errorCount ' + errors.length,\\n    ...errors,\\n    '--- log ---',\\n    ...lines,\\n  ].filter(Boolean).join('\\\\n');\\n  writeFileSync(scratch + '/launch-' + n + '.log', text);\\n  results.push({ n, failed, info, errors: errors.length });\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\n80→const phoneLines = [];\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/launch.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/** Two file:// boots plus the Chromium iPhone 14 touch gate. One browser at a time. */\\nimport { writeFileSync, mkdirSync } from 'node:fs';\\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium, devices } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst html = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html';\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\nconst url = pathToFileURL(html).href;\\nconst flags = [\\n  '--enable-unsafe-webgpu',\\n  '--enable-features=Vulkan',\\n  '--use-vulkan=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-angle=swiftshader',\\n  '--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader',\\n];\\n\\nfunction listen(page, lines) {\\n  page.on('console', (msg) => lines.push('console.' + msg.type() + ' ' + msg.text()));\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => lines.push('pageerror ' + (err && err.message)));\\n  page.on('requestfailed', (req) => lines.push('requestfailed ' + req.url() + ' ' + (req.failure() && req.failure().errorText)));\\n}\\n\\nasync function readState(page) {\\n  return page.evaluate(() => {\\n    const game = window.__GAME__;\\n    const engine = window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__;\\n    const state = game && game.state ? game.state() : null;\\n    return {\\n      documentTitle: document.title,\\n      aihubActive: typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' && !!AIHub.active,\\n      title: state && state.title,\\n      screen: state && state.screen,\\n      mode: state && state.mode,\\n      notice: state && state.notice,\\n      menu: state && state.menu,\\n      attract: state && state.attract,\\n      errors: engine && engine.errors ? engine.errors.map(String) : [],\\n    };\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nasync function boot(page) {\\n  await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'load', timeout: 90000 });\\n  await page.waitForFunction(() => window.__GAME__ && window.__GAME__.state && window.__GAME__.state().title, null, { timeout: 90000 });\\n}\\n\\nconst results = [];\\nfor (const n of [1, 2]) {\\n  const lines = [];\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1920, height: 1080 } });\\n  listen(page, lines);\\n  let info = null;\\n  let failed = null;\\n  try {\\n    await boot(page);\\n    await page.waitForTimeout(2000);\\n    info = await readState(page);\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    failed = String(err && err.stack || err);\\n  }\\n  const errors = lines.filter((line) => line.startsWith('console.error') || line.startsWith('pageerror') || line.startsWith('requestfailed'));\\n  const text = [\\n    'url ' + url,\\n    'boot ' + (failed ? 'FAIL' : 'ok'),\\n    failed || '',\\n    'state ' + JSON.stringify(info),\\n    'errorCount ' + errors.length,\\n    ...errors,\\n    '--- log ---',\\n    ...lines,\\n  ].filter(Boolean).join('\\\\n');\\n  writeFileSync(scratch + '/launch-' + n + '.log', text);\\n  results.push({ n, failed, info, errors: errors.length });\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\nconst phoneLines = [];\\n\",\"total_lines\":124}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-10","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→/** Four hub scenarios, one browser at a time, against the copied game. */\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\nconst site = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/.site';\\n10→const flags = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\\nconst scenarios = [\\n  'players=2&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave',\\n  'players=2&auto=1&scenario=server',\\n];\\n\\nconst srv = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: site });\\nconst port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n20→  const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('server did not print a port')), 8000);\\n  const on = (buf) => {\\n    const m = String(buf).match(/port (\\\\d+)/);\\n    if (m) { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(m[1]); }\\n  };\\n  srv.stderr.on('data', on);\\n  srv.stdout.on('data', on);\\n  srv.on('exit', (code) => reject(new Error('server exited ' + code)));\\n});\\n\\n30→const lines = ['server pid ' + srv.pid + ' port ' + port];\\nconst title = await (await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/game.html')).text();\\nconst found = (title.match(/<title>([^<]*)<\\\\/title>/) || [])[1] || 'MISSING';\\nlines.push('page title ' + found);\\n\\nconst out = [];\\nfor (const query of scenarios) {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  const notes = [];\\n40→  page.on('console', (msg) => { if (msg.type() === 'error') notes.push(msg.text()); });\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => notes.push('pageerror ' + err.message));\\n  const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + query;\\n  let result = null;\\n  try {\\n    await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000 });\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 120000 });\\n    result = await page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      complete: document.body.dataset.complete,\\n      pass: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.pass,\\n50→      checks: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.checks,\\n    }));\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    result = { complete: false, pass: false, error: String(err && err.message || err), notes };\\n  }\\n  out.push({ query, result });\\n  const failed = (result.checks || []).filter((c) => !c.pass);\\n  lines.push('SCENARIO ' + query);\\n  lines.push('complete ' + result.complete + ' pass ' + result.pass + (result.error ? ' error ' + result.error : ''));\\n  for (const c of failed) lines.push('FAIL ' + c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''));\\n60→  if (!failed.length && result.checks) lines.push('checks ' + result.checks.length + ' all passed');\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\nwriteFileSync(scratch + '/hub.log', lines.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n\\\\n' + JSON.stringify(out, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(lines.join('\\\\n'));\\nsrv.kill('SIGTERM');\\nawait new Promise((r) => srv.on('exit', r));\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→/** Four hub scenarios, one browser at a time, against the copied game. */\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\nconst site = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/.site';\\n10→const flags = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\\nconst scenarios = [\\n  'players=2&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave',\\n  'players=2&auto=1&scenario=server',\\n];\\n\\nconst srv = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: site });\\nconst port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n20→  const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('server did not print a port')), 8000);\\n  const on = (buf) => {\\n    const m = String(buf).match(/port (\\\\d+)/);\\n    if (m) { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(m[1]); }\\n  };\\n  srv.stderr.on('data', on);\\n  srv.stdout.on('data', on);\\n  srv.on('exit', (code) => reject(new Error('server exited ' + code)));\\n});\\n\\n30→const lines = ['server pid ' + srv.pid + ' port ' + port];\\nconst title = await (await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/game.html')).text();\\nconst found = (title.match(/<title>([^<]*)<\\\\/title>/) || [])[1] || 'MISSING';\\nlines.push('page title ' + found);\\n\\nconst out = [];\\nfor (const query of scenarios) {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  const notes = [];\\n40→  page.on('console', (msg) => { if (msg.type() === 'error') notes.push(msg.text()); });\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => notes.push('pageerror ' + err.message));\\n  const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + query;\\n  let result = null;\\n  try {\\n    await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000 });\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 120000 });\\n    result = await page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      complete: document.body.dataset.complete,\\n      pass: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.pass,\\n50→      checks: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.checks,\\n    }));\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    result = { complete: false, pass: false, error: String(err && err.message || err), notes };\\n  }\\n  out.push({ query, result });\\n  const failed = (result.checks || []).filter((c) => !c.pass);\\n  lines.push('SCENARIO ' + query);\\n  lines.push('complete ' + result.complete + ' pass ' + result.pass + (result.error ? ' error ' + result.error : ''));\\n  for (const c of failed) lines.push('FAIL ' + c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''));\\n60→  if (!failed.length && result.checks) lines.push('checks ' + result.checks.length + ' all passed');\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\nwriteFileSync(scratch + '/hub.log', lines.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n\\\\n' + JSON.stringify(out, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(lines.join('\\\\n'));\\nsrv.kill('SIGTERM');\\nawait new Promise((r) => srv.on('exit', r));\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/hub.mjs\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"/** Four hub scenarios, one browser at a time, against the copied game. */\\nimport { spawn } from 'node:child_process';\\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\\nimport { writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\\nconst require = createRequire('/home/micha/dev/my-3d2dge/package.json');\\nconst { chromium } = require('playwright');\\n\\nconst scratch = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer';\\nconst site = '/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/.site';\\nconst flags = ['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'];\\nconst scenarios = [\\n  'players=2&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1',\\n  'players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave',\\n  'players=2&auto=1&scenario=server',\\n];\\n\\nconst srv = spawn('python3', ['-u', '-m', 'http.server', '0', '--bind', '127.0.0.1'], { cwd: site });\\nconst port = await new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\\n  const timer = setTimeout(() => reject(new Error('server did not print a port')), 8000);\\n  const on = (buf) => {\\n    const m = String(buf).match(/port (\\\\d+)/);\\n    if (m) { clearTimeout(timer); resolve(m[1]); }\\n  };\\n  srv.stderr.on('data', on);\\n  srv.stdout.on('data', on);\\n  srv.on('exit', (code) => reject(new Error('server exited ' + code)));\\n});\\n\\nconst lines = ['server pid ' + srv.pid + ' port ' + port];\\nconst title = await (await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/game.html')).text();\\nconst found = (title.match(/<title>([^<]*)<\\\\/title>/) || [])[1] || 'MISSING';\\nlines.push('page title ' + found);\\n\\nconst out = [];\\nfor (const query of scenarios) {\\n  const browser = await chromium.launch({ headless: true, args: flags });\\n  const page = await browser.newPage({ viewport: { width: 1280, height: 720 } });\\n  const notes = [];\\n  page.on('console', (msg) => { if (msg.type() === 'error') notes.push(msg.text()); });\\n  page.on('pageerror', (err) => notes.push('pageerror ' + err.message));\\n  const url = 'http://127.0.0.1:' + port + '/harness.html?game=game.html&' + query;\\n  let result = null;\\n  try {\\n    await page.goto(url, { waitUntil: 'domcontentloaded', timeout: 30000 });\\n    await page.waitForFunction(() => document.body.dataset.complete === 'true', null, { timeout: 120000 });\\n    result = await page.evaluate(() => ({\\n      complete: document.body.dataset.complete,\\n      pass: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.pass,\\n      checks: window.__hubCheck && window.__hubCheck.checks,\\n    }));\\n  } catch (err) {\\n    result = { complete: false, pass: false, error: String(err && err.message || err), notes };\\n  }\\n  out.push({ query, result });\\n  const failed = (result.checks || []).filter((c) => !c.pass);\\n  lines.push('SCENARIO ' + query);\\n  lines.push('complete ' + result.complete + ' pass ' + result.pass + (result.error ? ' error ' + result.error : ''));\\n  for (const c of failed) lines.push('FAIL ' + c.name + ' ' + (c.detail || ''));\\n  if (!failed.length && result.checks) lines.push('checks ' + result.checks.length + ' all passed');\\n  await browser.close();\\n}\\n\\nwriteFileSync(scratch + '/hub.log', lines.join('\\\\n') + '\\\\n\\\\n' + JSON.stringify(out, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(lines.join('\\\\n'));\\nsrv.kill('SIGTERM');\\nawait new Promise((r) => srv.on('exit', r));\\n\",\"total_lines\":67}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-11","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"990→\\nTest as much as you like with headless tools. **One command:** `node tests/run.mjs`. It prints only failures and a one-line count, like `412 passed, 0 failed, 3 suites unchanged`. To rerun only after changing covered code, it hashes each suite's covered files into `tests/.stamps.json` and skips unchanged suites unless given `--all`. `--only <suite>` runs one. **Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.** Log what testing catches in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\\n**Suites:**\\n\\n1. **`static` (Node):** in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string in `src/content/` uses only the font's characters; every model passes `checkModel`, every texture `validateTexture`; every `Song` parses; every sound renders non-silent; every mission's site, tag, line and buddy resolves; every `TUNING` key has a slider or a reason.\\n\\n2. **`systems` (Node, `Engine.headless`, driven by `e.step` and actions):**\\n   - fire head speed 2-5 m/s, can't cross a road without strong wind, burnt can't re-burn, regrowth, save round-trip of the grid\\n   - wear math and jam frequency against the formula; jam blocks fire; reload clears it; gun falls apart at 0\\n1000→   - hit zones; syrette; surgery; down-with-buddy, down-without\\n   - fever: tablet clears it, ignoring collapses and costs stones\\n   - perception by stance and night; pass exemption; soldier burn panic\\n   - vehicle drive to waypoint, damage thresholds, repair, explode\\n   - map up while driving; cursor sets the waypoint\\n   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\\n   - pause (`timeScale` 0), menus by pad, by keyboard, by mouse hover and click\\n   - device switch changes `prompts` glyphs; Xbox setting; settings persistence; music 0.1\\n   - sliders and Reset; attract starts at frame 601 with no input, not before; any input exits; saves untouched; touch gate state with `matchMedia` stubbed\\n   - round rules (solo session): bank, drop, revive, time-up finish\\n1010→\\n3. **`playthrough` (Node):** a bot plays M0 through both endings, using `dev.teleport` between objectives but real actions for every objective (drive the truck, burn the tanks, plant the charge, choose at the buddy). It runs with god mode on and with buddies alive, and once with one buddy dead. After each mission, assert the world state and Ledger. This is the most important test.\\n\\n4. **`replay` (Node):** record one mission segment, replay it, compare `engine.fingerprint()`.\\n\\n5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\\n   `['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']`.\\n   Check:\\n   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\\n   - `AIHub.active` false\\n1020→   - title reached; mouse hover moves focus; click activates\\n   - pad stub via `addInitScript` (`navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`); keyboard flows\\n   - sound by `OfflineAudioContext` rendering of `renderSound` output, or an `AnalyserNode` on `audio.context` after a gesture\\n   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\\n\\n6. **`hub` (Playwright + a server you started):** copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port, kill it by its PID at the end), confirm the page's `<title>`, then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>` and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, passing when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true:\\n   - `players=2&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\\n   - `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server`\\n1030→   Run them one at a time. They take about 15 s each here. Print `__hubCheck.checks` entries that failed.\\n\\n7. **`link` (Playwright, two pages of one context on `file://`):** two windows on `linkSession` play a round to its end, with a shared fire, a shared case, and same standings.\\n\\n**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\\n\\n**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\\n\\n---\\n\\n1040→## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\",\"content_concise\":\"990→\\nTest as much as you like with headless tools. **One command:** `node tests/run.mjs`. It prints only failures and a one-line count, like `412 passed, 0 failed, 3 suites unchanged`. To rerun only after changing covered code, it hashes each suite's covered files into `tests/.stamps.json` and skips unchanged suites unless given `--all`. `--only <suite>` runs one. **Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.** Log what testing catches in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\\n**Suites:**\\n\\n1. **`static` (Node):** in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string in `src/content/` uses only the font's characters; every model passes `checkModel`, every texture `validateTexture`; every `Song` parses; every sound renders non-silent; every mission's site, tag, line and buddy resolves; every `TUNING` key has a slider or a reason.\\n\\n2. **`systems` (Node, `Engine.headless`, driven by `e.step` and actions):**\\n   - fire head speed 2-5 m/s, can't cross a road without strong wind, burnt can't re-burn, regrowth, save round-trip of the grid\\n   - wear math and jam frequency against the formula; jam blocks fire; reload clears it; gun falls apart at 0\\n1000→   - hit zones; syrette; surgery; down-with-buddy, down-without\\n   - fever: tablet clears it, ignoring collapses and costs stones\\n   - perception by stance and night; pass exemption; soldier burn panic\\n   - vehicle drive to waypoint, damage thresholds, repair, explode\\n   - map up while driving; cursor sets the waypoint\\n   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\\n   - pause (`timeScale` 0), menus by pad, by keyboard, by mouse hover and click\\n   - device switch changes `prompts` glyphs; Xbox setting; settings persistence; music 0.1\\n   - sliders and Reset; attract starts at frame 601 with no input, not before; any input exits; saves untouched; touch gate state with `matchMedia` stubbed\\n   - round rules (solo session): bank, drop, revive, time-up finish\\n1010→\\n3. **`playthrough` (Node):** a bot plays M0 through both endings, using `dev.teleport` between objectives but real actions for every objective (drive the truck, burn the tanks, plant the charge, choose at the buddy). It runs with god mode on and with buddies alive, and once with one buddy dead. After each mission, assert the world state and Ledger. This is the most important test.\\n\\n4. **`replay` (Node):** record one mission segment, replay it, compare `engine.fingerprint()`.\\n\\n5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\\n   `['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']`.\\n   Check:\\n   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\\n   - `AIHub.active` false\\n1020→   - title reached; mouse hover moves focus; click activates\\n   - pad stub via `addInitScript` (`navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`); keyboard flows\\n   - sound by `OfflineAudioContext` rendering of `renderSound` output, or an `AnalyserNode` on `audio.context` after a gesture\\n   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\\n\\n6. **`hub` (Playwright + a server you started):** copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port, kill it by its PID at the end), confirm the page's `<title>`, then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>` and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, passing when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true:\\n   - `players=2&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\\n   - `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server`\\n1030→   Run them one at a time. They take about 15 s each here. Print `__hubCheck.checks` entries that failed.\\n\\n7. **`link` (Playwright, two pages of one context on `file://`):** two windows on `linkSession` play a round to its end, with a shared fire, a shared case, and same standings.\\n\\n**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\\n\\n**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\\n\\n---\\n\\n1040→## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":990,\"limit\":60,\"raw_output\":\"\\nTest as much as you like with headless tools. **One command:** `node tests/run.mjs`. It prints only failures and a one-line count, like `412 passed, 0 failed, 3 suites unchanged`. To rerun only after changing covered code, it hashes each suite's covered files into `tests/.stamps.json` and skips unchanged suites unless given `--all`. `--only <suite>` runs one. **Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.** Log what testing catches in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\\n**Suites:**\\n\\n1. **`static` (Node):** in `src/`: no `Math.random`; no `TODO`, `FIXME`, `placeholder`, `stub`, `coming soon`. Every string in `src/content/` uses only the font's characters; every model passes `checkModel`, every texture `validateTexture`; every `Song` parses; every sound renders non-silent; every mission's site, tag, line and buddy resolves; every `TUNING` key has a slider or a reason.\\n\\n2. **`systems` (Node, `Engine.headless`, driven by `e.step` and actions):**\\n   - fire head speed 2-5 m/s, can't cross a road without strong wind, burnt can't re-burn, regrowth, save round-trip of the grid\\n   - wear math and jam frequency against the formula; jam blocks fire; reload clears it; gun falls apart at 0\\n   - hit zones; syrette; surgery; down-with-buddy, down-without\\n   - fever: tablet clears it, ignoring collapses and costs stones\\n   - perception by stance and night; pass exemption; soldier burn panic\\n   - vehicle drive to waypoint, damage thresholds, repair, explode\\n   - map up while driving; cursor sets the waypoint\\n   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\\n   - pause (`timeScale` 0), menus by pad, by keyboard, by mouse hover and click\\n   - device switch changes `prompts` glyphs; Xbox setting; settings persistence; music 0.1\\n   - sliders and Reset; attract starts at frame 601 with no input, not before; any input exits; saves untouched; touch gate state with `matchMedia` stubbed\\n   - round rules (solo session): bank, drop, revive, time-up finish\\n\\n3. **`playthrough` (Node):** a bot plays M0 through both endings, using `dev.teleport` between objectives but real actions for every objective (drive the truck, burn the tanks, plant the charge, choose at the buddy). It runs with god mode on and with buddies alive, and once with one buddy dead. After each mission, assert the world state and Ledger. This is the most important test.\\n\\n4. **`replay` (Node):** record one mission segment, replay it, compare `engine.fingerprint()`.\\n\\n5. **`browser` (Playwright, one Chromium):** the built single file on `file://`, 1920×1080, with these flags (the ones `check.mjs` uses; correct frames came from them):\\n   `['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']`.\\n   Check:\\n   - no page, console, game or GPU errors; backend WebGPU\\n   - `AIHub.active` false\\n   - title reached; mouse hover moves focus; click activates\\n   - pad stub via `addInitScript` (`navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`); keyboard flows\\n   - sound by `OfflineAudioContext` rendering of `renderSound` output, or an `AnalyserNode` on `audio.context` after a gesture\\n   - a phone profile in Chromium (Playwright's `iPhone 14` device, dropping its default browser type, then tap with `page.touchscreen`): shows the notice and Settings, tap opens Settings, attract runs\\n\\n6. **`hub` (Playwright + a server you started):** copy the built file to `tests/.site/game.html` beside a copy of `vendor/hub/*` (the harness only loads same-origin pages), serve that folder on `127.0.0.1` with an OS-picked port (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port, kill it by its PID at the end), confirm the page's `<title>`, then for each scenario open `harness.html?game=game.html&<scenario>` and wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, passing when `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true:\\n   - `players=2&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`\\n   - `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`\\n   - `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server`\\n   Run them one at a time. They take about 15 s each here. Print `__hubCheck.checks` entries that failed.\\n\\n7. **`link` (Playwright, two pages of one context on `file://`):** two windows on `linkSession` play a round to its end, with a shared fire, a shared case, and same standings.\\n\\n**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\\n\\n**Stand-ins for what this computer lacks** (your brief; runs have no display, so everything here is headless): a pad stub, Playwright phone profiles, Web Audio measurement, two pages for a second player, WebKit iPhone only as a rough touch-layout check (the engine needs WebGPU, so expect its failure message and test the notice logic with Chromium's phone profile), and 1920×1080 screenshots for the TV view.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-12","content":"{\"type\":\"BackgroundTaskStarted\",\"task_id\":\"2058257f-9003-482b-9aa2-05ab09822aa5\",\"task_type\":\"bash\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-8bcbf7c1-4737-4cd1-ba8e-2d558f86170a-12.log\",\"status\":\"running\",\"command\":\"cd \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917\\\" && node tests/run.mjs --all > \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/tests-all.log\\\" 2>&1; echo EXIT:$?; tail -n 30 \\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/tests-all.log\\\"\",\"su