mond mine. A truce holds at the railway town of **Mile Forty**, because both armies do their shopping there.\"},{\"line_number\":65,\"content\":\"- **Tibor** sells guns from a rail shed. Everything he sells has been returned at least once.\"},{\"line_number\":290,\"content\":\"| Mile Forty | (0, 40) | Truce town, no-fire zone radius 70 until mission M7: inside it your gun is slung and won't fire, and nobody shoots. Station, clinic, Tibor's shed, bar, market, notice board |\"},{\"line_number\":422,\"content\":\"**Slots:** melee (always), sidearm, main, special, plus throwables, plus a mounted MG when on a technical. You carry one of each slot, swapped at safehouse lockers or by picking guns off the ground.\"},{\"line_number\":441,\"content\":\"- Every gun has `cond` 0 to 100. Guns from a safehouse locker start at 100; guns off the ground start at 20 to 55.\"},{\"line_number\":528,\"content\":\"| Met | Freed from the cage, M2 | Tibor's shed, after M2; his plan in M4 | Clinic, after your first Mercy Run |\"},{\"line_number\":555,\"content\":\"- Spent at **Tibor's** (a gun rack and a table).\"},{\"line_number\":557,\"content\":\"**Tibor's stock:** the guns in section 8 (buying one unlocks clean copies at every locker for free, forever), bottles, charges, and four upgrades:\"},{\"line_number\":573,\"content\":\"**Trig points** (6): stone pillars on hilltops. Use one: a new note in Harrow's hand appears in your map's margin, and you can read it on the map. All six: he leaves you a clean `empire` at a locker. A note that says so.\"},{\"line_number\":611,\"content\":\"| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\"},{\"line_number\":616,\"content\":\"| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\"},{\"line_number\":635,\"content\":\"Each mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\"},{\"line_number\":645,\"content\":\"- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\"},{\"line_number\":733,\"content\":\"- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\"},{\"line_number\":802,\"content\":\"11. Tibor's rack, a line of his.\"},{\"line_number\":885,\"content\":\"- **People:** soldier (Concord, Harvest; 3 hat variants, 4 `skin` values), mercs (Ines, Dov, Mags, a silhouette each), Odile (veil, cigarette), Tibor (apron), Vance (peaked cap, medals), Ansa (headscarf, spectacles), Harrow (blanket, wide hat), Old Bakr, civilians (4 palettes), all on the rig from section 3.\"},{\"line_number\":906,\"content\":\"- **New whole-body clips:** BurnPanic (arms flailing, a stumbling run), Beg, Surrender, WoundedSit (clutching a side), DragBackward, CarryOver, DriveSit, UnjamSwear, WalkHandsTied, Shrug (Tibor), SmokeIdle (Odile), CleanRifleIdle (Vance), WriteAtDesk (Harrow), TeachPoint (Ansa).\"},{\"line_number\":1005,\"content\":\"   - tracker rate; trig note; post cleared then re-manned; rail halt; shop purchase; locker; sleep to hour; save and load\"},{\"line_number\":1034,\"content\":\"**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\"},{\"line_number\":1051,\"content\":\"| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"61c99ee6-3f53-4f07-aea0-a10ac51449e7"}
