{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_412","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Tibor screenshot shows \"REACH THE RANGER POST\" rather than the rack line. That step is later in the sequence.\n\nThe rack line was set as the subtitle, but the mission auto-advanced shortly after. The next step's text overwrote it. Vance's line was captured in the dialogue shot, yet the Tibor line itself did not appear.\n\nI'll retake the Tibor shot after the pipeline finishes, freezing time immediately after the subtitle is set so the line isn't overwritten. The surgery shot shows the FIELD SURGERY prompt and HP 20, though notes indicate HP 12 at evaluation time.\n\nThe surgery prompt and HP 20 are consistent with the nearPrompt logic. The fever subtitle overwrote HOLD STILL, which is expected. The ending, hub card, dev sliders, dialogue line, and title all look correct.\n\nI'll write exit-interview.json and PROGRESS.md now, since they don't require the browser to stay open. I'm also verifying the touch and link dependencies before finalizing the plan.\n\nExit-interview.json is being populated with source metadata. The entry records the date, Far Cry 2 as the source game, PLAN.md as the plan, and technical details including the Pixel Engine, three.js, Rapier, esbuild, and original simulation systems. Art direction specifies a pixel-art toon style at 480x270 with sand and orange land tones. Animation covers soldier rig clips, first-person hands, and mixer poses for reload, map, and surgery. Audio is entirely code-generated.\n\nAnimalese voices and music starting at ten percent are recorded. The AI Hub supports one to four players in a shared-world Cash Run via BroadcastChannel. Testing runs headless Engine.step playthroughs with Playwright Chromium and WebGPU flags across four hub scenarios. Research covers mechanics without source maps or plot. The environment is Grok CLI on Linux using xAI grok-4.7 with high reasoning effort. Usage is tracked per import. Feedback arrays include four testing answers, six engine items, and four prompt items. The AI Hub name is A Cry Too Far.\n\nThe AI Hub entry now includes a tagline, description, and tags. PROGRESS.md will be placed beside STAGE.md in the work folder, summarizing completed tasks and the fauna cut to allow compact resumption. Goal plan checkboxes need flipping. The 13-item test count in tests/ISSUES must be verified for accuracy.\n\nI'll draft the files now while the pipeline runs. Touch and link are still pending, so PROGRESS.md will note those as incomplete. The remaining checks should finish in a few more minutes.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-d2b92b90-e642-4275-888e-99c67501ab73-85","name":"get_command_or_subagent_output","input":{"task_ids":["e869d038-caee-4a4d-af2a-dcb11c9694ed"],"timeout_ms":180000}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8152,"output_tokens":1345,"cache_read_input_tokens":108928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f26548bc-400a-4f74-8fd9-066270c5fe0a"}
