{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_413","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both boots passed. The title is \"A Cry Too Far\". AIHub.active is false. No errors.\n\nShots passed with zero errors. Touch tests show exact notice, settings access, and attract mode at idle 10.03. Webkit shows gpu false and game false as expected. Link tests confirm host/join menu, both rounds, carrying round 1, both burning, and standings [[0,1]].\n\nI will check the webkit log for failure reasons. I may retake the Tibor shot because the PNG lacks his rack line shown in notes.json.\n\nThe Tibor retake will use timeScale 0 so the rack line stays visible. I will write the exit interview and PROGRESS file. I will flip the checklist. I will verify the webkit log and confirm hub.log was written. I will check that launch logs exist.\n\nThe Tibor retake will run a small Node script after advanceLines. It waits two seconds for a paint and overwrites tibor-rack.png. The night fire frame is fine as-is. The surgery image shows FIELD SURGERY correctly. I will retake Tibor and write the hand-in files in parallel.\n\nThe exit-interview can be written now because the retake does not change source. I will verify JSON with Node. PROGRESS.md will record fauna cuts and verification results. I will not add a deviations section, since fauna is not a deviation.\n\nI will flip all eight checklist boxes to checked. I will use an en dash in the players string as TASK.md suggests. I will verify the exit-interview wording and confirm no server processes remain.\n\nThe Tibor retake script will advance lines twice, then freeze time with timeScale 0. A two-second wait ensures the subtitle renders on a fresh frame before capture.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-21bc53f8-0e85-4f58-859d-37ed45079c95-86","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e1616