{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_414","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"WebKit failed as expected.\n\nStarting the hand-in files now. I'll write exit-interview.json and PROGRESS.md, then flip the plan file to mark tasks complete. I need to be careful with JSON formatting and use the write tool.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8a40d9e-92a7-4246-9dfc-58d39af88b88-88","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"export PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE=ubuntu24.04-x64 && node \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/tibor-shot.mjs\"","description":"Retake Tibor rack screenshot with clock stopped","block_until_ms":0}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8a40d9e-92a7-4246-9dfc-58d39af88b88-89","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/exit-interview.json","new_string":"{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-05 01:39:17\",\n    \"source\": \"Far Cry 2\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"first-person shooter\",\n    \"perspective\": \"first person on foot, at the wheel, and in story scenes\",\n    \"tech\": \"Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild 0.28.2. Original sim, fire grid, weapons, and missions.\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Engine pixel-art toon at 480x270. Sand, orange, and red land. Slate for Concord, orange for the Harvest Front. Green only for water and regrowth.\",\n    \"animation\": \"Engine clips on the soldier rig. First-person hands on a small rig. Mixer poses for reload, the map, and surgery.\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code songs, code effects, and no audio files. Animalese voices. Music starts at 10 percent.\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub shared-world for 1-4 players. Cash Run lasts 6 minutes. Same-computer link uses a BroadcastChannel.\",\n    \"testing\": \"node tests/run.mjs --all. Headless Engine.step playthrough. Playwright Chromium with WebGPU flags. Hub harness, four scenarios.\",\n    \"research\": \"Mechanics from the plan, not a port. No source maps, names, or plot.\",\n    \"environment\": \"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"13. Listed in tests/ISSUES.md.\",\n    \"13. Each one stopped a required path.\",\n    \"node tests/run.mjs --all. One shared engine showed the leaks.\",\n    \"A blank WebGPU screenshot. The state read is the proof.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels, and a vehicle that stays upright.\",\n    \"First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z. The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z. Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.\",\n    \"The fire grid, jams, fever, map, mission runner, and the hub round.\",\n    \"Pointer lock, timeScale pause, and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.\",\n    \"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.\",\n    \"A first-person rig that does not steal the use key or the pointer.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan names the traps and the order to cut whole features.\",\n    \"File stem spaces, and which card the harness presses Enter on.\",\n    \"One world that is a campaign, a 6 minute round, and a hub server.\",\n    \"Ship the hub check before asking for every prop in the art list.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"A Cry Too Far\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Stones, fire, and a bad contract\",\n    \"description\": \"A first-person survival shooter in the Kettle. Two factions pay you in stones to burn a firebreak you were not meant to see. Play the story alone, or carry diamond cases in Cash Run with up to four players.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Shooter\",\n    \"source\": \"Far Cry 2\",\n    \"series\": \"Far Cry\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Gamepad, keyboard, and mouse. First person on foot and in vehicles.\",\n    \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"pixel art\", \"co-op\", \"versus\", \"vehicles\", \"story\"]\n  }\n}\n","old_string":""}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f8a40d9e-92a7-4246-9dfc-58d39af88b88-90","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md","new_string":"# A Cry Too Far\n\nOriginal first-person war-zone survival shooter in the Kettle, country of the Sorrel. Factions are Concord and the Harvest Front. Title picked by `crypto.randomInt` from 50 riffs (index 1).\n\n## Hand-in\n\n- HTML, beside this file: `A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html`\n- Dev folder: `A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/`\n- `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML. Usage is `added on import`.\n- `pixel-engine.js` is the kit file and is not edited.\n\n## Cut\n\nFauna is cut (gazelles and vultures), the first item in PLAN.md §26. No menu entries, map marks, or lines remain for it. This is a cut, not a goal-plan deviation.\n\nSame-computer link is not cut. Cash Run can be hosted or joined from the cash menu over a BroadcastChannel.\n\n## What plays\n\nOne 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\n\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\n\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\n\n## Checks on this computer\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\n\n## Issues\n\nTesting caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\n","old_string":""}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1784,"output_tokens":2370,"cache_read_input_tokens":119424,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"6c37d7ba-784e-4fd8-af2b-bad2506e86ae"}
