nd stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\nTesting caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md has been created successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md has been created.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"\",\"old_line\":1,\"new_string\":\"# A Cry Too Far\\n\\nOriginal first-person war-zone survival shooter in the Kettle, country of the Sorrel. Factions are Concord and the Harvest Front. Title picked by `crypto.randomInt` from 50 riffs (index 1).\\n\\n## Hand-in\\n\\n- HTML, beside this file: `A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html`\\n- Dev folder: `A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/`\\n- `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML. Usage is `added on import`.\\n- `pixel-engine.js` is the kit file and is not edited.\\n\\n## Cut\\n\\nFauna is cut (gazelles and vultures), the first item in PLAN.md §26. No menu entries, map marks, or lines remain for it. This is a cut, not a goal-plan deviation.\\n\\nSame-computer link is not cut. Cash Run can be hosted or joined from the cash menu over a BroadcastChannel.\\n\\n## What plays\\n\\nOne 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\nTesting caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\",\"new_line\":1,\"context_before\":\"\",\"context_after\":\"\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c2df5756-3be7-4f40-929d-04f9efe95878"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_415","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Validating JSON and flipping the plan checklist.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57ba1189-7c6d-4fda-9596-9b76be3ed275-91","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"node -e '\nconst fs = require(\"fs\");\nconst p = \"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/exit-interview.json\";\nconst o = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(p, \"utf8\"));\nconst need = [\"date\",\"source\",\"plan\",\"genre\",\"perspective\",\"tech\",\"artDirection\",\"animation\",\"audio\",\"online\",\"testing\",\"research\",\"environment\",\"model\",\"usage\"];\nconst missing = need.filter(k => !(k in o.sourceInformation) || o.sourceInformation[k] === \"\");\nif (o.sourceInformation.usage !== \"added on import\") throw new Error(\"usage\");\nif (o.testingFeedback.length !== 4) throw new Error(\"testing\");\nif (o.engineFeedback.length !== 6) throw new Error(\"engine\");\nif (o.promptFeedback.length !== 4) throw new Error(\"prompt\");\nconst hub = [\"name\",\"tagline\",\"description\",\"type\",\"genre\",\"source\",\"series\",\"players\",\"controls\",\"tags\"];\nconst hmiss = hub.filter(k => o.aiHub[k] == null || o.aiHub[k] === \"\");\nif (hmiss.length) throw new Error(\"hub \" + hmiss);\nif (!Array.isArray(o.aiHub.tags) || o.aiHub.tags.length < 3) throw new Error(\"tags\");\nif (missing.length) throw new Error(\"missing \" + missing);\nconsole.log(\"json ok\", o.aiHub.name, o.testingFeedback[0]);\n'","description":"Parse exit-interview.json and check the key shape"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-57ba1189-7c6d-4fda-9596-9b76be3ed275-92","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/goal/plan.md","old_string":"- [ ] List 50 titles, pick one with a real RNG, record the list and the pick, create the dev subfolder, unzip the kit, vendor the hub client and harness, and prove `pixel-engine.js` matches the zip.\n- [ ] Scaffold the single-file build and a booting game so `file://` opens and all four hub scenarios pass. Start `PROGRESS.md`.\n- [ ] Add the basin, player locomotion, look and pointer-lock fixes, actions, device glyphs, minimal HUD, and pause. Cover them with headless tests.\n- [ ] Add weapons (wear, jam, break), hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, and fever, with the system tests in criterion 2.\n- [ ] Add the fire grid, ignition weapons, day and night, vehicles and repair, the held map, safehouses, stones, and save/load.\n- [ ] Add missions through both endings, buddies (rescue and finish-it), the Ledger, dialogue, music at 0.1, and code voices and effects. Add the bot playthrough.\n- [ ] Add title, menus, settings, the touch gate, attract, dev-mode sliders with reset, and About/Credits.\n- [ ] Finish Cash Run (host, client, solo bots, card listeners). Re-run `node tests/run.mjs --all`, the two `file://` launches, the phone-profile check, and the four hub scenarios. Write `exit-interview.json` and finish `PROGRESS.md`, including any §26 cuts.","new_string":"- [x] List 50 titles, pick one with a real RNG, record the list and the pick, create the dev subfolder, unzip the kit, vendor the hub client and harness, and prove `pixel-engine.js` matches the zip.\n- [x] Scaffold the single-file build and a booting game so `file://` opens and all four hub scenarios pass. Start `PROGRESS.md`.\n- [x] Add the basin, player locomotion, look and pointer-lock fixes, actions, device glyphs, minimal HUD, and pause. Cover them with headless tests.\n- [x] Add weapons (wear, jam, break), hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, and fever, with the system tests in criterion 2.\n- [x] Add the fire grid, ignition weapons, day and night, vehicles and repair, the held map, safehouses, stones, and save/load.\n- [x] Add missions through both endings, buddies (rescue and finish-it), the Ledger, dialogue, music at 0.1, and code voices and effects. Add the bot playthrough.\n- [x] Add title, menus, settings, the touch gate, attract, dev-mode sliders with reset, and About/Credits.\n- [x] Finish Cash Run (host, client, solo bots, card listeners). Re-run `node tests/run.mjs --all`, the two `file://` launches, the phone-profile check, and the four hub scenarios. Write `exit-interview.json` and finish `PROGRESS.md`, including any §26 cuts."}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2869,"output_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":121088,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"b2f03bc4-88ba-4e43-86a3-4500e2ae337e"}
