 the pick, create the dev subfolder, unzip the kit, vendor the hub client and harness, and prove `pixel-engine.js` matches the zip.\\n- [x] Scaffold the single-file build and a booting game so `file://` opens and all four hub scenarios pass. Start `PROGRESS.md`.\\n- [x] Add the basin, player locomotion, look and pointer-lock fixes, actions, device glyphs, minimal HUD, and pause. Cover them with headless tests.\\n- [x] Add weapons (wear, jam, break), hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, and fever, with the system tests in criterion 2.\\n- [x] Add the fire grid, ignition weapons, day and night, vehicles and repair, the held map, safehouses, stones, and save/load.\\n- [x] Add missions through both endings, buddies (rescue and finish-it), the Ledger, dialogue, music at 0.1, and code voices and effects. Add the bot playthrough.\\n- [x] Add title, menus, settings, the touch gate, attract, dev-mode sliders with reset, and About/Credits.\\n- [x] Finish Cash Run (host, client, solo bots, card listeners). Re-run `node tests/run.mjs --all`, the two `file://` launches, the phone-profile check, and the four hub scenarios. Write `exit-interview.json` and finish `PROGRESS.md`, including any §26 cuts.\",\"new_line\":37,\"context_before\":\"Follow PLAN.md §25 in order and §26 when cutting. Keep this as guidance, not a file-layout contract. Separate simulation data from meshes so headless tests never need a GPU. Put missions, weapons, sites, dialogue, tuning defaults, and model defs in plain data. Gameplay reads named actions, not raw keys. Simulate in the fixed step and draw in the frame update. Read tuning values at the moment of use. One game object owns the world; title, attract, campaign, and the round are modes, not a fresh terrain load. Guard every use of `window`, `document`, `navigator`, and `localStorage`. Randomness comes from the engine's seeded generator, forked by name. Build the single HTML the way PLAN.md §23 specifies (session script first, then hub meta tags, then the bundled module) so `file://` boots. Keep the four hub scenarios passing from the first bootable build. Log defects in the dev folder's issues note as tests catch them. Update `PROGRESS.md` at each step so a compacted context can resume.\\n\\n## Task checklist\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n## Risks / Contradictions\\n- PLAN.md §27 demands the full game and zero failing tests; §26 allows cutting whole features from the top of its list if time runs out. A cut that leaves a stub, menu entry, or map mark fails. Never-cut systems stay even if that forces a cut higher on the list.\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f6ebfd0e-62e7-46d3-befb-20e67c0d47b0"}
