s wear/jam/break, hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, fever\\n- [completed] worldsys: worldsys: Fire grid, ignition, day/night, vehicles, held map, safehouses, stones, save/load\\n- [completed] story: story: Missions through both endings, buddies, Ledger, dialogue, music, voices, bot playthrough\\n- [completed] shell: shell: Title, menus, settings, touch gate, attract, dev sliders, About/Credits\\n- [completed] cashrun: cashrun: Rebuild final HTML, re-run tests and hub, screenshots, exit-interview, PROGRESS, flip plan\\n- [completed] hub-rerun: Re-run four hub scenarios against the shipped HTML and write hub.log\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"titles: List 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create dev folder, unzip kit, vendor hub, prove pixel-engine.js match\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"scaffold: Syntax-check sim, boot headless world, wire game.js/main.js and single-file build\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"locomotion: Basin, locomotion, look, actions, glyphs, HUD, pause + headless tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"combat: Weapons wear/jam/break, hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, fever\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"worldsys: Fire grid, ignition, day/night, vehicles, held map, safehouses, stones, save/load\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"story: Missions through both endings, buddies, Ledger, dialogue, music, voices, bot playthrough\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"shell: Title, menus, settings, touch gate, attract, dev sliders, About/Credits\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"cashrun: Rebuild final HTML, re-run tests and hub, screenshots, exit-interview, PROGRESS, flip plan\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Re-run four hub scenarios against the shipped HTML and write hub.log\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"titles\":{\"content\":\"titles: List 50 titles, RNG-pick one, create dev folder, unzip kit, vendor hub, prove pixel-engine.js match\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"scaffold\":{\"content\":\"scaffold: Syntax-check sim, boot headless world, wire game.js/main.js and single-file build\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"locomotion\":{\"content\":\"locomotion: Basin, locomotion, look, actions, glyphs, HUD, pause + headless tests\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"combat\":{\"content\":\"combat: Weapons wear/jam/break, hits, soldiers, health, syrette, surgery, fever\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"worldsys\":{\"content\":\"worldsys: Fire grid, ignition, day/night, vehicles, held map, safehouses, stones, save/load\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"story\":{\"content\":\"story: Missions through both endings, buddies, Ledger, dialogue, music, voices, bot playthrough\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"shell\":{\"content\":\"shell: Title, menus, settings, touch gate, attract, dev sliders, About/Credits\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"cashrun\":{\"content\":\"cashrun: Rebuild final HTML, re-run tests and hub, screenshots, exit-interview, PROGRESS, flip plan\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"hub-rerun\":{\"content\":\"Re-run four hub scenarios against the shipped HTML and write hub.log\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"de15ce62-48f9-4454-9acd-f25564009859"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_422","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hub re-run is complete and logged.\n\nAll four scenarios passed. The page title was \"A Cry Too Far\". The server was killed by the script's PID. The final reply will be concise.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"All four hub scenarios passed on the shipped HTML. The page title was `A Cry Too Far`. Each run set `document.body.dataset.complete` to `true` and `window.__hubCheck.pass` to `true`. The server was stopped by its own PID. The log is in the scratch `hub.log`.\n\n| Scenario | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `players=2&auto=1` | complete true, pass true, 14 checks |\n| `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` | complete true, pass true, 14 checks |\n| same, plus `scenario=host-leave` | complete true, pass true, 14 checks |\n| `players=2&auto=1&scenario=server` | complete true, pass true, 15 checks |\n\n## Source Information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17\n- Source: Far Cry 2\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: first-person shooter; first person on foot, at the wheel, and in story scenes\n- Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild 0.28.2, plus the original sim, fire grid, weapons, and missions\n- Art Direction: engine pixel-art toon at 480×270; sand, orange, and red land; slate Concord and orange Harvest Front; green only for water and regrowth\n- Animation: engine clips on the soldier rig; first-person hands on a small rig; mixer poses for reload, the map, and surgery\n- Audio: code songs, code effects, no audio files; Animalese voices; music starts at 10 percent\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world, 1–4 players; Cash Run, 6 minutes; same-computer link on a BroadcastChannel\n- Testing: `node tests/run.mjs --all`; headless `Engine.step` playthrough; Playwright Chromium with WebGPU flags; hub harness, four scenarios\n- Research: mechanics from the plan, not a port; no source maps, names, or plot\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch? 13. Listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\n- How many would be game breaking? 13. Each one stopped a required path.\n- Most helpful test: `node tests/run.mjs --all`. One shared engine showed the leaks.\n- Least helpful test: a blank WebGPU screenshot. The state read is the proof.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n\n- Liked most: headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels, and a vehicle that stays upright.\n- Stuck or guessed wrong: first-person yaw 0 looks down −Z. The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z. Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.\n- Built ourselves: the fire grid, jams, fever, map, mission runner, and the hub round.\n- Hardest part of the engine: pointer lock, timeScale pause, and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.\n- Changed in the engine: none. `pixel-engine.js` is the kit file.\n- One change we would make: a first-person rig that does not steal the use key or the pointer.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n\n- Liked most: the plan names the traps and the order to cut whole features.\n- Confusing: file-stem spaces, and which card the harness presses Enter on.\n- Hardest thing: one world that is a campaign, a 6 minute round, and a hub server.\n- Change we would make: ship the hub check before asking for every prop in the art list."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":801,"output_tokens":1170,"cache_read_input_tokens":131456,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ba3084a6-5ce5-41ee-951c-a420f79c1b1c"}
