{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_427","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test file is large. I need to continue reading it and check the game implementation for real bugs.\n\nThe tests appear honest. They use real source code and headless engine steps. The runner only prints failures and a total count.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":1040,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md","offset":590,"limit":200}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-18","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":200,"limit":400}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5533,"output_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":44800,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3b3c0fd9-bf20-4ac2-b447-7467e3dfcac8"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-16","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1040→## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\\n1050→| 4 Drive | Vehicles, driving view, damage, repair, patrols, posts, train | Run a checkpoint in a pickup and break down after |\\n| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\\n| 6 Story | Mission runner, dialogue, voices, buddies, rescues, M0 to End, Ledger, endings. Playthrough suite | A bot and you both finish it |\\n| 7 Shell | Title, all menus, settings, glyph sets, About, touch gate, attract, dev mode | Every screen works by pad, keyboard and mouse |\\n| 8 Multiplayer | Sim/view puppets, host, client, sessions, Cash Run, card, solo bots, link | Hub and link suites pass with a real round |\\n| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\\n| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\\n\\n---\\n\\n1060→## 26. Cut order\\n\\nIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\\n\\n1. Fauna (vultures first).\\n2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\\n3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\\n4. Chase camera; dust weather.\\n5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\\n6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\\n1070→7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\\n8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\\n9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\\n\\nNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 27. Done, reports, coverage\\n\\n1080→**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\\n- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\\n- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\\n- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\\n- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\\n- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\\n- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\\n1090→\\n**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\\n- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \\\"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\\\".\\n\\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\\n\\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\\n\\n1100→**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\\n\\n| Brief item | Section |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\\n1110→| Art direction: native base, new assets, library for generic props | 20 |\\n| Animation: native base, new animations | 21 |\\n| Audio in code, Animalese voices, music 10% | 22 |\\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 19 |\\n| Dev subfolder, what not to read, shared ports and processes | 4, 24 |\\n| Performance out of scope | 3 |\\n| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\\n| Effort | Yours to spend; 25 and 26 order it |\\n| This computer and its stand-ins | 3, 4, 24 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\",\"content_concise\":\"1040→## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\\n1050→| 4 Drive | Vehicles, driving view, damage, repair, patrols, posts, train | Run a checkpoint in a pickup and break down after |\\n| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\\n| 6 Story | Mission runner, dialogue, voices, buddies, rescues, M0 to End, Ledger, endings. Playthrough suite | A bot and you both finish it |\\n| 7 Shell | Title, all menus, settings, glyph sets, About, touch gate, attract, dev mode | Every screen works by pad, keyboard and mouse |\\n| 8 Multiplayer | Sim/view puppets, host, client, sessions, Cash Run, card, solo bots, link | Hub and link suites pass with a real round |\\n| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\\n| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\\n\\n---\\n\\n1060→## 26. Cut order\\n\\nIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\\n\\n1. Fauna (vultures first).\\n2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\\n3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\\n4. Chase camera; dust weather.\\n5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\\n6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\\n1070→7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\\n8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\\n9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\\n\\nNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 27. Done, reports, coverage\\n\\n1080→**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\\n- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\\n- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\\n- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\\n- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\\n- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\\n- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\\n1090→\\n**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\\n- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \\\"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\\\".\\n\\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\\n\\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\\n\\n1100→**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\\n\\n| Brief item | Section |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\\n1110→| Art direction: native base, new assets, library for generic props | 20 |\\n| Animation: native base, new animations | 21 |\\n| Audio in code, Animalese voices, music 10% | 22 |\\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 19 |\\n| Dev subfolder, what not to read, shared ports and processes | 4, 24 |\\n| Performance out of scope | 3 |\\n| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\\n| Effort | Yours to spend; 25 and 26 order it |\\n| This computer and its stand-ins | 3, 4, 24 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1040,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"## 25. Build order\\n\\nEach step ends with a playable build and passing tests, and leaves nothing half-done. Do them in order. Write sound, feedback and tests with each feature rather than at the end.\\n\\n| Step | Do | Done when |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| 0 Pipeline | Pick the title. Unzip the kit. Download `vendor/`. `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` with the hub suite. A blank `createGame()` with a shared-world round that does nothing | Single file opens on `file://`; **all four hub scenarios pass from day one**. Keep them passing |\\n| 1 Walk | Terrain, roads, river, sky, wind, grass, trees. Player, `installLook`, actions, pad codes, device tracking, HUD basics, pause | You can walk the Kettle by pad or mouse |\\n| 2 Shoot | Hands rig and `tractor` first, soldier rig, one AI squad, damage, health, syrette, wear, jam, reload. SFX for each | A fight at P2 is fun on its own. Add the other guns |\\n| 3 Burn | Fire grid, flare, bottle, flamethrower, scars, regrowth, soldier panic, day and night. Fire sounds | Lighting a field at night makes you stop and watch |\\n| 4 Drive | Vehicles, driving view, damage, repair, patrols, posts, train | Run a checkpoint in a pickup and break down after |\\n| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\\n| 6 Story | Mission runner, dialogue, voices, buddies, rescues, M0 to End, Ledger, endings. Playthrough suite | A bot and you both finish it |\\n| 7 Shell | Title, all menus, settings, glyph sets, About, touch gate, attract, dev mode | Every screen works by pad, keyboard and mouse |\\n| 8 Multiplayer | Sim/view puppets, host, client, sessions, Cash Run, card, solo bots, link | Hub and link suites pass with a real round |\\n| 9 Polish | All music, ambience, feel, art passes, balance with the sliders, screenshots | You'd show it to someone |\\n| 10 Ship | Final build, About pages, exit interview, chat reply, `node tests/run.mjs --all` | Section 27 is all true |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 26. Cut order\\n\\nIf you can't finish everything, cut whole things from the top of this list. Don't leave stubs, and remove all traces (menu entries, map marks, lines). Keep every feature in the demo reachable and shown.\\n\\n1. Fauna (vultures first).\\n2. Same-computer link (keep hub and solo).\\n3. The game's own hub card (use the hub's card: `card:false`).\\n4. Chase camera; dust weather.\\n5. Mercy Runs after the first; trig points down to 3; cases down to 6.\\n6. M5 (Mags offers her alternate plan in M6 instead: get the field workers out first, for less pay).\\n7. M4 (give the tracker in M3; use the MG in M7; Dov joins at the bar).\\n8. M8 (the column just starts walking after M7).\\n9. Shared-world → ghost → parallel (section 19).\\n\\nNever cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and native mouse, touch gate, the hub check, music at 10%, the voices.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 27. Done, reports, coverage\\n\\n**Done means:** every line below is true and you've checked it.\\n- [ ] Your title, chosen by the brief's procedure, appears on the title screen and in `<title>`.\\n- [ ] The one HTML file runs from `file://` with nothing else beside it.\\n- [ ] `node tests/run.mjs --all` reports 0 failed.\\n- [ ] All four hub scenarios pass, and the game still runs outside a session.\\n- [ ] You finished the game yourself by bot, both endings.\\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features anywhere.\\n- [ ] Every screen shows native prompts for pad (PlayStation and Xbox glyphs) and keyboard/mouse.\\n- [ ] You looked at the screenshots.\\n- [ ] `pixel-engine.js` is byte-identical to the copy in the kit's zip (keep the zip in `vendor/` and compare in the `static` suite).\\n\\n**About and Credits screen** (in-game, paged, reached from main menu and pause; text in `src/content/about.js`). Your brief marks this as critical. It must show:\\n- **Source Information,** with every field your brief lists: Date (from your brief), Source (Far Cry 2), Plan (the file name of this plan as you received it), Genre and Perspective, Tech (engine and its version, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild, your additions), Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model (from your brief), and Usage: *added on import*. Write \\\"unknown\\\" for anything you can't confirm.\\n- **Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback:** your brief's questions and your honest answers, in order, each on its own page. Don't estimate cost.\\n- **Credits:** Pixel Engine (MIT), three.js (MIT), Rapier (Apache-2.0), the AI Hub session client, and \\\"Inspired by Far Cry 2; not affiliated\\\".\\n\\n**Your final chat reply** repeats the same Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback.\\n\\n**The exit interview file** your brief specifies goes beside the HTML, in the exact JSON shape it gives, every value filled, and must parse. Suggested catalogue values: type `Game`; genre `Shooter`; source `Far Cry 2`; series `Far Cry`; players `1–4`; tags such as `first-person`, `pixel art`, `co-op`, `versus`, `vehicles`, `story`; the name is your title.\\n\\n**Where each line of your brief is covered:**\\n\\n| Brief item | Section |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Source, original game, capture world, characters, themes, tone | 1, 2, 15 |\\n| Genre, perspective | 1 |\\n| Title by random pick (left to you) | top, 25 |\\n| Research | 3 (done for you; research more if you want) |\\n| Single HTML package, CDN allowance, bundle into root | 23 |\\n| Engine kit kept as shipped, systems added on top | 3, 4, 23 |\\n| Art direction: native base, new assets, library for generic props | 20 |\\n| Animation: native base, new animations | 21 |\\n| Audio in code, Animalese voices, music 10% | 22 |\\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 19 |\\n| Dev subfolder, what not to read, shared ports and processes | 4, 24 |\\n| Performance out of scope | 3 |\\n| Testing: headless, scripted playthrough, one command, screenshots only when needed, no review subagents | 24 |\\n| Effort | Yours to spend; 25 and 26 order it |\\n| This computer and its stand-ins | 3, 4, 24 |\\n| Feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure for later build-out | 4, 14, 25 |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-17","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"590→## 14. Missions\\n\\n**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\\n```js\\n{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\\n  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\\n  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\\n  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\\n          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\\n          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\\n600→          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\\n```\\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\\n\\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\\n\\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\\n610→| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \\\"feeds the Harvest\\\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\\n620→\\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\\n\\n**Ending cards:**\\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\\n\\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\\n\\n---\\n630→\\n## 15. Writing\\n\\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\\n\\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\\n\\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\\n\\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\\n640→\\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\\n650→- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\\n660→\\n---\\n\\n## 16. UI and UX\\n\\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\\n\\n**Layout rules:**\\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\\n670→- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\\n- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\\n\\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\\n680→- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\\n\\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\\n690→| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\\n| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\\n700→| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\\n\\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\\n\\n710→**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\\n\\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\\n\\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\\n720→- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\\n\\n**Screens:**\\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\\n730→- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\\n\\n740→**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 17. Dev mode\\n\\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\\n\\n| Tab | Contents |\\n| --- | --- |\\n750→| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\\n\\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\\n\\n760→| Slider | Default | Range |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n770→| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\\n780→| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\\n\\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 18. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\",\"content_concise\":\"590→## 14. Missions\\n\\n**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\\n```js\\n{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\\n  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\\n  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\\n  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\\n          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\\n          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\\n600→          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\\n```\\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\\n\\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\\n\\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\\n610→| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \\\"feeds the Harvest\\\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\\n620→\\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\\n\\n**Ending cards:**\\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\\n\\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\\n\\n---\\n630→\\n## 15. Writing\\n\\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\\n\\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\\n\\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\\n\\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\\n640→\\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\\n650→- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\\n660→\\n---\\n\\n## 16. UI and UX\\n\\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\\n\\n**Layout rules:**\\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\\n670→- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\\n- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\\n\\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\\n680→- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\\n\\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\\n690→| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\\n| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\\n700→| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\\n\\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\\n\\n710→**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\\n\\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\\n\\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\\n720→- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\\n\\n**Screens:**\\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\\n730→- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\\n\\n740→**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 17. Dev mode\\n\\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\\n\\n| Tab | Contents |\\n| --- | --- |\\n750→| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\\n\\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\\n\\n760→| Slider | Default | Range |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n770→| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\\n780→| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\\n\\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 18. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":590,\"limit\":200,\"raw_output\":\"## 14. Missions\\n\\n**Format** (`src/content/missions.js`), a sketch:\\n```js\\n{ id:'m3', title:'FUEL FOR THE PEACE', giver:'vance', requires:['m2'], pay:15, wind:{ dir:[-0.8,-0.6], speed:5 },\\n  brief:['vance:m3.brief.1','vance:m3.brief.2'],\\n  alt:{ buddy:'ines', call:'ines:m3.alt', bonus:5, steps:[ {do:'steal',tag:'tanker',text:'TAKE THE TANKER AT P3'} ] },\\n  steps:[ {do:'goto',site:'east-siding',r:140,text:'REACH THE SIDING'},\\n          {do:'destroy',tag:'fuel-tank',n:3,text:'BURN THE TANKS'},\\n          {do:'leave',site:'east-siding',r:220,text:'GET OUT'},\\n          {do:'report',to:'vance',text:'REPORT TO VANCE'} ],\\n  onDone:[ {burnStrip:'A'}, {ledger:{paid:15}} ] }\\n```\\n**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\\n\\nContracts are taken in person (a short FP scene: the camera holds on the giver, subtitles, then Accept or Not Yet) or through the notice board in Mile Forty. After M2, the order within M3/M4 and M5/M6 is free; M5 needs M3 and M6 needs M4 (one faction's path each); M7 needs all four. Acts, for the fever's pace: act 1 is M0 to M2, act 2 is M3 to M6, act 3 is M7 onward.\\n\\n| # | Title (giver) | Length, time | What happens | Teaches | Alternate plan | Consequence, pay |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\\n| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\\n| M2 | A Cage at the Post (Tibor) | 7 min, best at night | Ines owes Tibor. She's in a cage at Ranger Post (8 Concord, a tower). Scout with the monocular, cross in grass, cane knife, or go loud. Open the cage (hold). Ines fights her way out with you. She explains rescues by doing one if you fall | Monocular, stealth, melee, sleep to choose the hour, safehouse capture, buddy | - | Ranger Post safehouse, 8 stones, Ines |\\n| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\\n| M4 | Seed Money (Ansa) | 7 min | Payroll convoy (2 technicals, a truck) crosses the Salt Pan on a loop. Stop it, take the case. It flies out when the truck blows: you get the tracker to find it in the salt | Vehicle combat, MG, tracker | Dov: plant his charges on the bridge, detonate as the convoy crosses | 20 stones (+5), tracker, Dov |\\n| M5 | The Water Question (Vance) | 7 min | Destroy the pump on the Mercy, because Three Wells \\\"feeds the Harvest\\\" | Charges, defending, moral cost | Mags: first open the bypass and hold the pump house for 60 s, so the cistern fills | Without alt: Three Wells empties, a line of people walks the road to the clinic, its huts go dark, Odile refuses tablets until you do a Mercy Run free. With alt: village stays, pay 10 instead of 20 |\\n| M6 | The Long Field (Ansa) | 9 min, forced night | Burn the Concord's crop and its ammo bunker. Your highest-trust buddy comes along (with no buddy alive, a Harvest guide named Pell does). At about 70% the wind turns (scripted) and they go down on fire: **Syrette or Finish It** | Night fire, buddy choice | The mission itself | Scar B, 25 stones, the Ledger's first hard line |\\n| M7 | The Cut (Harrow's note) | 10 min | A note at your safehouse: *You have drawn well. Come and see.* Truce collapses: both armies fight for the mine. Reach the sluice house through crossfire and wildfire, take his ledger. In it: *One contractor, paid in advance, to walk the Kettle.* Signed by him | Three-way fight, technical MG, big fire | A surviving buddy calls: they hold the east road if you go in from the pit side (no bonus stones, +1 trust) | Scar C. Truce over: Mile Forty loses its no-fire zone, Tibor moves his stock into safehouse lockers. Act 2 fever pace |\\n| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\\n| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\\n| End | The Pass | 3 to 4 min | Either walk to the Pass alone, or take the sheet to the column and hold behind them. Surviving buddies arrive (200 HP, real AI, last lines), with pursuit from both armies. Rain stops. The last grass is yours to light | Everything | - | Ending card, Ledger, credits, title. Continue returns to the last safehouse for free roam |\\n\\n**Story scars.** On completing M3, M6 and M7, call `burnStrip('A'|'B'|'C')` so the arc exists whatever the player actually burned: A from East Siding west to the Cut, C across the Cut, B from the Cut west through the Long Field to the Pass road. The player sees it first in M9.\\n\\n**Ending cards:**\\n- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\\n- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\\n\\n**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 15. Writing\\n\\n**Voice.** Weary, literary and exact. Short declarative sentences. Euphemism as cruelty. Gallows humour without a wink. Nobody explains the theme. Nobody is your friend without a price. People are tired, and they're smart. Think of a war correspondent who stopped filing years ago. Don't quote real authors, and don't imitate the source's lines.\\n\\nEach mission gets 8 to 15 spoken lines in this voice. Each character has a tic: **Vance** invoices (*conclude, regrettable, the matter of*). **Ansa** corrects grammar. **Odile** counts things. **Tibor** talks about returns. **Bakr** tells you what stations used to be called. **Ines** owes people, or they owe her. **Dov** tells a three-sentence story that ends badly. **Mags** narrates what she is doing to you. **Harrow** writes like a surveyor's notebook.\\n\\nAll game text must be in the HUD font's character set. Subtitle lines stay under 60 characters, two lines at most: split long sentences across lines in sequence.\\n\\nUse these lines verbatim, and write the rest to match:\\n\\n- **Bakr, M0:** *Forty miles of track and not one station that remembers its name.* / *They paint the signs over. Whoever won last.* / *You have the look of a man who read about this place. Reading is a good way to visit.* / *Up there they will ask you which side. Say yes.*\\n- **Odile:** *Three tablets. The fourth you pay for. I do not mean in stones.* / *I do not need you to be good. I need you to be on time.* / *Sixty-one beds. Forty blankets. You are the math.*\\n- **Vance:** *We do not burn villages. We conclude them.* / *The water question has been a great sorrow to this office.* / *Your invoice will be honoured, regrettably.*\\n- **Ansa:** *You said less people. Fewer. Fewer people. It will matter by the end of the month.* / *Burn the field. A hungry man learns to read the wind.*\\n- **Tibor:** *Everything on this rack has been returned at least once.* / *It fires. If you want it to fire twice, that is a different price.*\\n- **Ines:** *I flew for both of them. Neither paid. Get in.* / *You owe me a truck. You owe me several trucks.*\\n- **Dov:** *Two fingers I left in this country. I came back to see what they are doing.* / *A man asked me to mine his own road, so he would know where it was safe. He was right for a week.*\\n- **Mags:** *Hold still. No, you can't feel that. No, that's normal. Hold still.* / *Not today. Today you owe me money.*\\n- **A burning buddy:** *Don't let it be the fire. Please. Not the fire.*\\n- **Barks:** *There! In the grass!* / *Who lit that?* / *It's stuck! It's stuck again!* / *Leave him, he's already gone.*\\n- **Harrow's margin notes,** one per trig point, in order:\\n  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\\n  2. *I drew the river where the Company wanted it. The river was slow to comply, but it came round.*\\n  3. *Both armies buy from me. The Concord pays on time. The Harvest pays in grain and tears. I have eaten better on the tears.*\\n  4. *You will have noticed that you follow roads. I drew those too.*\\n  5. *Grass is the only honest border. It goes where the wind tells it, and it keeps a record.*\\n  6. *By now you have burned what I marked. Look at it from the ridge. Tell me that is not a line.*\\n- **Harrow, M9:** *You are late. I said you would be. Sit down, it won't take long, neither of us has long.* / *I drew the lines that started this. I would like to draw one more.* / *You have been drawing for me. Look at it.* / *Burned grass cannot burn twice. It is the only safe road in the country, and you built it for wages.*\\n- **Load-screen epigraphs** (*from Harrow's field notes*): write 12 in the same voice.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 16. UI and UX\\n\\n**10-foot and controller first.** A PS5 DualSense on a TV at ten feet is the design target. Mouse and keyboard play the same game on the same screens and feel native. Everything is drawn with `ctx.hud` in art pixels; there is no DOM UI at all, so it all works in Node tests. Test the view at 1920×1080.\\n\\n**Layout rules:**\\n- Safe area 24 px horizontal, 14 px vertical.\\n- Menu items at scale 2; the smallest text anywhere is scale 1 (subtitles, prompts).\\n- At most 6 items on a screen, one idea per screen.\\n- No tables, no scroll lists, no web-style data screens. Long content is paged.\\n- A focused item has a full-width bar in `orange` and a small marker. Move and confirm sounds.\\n- Only the title and pause menus cover the view. Every other screen is in your hands or an overlay with the world visible behind it.\\n\\n**HUD in play is minimal** and hides 6 s after it last changed:\\n- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\\n- Ammo and the gun's condition icon bottom-right.\\n- A dot reticle (hidden while scoped; the scope has its own black mask).\\n- Prompts centre-bottom. Subtitles above them with the speaker's name in a colour.\\n- Mission step at the top for 5 s when it changes.\\n\\n**Controls** (`src/core/actions.js`):\\n\\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox glyph | Keyboard and mouse |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| Move / look | L stick / R stick | same | WASD / mouse |\\n| Fire / aim | R2 / L2 | RT / LT | LMB / RMB |\\n| Use (when a prompt shows), else reload | Square | X | E / R |\\n| Jump | Cross | A | Space |\\n| Crouch | Circle | B | C (never Ctrl: Ctrl+W closes the browser tab) |\\n| Sprint | L3 (click) | LS | Left Shift |\\n| Melee | R3 | RS | F |\\n| Next weapon | Triangle | Y | Wheel, or 1-4 |\\n| Throw / plant | R1 | RB | G |\\n| Syrette, surgery | L1 | LB | Q |\\n| Map up / down | D-pad Up | D-pad Up | M or Tab |\\n| Tablet | D-pad Down | D-pad Down | H |\\n| Tracker | D-pad Left | D-pad Left | T |\\n| Monocular (hold) | D-pad Right | D-pad Right | V |\\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc |\\n| Ledger | Create | View | J |\\n| **Driving:** gas / brake-reverse / steer | R2 / L2 / L stick | RT / LT / L stick | W / S / A-D |\\n| Handbrake | Cross | A | Space |\\n| Get out / repair | Square | X | E |\\n| Swap to gun | Triangle | Y | F |\\n| Chase camera | R3 | RS | C |\\n\\nUse `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')` etc. Analog triggers: each frame, read `navigator.getGamepads()` buttons 6 and 7 `value` and `input.send({ tr:[l2, r2] })` when changed, so recordings keep it, and use it for throttle and brake. Rumble: `pad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', {...})`, guarded, Settings toggle.\\n\\n**Glyphs.** Prompts follow the input used last:\\n- `device` flips to `kbm` on keydown, mouse button or real mouse movement, and to `pad` on any `Pad*` code or a stick past 0.35.\\n- `src/ui/glyphs.js` is pixel art as `hud.sprite` rows, about 11 × 11: Cross, Circle, Square, Triangle, L1, L2, R1, R2, L3, R3, D-pad directions, Options, Create; Xbox A, B, X, Y, LB, LT, RB, RT, LS, RS, Menu, View; a key cap drawn around any letter; LMB, RMB, MMB, wheel.\\n- Settings has **Glyphs: PlayStation / Xbox**, default PlayStation.\\n- `game.state().prompts` lists what's on screen, so tests can check it.\\n\\n**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\\n\\n**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\\n- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\\n- Baked at start: contour lines every 8 m on sand paper, river, roads, rail, labels in your own 5×7 `pixfont.js`.\\n- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\\n- Raise and lower takes 0.4 s with paper sound. **The world never stops.** You can walk and drive with it up. While it's up, the look input moves the map cursor.\\n- Square/LMB on a marker sets the waypoint; Triangle or wheel toggles a closer zoom.\\n- It works at night because the paper uses a dim lit toon plus a small hand torch `lights.request` following the view group.\\n\\n**Screens:**\\n- **Loading:** the engine's, then a black screen with one Harrow epigraph.\\n- **Title:** live 3D scene (dusk, fixed slow camera over burning grass on the Long Field, music), the title large (scale 4, or 3 if it won't fit), the latest input's *Press [glyph]*. Then the main menu.\\n- **Main menu:** Continue (when a save exists), New Game, Cash Run, Settings, About and Credits.\\n- **Pause** (`timeScale = 0`): Resume, Ledger, Settings, Dev Mode, About and Credits, Quit to Title. In a hub session: Resume and Settings only.\\n- **Settings:** Sound (Music slider **default 10%**, Effects, Voices), Controls (Look sensitivity for pad, for mouse; Invert Y; Aim assist; Rumble; Glyphs), Picture (Fullscreen, for the TV; Pixel size Fine/Chunky via `engine.settings.set`; Quality; Field of view), Comfort (Subtitle size; Reduce flashes; Fever effects reduced), Reset to Defaults. Saved in your own `localStorage` entry and re-applied at boot: `settings:{ button:false, key:false }` hides the engine's panel and stops the engine saving its own copy.\\n- **Dialogue:** the camera holds on the speaker; subtitles; two big buttons at most.\\n- **Tibor's rack:** one gun at a time, large (its first-person model turned to the side on a table), name, three bars (Damage, Range, Reliability), price. Left/right cycles. Buy or Take.\\n- **Locker:** one row per slot, left/right picks.\\n- **Bed:** Dawn, Noon, Dusk, Midnight, Leave.\\n- **Ledger:** section 13.\\n- **Game Over, Ending card, Credits.**\\n- **About and Credits:** paged, see section 27.\\n\\n**Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this screen. A key press or pad connecting clears the gate and shows the normal title.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 17. Dev mode\\n\\nPause menu → **Dev Mode** (hidden in a hub session). An overlay with tabs (L1/R1 or Q/E), world visible behind, playing or frozen by a toggle.\\n\\n| Tab | Contents |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| Cheats | God mode, infinite ammo, no jams, no fever, invisible to AI, noclip fly |\\n| Teleport | Every site, every post, every case, the crosshair point |\\n| Spawn | Squad of each faction, pickup, technical, truck, a stone case, a buddy |\\n| World | Hour slider, wind direction and speed sliders, weather (clear, dust, storm), ignite at crosshair, extinguish all, regrow all, sleep +6 h |\\n| Mission | Start any mission, complete current step, set story flags, give stones, tablets, syrettes, all guns; break gun; force jam; force fever; down a buddy |\\n| **Balance** | Live sliders (below), **Reset to Defaults** for all, Square/R resets one |\\n| Debug | Fire-grid overlay, nav overlay, AI state text over heads, counts (actors, burning cells, draw info from `engine.state()`), engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug`), free camera (`engine.setCamera({ preset:'free' })`, restored after; re-install `step` in `onCameraChange`), crosshair coordinates for placing things in `src/content/`, Quick Save/Load, show `status()` |\\n\\n**Balance sliders** (left/right steps, hold accelerates, mouse drags). Defaults in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`:\\n\\n| Slider | Default | Range |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `playerSpeed` multiplier | 1 | 0.5-2 |\\n| `playerDamageTaken` multiplier | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `weaponDamage` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyHealth` multiplier | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `enemyAccuracy` | 1 | 0.25-3 |\\n| `enemyVision` (m) | 90 | 20-200 |\\n| `enemyReaction` (s) | 0.45 | 0.1-2 |\\n| `wearRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `jamRate` | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `fireSpread` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `fireDamage` (HP/s) | 8 | 0-30 |\\n| `windEffect` | 1 | 0-3 |\\n| `feverMinutes` | 12 | 2-40 |\\n| `vehicleTopSpeed` (m/s) | 26 | 10-45 |\\n| `vehicleToughness` | 1 | 0.25-4 |\\n| `stonesReward` multiplier | 1 | 0-5 |\\n| `buddyWoundChance` | 0.15 | 0-1 |\\n| `dayMinutes` | 30 | 2-120 |\\n| `postRemanHours` | 24 | 1-96 |\\n| `regrowHours` | 48 | 1-200 |\\n\\nA test sets every slider, checks the system responds, presses Reset, and checks every value equals its default.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 18. Attract mode\\n\\nAfter **10 seconds with no input on the title screen or main menu**, start a looping demo (`src/attract/`). Settings and About are exempt, because people stop to read them. It's a director with a list of beats, using the real game with `cam.override`, god mode, infinite ammo and bot input through the same action layer. It cheats freely: teleports, spawns, sets the hour and wind. A `save.disabled` flag stops it touching saves.\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3331b995-1aeb-409f-ac1b-d2caf02ebd30-18","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"200→    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\\n210→      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\\n      release();\\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\\n220→      engine.step(frames, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\\n      choiceI += 1;\\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\\n    }\\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\\n230→      const p = w.feet();\\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\\n  release();\\n}\\n\\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n240→    const path = join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\ntest('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n250→  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n260→  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n270→    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n280→});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n290→  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n300→  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n310→  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n320→    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n330→  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n340→\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n350→  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n360→  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n370→  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n380→  w.lines = [];\\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\\n  w.teleport(200, -200);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\\n  arm('m38');\\n  const before = w.guns.length;\\n  tapFire();\\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\\n390→  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  w.jamScript = 5;\\n  w.noJam = false;\\n  holdFire(40);\\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\\n  holdFire(20);\\n400→  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\\n  const hp = civil.hp;\\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\\n  w.tablets = 1;\\n410→  w.stones = 50;\\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\\n  w.feverOn = false;\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\\n  w.feverOn = true;\\n  w.feverClear = 0;\\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\\n420→  w.tablets = 0;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\\n  w.hp = 15;\\n  tap('KeyQ');\\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\\n  w.startMission('m3');\\n430→  w.lines = [];\\n  w.hp = 1;\\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT <= 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp + ' t ' + w.rescueT);\\n  w.syrettes = 1;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\\n440→  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\\n  w.syrettes = 0;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\\n});\\n\\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n450→  w.startMission('m1');\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\\n  engine.step(20, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\\n460→  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0, 0, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.02, -0.01, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\\n470→  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\\n480→    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\\n  }\\n  game.resetSliders();\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\\n});\\n490→\\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.world.deadBuddies.clear();\\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\\n500→  playMission('m7');\\n  playMission('m8');\\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\\n510→  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\\n});\\n\\ntest('solo round', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.startSolo();\\n520→  const round = game.world.round;\\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 10 && !merc.down; n++) {\\n    const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.seat === merc.id);\\n    if (!foe) break;\\n    placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n    holdFire(10);\\n530→  }\\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing ' + merc.hp);\\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop ' + merc.hp);\\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n540→  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\\n});\\n550→\\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  game.attract = false;\\n  game.mode = 'title';\\n  game.screen = 'title';\\n  const saves = game.saves;\\n  engine.step(600, DT);\\n560→  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.screen = 'settings';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n570→  game.idle = 0;\\n  engine.step(700, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\\n  game.screen = 'cash';\\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\\n580→  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\\n  game.screen = 'menu';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\\n590→  tap('Escape');\\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\",\"content_concise\":\"200→    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\\n210→      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\\n      release();\\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\\n220→      engine.step(frames, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\\n      choiceI += 1;\\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\\n    }\\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\\n230→      const p = w.feet();\\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\\n  release();\\n}\\n\\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n240→    const path = join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\ntest('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n250→  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n260→  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n270→    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n280→});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n290→  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n300→  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n310→  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n320→    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n330→  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n340→\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n350→  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n360→  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n370→  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n380→  w.lines = [];\\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\\n  w.teleport(200, -200);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\\n  arm('m38');\\n  const before = w.guns.length;\\n  tapFire();\\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\\n390→  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  w.jamScript = 5;\\n  w.noJam = false;\\n  holdFire(40);\\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\\n  holdFire(20);\\n400→  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\\n  const hp = civil.hp;\\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\\n  w.tablets = 1;\\n410→  w.stones = 50;\\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\\n  w.feverOn = false;\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\\n  w.feverOn = true;\\n  w.feverClear = 0;\\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\\n420→  w.tablets = 0;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\\n  w.hp = 15;\\n  tap('KeyQ');\\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\\n  w.startMission('m3');\\n430→  w.lines = [];\\n  w.hp = 1;\\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT <= 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp + ' t ' + w.rescueT);\\n  w.syrettes = 1;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\\n440→  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\\n  w.syrettes = 0;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\\n});\\n\\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n450→  w.startMission('m1');\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\\n  engine.step(20, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\\n460→  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0, 0, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.02, -0.01, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\\n470→  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\\n480→    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\\n  }\\n  game.resetSliders();\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\\n});\\n490→\\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.world.deadBuddies.clear();\\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\\n500→  playMission('m7');\\n  playMission('m8');\\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\\n510→  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\\n});\\n\\ntest('solo round', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.startSolo();\\n520→  const round = game.world.round;\\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 10 && !merc.down; n++) {\\n    const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.seat === merc.id);\\n    if (!foe) break;\\n    placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n    holdFire(10);\\n530→  }\\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing ' + merc.hp);\\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop ' + merc.hp);\\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n540→  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\\n});\\n550→\\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  game.attract = false;\\n  game.mode = 'title';\\n  game.screen = 'title';\\n  const saves = game.saves;\\n  engine.step(600, DT);\\n560→  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.screen = 'settings';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n570→  game.idle = 0;\\n  engine.step(700, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\\n  game.screen = 'cash';\\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\\n580→  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\\n  game.screen = 'menu';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\\n590→  tap('Escape');\\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":200,\"limit\":400,\"raw_output\":\"    } else if (step.do === 'clear') {\\n      const foe = w.actors.find((a) => a.alive && a.post === step.tag);\\n      if (!foe) throw new Error('no foe ' + step.tag);\\n      placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      holdFire(80);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'use' || step.do === 'collect' || step.do === 'report') {\\n      const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.tag === step.tag && p.alive !== false && !p.hidden);\\n      const site = step.to ? siteById(step.to) : null;\\n      const x = prop ? prop.x : site ? site.x : w.feet().x;\\n      const z = prop ? prop.z : site ? site.z : w.feet().z;\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      w.teleport(x, z + 1);\\n      engine.step(1, DT);\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'buddy-down') {\\n      tap('KeyE');\\n    } else if (step.do === 'hold' || step.do === 'ride') {\\n      release();\\n      const frames = Math.ceil(step.time * 60) + 30;\\n      engine.step(frames, DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'choice') {\\n      const pick = (opts.picks || [])[choiceI] || 0;\\n      choiceI += 1;\\n      if (pick === 1) tap('ArrowRight');\\n      tap('Enter');\\n    } else {\\n      throw new Error('unhandled step ' + step.do);\\n    }\\n    if (w.mission && !w.mission.done && w.mission.index === before) {\\n      const p = w.feet();\\n      throw new Error(id + ' stuck on ' + step.do + ' ' + (step.text || '') + ' at ' + p.x.toFixed(0) + ',' + p.z.toFixed(0));\\n    }\\n  }\\n  assert(w.mission?.done, id + ' did not finish');\\n  release();\\n}\\n\\nfunction walkSrc(dir, hit) {\\n  for (const name of readdirSync(dir)) {\\n    const path = join(dir, name);\\n    if (statSync(path).isDirectory()) walkSrc(path, hit);\\n    else if (name.endsWith('.js')) hit.push(readFileSync(path, 'utf8'));\\n  }\\n}\\n\\ntest('static files', () => {\\n  const files = [];\\n  walkSrc(join(root, 'src'), files);\\n  const blob = files.join('\\\\n');\\n  assert(!blob.includes('Math.random'), 'Math.random in src');\\n  for (const word of ['TODO', 'FIXME', 'placeholder', 'stub', 'coming soon']) {\\n    assert(!blob.toLowerCase().includes(word), 'forbidden ' + word);\\n  }\\n  const zip = join(root, 'vendor', 'pixel-engine.zip');\\n  const packed = execFileSync('unzip', ['-Z1', zip], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim().split('\\\\n');\\n  const entry = packed.find((line) => line.endsWith('pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(entry, 'zip has no pixel-engine.js');\\n  const fromZip = execFileSync('unzip', ['-p', zip, entry], { maxBuffer: 16 * 1024 * 1024 });\\n  const onDisk = readFileSync(join(root, 'pixel-engine.js'));\\n  assert(createHash('sha256').update(fromZip).digest('hex') === createHash('sha256').update(onDisk).digest('hex'), 'pixel-engine.js differs from the kit zip');\\n  for (const song of Object.values(SONGS)) {\\n    const parsed = parseSong(song);\\n    assert(parsed.notes.length > 0, 'silent song');\\n  }\\n  for (const model of MODELS) {\\n    const check = checkModel(model);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, model.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  for (const tex of TEXTURES) {\\n    const check = validateTexture(tex);\\n    assert(check.problems.length === 0, tex.id + ' ' + check.problems.join('; '));\\n  }\\n  const allowed = new Set(' ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.,!?;:\\\\'-/()%+#&');\\n  const shown = [...Object.values(LINES), ...aboutPages().flat()];\\n  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const crouch = z1 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(crouch > 1 && crouch < 3, 'crouch ' + crouch.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', true);\\n  const z2 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 40);\\n  engine.input.setKey('ShiftLeft', false);\\n  const sprint = (z2 - w.feet().z) / (40 / 60);\\n  assert(sprint > 6, 'sprint ' + sprint.toFixed(2));\\n  const y0 = w.feet().y;\\n  tap('Space');\\n  engine.step(8, DT);\\n  assert(w.feet().y > y0 + 0.2, 'jump');\\n  w.teleport(300, -120);\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const zw = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const wade = zw - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(wade > 1.5 && wade < 3.5, 'wade ' + wade.toFixed(2));\\n});\\n\\ntest('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m2');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  const worn = w.spawnGroundGun('mule');\\n  assert(worn.cond >= 20 && worn.cond <= 55, 'ground cond ' + worn.cond);\\n  w.teleport(200, -200);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  w.giveGun('m38', 0.4);\\n  arm('m38');\\n  const before = w.guns.length;\\n  tapFire();\\n  assert(!w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'm38'), 'cond 0 kept the gun');\\n  assert(w.guns.length === before - 1, 'slot not emptied');\\n  w.giveGun('tractor', 100);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  w.jamScript = 5;\\n  w.noJam = false;\\n  holdFire(40);\\n  const jammed = w.guns.find((g) => g.id === 'tractor');\\n  assert(jammed.jammed, 'did not jam');\\n  const shots = jammed.shots;\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(jammed.shots === shots, 'jammed gun fired');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 5 && jammed.jammed; n++) tap('KeyR');\\n  assert(!jammed.jammed, 'reload did not clear jam');\\n  const civil = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'civil');\\n  const hp = civil.hp;\\n  placeFacing(civil.x, civil.z);\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  holdFire(20);\\n  assert(civil.alive && civil.hp === hp && civil.fleeing, 'civilian was killed');\\n  w.tablets = 1;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  w.feverT = 0.05;\\n  w.feverOn = false;\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  assert(w.feverOn, 'fever did not start');\\n  holdKey('KeyH', 80);\\n  assert(!w.feverOn || w.feverClear > 0, 'tablet did not clear fever');\\n  w.feverOn = true;\\n  w.feverClear = 0;\\n  w.feverIgnore = 0;\\n  w.tablets = 0;\\n  w.stones = 50;\\n  engine.step(26 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.stones <= 40.01, 'ignore did not cost stones ' + w.stones);\\n  w.hp = 15;\\n  tap('KeyQ');\\n  assert(w.surgeryT > 0, 'no surgery');\\n  engine.step(5 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40, 'surgery hp ' + w.hp);\\n  w.startMission('m3');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  w.hp = 1;\\n  w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(w.rescueT > 0, 'no rescue');\\n  engine.step(4 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(w.hp >= 40 && w.rescueT <= 0, 'rescue failed ' + w.hp + ' t ' + w.rescueT);\\n  w.syrettes = 1;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  const ines = w.buddies.find((b) => b.id === 'ines');\\n  assert(!ines.down && w.syrettes === 0, 'syrette did not pick the buddy up');\\n  w.syrettes = 0;\\n  w.downBuddy('ines', { burning: false });\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'finish-it did not record the death');\\n});\\n\\ntest('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m1');\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.inVehicle, 'did not enter');\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', true);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', true);\\n  engine.step(20, DT);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyM', false);\\n  engine.input.setKey('KeyW', false);\\n  assert(w.map.up && w.inVehicle, 'map not held while driving');\\n  assert(w.feet().z !== z0, 'world paused on the map');\\n  const cx = w.map.cx;\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0, 0, false);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  engine.input.setPointer(0.02, -0.01, false);\\n  engine.step(2, DT);\\n  assert(w.map.cx !== cx, 'cursor did not move');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(w.waypoint, 'no waypoint');\\n  w.spawnSoldier({ x: 20, z: 20, faction: 'concord' });\\n  const soldier = w.actors.find((a) => a.kind === 'soldier' && a.alive);\\n  const maxBefore = soldier.max;\\n  game.applySlider('enemyHealth', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.enemyHealth === 2 && soldier.max === maxBefore * 2, 'enemy health slider');\\n  game.applySlider('vehicleTopSpeed', 40);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === 40, 'top speed slider');\\n  game.applySlider('playerSpeed', 2);\\n  assert(TUNING.playerSpeed === 2, 'player speed');\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) {\\n    const [a, b] = TUNING_RANGES[key];\\n    game.applySlider(key, a);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === a, key + ' low');\\n    game.applySlider(key, b);\\n    assert(TUNING[key] === b, key + ' high');\\n  }\\n  game.resetSliders();\\n  for (const key of SLIDER_KEYS) assert(TUNING[key] === TUNING_DEFAULTS[key], 'reset ' + key);\\n  assert(w.car.o.topSpeed === TUNING_DEFAULTS.vehicleTopSpeed, 'reset speed');\\n});\\n\\ntest('story both endings', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.world.deadBuddies.clear();\\n  const chain = ['m0', 'm1', 'm2', 'm3', 'm4', 'm5'];\\n  for (const id of chain) playMission(id);\\n  const burntBefore = game.world.fire.burntCount;\\n  playMission('m6', { dead: ['dov'] });\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy was not kept');\\n  assert(game.world.fire.burntCount > burntBefore, 'story scar missing');\\n  playMission('m7');\\n  playMission('m8');\\n  playMission('m9', { picks: [0, 0] });\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.killed >= 1, 'shoot choice did not pay a kill');\\n  assert(game.world.sheet === 'walk', 'walk sheet ' + game.world.sheet);\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'walk' });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'walk', 'walk card ' + game.ending);\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('dov'), 'dead buddy lost before the ending');\\n  playMission('end', { sheet: 'give', dead: ['ines'] });\\n  assert(game.ending === 'give', 'give card');\\n  assert(game.world.deadBuddies.has('ines'), 'second ending had no dead buddy');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.moved > 0, 'nobody moved');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.stonesEarned > 0, 'no stones');\\n  assert(game.world.ledger.friends >= 1, 'no friends lost');\\n});\\n\\ntest('solo round', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.startSolo();\\n  const round = game.world.round;\\n  const seat = round.seat(0);\\n  const merc = round.seats.find((s) => s.ai);\\n  const startHp = merc.hp;\\n  arm('tractor');\\n  for (let n = 0; n < 10 && !merc.down; n++) {\\n    const foe = game.world.actors.find((a) => a.seat === merc.id);\\n    if (!foe) break;\\n    placeFacing(foe.x, foe.z);\\n    holdFire(10);\\n  }\\n  assert(merc.hp < startHp, 'friendly fire did nothing ' + merc.hp);\\n  assert(merc.down, 'merc did not drop ' + merc.hp);\\n  game.world.teleport(merc.x, merc.z + 1);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  holdKey('KeyE', 200);\\n  assert(!merc.down && merc.hp > 0, 'revive failed');\\n  const box = round.cases.find((c) => !c.taken && !c.carrier);\\n  game.world.teleport(box.x, box.z);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(seat.carrying === box.id, 'did not pick up');\\n  game.world.hurt(500, 'bullet', true);\\n  assert(round.localDown && box.carrier == null && !box.taken, 'down did not drop the case');\\n  game.session.emit('time-up');\\n  assert(game.session.ended, 'time-up did not finish');\\n  const standings = game.session.outcome.standings;\\n  assert(Array.isArray(standings) && standings.length > 0, 'no standings');\\n  assert(game.session.outcome.stats[0].Stones != null, 'no stats');\\n});\\n\\ntest('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  game.attract = false;\\n  game.mode = 'title';\\n  game.screen = 'title';\\n  const saves = game.saves;\\n  engine.step(600, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.idle < 10.01, 'attract early ' + game.idle);\\n  engine.step(1, DT);\\n  assert(game.attract && game.state().attract, 'attract did not start');\\n  engine.step(70 * 60, DT);\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'attract errors');\\n  tap('KeyE');\\n  assert(!game.attract && game.screen === 'title', 'attract exit ' + game.screen);\\n  assert(game.saves === saves, 'attract wrote a save');\\n  game.screen = 'settings';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.idle = 0;\\n  engine.step(700, DT);\\n  assert(!game.attract, 'attract on settings');\\n  game.toTitle();\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'menu', 'title confirm');\\n  const labels = game.items().map((item) => item.label);\\n  assert(labels.includes('HOST ON THIS COMPUTER') === false, 'host is not on the root menu');\\n  game.screen = 'cash';\\n  const cash = game.items().map((item) => item.id);\\n  assert(cash.includes('host') && cash.includes('join') && cash.includes('solo'), 'link menu missing');\\n  game.screen = 'menu';\\n  game.mode = 'menu';\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'settings');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'settings', 'settings');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'glyphs');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.glyphSet === 'xbox', 'glyphs');\\n  game.world.startMission('m2');\\n  tap('Escape');\\n  assert(engine.timeScale === 0 && game.mode === 'pause', 'pause');\\n  const clock = game.world.clock;\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  assert(game.world.clock === clock, 'pause stepped the sim');\\n  const dev = game.items().some((item) => item.id === 'dev');\\n  assert(dev, 'dev mode hidden');\\n  game.focus = game.items().findIndex((item) => item.id === 'about');\\n  tap('Enter');\\n  assert(game.screen === 'about', 'about from pause');\\n\",\"total_lines\":640}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"99f56f8c-405f-47b9-bc86-c430d5cf092d"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_428","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The session plan's acceptance criteria are a derived checklist summarizing PLAN.md.\n\nThe agent claims to have finished everything except fauna. I need to verify whether major features are actually implemented or merely stubs and incomplete cuts.\n\nCriterion 2 never-cut requires core systems that may be missing. These include:\n- 1280x1280 basin, movement states, and first-person driving\n- Gun wear, jamming, and breaking\n- Fire grid, wind speed, fever tablet, and collapse mechanics\n- Surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it\n- Map while walking and driving\n- Music, gibberish voices, and non-silent code sounds\n\nNo audio files exist.\n\nCriterion 3 requires the full story arc from opening through firebreak reveal, both endings, and the §26 never-cut list. It also demands original names, story scars, a ledger, non-civilian bullets, and missions that are fully startable and finishable.\n\nCriterion 4 requires a HUD not built in DOM, glyphs for PS/Xbox/KBM, mouse hover focus with click activation, pause via timeScale 0, exact touch gate text, attract mode only on title and main menu, and dev mode sliders.\n\nCriterion 5 requires Cash Run for one to four players lasting roughly six minutes.\n\nThe remaining criteria cover carry cases, friendly fire, solo versus AI, normal boot reaching the title, hub protocol, four passing scenarios, and same-computer link.\n\nI am now scrutinizing whether the tests are honest or cheat by setting internal state past the unit under test. The theater fire test appears genuine: it uses real fire grid cells, steps sixteen seconds, and measures spread directly. The internal `lightIndex` and `ignite` methods are acceptable because they are part of the simulation unit itself.\n\nLocomotion tests use real input keys and measure movement honestly. The test starts mission m7 first to enter the world, then teleports for wade.\n\nGun tests set up conditions via internal methods like `giveGun`, `jamScript`, and `spawnGroundGun`. Real fire is triggered through input. Condition 0 empties the slot, jam blocks firing, reload clears it, civilians are not killed, fever is tested by stepping, surgery by KeyQ, rescue by hurt(), and finish-it by downBuddy with KeyE.\n\nOne concern remains: the third argument of `w.hurt(50, 'bullet', true)` might be ambiguous.\n\nI need to verify whether rescue actually follows the real death path.\n\nThe map test uses KeyE while driving. The first press enters the vehicle. The second press sets a waypoint if the design allows it.\n\nThe slider test calls `game.applySlider` directly instead of through the menu UI. This may still satisfy the criterion if the UI delegates to that function.\n\nThe slider test only checks that the tuning store updates. It does not verify that the game systems actually read those values at runtime. The verification plan requires both live system changes and a full reset to defaults.\n\nI need to inspect how `applySlider` and the `TUNING` store are wired into gameplay systems. If every system reads tuning values at runtime, then updating the store would change behavior. The acceptance test only checks the store, so it cannot prove that systems actually consume those values. This may be a real gap.\n\nStory tests use teleportation to reach objectives, but they still perform real actions such as firing flares and shooting. The burn, destroy, and goto steps appear reasonably honest.\n\nThe solo Cash Run test uses real inputs for shooting, reviving, picking up cases, and dropping them on hurt. It finishes by emitting a time-up event. I need to verify whether that event follows the actual timer path or merely shortcuts it.\n\nThe attract-mode test advances exactly 600 frames at one-sixtieth second intervals. That equals ten seconds. It asserts the game is idle before attract mode starts. Then it steps once more to trigger attract mode.\n\nThe attract-mode test reveals the idle threshold is strictly greater than ten seconds. After exactly 600 frames the game remains idle and attract mode has not started. It triggers on the very next frame, confirming the boundary is a strict upper bound rather than an inclusive one.\n\nThe attract-mode test sets `game.idle` and `game.mode` directly before stepping the engine. If the idle counter increments during that real update, the test remains honest.\n\nA potential bug exists: `engine.step(600, DT)` might use a fixed timestep instead of the passed delta time. If so, the idle counter could fail to reach ten seconds.\n\nThe test log shows ten passes and zero failures, so the assertions held. I should trust that captured run unless I re-run it. I need to verify whether the test file matches what was actually executed, but I will avoid re-running expensive story missions to minimize tool calls.\n\nA full playthrough of every mission would take minutes, so I will hunt for real bugs in the code instead.\n\nI am now inspecting critical systems. I need to verify whether the missions are fully implemented or merely stubbed steps that auto-complete.\n\nI also noticed a discrepancy in the settings menu. PLAN.md requires many controls such as look sensitivity, aim assist, rumble, and quality settings. The touch log only shows MUSIC, EFFECTS, VOICES, GLYPHS, INVERT Y, RESET, and BACK.\n\nThe settings menu is smaller than PLAN §16 specifies. Criterion 4 only requires PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox glyph setting, and keyboard or mouse glyphs. The session plan is a derived checklist that may clarify but never narrow the objective.\n\nI am weighing whether the smaller settings menu is a plan gap that misses the objective's core intent. The rules forbid refuting for missing edge cases or extensions beyond the contract. I will not invent requirements beyond the plan.\n\nI am applying the rule that OBJECTIVE and its named artifacts are authoritative, while the plan's numbered acceptance criteria are only a derived checklist. I must determine whether missing settings options are polish or core requirements, and whether omitted mission mechanics would violate the story criterion.\n\nI will read missions.js to verify the story content is not hollow. I will also check about.js for required fields, inspect HTML packaging for file:// boot, look for Far Cry 2 proper nouns, and confirm audio files exist.\n\nI will inspect game.js for attract, pause, touch, and hub logic. I will also audit fire.js for spread bugs and weapons for jam or break bugs. I need to verify whether civilians can be killed. I should check if dev mode sliders actually affect gameplay systems and confirm the same-computer link is real. The missing p3 in four-player traffic might be a harness display limit rather than a bug. I will read tests/ISSUES.md and the rest of run.mjs. I must also verify the HTML file exists with the correct structure and pixel-engine hash.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The logs show the four gates green. I’ll read the mission runner, weapons, and shell next to see whether those passes are real."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0cb5c844-e118-4783-a74b-c6d1841e8e2a-19","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":590,"limit":250}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0cb5c844-e118-4783-a74b-c6d1841e8e2a-20","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"^(export )?(const|function|let) |id: 'm|id: \\\"m|burnStrip|sheet|ending","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/missions.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-0cb5c844-e118-4783-a74b-c6d1841e8e2a-21","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"Math\\.random|localStorage|document\\.|window\\.|audio files|\\.mp3|\\.wav|\\.ogg","path":"/