.loop` for the nearest cluster, volume by size (section 22).\\n- Burn scars show on your held map.\\n\\n**Save:** run-length encode `state` into the save JSON.\\n\\n**Wind.** One vector, a slow random walk (direction changes by up to 15° a minute, speed 0 to 8 m/s). It drives `grass.wind`, `WindUniforms` (trees via `swayObject`) and rain. Read it from the grass, from a strip of red cloth on every post (`clothGrid` + `SoftMesh`), and from a small wind arrow on the GPS. Missions can pin it (`wind` field).\\n\\n**Time.** Full day = `TUNING.dayMinutes` (30 real minutes). Call `applySky(engine, skyAt(hour))` at up to 10 Hz. Paint the dome from this table, interpolated:\\n\\n| Hour | Top | Middle | Horizon |\\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\\n| 5.5 | `#3a4a6b` | `#d99a6c` | `#f0b070` |\\n| 9 | `#6f9fb5` | `#c9d6c4` | `#e3cf9e` |\\n| 13 | `#7fa6b8` | `#d8dcc0` | `#ecd9a6` |\\n| 16.5 | `#7fa6b8` | `#e9c98f` | `#d98a4e` |\\n| 19 | `#2b2f52` | `#8a4f5c` | `#c8643c` |\\n| 22 | `#0b0f20` | `#141a2e` | `#1c2238` |\\n\\nAdd a sun disc (`glowMaterial`), a moon, and stars at night (a `SpriteBatch` following the camera). Night cuts AI vision (section 10), which is why sleeping until midnight is a tactic.\\n\\n**Weather.** Dry by default. A dust wind (`particles`, stronger wind, haze raised) and a storm (`Precipitation` rain, lightning `screen.flash` + thunder, fire damped). Storms are rare, scripted for M9, and available from dev mode.\\n\\n**The look.** The engine's native pixel pipeline plus a light grade. Keep these filters always on and change only parameters, since parameters are free and adding a filter rebuilds the pipeline:\\n```js\\nexport const LOOK = {\\n  scene: [{ id:'adjust', params:{ brightness:0, contrast:1.06, saturation:1.05, warmth:0.04 } }, { id:'chromatic', params:{ spread:0 } }, { id:'vignette', params:{ intensity:0.28, softness:0.7, amount:1 } }],\\n  actors: { pixel:{ size:1, outline:0.45, crease:0.08 }, filters:[] },\\n  environment: { pixel:{ size:1, outline:0.32, crease:0.05 }, filters:[] },\\n};\\n```\\nFever, low health and flames adjust `spread`, `saturation`, `warmth` and `intensity` through `engine.setLook` (at up to 15 Hz).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Player\\n\\nA `CharacterController` capsule with `eyePosition` at feet + 1.55 (crouched 0.95). No visible body. Head-bob and landing dip go in the view group, not the camera.\\n\\n| Move | Speed (m/s) | Notes |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| Walk (stick partly tilted; Caps Lock toggles it on keyboard, never Alt, since Alt+D jumps to the address bar) | 3.6 | Quiet |\\n| Run (default) | 5.4 | Heard at 25 m |\\n| Sprint (click L3 or hold Shift while moving forward) | 7.4 | 6 s of stamina, 8 s to refill, heard at 40 m, can't fire or aim |\\n| Crouch | 2.0 | Quiet; hidden in tall grass |\\n\",\"total_lines\":1128}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"2fc9a2dc-b171-43b7-a80c-0a43ef449e7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_433","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A potential bug in damageProp looks suspicious.\n\nThe `damageProp` method contains a convoluted conditional that checks `currentStep()` and tags like 'fuel-tank', 'pump', and 'convoy'. This logic appears to be the source of the bug.\n\nThe convoluted logic prevents fuel-tank and pump props from being destroyed during a destroy step. When their HP is above zero, the first conditional fails and the second conditional's tag check blocks execution, so those props survive.\n\nThe shortcut actually destroys fuel tanks and pumps instantly on the first hit during a destroy step, regardless of HP. This may be acceptable for a demo if one shot is enough.\n\nThe instant-destroy shortcut is a balance choice, not a failure of the real-actions criterion. Now investigating a potential surgery bug: the heal logic triggers when HP drops below 20, and the test sets w.hp to 15 before tapping KeyQ.\n\nThe surgery test asserts that tapping KeyQ triggers a 4-second healing timer, then steps the engine for five seconds to verify HP recovery. The next focus is whether the map action consumes presses correctly while driving, specifically checking if KeyM maps to the map action and if consumePress works with setKey.\n\nWaypoint placement works correctly. The test moves the map cursor slightly from the player position and asserts a waypoint exists, which passed for seed 1 at m1.\n\nThe attract save test checks that the saves counter does not change. The choice shoot test plays mission 9 with picks [0, 0] and asserts ledger.killed is at least one.\n\nThe ending cards text still needs to be verified.\n\nThe 120-second hold step runs for 7230 frames. The player starts at the hold point so they remain within radius and the hold completes.\n\nThe 60-second ride step simply increments time. It does not simulate an actual train ride.\n\nThe flatcar MG ride step is just a timer flag. It does not simulate actual train movement or combat. This may violate the \"real actions\" criterion.\n\nCriterion 1 forbids half-built features, stubs, and placeholders. The ride step is a simplified complete feature rather than a stub if the player still experiences a hold. The plan's implementation approach is guidance, not contract. Criterion 3 requires each shipped mission to start from its own setup and finish with real actions.\n\nThe \"real actions\" criterion requires the bot to use actual game actions rather than simply setting mission.done. PLAN.md defines hold and ride as valid step types, so a timer-based flatcar is acceptable if the mission completes through those defined steps. The core tension is whether to implement full train combat or accept the simplified version specified in the plan.\n\nPLAN.md describes a full Far Cry 2-like game with dozens of complex systems. The session plan deliberately summarizes these into testable acceptance criteria and requires cuts to be whole items from section 26. The implementation only cut fauna, leaving many other PLAN features simplified or absent.\n\nSpecific missing features include alternate plans, monocular vision, stealth, melee combat, mercies, convoy vehicles, train rails, boarding mechanics, dev mode tabs, settings, Tibor's shop, lockers, beds, safehouses, and stone cases. The fauna cut is the only allowed change.\n\nThe session plan may only be refuted if it omits a core objective requirement. PLAN_FILE is a derived checklist that must never narrow or override the OBJECTIVE. The implementer followed the planner's guidance, so any missing features from PLAN.md are acceptable unless they violate the core intent.\n\nThe refutation rules explicitly forbid challenging the absence of anything listed under Non-goals. When all criteria are satisfied, the verdict must be Not Refuted even if more could have been built. The session plan's criteria 1 through 5 capture the never-cut systems, the story spine, and multiplayer. This suggests the missing depth may not violate the core intent.\n\nExact probabilities, dialogue, and UI layout are implementation specifics. Diverging from them is never grounds to refute working code. The acceptance criteria and objective requirements are the actual contract for judging. The objective explicitly requires building the game PLAN.md describes and completing everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer.\n\nThe verifier instructions explicitly warn against inventing requirements beyond the contract. They instruct judging criteria as met or unmet, and advise not refuting for missing edge cases. This reinforces that narrowing PLAN.md's full scope to a subset of features would be a plan gap.\n\nThe session plan explicitly permits cutting whole items from PLAN.md §26. This formalizes the allowed cut mechanism, so the full PLAN.md scope is not a strict requirement.\n\nI will inspect game.js menus, dev mode, sites, weapons, and dialogue to verify actual implementation scope before refuting anything.\n\nThe code-correctness floor only applies to core OBJECTIVE purposes. Missing optional fidelity like exact fire probability is not a core issue if the behavior works. Missing entire PLAN.md features such as Tibor's shop, sleep, monocular vision, alternate mission plans, or dev mode tabs may be a core issue. PLAN §26 will be reviewed next.\n\nThe never-cut list covers fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs, native mouse, touch gate, hub check, music at ten percent, and voices. These are implemented at some level. Features not on either list should still exist unless cut from the top of the allowed cuts.\n\nThe session plan's Criterion 3 explicitly defines the verification bar: anything left out must be a whole item from PLAN.md §26, with its menu entries, map marks, and lines removed. The never-cut list is all present. This formalizes the agreed checklist and prevents the verifier from inventing extra requirements beyond the contract.\n\nConcrete features to audit include dev mode tabs, monocular vision, sleep and beds, Tibor's shop, alternate mission plans, vehicles beyond the single truck, safehouses, campaign stones and tracker, required dialogue lines, weapons list, and held map visual.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce6dc4f7-1070-4723-9028-98e2b70759c7-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"monocular|sleep|tibor|locker|bed|alternate|alt\\.|chase|technical|flamethrower|molotov|empire|charge|tracker|safehouse|dev tab|screen === 'dev'","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src","glob":"*.js","head_limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce6dc4f7-1070-4723-9028-98e2b70759c7-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/content/weapons.js","limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-ce6dc4f7-1070-4723-9028-98e2b70759c7-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js","offset":300,"limit":450}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8882,"output_tokens":3370,"cache_read_input_tokens":85504,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"5276d551-14af-4d4f-8ea3-10e00d8d9fea"}
