{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_446","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Checking a potential bug where solo round tests assert stats by index, but finish uses seat IDs.\n\nPlayer ID 0 exists. The audio test only checks that the engine's internal counter increased, which is weaker than OfflineAudioContext verification. Since the sounds are real SoundDefs passed through the engine, confirming the engine received a non-silent definition is reasonable.\n\nspawnGroundGun returns the weapon after giveGun. The test checks worn.cond to confirm the new gun is selected.\n\nThe map cursor only sets waypoints for seen sites within 18m. This restricts waypoint placement to nearby known locations. The test passes this criterion, but the visual behavior remains problematic.\n\nA dev mode bug breaks mouse interaction on the 24-item menu. The HUD is 270px tall, yet only nine items fit in the draw window. Items nine through twenty-three are clipped from the viewport but remain hoverable. This mismatch between drawn positions and hover coordinates prevents criterion four from passing.\n\nThe lower menu items sit outside the 270-pixel canvas. The Reset button is at y=438, so it is completely off-screen. This means half the dev mode sliders are unreachable by mouse while the list is scrolled. Keyboard navigation still works. This may violate the criterion that pad, keyboard, and mouse must operate the same menus.\n\nSettings and main menu items sit entirely within the visible canvas, so mouse interaction works there. The buddy syrette bug is confirmed in world.js: knockBuddy sets burning to true, tryUse only applies the syrette if burning is false, and game.js draw contains no map blit.\n\nThe map pixel buffer is computed but never consumed by a texture. The spawnSoldier function only creates data without instantiating the soldier mesh in models.js. The headless suite stays green because it does not render-check the map. The implementer must display the map pixels on screen rather than patching the test. A test that verifies a visible mesh exists would be honest.\n\nInvisible soldiers may exceed the acceptance criteria. Criterion 2 only requires first-person movement and guns, not visibility. The test completes by raycasting at guard positions rather than seeing meshes. The launch screenshot shows terrain and HUD with no people. Yet the objective implies a first-person shooter where enemies are visible.\n\nThe PLAN.md specifies soldiers and AI with a rig, yet the soldier model is never placed in the world. Combat uses invisible points instead, leaving a half-built feature that violates criterion 1. This will be included as a finding, though the map and syrette bugs alone may suffice.\n\nThe screenshot shows a beige box that is likely the clinic tent addBlock rather than the vehicle. The image description mentions terrain but not a map or truck interior. The code never draws mapPx, so the map pixel buffer remains unused.\n\nThe GPS widget is also absent from draw(). Both the paper map and GPS are required by the criterion to be held in the hands, yet neither appears visually.\n\nThe audio count property exists on the engine, since the test passed without error. The single-line test log is sufficient evidence because it reports zero failures and the runner explicitly exits with code zero.\n\nHub, link, touch, and launch logs all pass. The refute targets shipped bugs rather than missing gate logs.\n\nThe scroll bug is decisive for criterion four. Clicking the drawn \"RESET TO DEFAULTS\" button while scrolled activates a different slider underneath it. The map and buddy choice bugs remain the primary play issues. The syrette bug may be acceptable because burning buddies are a special case, and the test proves the offer works for non-burning targets.\n\nThe campaign mission that teaches the syrette offers no choice. knockBuddy sets burning for the buddy's plea line, but the player can still finish the downed buddy with melee input even while burning. Syrette is only available when the buddy is not burning. This makes the mission's offer effectively useless.\n\nThe PLAN.md explicitly requires a burning buddy to offer Syrette or Finish It. The code currently blocks Syrette for burning buddies, so the story beat is impossible. Non-burning buddies still allow both actions. I will now write the files.\n\nThe M6 mission test only reaches the finish-It path, leaving the Syrette option untested and effectively unreachable. Confidence is high for the map and syrette bugs because they were read directly from the source code. These issues are model-fixable and do not block release. The system prompt will be omitted from the findings.\n\nThe solo round test never walks to the truck to bank a case. It only picks up and drops the case. The tryUse logic appears correct, so this is an untested gap rather than a confirmed bug.\n\nThe banking gap is dropped. The pickup order correctly prioritizes bank, revive, and pickup. No audio files exist in the source directory. The map pixel buffer is confirmed unused in game.js.\n\nThe user confirmed only two verdict files will be written. I am finalizing the details markdown and JSON with exact line citations for the map, syrette, soldier mesh, and dev menu scroll bugs.\n\nThe tests avoid the broken paths. The map test only checks internal state and waypoints, so it passes while the map remains invisible. The buddy test calls downBuddy with burning:false, which skips the mission path entirely. The syrette test is dishonest because it pre-positions a non-burning downed buddy that the campaign never produces.\n\nThe instruction requires refactoring shipped code into a directly-callable pure unit rather than patching the test around an untestable one. The fix is to change knockBuddy and tryUse so burning buddies can still be syretted, then verify the behavior through the mission step or knockBuddy() instead of pre-positioning state in the test.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The gates are green, but the held map is never drawn and the buddy syrette choice is unreachable in the mission that is supposed to offer it. I’ll record those as defects."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23cd7103-c28a-40a1-8149-080ebde6f737-76","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/goal-verdict-e16164d1c2de-1-0.json","content":"{\n  \"refuted\": true,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js:174\",\n      \"detail\": \"The held map/GPS never appears: mapPx is painted and map.up only moves a hidden cursor. No mesh, DataTexture, or HUD blit reads it (map-sheet in models.js is unused). Draw the map in the hands from mapPx while walking and driving, and assert that path, not only map.up.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js:473\",\n      \"detail\": \"M6 knockBuddy() always sets burning:true, and tryUse() at world.js:1115 refuses a syrette when burning, so the campaign only offers finish-it. Allow syrette or finish-it on that down (finish-it only when no syrette is left) and assert it through knockBuddy(), not downBuddy(..., {burning:false}).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js:1352\",\n      \"detail\": \"Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians are data-only. spawnSoldier never adds the soldier model (or any mesh) to the scene, so a first-person fight has nothing to see or aim at. Instance the rig in the world and move it with the actor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"bug\",\n      \"location\": \"A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/game.js:628\",\n      \"detail\": \"Dev Mode lists 24 rows but draw() windows 9 at y=86+i*16 while hover() hit-tests y=86+index*16. Once focus>6, a click activates the wrong slider and Reset is off the 270px HUD. Hit-test the same window the HUD draws.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"evidence\": \"tests-all.log is `passed 10 failed 0` and hub/launch/touch/link logs pass, but world.js mapPx is never drawn (shots/map-truck.png shows no map), knockBuddy forces burning so syrette is impossible, and spawnSoldier adds no mesh.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"blocking\": \"none\",\n  \"details_md\": \"See goal-classifier markdown. Headless suite, file:// boots, touch gate, hub scenarios, and link log all pass. Shipped play still fails criterion 2: the paper map is an invisible cursor, the buddy syrette choice is unreachable on the mission down, and soldiers are never put in the scene. Dev-mode mouse hits do not match the scrolled slider list.\"\n}\n"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-23cd7103-c28a-40a1-8149-080ebde6f737-77","name":"write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/goal-classifier-e16164d1c2de-1-skeptic-0.md","content":"# Verdict: Refuted\n\nThe captured gates match the verification plan: `tests-all.log` is `passed 10 failed 0`, both `file://` launches report title `A Cry Too Far` with `AIHub.active` false and no errors, `touch.log` has the exact notice and a Settings-only menu with attract after idle 10, all four hub scenarios set `complete` and `pass`, and `link.log` shows one shared case and fire with matching standings. Those passes do not cover the play bugs below. The headless tests stay green because they assert flags the player never sees.\n\n## Held map is not held\n\nCriterion 2 requires the paper map and GPS in the hands while walking and driving, with the world still moving. `World` fills a 320×240 `mapPx` buffer (`src/sim/world.js` around 174–217) and `map.up` moves `map.cx` / `map.cz` and can set a waypoint. Nothing reads `mapPx` except `mapHasScar()`. `draw()` in `src/game.js` (about 689–764) never blits it. `map-sheet` in `src/art/models.js` is never instantiated. `shots/map-truck.png` is the basin and HUD with the map flag set and no map in frame. The suite only checks `w.map.up` and a waypoint (`tests/run.mjs` around 447–469).\n\nPut the buffer on a mesh in the view (hands / GPS) while walking and driving, and assert that the displayed pixels change when a scar or the player dot is stamped. Do not only assert `map.up`.\n\n## Syrette or finish-it is unreachable on the story down\n\n`knockBuddy()` (`world.js` 473–480) is what M6's `buddy-down` step calls, and it always passes `{ burning: true }`. `tryUse()` (1115–1126) syrettes only when `!buddy.burning`; a burning down is always finish-it, even if syrettes remain. The only campaign down therefore cannot be saved. The suite calls `downBuddy('ines', { burning: false })` and never `knockBuddy()`, so it does not exercise the mission entry.\n\nOn that down, E (or the use action) must still be able to spend a syrette, and finish-it must be the only option when none remain. Assert that through `knockBuddy()` / the m6 step.\n\n## Soldiers are not in the world\n\n`spawnSoldier()` (`world.js` 1352–1362) pushes a plain object. The `soldier` model in `src/art/models.js` is never compiled or added to the scene. Mercs, buddies, and the civilian are the same kind of record. Rays hit coordinates the player cannot see. Instance the rig and move it with the actor each step.\n\n## Dev-mode mouse hits the wrong row\n\n`items()` on the dev screen is every slider plus Reset and Back (24 rows). `draw()` shows nine rows starting at `focus - 6`, at `y = 86 + i * 16`. `hover()` (`game.js` 628) hit-tests `y = 86 + index * 16` with no window. After the focus passes 6, the row under the cursor is not the row that was drawn, and Reset sits past the 270px HUD so the mouse cannot reach it. Keyboard still works. Hit-test the same slice the HUD draws, and cover that with a pointer event on a scrolled slider.\n"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5017,"output_tokens":4831,"cache_read_input_tokens":153984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"8422627b-c2c8-4408-8eee-088b60d38839"}
