,117,110,116,105,108,32,49,48,32,115,32,111,114,32,109,111,114,101,32,104,97,118,101,32,112,97,115,115,101,100,44,32,97,110,100,32,116,97,107,101,32,116,104,101,32,115,99,114,101,101,110,115,104,111,116,59,32,97,98,111,117,116,32,49,32,102,114,97,109,101,32,97,32,115,101,99,111,110,100,32,105,115,32,110,111,114,109,97,108,32,104,101,114,101,46,10,49,48,53,49,58,124,32,53,32,87,111,114,108,100,32,124,32,65,108,108,32,115,105,116,101,115,44,32,115,97,102,101,104,111,117,115,101,115,44,32,84,105,98,111,114,44,32,115,116,111,110,101,115,44,32,116,114,97,99,107,101,114,44,32,102,101,118,101,114,44,32,116,97,98,108,101,116,115,44,32,115,117,114,103,101,114,121,44,32,109,111,110,111,99,117,108,97,114,44,32,104,101,108,100,32,109,97,112,44,32,114,97,105,108,32,104,97,108,116,115,44,32,116,114,105,103,32,112,111,105,110,116,115,44,32,115,97,118,101,32,97,110,100,32,108,111,97,100,32,124,32,65,32,119,104,111,108,101,32,115,101,115,115,105,111,110,32,119,105,116,104,111,117,116,32,109,105,115,115,105,111,110,115,32,119,111,114,107,115,32,124,10,49,48,55,52,58,78,101,118,101,114,32,99,117,116,58,32,102,105,114,101,44,32,119,101,97,114,32,97,110,100,32,106,97,109,115,44,32,102,101,118,101,114,44,32,116,104,101,32,104,101,108,100,32,109,97,112,44,32,98,117,100,100,121,32,114,101,115,99,117,101,32,97,110,100,32,116,104,101,32,102,105,110,105,115,104,45,105,116,32,99,104,111,105,99,101,44,32,72,97,114,114,111,119,39,115,32,116,119,105,115,116,44,32,100,101,118,32,109,111,100,101,32,119,105,116,104,32,115,108,105,100,101,114,115,44,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,32,109,111,100,101,44,32,103,108,121,112,104,115,32,97,110,100,32,110,97,116,105,118,101,32,109,111,117,115,101,44,32,116,111,117,99,104,32,103,97,116,101,44,32,116,104,101,32,104,117,98,32,99,104,101,99,107,44,32,109,117,115,105,99,32,97,116,32,49,48,37,44,32,116,104,101,32,118,111,105,99,101,115,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":13,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"**Perspective:** first person on foot, at the wheel and in story scenes, with an optional chase camera in vehicles only. The source's best ideas (a gun jamming, tablets in your palm, pliers in your own forearm, a paper map in your hands while someone shoots at you) only work through your own eyes and hands.\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"| Map and GPS held in hand | Paper map and GPS held in hand, and the map turns out to be the plot (sections 14, 16) |\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"**The map in your hands works.** A `THREE.DataTexture` (RGBA `Uint8Array`, nearest filter, `colorSpace = SRGBColorSpace`) on a `PlaneGeometry` with `toonMaterial(0xffffff, { map })`, parented to the camera, reads crisp. It needs no DOM, so it also runs in Node. Draw into the array yourself.\"},{\"line_number\":365,\"content\":\"- Burn scars show on your held map.\"},{\"line_number\":369,\"content\":\"**Wind.** One vector, a slow random walk (direction changes by up to 15° a minute, speed 0 to 8 m/s). It drives `grass.wind`, `WindUniforms` (trees via `swayObject`) and rain. Read it from the grass, from a strip of red cloth on every post (`clothGrid` + `SoftMesh`), and from a small wind arrow on the GPS. Missions can pin it (`wind` field).\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\"},{\"line_number\":718,\"content\":\"**The held map** (`src/world/map-texture.js`). The heart of pillar 3.\"},{\"line_number\":719,\"content\":\"- 320 × 240 DataTexture on a plane about 0.5 × 0.375 m, about 0.42 m in front of the camera, tilted, in both hands (the `hand` model and hands rig), filling about 70% of the width, so one texel is about one art pixel. A 0.62 m plane, which I tried first, was too big.\"},{\"line_number\":721,\"content\":\"- Redrawn at up to 2 Hz on a copy: burn scars (ink), your position and heading, the waypoint, sites you've seen, mission step and Harrow's notes in the margin, wind arrow and clock on a small GPS clipped to the corner.\"},{\"line_number\":886,\"content\":\"- **First-person:** arms and hands (sleeve, skin); `cane`, `m38`, `flare`, `tractor`, `mule`, `empire`, `weed` with tank and hose, `tube`, bottle, charge, detonator; each gun with named rust and tape parts; syrette, tablet bottle, pliers, knife, lighter, wrench, monocular, tracker, map plane, GPS; steering wheel and dash for each vehicle.\"},{\"line_number\":1034,\"content\":\"**Screenshots** only for what a script can't check, at 1920×1080, once each near the end, and whenever you've changed the art they show: title; day first-person with gun; night fire; held map in a truck; Tibor's rack; dialogue; surgery; dev sliders; hub card; ending. Set `e.manual = false`, wait until 10 s or more have passed, and take the screenshot; about 1 frame a second is normal here.\"},{\"line_number\":1051,\"content\":\"| 5 World | All sites, safehouses, Tibor, stones, tracker, fever, tablets, surgery, monocular, held map, rail halts, trig points, save and load | A whole session without missions works |\"},{\"line_number\":1074,\"content\":\"Never cut: fire, wear and jams, fever, the held map, buddy rescue and the finish-it choice, Harrow's twist, dev mode with sliders, attract mode, glyphs and 