{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b42d86a-593e-442f-a223-f09d912fdef6-120","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"679→  tickActors(dt) {\\n680→    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n690→        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n        }\\n        continue;\\n700→      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n710→          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n720→    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n730→    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n740→  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\\n      if (b.downLeft <= 0) {\\n        b.alive = false;\\n750→        b.down = false;\\n        if (!this.deadBuddies.has(b.id)) {\\n          this.deadBuddies.add(b.id);\\n          this.ledger.friends += 1;\\n        }\\n        if (this.currentStep()?.do === 'buddy-down') this.completeStep();\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (this.rescueT > 0) {\\n      this.rescueT -= dt;\\n760→      if (this.rescueT <= 0 && this.rescueBuddy) {\\n        const mags = this.rescueBuddy.id === 'mags';\\n        this.hp = mags ? 60 : 40;\\n        this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60;\\n        if (this.rng.next() < TUNING.buddyWoundChance) {\\n          this.rescueBuddy.wound = true;\\n          this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60 * 2;\\n        }\\n        this.rescueBuddy = null;\\n        this.dead = false;\\n770→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPosts() {\\n    for (const post of this.posts) {\\n      if (post.alive || post.clearedAt == null) continue;\\n      if (this.gameHours - post.clearedAt >= TUNING.postRemanHours) {\\n        post.alive = true;\\n        post.clearedAt = null;\\n780→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPlayer(dt) {\\n    if (this.round?.localDown) return;\\n    if (this.dead && this.rescueT <= 0) return;\\n    const input = this.ctx.input;\\n    const bot = this.game.mode === 'attract' ? this.game.bot : null;\\n    if (!bot && this.lines.length) {\\n790→      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.advanceLines();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!bot && this.choice) {\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'left')) this.choice.focus = Math.max(0, this.choice.focus - 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'right')) this.choice.focus = Math.min(this.choice.options.length - 1, this.choice.focus + 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.choicePick = this.choice.focus;\\n      return;\\n    }\",\"content_concise\":\"679→  tickActors(dt) {\\n680→    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n690→        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n        }\\n        continue;\\n700→      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n710→          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n720→    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n730→    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n740→  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\\n      if (b.downLeft <= 0) {\\n        b.alive = false;\\n750→        b.down = false;\\n        if (!this.deadBuddies.has(b.id)) {\\n          this.deadBuddies.add(b.id);\\n          this.ledger.friends += 1;\\n        }\\n        if (this.currentStep()?.do === 'buddy-down') this.completeStep();\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (this.rescueT > 0) {\\n      this.rescueT -= dt;\\n760→      if (this.rescueT <= 0 && this.rescueBuddy) {\\n        const mags = this.rescueBuddy.id === 'mags';\\n        this.hp = mags ? 60 : 40;\\n        this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60;\\n        if (this.rng.next() < TUNING.buddyWoundChance) {\\n          this.rescueBuddy.wound = true;\\n          this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60 * 2;\\n        }\\n        this.rescueBuddy = null;\\n        this.dead = false;\\n770→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPosts() {\\n    for (const post of this.posts) {\\n      if (post.alive || post.clearedAt == null) continue;\\n      if (this.gameHours - post.clearedAt >= TUNING.postRemanHours) {\\n        post.alive = true;\\n        post.clearedAt = null;\\n780→      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPlayer(dt) {\\n    if (this.round?.localDown) return;\\n    if (this.dead && this.rescueT <= 0) return;\\n    const input = this.ctx.input;\\n    const bot = this.game.mode === 'attract' ? this.game.bot : null;\\n    if (!bot && this.lines.length) {\\n790→      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.advanceLines();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!bot && this.choice) {\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'left')) this.choice.focus = Math.max(0, this.choice.focus - 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'right')) this.choice.focus = Math.min(this.choice.options.length - 1, this.choice.focus + 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.choicePick = this.choice.focus;\\n      return;\\n    }\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js\",\"offset\":679,\"limit\":120,\"raw_output\":\"  tickActors(dt) {\\n    const night = this.hour < 5.5 || this.hour >= 19;\\n    const p = this.feet();\\n    for (const a of this.actors) {\\n      if (!a.alive) continue;\\n      const cell = this.fire.cellAt(a.x, a.z);\\n      if (cell && this.fire.state[cell.i] === 1 && a.kind === 'soldier') {\\n        a.state = 'panic';\\n        a.burnT = (a.burnT || 0) + dt;\\n        a.x += Math.cos(a.burnT) * dt * 3;\\n        a.z += Math.sin(a.burnT * 1.3) * dt * 3;\\n        this.fire.ignite(a.x, a.z, 0);\\n        if (a.burnT > 5) a.alive = false;\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind === 'civil') {\\n        if (a.fleeing) {\\n          a.x += dt * 2;\\n          a.z += dt;\\n        }\\n        continue;\\n      }\\n      if (a.kind !== 'soldier') continue;\\n      const see = this.soldierSees(a, p, night);\\n      a.sees = see;\\n      if (see && this.hostile(a)) {\\n        a.react = (a.react || 0) + dt;\\n        a.state = 'alert';\\n        if (a.react >= TUNING.enemyReaction) {\\n          const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n          this.aimError = (1.2 + (5 - 1.2) * Math.min(1, dist / 80)) / TUNING.enemyAccuracy;\\n          if (this.rng.next() < 0.5 * dt * 4) this.hurt(9, 'bullet', false);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        a.react = 0;\\n        a.state = see ? 'suspicious' : 'idle';\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  soldierSees(a, p, night) {\\n    if (this.invisible) return false;\\n    let range = TUNING.enemyVision;\\n    if (this.crouch) range *= 0.55;\\n    if (night) range *= 0.45;\\n    if (this.burning > 0) range *= 2;\\n    const dist = Math.hypot(a.x - p.x, a.z - p.z);\\n    if (dist > range) return false;\\n    const ang = Math.atan2(p.x - a.x, p.z - a.z);\\n    let diff = Math.abs(ang - (a.yaw || 0));\\n    while (diff > Math.PI) diff = Math.abs(diff - Math.PI * 2);\\n    return diff < (120 * Math.PI) / 360;\\n  }\\n\\n  hostile(a) {\\n    if (a.kind === 'civil') return false;\\n    if (this.pass && a.faction === this.pass && !this.provoked) return false;\\n    if (this.truce && this.inTown(a.x, a.z)) return false;\\n    return true;\\n  }\\n\\n  inTown(x, z) {\\n    return this.truce && Math.hypot(x, z - 40) < 70;\\n  }\\n\\n  tickBuddies(dt) {\\n    for (const b of this.buddies) {\\n      if (!b.alive || !b.down) continue;\\n      b.downLeft -= dt;\\n      if (b.downLeft <= 0) {\\n        b.alive = false;\\n        b.down = false;\\n        if (!this.deadBuddies.has(b.id)) {\\n          this.deadBuddies.add(b.id);\\n          this.ledger.friends += 1;\\n        }\\n        if (this.currentStep()?.do === 'buddy-down') this.completeStep();\\n      }\\n    }\\n    if (this.rescueT > 0) {\\n      this.rescueT -= dt;\\n      if (this.rescueT <= 0 && this.rescueBuddy) {\\n        const mags = this.rescueBuddy.id === 'mags';\\n        this.hp = mags ? 60 : 40;\\n        this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60;\\n        if (this.rng.next() < TUNING.buddyWoundChance) {\\n          this.rescueBuddy.wound = true;\\n          this.rescueBuddy.spentUntil = this.clock + TUNING.dayMinutes * 60 * 2;\\n        }\\n        this.rescueBuddy = null;\\n        this.dead = false;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPosts() {\\n    for (const post of this.posts) {\\n      if (post.alive || post.clearedAt == null) continue;\\n      if (this.gameHours - post.clearedAt >= TUNING.postRemanHours) {\\n        post.alive = true;\\n        post.clearedAt = null;\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n\\n  tickPlayer(dt) {\\n    if (this.round?.localDown) return;\\n    if (this.dead && this.rescueT <= 0) return;\\n    const input = this.ctx.input;\\n    const bot = this.game.mode === 'attract' ? this.game.bot : null;\\n    if (!bot && this.lines.length) {\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.advanceLines();\\n      return;\\n    }\\n    if (!bot && this.choice) {\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'left')) this.choice.focus = Math.max(0, this.choice.focus - 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'right')) this.choice.focus = Math.min(this.choice.options.length - 1, this.choice.focus + 1);\\n      if (consumeAction(input, 'confirm')) this.choicePick = this.choice.focus;\\n      return;\\n    }\\n\",\"total_lines\":1400}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b42d86a-593e-442f-a223-f09d912fdef6-121","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1360→```ts\\nfunction toonify(root: Object3D, options: ToonifyOptions = {}): Object3D\\n```\\n\\nReplace every mesh material under `root` with the shared toon material of the same base\\ncolor, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n1370→```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n1380→### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n1390→\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\",\"content_concise\":\"1360→```ts\\nfunction toonify(root: Object3D, options: ToonifyOptions = {}): Object3D\\n```\\n\\nReplace every mesh material under `root` with the shared toon material of the same base\\ncolor, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n1370→```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n1380→### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n1390→\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":1360,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"```ts\\nfunction toonify(root: Object3D, options: ToonifyOptions = {}): Object3D\\n```\\n\\nReplace every mesh material under `root` with the shared toon material of the same base\\ncolor, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-8b42d86a-593e-442f-a223-f09d912fdef6-122","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,