2,32,123,10,52,52,55,58,116,101,115,116,40,39,109,97,112,32,119,104,105,108,101,32,100,114,105,118,105,110,103,32,97,110,100,32,115,108,105,100,101,114,115,39,44,32,97,115,121,110,99,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,52,57,49,58,116,101,115,116,40,39,115,116,111,114,121,32,98,111,116,104,32,101,110,100,105,110,103,115,39,44,32,97,115,121,110,99,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,53,49,54,58,116,101,115,116,40,39,115,111,108,111,32,114,111,117,110,100,39,44,32,97,115,121,110,99,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,53,53,49,58,116,101,115,116,40,39,109,101,110,117,115,32,97,116,116,114,97,99,116,32,112,97,117,115,101,32,116,111,117,99,104,39,44,32,97,115,121,110,99,32,40,41,32,61,62,32,123,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":9,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":246,\"content\":\"test('static files', () => {\"},{\"line_number\":282,\"content\":\"test('title music and basin', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":299,\"content\":\"test('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":341,\"content\":\"test('locomotion', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":376,\"content\":\"test('guns fever surgery rescue finish', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":447,\"content\":\"test('map while driving and sliders', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":491,\"content\":\"test('story both endings', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":516,\"content\":\"test('solo round', async () => {\"},{\"line_number\":551,\"content\":\"test('menus attract pause touch', async () => {\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c607b2e1-bc1e-4af9-aa25-bf11e8c6a390"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_463","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The shared engine is last.\n\nResetting sliders at the end is safe. The catch block already resets timeScale to 0, matching existing tests. Spawning soldiers in the story test should be fine. buildModel likely works in headless Node since it only uses geometry. toonMaterial might need a renderer.\n\ntoonMaterial will be tried first. If headless Node throws, MeshBasicMaterial with the DataTexture map will be used instead. paintGps and refreshMap already write into mapPx so the held sheet shows scars.\n\nposeMap will remount the map sheet if its parent camera changes. game.update will call world.poseMap() and world.syncViews(). syncViews after fixed is unnecessary because update runs after fixed.\n\nspawnSoldier will attach immediately so tests can assert parentage before step. Civil will attach in spawnTown. Buddy will attach in makeBuddy, which runs during build when the scene exists.\n\nDead buddies remain invisible because placeRig sets visibility based on the alive flag. round.js leaks views by leaving world.buddies as an array; it will be replaced with a clearBuddies method that drops each view before clearing the list. resetDynamic will also drop every actor view and empty the actors array.\n\nresetDynamic will drop views for non-civil actors, filter the array, and then clear buddies. toTitle will use a new keepCivilians method that drops non-civil views and keeps only civilians. A small hat mesh with MeshBasicMaterial may be added to distinguish factions.\n\nThe soldier model itself is the visible rig, so no extra hat mesh is needed. Harvest and concord prompts will skip tinting if shared materials are used. The `floats: true` flag means the model does not sit on the ground; position is handled manually. Tests will import unchanged if they use the world API. New prompt strings already exist for font scanning. Math.random must be avoided. nearPrompt ordering may return the fever prompt before the buddy.\n\nThe tablet prompt is blocked while fever is active, so the buddy prompt appears first. In m6, setup leaves feverIn undefined and tablets at two, meaning fever never starts and the buddy prompt wins. Tests that complete steps instantly also avoid triggering fever. A bug in m6 lines: completeStep increments progress without checking that _linesDone is set, so calling it from a test skips the requirement.\n\nThe knockBuddy bug is harmless because the test uses KeyE for syrettes. After the fix, burning stays false when knockBuddy runs. m6 setup gives one syrette. The second knockBuddy may target the same buddy again, but downs them and finishes with deadBuddies populated. In the story m6 path where Ines syrettes a dead Dov, the step completes without killing her.\n\nA test will verify the \"FINISH IT\" prompt when downBuddy is called with burning set to true. This preserves the fire refusal rule.\n\nA `clickHud` helper will convert screen Y coordinates to normalized pointer values for menu tests. The menus test needs this helper. I should verify that input still processes while timeScale is zero.\n\nThe dev menu opens without setting menuArm. For the Focus 10 click, I will release any lingering pointer and keys first, then set focus to 10, step once to clear stale input, and finally click at y=86. The menus test already steps thirty frames while paused before opening the dev menu. attachRig does not check actor kind, so mercs can be attached too.\n\nMercs are not moved by tickActors, so tests can set their x position and rely on syncViews during update to move the view. Civilians fleeing is not required. The driving test will gain a map assertion and a short on-foot section before entering the truck. poseMap in update will retry mounting the map sheet if build() runs before the camera is assigned.\n\nA tiny probe will verify headless camera access if tests fail. Map assertions will check that the texture image data matches the held mapPx buffer. GPS assertions will confirm the gps object exists and its texture data matches gpsPx. paintGps writes a pixel based on wind direction.\n\nThe GPS hot pixel is placed six pixels from the center in the direction of the wind angle. Tests will verify this shifts when the wind direction changes. The player position is stamped during map refresh, so a step with the map visible will leave a white pixel that the texture reads back.\n\napplySetup keeps civilian views because the keep filter only drops soldiers. resetDynamic removes all actors and spawns new civilians. Attract mode also calls resetDynamic, so it respawns civilians cleanly. Props have no views, so clearing props is safe. The plan is solid and ready to implement.\n\nThe hover bug only affects rows that overlap. At 16-pixel spacing, rows touch at the boundary but do not overlap, so the last match wins safely. A nine-row menu keeps the reset button inside the 270-pixel HUD, so it can be clicked. Before the fix, the reset button sat at y=470 and was off-screen.\n\nThe reset button now sits inside the nine-row menu window, so tests can click it directly. No new exports are needed. The about page currently lists 13 issues; the skeptic found four more, so I will add them to ISSUES.md and raise the count to 17. This requires updating about.js, rebuilding, and aligning the exit interview.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4f292a34-a041-4e34-a52d-75115bb3d3f2-144","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/ISSUES.md","limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4162,"output_tokens":2997,"cache_read_input_tokens":186624,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"d7a3d271-4e36-447a-ac2a-1fc20a09332c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-4f292a34-a041-4e34-a52d-75115bb3d3f2-144","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1→# Issues testing caught\\n\\n13 game-breaking defects. Each one stopped a path the suite has to finish. The fixes are in the shipped game.\\n\\n1. A mouse click counted as a controller, so the touch gate closed and the title's first item opened the menu instead of Settings.\\n2. Attract left the player in the truck, in god mode, with the map up. The next mission inherited that and could not walk.\\n3. A truck that already existed stayed at the attract spawn, so the clinic enter failed.\\n4. Returning to the title left the solo session attached, so attract never started.\\n5. Mission setup left earlier soldiers alive. One of them killed the player during the train hold.\\n10→6. Cash Run did not revive a dead player, so friendly fire never left the gun.\\n7. The title still ran soldier damage. Mercs from a finished round opened the death screen and froze the clock, so attract could not start.\\n8. The flare's click dismissed the ending card on the same frame.\\n9. The last burn sat on ground that cannot burn, so the ending mission could not finish. Completion now accepts fresh flame inside the radius.\\n10. The payroll case was hidden on the convoy, so the shots that stopped the truck destroyed the case too.\\n11. A random jam cleared the scripted jam count, so the scripted jam never arrived.\\n12. A same-computer session started after boot never opened its network timer, so the join never saw the host.\\n13. The link finish message was dropped because the session marked itself ended before the send.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"1→# Issues testing caught\\n\\n13 game-breaking defects. Each one stopped a path the suite has to finish. The fixes are in the shipped game.\\n\\n1. A mouse click counted as a controller, so the touch gate closed and the title's first item opened the menu instead of Settings.\\n2. Attract left the player in the truck, in god mode, with the map up. The next mission inherited that and could not walk.\\n3. A truck that already existed stayed at the attract spawn, so the clinic enter failed.\\n4. Returning to the title left the solo session attached, so attract never started.\\n5. Mission setup left earlier soldiers alive. One of them killed the player during the train hold.\\n10→6. Cash Run did not revive a dead player, so friendly fire never left the gun.\\n7. The title still ran soldier damage. Mercs from a finished round opened the death screen and froze the clock, so attract could not start.\\n8. The flare's click dismissed the ending card on the same frame.\\n9. The last burn sat on ground that cannot burn, so the ending mission could not finish. Completion now accepts fresh flame inside the radius.\\n10. The payroll case was hidden on the convoy, so the shots that stopped the truck destroyed the case too.\\n11. A random jam cleared the scripted jam count, so the scripted jam never arrived.\\n12. A same-computer session started after boot never opened its network timer, so the join never saw the host.\\n13. The link finish message was dropped because the session marked itself ended before the send.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/ISSUES.md\",\"offset\":null,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"# Issues testing caught\\n\\n13 game-breaking defects. Each one stopped a path the suite has to finish. The fixes are in the shipped game.\\n\\n1. A mouse click counted as a controller, so the touch gate closed and the title's first item opened the menu instead of Settings.\\n2. Attract left the player in the truck, in god mode, with the map up. The next mission inherited that and could not walk.\\n3. A truck that already existed stayed at the attract spawn, so the clinic enter failed.\\n4. Returning to the title left the solo session attached, so attract never started.\\n5. Mission setup left earlier soldiers alive. One of them killed the player during the train hold.\\n6. Cash Run did not revive a dead player, so friendly fire never left the gun.\\n7. The title still ran soldier damage. Mercs from a finished round opened the death screen and froze the clock, so attract could not start.\\n8. The flare's click dismissed the ending card on the same frame.\\n9. The last burn sat on ground that cannot burn, so the ending mission could not finish. Completion now accepts fresh flame inside the radius.\\n10. The payroll case was hidden on the convoy, so the shots that stopped the truck destroyed the case too.\\n11. A random jam cleared the scripted jam count, so the scripted jam never arrived.\\n12. A same-computer session started after boot never opened its network timer, so the join never saw the host.\\n13. The link finish message was dropped because the session marked itself ended before the send.\\n\",\"total_lines\":17}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3b0416c1-afcc-4c63-8839-c4e4ac9e1a2b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_464","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue count will be updated to 17 after the fixes are verified.\n\nAbout strings must stay within the HUD font. I will implement all code changes now. I need to check world.js nearPrompt and tryUse so knockBuddy burning false works with the existing tryUse order. I also need to fix game.js toTitle and add sync in update. buildModel soldier definitions use palette names. dropView must handle actors without a parent view.\n\nattachRig will skip if the scene is missing. placeRig now places buddies at the player's feet when x or z is null, and it uses ground() after build. I am also starting syncViews.\n\nsyncViews now iterates over actors and buddies, attaching rigs and placing them before calling poseMap. It will be invoked from game.update. mountMap needs the toonMaterial import, and PlaneGeometry is available in three r186. A quick camera property check will follow via test. The story bot buddy-down with syrette case uses KeyE for consumeAction.\n\nThe tryUse order correctly prioritizes syrettes over melee when the buddy is down. The story test should still pass because m6 starts with one syrette and the bot never heals. I will replace the downs-in-buddy-then-KeyE block in the guns test.\n\nStarting mission m6 at the end of the guns test is safe because completeStep is instant. Fever from m6 is not a concern. I am checking whether lines from a previous step persist into the buddy-down step, since announceStep only clears the lines array when the new step explicitly sets lines.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3225fd22-d9f8-4af7-bea2-2c10b2319520-145","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":140,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-3225fd22-d9f8-4af7-bea2-2c10b2319520-146","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","offset":434,"limit":20}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3396,"output_tokens":1093,"cache_read_input_tokens":190720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"56b6a2b0-9719-42f8-96a2-db3a9fc8a945"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-3225fd22-d9f8-4af7-bea2-2c10b2319520-145","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"140→      engine.step(Math.ceil(26 * 60), DT);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'tablet') {\\n      holdKey('KeyH', 90);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'goto' || step.do === 'drive' || step.do === 'leave') {\\n      const site = step.site ? siteById(step.site) : null;\\n      const x = site ? site.x : step.x;\\n      const z = site ? site.z : step.z;\\n      const radius = step.r || (step.do === 'leave' ? 40 : 20);\\n      if (step.do === 'leave') {\\n        goTo(x + radius + 30, z, 8);\\n150→      } else goTo(x, z, Math.max(4, radius - 2));\\n    } else if (step.do === 'jam') {\\n      arm('tractor');\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 24 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'jam'; n++) {\\n        if (w.weapon?.jammed) tap('KeyR');\\n        else holdFire(15);\\n      }\\n    } else if (step.do === 'repair') {\\n      holdKey('KeyE', 220);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'syrette') {\\n160→      holdKey('KeyQ', 70);\\n    } else if (step.do === 'destroy') {\\n      for (let n = 0; n < 8 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'destroy'; n++) {\\n        const prop = w.props.find((p) => p.alive !== false && p.tag === step.tag);\\n        if (!prop) break;\\n        placeFacing(prop.x, prop.z);\\n        if (w.guns.some((g) => g.id === 'tractor')) arm('tractor');\\n        engine.input.setButtons(1);\\n        for (let f = 0; f < 90 && w.currentStep()?.do === 'destroy'; f++) engine.step(1, DT);\\n        engine.input.setButtons(0);\\n170→        engine.step(1, DT);\\n      }\\n    } else if (step.do === 'burn') {\\n      if (w.inVehicle && w.vehicleHp >= 50) tap('KeyE');\\n      const r = step.r || 12;\\n      const origin = w.fire.cellAt(step.x, step.z);\\n      let lx = step.x;\\n      let lz = step.z;\\n      const reach = Math.ceil(r / 5);\\n      let best = Infinity;\",\"content_concise\":\"140→      e