{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_485","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Prior tests may have killed buddies.\n\nDeadBuddies is empty before the guns test. Ines and Dov start alive in m6. Story clears at test start. Map tests between missions reset state correctly. The story test skips toTitle.\n\nstartMission replaces the active mission cleanly. The dev menu test pauses with timeScale 0 and steps 30 frames without advancing the clock. The pixel engine likely uses a fixed timestep, so updates may still run but with zero delta.\n\nThe pause test only proves the clock stops. It does not prove update still runs when timeScale is zero. I need to check the engine step code or API.md to confirm whether fixed timestep executes with zero delta.\n\nI will verify whether the engine still runs update and hover while timeScale is zero. If it skips updates, I can set timeScale to 1 in dev mode instead. blocksSim returns true outside play and attract modes, so the simulation will not advance but update will still execute. This lets me test hover without relying on timeScale.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5f0d4645-443a-4e40-ad4f-16a1f7b44852-39","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"timeScale","glob":"**/API.md"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-5f0d4645-443a-4e40-ad4f-16a1f7b44852-40","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scale === 0|timeScale|this\\.scale","glob":"**/GUIDE.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1589,"output_tokens":653,"cache_read_input_tokens":82816,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"3318c11d-fc5f-41a4-a1f3-785b77327ac5"}
