opped, like a pause). Scales game time, physics, animation, particles, tweens and the camera follow; not transitions, shake or the render loop. Back to 1 when…\"},{\"line_number\":185,\"content\":\"- `state(): { version: string; game: string; seed: number; ready: boolean; paused: boolean; time: number; timeScale: number; hitstop: number; screen: ScreenFxState; backend: BackendName; ... 19 more ...; status: string; }`: Snapshot for tests, tooling and agents.\"},{\"line_number\":4186,\"content\":\"pads. Game time (they pause, slow down and freeze with `engine.timeScale` and hitstops)\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-5f0d4645-443a-4e40-ad4f-16a1f7b44852-40","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,32,67,114,121,32,84,111,111,32,70,97,114,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,47,71,85,73,68,69,46,109,100,10,52,55,52,58,99,116,120,46,101,110,103,105,110,101,46,116,105,109,101,83,99,97,108,101,32,61,32,48,46,50,53,59,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,32,47,47,32,115,108,111,119,32,109,111,116,105,111,110,32,40,49,32,110,111,114,109,97,108,44,32,48,32,97,32,102,114,111,122,101,110,32,109,101,110,117,41,59,32,108,111,97,100,71,97,109,101,32,114,101,115,101,116,115,32,105,116,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":1,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/GUIDE.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":474,\"content\":\"ctx.engine.timeScale = 0.25;                 // slow motion (1 normal, 0 a frozen menu); loadGame resets it\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"4655bb8d-bdad-4dd0-bc10-f4052f8cb646"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_486","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A critical issue was noted: key presses during a frozen state are dropped, similar to a pause.\n\nThe render loop still runs when timeScale is 0, but input presses are dropped. This explains why the touch test works on the title screen while clicks fail in dev mode. A paused player opening dev mode would also be unable to click.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-21cbc06e-6db2-49cd-bc7f-1384aecd029e-41","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md","offset":150,"limit":40}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-21cbc06e-6db2-49cd-bc7f-1384aecd029e-42","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"presses made|dropped|timeScale","glob":"**/API.md","head_limit":30}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1176,"output_tokens":316,"cache_read_input_tokens":84352,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"8ba2285a-f070-4d89-a169-cf11d88e64e9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-21cbc06e-6db2-49cd-bc7f-1384aecd029e-41","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"150→- `debugKeys: DebugKeyMap`: Active engine hotkeys (from EngineOptions.debugKeys; none until the engine starts).\\n- `manual: boolean`: Tooling: the render loop stops driving the game; advance it yourself with `step()`. Frame-exact and independent of how fast the browser renders (filmstrips, replays).\\n- `frame: number`\\n- `fps: number`: Rendered frames per second (measured over ~0.5 s).\\n- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`: Requested quality (`auto` adapts); `quality` is the level in use.\\n- `time: number`\\n- `readonly renderer: View`\\n- `readonly physics: Physics`\\n- `camera: CameraRig`\\n- `readonly scene: Scene`\\n160→- `get gpu: PixelRenderer | null`: The page's renderer, for direct GPU work (readbacks, the canvas, compute): null headless (`Engine.headless`), where nothing is drawn. Gameplay reads `renderer`, which both have.\\n- `get game: Game`: The running game. Replace it with `loadGame()`.\\n- `get paused: boolean`: Freeze simulation, animation, particles and game time (rendering continues). For tooling, capture and pause menus. Queued key presses are dropped while paused.\\n- `get lights: LightPool`: The dynamic light pool (render/lights.ts), engine-owned: its lights stay in the scene across levels, so loading another level never changes the light count (no recompiles). Created on first use; sized by quality.\\n- `get timeScale: number`: Game speed: 1 normal, 0.25 slow motion, 2 double, 0 frozen (a menu: key presses made meanwhile are dropped, like a pause). Scales game time, physics, animation, particles, tweens and the camera follow; not transitions, shake or the render loop. Back to 1 when…\\n- `hitstop(seconds: number): void`: Freeze the game for `seconds` of real time: impact frames that sell a hit. Rendering, screen shake and transitions keep going; overlapping hitstops keep the longest. Key presses made during a hitstop still count afterwards (a buffered jump).\\n- `get screen: ScreenFx`: Transitions, flashes and shockwaves (render/screenFx.ts): `await engine.screen.cover('iris')`.\\n- `get sunDir: Vector3`: The direction sunlight comes from (unit, pointing at the sun).\\n- `setSunDirection(dir: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]): void`: Point the sun (and its shadows): a direction toward the sun, normalised here. A level's time of day or a sun dial; reset to the engine default when the level unloads. Below the horizon the sun is kept just above it (lower `sun.intensity` for night instead).\\n- `get quality: QualityLevel`: The quality level in use (see `EngineOptions.quality`).\\n170→- `useQuality(option: QualityOption): void`: Quality by option: a level, or `auto`: the device's level (low on phones and tablets, else medium), lowered once if a few seconds of frames are slow (measured once, then remembered).\\n- `get debugShown: boolean`: Whether the debug panel is showing.\\n- `showDebug(on: boolean): void`: Show or hide the debug panel (created the first time it shows, filled at once: the loop fills it only while the game runs).\\n- `setQuality(level: QualityLevel): void`\\n- `get maxFps: number`: Frame cap of the render loop (0 = display rate).\\n- `setCamera(config: CameraConfig, options: { syncUrl?: boolean } = {}): CameraRig`: Swap the camera preset mid-game (review tool: presets are a per-game choice). The player, physics and the rest of the world are left exactly as they are. `free` and `fixed` without an explicit position start from the view currently on screen. Keeps `?camera=`…\\n- `toggleMode(): RenderMode`\\n- `toggleResolution(): Resolution`\\n- `get availableFilters: readonly string[]`: Every filter id the engine ships (see render/filters.ts).\\n- `get filters: readonly string[]`\\n180→- `setFilters(ids: readonly string[]): void`\\n- `get look: Look`: The current look (a copy): per-layer pixel art and filters, whole-scene filters.\\n- `get lookPresets: Readonly<Record<string, Look>>`: Every named look (LOOK_PRESETS): `engine.setLook(engine.lookPresets.pixel_heroes)`.\\n- `setLook(look: Look): void`: Apply a look (render/look.ts); `LOOK_PRESETS` has named ones.\\n- `cycleLook(step: 1 | -1): string`: Cycle through LOOK_PRESETS ([ and ] keys).\\n- `state(): { version: string; game: string; seed: number; ready: boolean; paused: boolean; time: number; timeScale: number; hitstop: number; screen: ScreenFxState; backend: BackendName; ... 19 more ...; status: string; }`: Snapshot for tests, tooling and agents.\\n- `step(n = 1, dt = 1 / 60): void`: Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation, animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n- `loadGame(game: Game, options: { camera?: CameraConfig } = {}): Promise<void>`: Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas, camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM, GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n- `get seed: number`: The seed every level's `ctx.random` comes from (`EngineOptions.seed`, `?seed=`; a replay sets it).\",\"content_concise\":\"150→- `debugKeys: DebugKeyMap`: Active engine hotkeys (from EngineOptions.debugKeys; none until the engine starts).\\n- `manual: boolean`: Tooling: the render loop stops driving the game; advance it yourself with `step()`. Frame-exact and independent of how fast the browser renders (filmstrips, replays).\\n- `frame: number`\\n- `fps: number`: Rendered frames per second (measured over ~0.5 s).\\n- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`: Requested quality (`auto` adapts); `quality` is the level in use.\\n- `time: number`\\n- `readonly renderer: View`\\n- `readonly physics: Physics`\\n- `camera: CameraRig`\\n- `readonly scene: Scene`\\n160→- `get gpu: PixelRenderer | null`: The page's renderer, for direct GPU work (readbacks, the canvas, compute): null headless (`Engine.headless`), where nothing is drawn. Gameplay reads `renderer`, which both have.\\n- `get game: Game`: The running game. Replace it with `loadGame()`.\\n- `get paused: boolean`: Freeze simulation, animation, particles and game time (rendering continues). For tooling, capture and pause menus. Queued key presses are dropped while paused.\\n- `get lights: LightPool`: The dynamic light pool (render/lights.ts), engine-owned: its lights stay in the scene across levels, so loading another level never changes the light count (no recompiles). Created on first use; sized by quality.\\n- `get timeScale: number`: Game speed: 1 normal, 0.25 slow motion, 2 double, 0 frozen (a menu: key presses made meanwhile are dropped, like a pause). Scales game time, physics, animation, particles, tweens and the camera follow; not transitions, shake or the render loop. Back to 1 when…\\n- `hitstop(seconds: number): void`: Freeze the game for `seconds` of real time: impact frames that sell a hit. Rendering, screen shake and transitions keep going; overlapping hitstops keep the longest. Key presses made during a hitstop still count afterwards (a buffered jump).\\n- `get screen: ScreenFx`: Transitions, flashes and shockwaves (render/screenFx.ts): `await engine.screen.cover('iris')`.\\n- `get sunDir: Vector3`: The direction sunlight comes from (unit, pointing at the sun).\\n- `setSunDirection(dir: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]): void`: Point the sun (and its shadows): a direction toward the sun, normalised here. A level's time of day or a sun dial; reset to the engine default when the level unloads. Below the horizon the sun is kept just above it (lower `sun.intensity` for night instead).\\n- `get quality: QualityLevel`: The quality level in use (see `EngineOptions.quality`).\\n170→- `useQuality(option: QualityOption): void`: Quality by option: a level, or `auto`: the device's level (low on phones and tablets, else medium), lowered once if a few seconds of frames are slow (measured once, then remembered).\\n- `get debugShown: boolean`: Whether the debug panel is showing.\\n- `showDebug(on: boolean): void`: Show or hide the debug panel (created the first time it shows, filled at once: the loop fills it only while the game runs).\\n- `setQuality(level: QualityLevel): void`\\n- `get maxFps: number`: Frame cap of the render loop (0 = display rate).\\n- `setCamera(config: CameraConfig, options: { syncUrl?: boolean } = {}): CameraRig`: Swap the camera preset mid-game (review tool: presets are a per-game choice). The player, physics and the rest of the world are left exactly as they are. `free` and `fixed` without an explicit position start from the view currently on screen. Keeps `?camera=`…\\n- `toggleMode(): RenderMode`\\n- `toggleResolution(): Resolution`\\n- `get availableFilters: readonly string[]`: Every filter id the engine ships (see render/filters.ts).\\n- `get filters: readonly string[]`\\n180→- `setFilters(ids: readonly string[]): void`\\n- `get look: Look`: The current look (a copy): per-layer pixel art and filters, whole-scene filters.\\n- `get lookPresets: Readonly<Record<string, Look>>`: Every named look (LOOK_PRESETS): `engine.setLook(engine.lookPresets.pixel_heroes)`.\\n- `setLook(look: Look): void`: Apply a look (render/look.ts); `LOOK_PRESETS` has named ones.\\n- `cycleLook(step: 1 | -1): string`: Cycle through LOOK_PRESETS ([ and ] keys).\\n- `state(): { version: string; game: string; seed: number; ready: boolean; paused: boolean; time: number; timeScale: number; hitstop: number; screen: ScreenFxState; backend: BackendName; ... 19 more ...; status: string; }`: Snapshot for tests, tooling and agents.\\n- `step(n = 1, dt = 1 / 60): void`: Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation, animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n- `loadGame(game: Game, options: { camera?: CameraConfig } = {}): Promise<void>`: Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas, camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM, GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n- `get seed: number`: The seed every level's `ctx.random` comes from (`EngineOptions.seed`, `?seed=`; a replay sets it).\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":150,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"- `debugKeys: DebugKeyMap`: Active engine hotkeys (from EngineOptions.debugKeys; none until the engine starts).\\n- `manual: boolean`: Tooling: the render loop stops driving the game; advance it yourself with `step()`. Frame-exact and independent of how fast the browser renders (filmstrips, replays).\\n- `frame: number`\\n- `fps: number`: Rendered frames per second (measured over ~0.5 s).\\n- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`: Requested quality (`auto` adapts); `quality` is the level in use.\\n- `time: number`\\n- `readonly renderer: View`\\n- `readonly physics: Physics`\\n- `camera: CameraRig`\\n- `readonly scene: Scene`\\n- `get gpu: PixelRenderer | null`: The page's renderer, for direct GPU work (readbacks, the canvas, compute): null headless (`Engine.headless`), where nothing is drawn. Gameplay reads `renderer`, which both have.\\n- `get game: Game`: The running game. Replace it with `loadGame()`.\\n- `get paused: boolean`: Freeze simulation, animation, particles and game time (rendering continues). For tooling, capture and pause menus. Queued key presses are dropped while paused.\\n- `get lights: LightPool`: The dynamic light pool (render/lights.ts), engine-owned: its lights stay in the scene across levels, so loading another level never changes the light count (no recompiles). Created on first use; sized by quality.\\n- `get timeScale: number`: Game speed: 1 normal, 0.25 slow motion, 2 double, 0 frozen (a menu: key presses made meanwhile are dropped, like a pause). Scales game time, physics, animation, particles, tweens and the camera follow; not transitions, shake or the render loop. Back to 1 when…\\n- `hitstop(seconds: number): void`: Freeze the game for `seconds` of real time: impact frames that sell a hit. Rendering, screen shake and transitions keep going; overlapping hitstops keep the longest. Key presses made during a hitstop still count afterwards (a buffered jump).\\n- `get screen: ScreenFx`: Transitions, flashes and shockwaves (render/screenFx.ts): `await engine.screen.cover('iris')`.\\n- `get sunDir: Vector3`: The direction sunlight comes from (unit, pointing at the sun).\\n- `setSunDirection(dir: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number]): void`: Point the sun (and its shadows): a direction toward the sun, normalised here. A level's time of day or a sun dial; reset to the engine default when the level unloads. Below the horizon the sun is kept just above it (lower `sun.intensity` for night instead).\\n- `get quality: QualityLevel`: The quality level in use (see `EngineOptions.quality`).\\n- `useQuality(option: QualityOption): void`: Quality by option: a level, or `auto`: the device's level (low on phones and tablets, else medium), lowered once if a few seconds of frames are slow (measured once, then remembered).\\n- `get debugShown: boolean`: Whether the debug panel is showing.\\n- `showDebug(on: boolean): void`: Show or hide the debug panel (created the first time it shows, filled at once: the loop fills it only while the game runs).\\n- `setQuality(level: QualityLevel): void`\\n- `get maxFps: number`: Frame cap of the render loop (0 = display rate).\\n- `setCamera(config: CameraConfig, options: { syncUrl?: boolean } = {}): CameraRig`: Swap the camera preset mid-game (review tool: presets are a per-game choice). The player, physics and the rest of the world are left exactly as they are. `free` and `fixed` without an explicit position start from the view currently on screen. Keeps `?camera=`…\\n- `toggleMode(): RenderMode`\\n- `toggleResolution(): Resolution`\\n- `get availableFilters: readonly string[]`: Every filter id the engine ships (see render/filters.ts).\\n- `get filters: readonly string[]`\\n- `setFilters(ids: readonly string[]): void`\\n- `get look: Look`: The current look (a copy): per-layer pixel art and filters, whole-scene filters.\\n- `get lookPresets: Readonly<Record<string, Look>>`: Every named look (LOOK_PRESETS): `engine.setLook(engine.lookPresets.pixel_heroes)`.\\n- `setLook(look: Look): void`: Apply a look (render/look.ts); `LOOK_PRESETS` has named ones.\\n- `cycleLook(step: 1 | -1): string`: Cycle through LOOK_PRESETS ([ and ] keys).\\n- `state(): { version: string; game: string; seed: number; ready: boolean; paused: boolean; time: number; timeScale: number; hitstop: number; screen: ScreenFxState; backend: BackendName; ... 19 more ...; status: string; }`: Snapshot for tests, tooling and agents.\\n- `step(n = 1, dt = 1 / 60): void`: Tooling: switch to manual time and advance `n` frames of `dt` seconds (simulation, animation, camera). Nothing is drawn; call `renderer.capture()` to see the result.\\n- `loadGame(game: Game, options: { camera?: CameraConfig } = {}): Promise<void>`: Unload the running game and start `game` in the same engine (renderer, canvas, camera rig, input, audio context and debug UI stay).\\n- `dispose(): void`: Stop the loop and free everything: game, scene, physics, audio, input listeners, DOM, GPU. With a `loadGame()` in flight, the world and GPU resources are freed once its `setup()` has finished (it never runs against a freed physics world or renderer).\\n- `get seed: number`: The seed every level's `ctx.random` comes from (`EngineOptions.seed`, `?seed=`; a replay sets it).\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-21cbc06e-6db2-49cd-bc7f-1384aecd029e-42","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,70,111,117,110,100,32,49,51,32,109,97,116,99,104,105,110,103,32,108,105,110,101,115,10,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,47,65,32,67,114,121,32,84,111,111,32,70,97,114,45,70,97,114,32,67,114,121,32,50,45,103,114,111,107,45,52,46,55,45,120,104,105,103,104,45,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,47,65,80,73,46,109,100,10,57,51,58,83,105,110,103,108,101,32,104,111,116,107,101,121,115,32,109,111,118,101,100,32,40,97,32,107,101,121,32,99,111,100,101,44,32,97,32,108,105,115,116,32,111,102,32,99,111,100,101,115,41,32,111,114,32,100,114,111,112,112,101,100,32,40,96,110,117,108,108,96,32,47,32,96,91,93,96,41,46,10,49,54,50,58,45,32,96,103,101,116,32,112,97,117,115,101,100,58,32,98,111,111,108,101,97,110,96,58,32,70,114,101,101,122,101,32,115,105,109,117,108,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,97,110,105,109,97,116,105,111,110,44,32,112,97,114,116,105,99,108,101,115,32,97,110,100,32,103,97,109,101,32,116,105,109,101,32,40,114,101,110,100,101,114,105,110,103,32,99,1