6,116,111,110,115,93,44,111,61,97,46,106,111,105,110,40,96,44,96,41,59,10],\"output_for_prompt\":\"exit: 0\\n\\n==== beginFrame( 1262174\\nbeginFrame(e,t,n){this.pollGamepads(t,n),this.now=e,this.analog.x+=0,this.analog.y+=0,this.padAxis.x+=0,this.padAxis.y+=0,this.mouseDelta.x+=0,this.mouseDelta.y+=0;for(let[t,n]of this.queued)e-n>this.pressWindow&&this.queued.delete(t)}get pointerLocked(){return this.lockTarget!==null&&document.pointerLockElement===this.lockTarget}isDown(...e){return this.anyDown(e)}anyDown(e){for(let t of e)if(this.held.has(t)||this.padHeld.has(t))return!0;return!1}wasPressed(...e){return e.some(e=>this.pressed.has(e))}consumePress(...e){return this.consumeAny(e)}consumeAny(e){let t=!1;for(let n of e){let e=this.queued.get(n);e!==void 0&&(this.queued.delete(n),this.now-e<=this.pressWindow&&(t=!0))}return t}s\\n\\n==== clearQueued( 1263628\\nclearQueued(...e){e.length===0&&this.queued.clear();for(let t of e)this.queued.delete(t)}moveAxis(){let e=Math.hypot(this.analog.x,this.analog.y),t=Math.hypot(this.padAxis.x,this.padAxis.y),n=e>.12&&e>=t?this.analog:t>0?this.padAxis:null;if(n){let e=Math.hypot(n.x,n.y);return e>1?{x:n.x/e,y:n.y/e}:{x:n.x,y:n.y}}let r=+!!this.isDown(`KeyD`,`ArrowRight`)-!!this.isDown(`KeyA`,`ArrowLeft`),i=+!!this.isDown(`KeyW`,`ArrowUp`)-!!this.isDown(`KeyS`,`ArrowDown`),a=Math.hypot(r,i);return a>1?{x:r/a,y:i/a}:{x:r,y:i}}endFrame(){this.pressed.clear(),this._commands=[],this._buttonEvents=[],this.mouseDelta.x=0,this.mouseDelta.y=0,this.wheel=0}setKey(e,t){this._playing||(t?(this.held.has(e)||this.press(e),t\\n\\n==== deliver(){ 1265131\\ndeliver(){this._commands=this.outbox,this.outbox=[]}addPointer(e,t,n=0){this._playing||(this.mouseDelta.x+=e,this.mouseDelta.y+=t,this.wheel+=n)}snapshot(e,t){let n={dt:e},r=[.../* @__PURE__ */ new Set([...this.held,...this.padHeld])].sort(),i=r.join(`,`);(!t||i!==t.held)&&(n.held=r),this.pressed.size&&(n.pressed=[...this.pressed].sort()),(this.analog.x||this.analog.y)&&(n.analog=[this.analog.x,this.analog.y]),(this.padAxis.x||this.padAxis.y)&&(n.pad=[this.padAxis.x,this.padAxis.y]),(this.mouseDelta.x||this.mouseDelta.y)&&(n.delta=[this.mouseDelta.x,this.mouseDelta.y]),this.wheel&&(n.wheel=this.wheel);let a=[this.pointer.x,this.pointer.y,+!!this.pointer.over,this.mouseButtons],o=a.join(`,`);\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"command\":\"python3 - << 'PY'\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\ntext = Path(\\\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.js\\\").read_text()\\nfor needle in [\\\"beginFrame(\\\", \\\"clearQueued(\\\", \\\"deliver(){\\\"]:\\n    i = text.find(needle)\\n    print(\\\"\\\\n====\\\", needle, i)\\n    print(text[i:i+700])\\nPY\",\"truncated\":false,\"signal\":null,\"timed_out\":false,\"description\":\"Read input beginFrame, deliver, clearQueued\",\"current_dir\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work\",\"output_file\":\"/home/micha/.grok/sessions/%2Fhome%2Fmicha%2Fdev%2Fcc-matrix%2Fruns%2Fgrok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c%2Fwork/01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df/terminal/call-7a182926-13ce-4bab-9321-c90daf1150de-48.log\",\"total_bytes\":2181}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c23ea559-66fb-4ddc-8671-3f18a175ecdc"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_493","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Button events survive clearQueued.\n\nwasPressed still works during frozen frames because the pressed set clears at endFrame, not clearQueued. consumePress is dropped during pause since queued events are cleared before advance. The pause test taps Escape before openPause occurs.\n\nThe Escape key press occurs while timeScale is still 1, so openPause freezes the following frames. Clicks work during freeze because buttonEvents bypass the queued system. I will now write the tests and add helper functions near placeFacing.\n\nI will add an `igniteStep()` helper to the test file that duplicates the existing burn loop from `playMission`. This reuses the real player action path instead of reimplementing fire rules.\n\nRefactoring `playMission` to use a shared `doBurn()` function is cleaner than duplicating the burn loop. The knock test cannot use `playMission` because it would syrette and finish the mission before asserting the prompt and burning state. I will stop at buddy-down instead. I am now drafting the `reachBuddyDown()` helper.\n\nI am writing the `texBytes()` helper to extract raw texture data from a map texture. I am also drafting the `assertHeldMap()` assertion that checks the map sheet is visible, parented to the camera, uses the correct texture, and contains a visible GPS object.\n\nassertHeldMap now also verifies the GPS texture matches gpsPx and that the wind marker was painted. I am writing assertRig to confirm an actor's rig is in the scene and its position updates correctly after a step.\n\nassertRig now asserts the rig moved within 0.05 units after a step. I am writing `lightCurrentBurn()` to find the nearest fire cell to light the current burn step.\n\n`lightCurrentBurn()` now selects the nearest valid fire cell to light, teleports to it, arms the flare, fires, and steps forward. Refactoring `playMission` to call this shared helper would eliminate duplication.\n\nThe guns test now replaces the old path. It starts mission m6, advances through lines and goto, teleports to the long-field site, lights the current burn with `lightCurrentBurn()`, and asserts the step reaches buddy-down.\n\nThe knockBuddy test now asserts the downed buddy is not burning and has a rig in the scene. It checks that the syrette prompt appears and that the campaign has syrettes available. Tapping E syrettes the buddy back up, confirming it recovers health and the syrette count drops by one.\n\nThe knockBuddy test now asserts the campaign syrette count reaches zero. It knocks a second buddy down and verifies that knock leaves no burn. The finish-it prompt appears, and tapping E records the death in deadBuddies. A live buddy is then downed with burning enabled to test the finish-it path.\n\nThe burning-down test now asserts the prompt is FINISH IT, taps E, and confirms the buddy dies while the syrette count stays at one. The knockBuddy logic downs the first alive buddy, so a syrette can pick that same buddy up.\n\nknockBuddy selects the first alive buddy in the list, so a syretted buddy can be knocked down again. The rig is attached by makeBuddy and placed with rotation.z set after down.\n\nThe rig view stays in the scene and syncViews places it on step. A failed attachRig would be caught by the test. The fever prompt appears because m6 tablets are 2 and feverT is full, but the burn lasts only 20 frames plus a few steps, not 12 minutes. Tapping Enter advances the lines step to goto. The long-field site is reachable within one step, so two steps suffice. Then lightCurrentBurn handles the burn.\n\nThe long-field site at (-260, -300) may already be scarred from the m6 setup. If every cell in the burn radius is burnt or fuelless, the flare search finds nothing and the burn step cannot start. The story test passed with the same logic, so some cell must still be available.\n\nThe map test now inserts an on-foot section and asserts the held map during driving. The actor rig is checked after spawn, and a civil rig is added at the start. The mercenary search is placed after the soldier slider to avoid confusion.\n\nThe 0.05-unit rig position tolerance covers a fleeing civil actor, since the step tick adds only about 0.033 units before syncViews updates the view. A non-fleeing soldier stays exactly at the actor's x coordinate. The dev test will be placed before the about section or after pause.\n\nThe dev test locates the dev item, taps Enter, and asserts the dev screen opens. It checks that more than nine items are listed. It then scrolls by clicking HUD position 86 and verifies the focus lands on the expected top row. Finally it applies a slider change to wearRate.\n\nThe dev test now verifies the wearRate slider reaches 5 and that clicking the reset row restores the default value. It also checks that the reset item remains focused after the click. A problem was spotted: while timeScale is frozen to zero, clearQueued drops queued presses before advance, so a tap Enter during the menu would be lost.\n\nThe existing pause test opens the about menu by tapping Enter while paused. This contradicts the theory that clearQueued empties the input queue before advance, which would drop the press. The actual behavior needs to be checked.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-91aec5f0-53a3-408b-9612-098094047c21-49","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function pressed|consumeAction|function consumeAction","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1448,"output_tokens":3342,"cache_read_input_tokens":94720,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"092f10cd-04fa-4131-bdbf-a8989fe19c1e"}
