olve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\"},{\"line_number\":3231,\"content\":\"`modelSheet`'s options: `buildModel`'s (`params`, `seed`, `palette`, `light`, `catalog` where\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"bd74efe3-6f49-498a-95b2-b5d05965b031"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_497","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-72787da3-c734-4b8e-8c70-98eedcb28268-54","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md","offset":2884,"limit":80}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":867,"output_tokens":100,"cache_read_input_tokens":104576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"70e8ae92-59b5-48b4-9588-d044d651244b"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-72787da3-c734-4b8e-8c70-98eedcb28268-54","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2884→### buildModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\\n```\\n\\n2890→### class Catalog\\n\\n- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\\n- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\\n- `has(id: string): boolean`\\n- `get(id: string): T`\\n- `all(): T[]`\\n- `find(q: { tags?: readonly string[]; text?: string } = {}): T[]`: Defs with every tag in `tags` whose id, about or tags contain every word of `text`.\\n- `search(text: string, o: SearchOptions = {}): T[]`: Defs ranked by how well they match `text`, best first (`searchDefs`).\\n\\n2900→### interface CatalogEntry\\n\\nDefs by id: the engine's built-in libraries (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and a game's\\nown. Ids are how parts, layers and saves refer to defs, so an id names one def per catalog.\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n\\n### checkModel()\\n2910→\\n```ts\\nfunction checkModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: CheckOptions = {}): ModelCheck\\n```\\n\\nEvery check over the model's range: the defaults, then each param at its min and at its max\\n(one at a time), each at seeds 1, 2 and 3 when the parts read the rng. Messages say which\\nbuild they came from unless every build agrees.\\n\\n### decodePng()\\n2920→\\n```ts\\nfunction decodePng(bytes: Uint8Array, inflate: Inflate): RgbaImage\\n```\\n\\nDecode a PNG file's bytes to RGBA (see the file comment for what it reads).\\n\\n### DEFAULT_TEXEL\\n\\n```ts\\n2930→const DEFAULT_TEXEL: 8\\n```\\n\\nTexels per metre for `tex` parts when the def doesn't set `texel`: the densest Gate B passed for\\nsurfaces the camera zooms over (docs/assets/textures.md *Texel density*). A model that moves may set\\nup to `MOVING_TEXEL`.\\n\\n### interface ExpandedModel\\n\\nA model as plain data: no functions, no `use`, every primitive with its slot.\\n2940→\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, Binding>>`\\n- `readonly params: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`\\n- `readonly seed: number`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[]`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`\\n- `readonly anchors?: Readonly<Record<string, Anchor>>`\\n2950→- `readonly light?: ModelLight`\\n- `readonly collider: 'box' | 'cyl' | 'hull' | 'parts' | 'none'`\\n- `readonly texel?: number`\\n- `readonly floats?: boolean`\\n- `readonly source?: Provenance`\\n\\n### expandModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction expandModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ExpandedModel\\n2960→```\\n\\nThe plain-JSON form of a model: params applied, `use` resolved (throws a ModelError on problems).\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"2884→### buildModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\\n```\\n\\n2890→### class Catalog\\n\\n- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\\n- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\\n- `has(id: string): boolean`\\n- `get(id: string): T`\\n- `all(): T[]`\\n- `find(q: { tags?: readonly string[]; text?: string } = {}): T[]`: Defs with every tag in `tags` whose id, about or tags contain every word of `text`.\\n- `search(text: string, o: SearchOptions = {}): T[]`: Defs ranked by how well they match `text`, best first (`searchDefs`).\\n\\n2900→### interface CatalogEntry\\n\\nDefs by id: the engine's built-in libraries (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and a game's\\nown. Ids are how parts, layers and saves refer to defs, so an id names one def per catalog.\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n\\n### checkModel()\\n2910→\\n```ts\\nfunction checkModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: CheckOptions = {}): ModelCheck\\n```\\n\\nEvery check over the model's range: the defaults, then each param at its min and at its max\\n(one at a time), each at seeds 1, 2 and 3 when the parts read the rng. Messages say which\\nbuild they came from unless every build agrees.\\n\\n### decodePng()\\n2920→\\n```ts\\nfunction decodePng(bytes: Uint8Array, inflate: Inflate): RgbaImage\\n```\\n\\nDecode a PNG file's bytes to RGBA (see the file comment for what it reads).\\n\\n### DEFAULT_TEXEL\\n\\n```ts\\n2930→const DEFAULT_TEXEL: 8\\n```\\n\\nTexels per metre for `tex` parts when the def doesn't set `texel`: the densest Gate B passed for\\nsurfaces the camera zooms over (docs/assets/textures.md *Texel density*). A model that moves may set\\nup to `MOVING_TEXEL`.\\n\\n### interface ExpandedModel\\n\\nA model as plain data: no functions, no `use`, every primitive with its slot.\\n2940→\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, Binding>>`\\n- `readonly params: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`\\n- `readonly seed: number`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[]`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`\\n- `readonly anchors?: Readonly<Record<string, Anchor>>`\\n2950→- `readonly light?: ModelLight`\\n- `readonly collider: 'box' | 'cyl' | 'hull' | 'parts' | 'none'`\\n- `readonly texel?: number`\\n- `readonly floats?: boolean`\\n- `readonly source?: Provenance`\\n\\n### expandModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction expandModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ExpandedModel\\n2960→```\\n\\nThe plain-JSON form of a model: params applied, `use` resolved (throws a ModelError on problems).\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":2884,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"### buildModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\\n```\\n\\n### class Catalog\\n\\n- `new Catalog(defs: readonly T[] = [], kind = 'def', tool = '')`\\n- `add(...defs: readonly T[]): this`: Add defs; an id that is already taken throws.\\n- `has(id: string): boolean`\\n- `get(id: string): T`\\n- `all(): T[]`\\n- `find(q: { tags?: readonly string[]; text?: string } = {}): T[]`: Defs with every tag in `tags` whose id, about or tags contain every word of `text`.\\n- `search(text: string, o: SearchOptions = {}): T[]`: Defs ranked by how well they match `text`, best first (`searchDefs`).\\n\\n### interface CatalogEntry\\n\\nDefs by id: the engine's built-in libraries (`MODEL_LIBRARY`, `TEXTURE_LIBRARY`) and a game's\\nown. Ids are how parts, layers and saves refer to defs, so an id names one def per catalog.\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n\\n### checkModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction checkModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: CheckOptions = {}): ModelCheck\\n```\\n\\nEvery check over the model's range: the defaults, then each param at its min and at its max\\n(one at a time), each at seeds 1, 2 and 3 when the parts read the rng. Messages say which\\nbuild they came from unless every build agrees.\\n\\n### decodePng()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction decodePng(bytes: Uint8Array, inflate: Inflate): RgbaImage\\n```\\n\\nDecode a PNG file's bytes to RGBA (see the file comment for what it reads).\\n\\n### DEFAULT_TEXEL\\n\\n```ts\\nconst DEFAULT_TEXEL: 8\\n```\\n\\nTexels per metre for `tex` parts when the def doesn't set `texel`: the densest Gate B passed for\\nsurfaces the camera zooms over (docs/assets/textures.md *Texel density*). A model that moves may set\\nup to `MOVING_TEXEL`.\\n\\n### interface ExpandedModel\\n\\nA model as plain data: no functions, no `use`, every primitive with its slot.\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, Binding>>`\\n- `readonly params: Readonly<Record<string, number>>`\\n- `readonly seed: number`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[]`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`\\n- `readonly anchors?: Readonly<Record<string, Anchor>>`\\n- `readonly light?: ModelLight`\\n- `readonly collider: 'box' | 'cyl' | 'hull' | 'parts' | 'none'`\\n- `readonly texel?: number`\\n- `readonly floats?: boolean`\\n- `readonly source?: Provenance`\\n\\n### expandModel()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction expandModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ExpandedModel\\n```\\n\\nThe plain-JSON form of a model: params applied, `use` resolved (throws a ModelError on problems).\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"c4d491d7-af04-4d7b-b04b-b3d10a259fe7"}
