{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a14cfffb-8521-4cf5-900b-a4255960f804-56","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"3094→### interface ModelBuild\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\\n3100→- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\\n\\n### class ModelCatalog\\n\\nModels by id: the engine's built-in library (`MODEL_LIBRARY`) or a game's own. `use` parts\\nand `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\\na game adds its models to the library, or builds a catalog of its own on top of it.\\n\\n3110→- `new ModelCatalog(defs: readonly ModelDef[] = [])`\\n\\n### interface ModelCheck\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly problems: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly warnings: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly metrics: ModelMetrics | null`: At the default params and seed (null when it can't be built).\\n\\n### type ModelCollider\\n3120→\\n```ts\\ntype ModelCollider = | { readonly kind: 'box'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly half: Vec3 } | { readonly kind: 'cyl'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly radius: number; readonly halfHeight: number } | { readonly kind: 'hull'; readonly points: readonly number[] }\\n```\\n\\n### interface ModelDef\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`: One line, searched by `find`.\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n3130→- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, PaletteColor>>`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`: Declared bounds, checked (10% slack).\\n- `readonly params?: Readonly<Record<string, ParamSpec>>`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[] | ((p: Readonly<Record<string, number>>, rng: Rng) => readonly Part[])`\",\"content_concise\":\"3094→### interface ModelBuild\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\\n3100→- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\\n\\n### class ModelCatalog\\n\\nModels by id: the engine's built-in library (`MODEL_LIBRARY`) or a game's own. `use` parts\\nand `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\\na game adds its models to the library, or builds a catalog of its own on top of it.\\n\\n3110→- `new ModelCatalog(defs: readonly ModelDef[] = [])`\\n\\n### interface ModelCheck\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly problems: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly warnings: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly metrics: ModelMetrics | null`: At the default params and seed (null when it can't be built).\\n\\n### type ModelCollider\\n3120→\\n```ts\\ntype ModelCollider = | { readonly kind: 'box'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly half: Vec3 } | { readonly kind: 'cyl'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly radius: number; readonly halfHeight: number } | { readonly kind: 'hull'; readonly points: readonly number[] }\\n```\\n\\n### interface ModelDef\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`: One line, searched by `find`.\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n3130→- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, PaletteColor>>`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`: Declared bounds, checked (10% slack).\\n- `readonly params?: Readonly<Record<string, ParamSpec>>`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[] | ((p: Readonly<Record<string, number>>, rng: Rng) => readonly Part[])`\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":3094,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"### interface ModelBuild\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\\n- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\\n\\n### class ModelCatalog\\n\\nModels by id: the engine's built-in library (`MODEL_LIBRARY`) or a game's own. `use` parts\\nand `buildModel('id')` resolve ids through one (the library unless a build passes another);\\na game adds its models to the library, or builds a catalog of its own on top of it.\\n\\n- `new ModelCatalog(defs: readonly ModelDef[] = [])`\\n\\n### interface ModelCheck\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly problems: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly warnings: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly metrics: ModelMetrics | null`: At the default params and seed (null when it can't be built).\\n\\n### type ModelCollider\\n\\n```ts\\ntype ModelCollider = | { readonly kind: 'box'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly half: Vec3 } | { readonly kind: 'cyl'; readonly center: Vec3; readonly radius: number; readonly halfHeight: number } | { readonly kind: 'hull'; readonly points: readonly number[] }\\n```\\n\\n### interface ModelDef\\n\\n- `readonly id: string`\\n- `readonly about: string`: One line, searched by `find`.\\n- `readonly tags: readonly string[]`\\n- `readonly palette: Readonly<Record<Slot, PaletteColor>>`\\n- `readonly size?: Vec3`: Declared bounds, checked (10% slack).\\n- `readonly params?: Readonly<Record<string, ParamSpec>>`\\n- `readonly parts: readonly Part[] | ((p: Readonly<Record<string, number>>, rng: Rng) => readonly Part[])`\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-a14cfffb-8521-4cf5-900b-a4255960f804-57","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"2822→### addModelColliders()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\\n```\\n\\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\\n2830→\\n### around()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction around(n: number, part: Each<[i: number]>, o: { r?: number; phase?: number } = {}): Part[]\\n```\\n\\n`n` copies turned about Y, `360 / n` degrees apart from `phase`. `r` first pushes each copy\\nout along its own +Z; with the default 0 the part's own `at` places it.\\n\\n2840→### assetProgress()\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"2822→### addModelColliders()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\\n```\\n\\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\\n2830→\\n### around()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction around(n: number, part: Each<[i: number]>, o: { r?: number; phase?: number } = {}): Part[]\\n```\\n\\n`n` copies turned about Y, `360 / n` degrees apart from `phase`. `r` first pushes each copy\\nout along its own +Z; with the default 0 the part's own `at` places it.\\n\\n2840→### assetProgress()\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":2822,\"limit\":20,\"raw_output\":\"### addModelColliders()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\\n```\\n\\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\\n\\n### around()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction around(n: number, part: Each<[i: number]>, o: { r?: number; phase?: number } = {}): Part[]\\n```\\n\\n`n` copies turned about Y, `360 / n` degrees apart from `phase`. `r` first pushes each copy\\nout along its own +Z; with the default 0 the part's own `at` places it.\\n\\n### assetProgress()\\n\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"a10f8cd4-172b-40e3-9aef-63924e86a86b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_500","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"buildModel returns collider data without adding it. addModelColliders must be called separately.\n\nMeshes are visual only. toonMaterial might throw in headless WebGL during boot, so a targeted test will run first. A makeBuddy bug with dead unlisted copies could copy THREE objects incorrectly. resetDynamic drops actor views but leaves buddy views; attract exit calls it, though that is out of scope.\n\nclearBuddies drops buddy views before makeBuddy recreates them. The first makeBuddy runs during the guns test after scene creation. Civil attachRig runs during World setup and falls back to syncViews if the scene is missing. attachRig skips double attachment when a view already exists. poseMap updates every syncViews and update cycle. The map sheet mounts on the first pose if build's mountMap failed, and build calls mountMap after paint once the camera exists.\n\nbuildModel runs only when an actor lacks a view, so performance is acceptable. The burn block in playMission will be replaced with lightCurrentBurn(). The guns test and dev-click-in-menus test need updates. Map assertions are required. sheet.getObjectByName works correctly for the gps object.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-79f6d031-ce61-48a5-8c11-9469612a8630-58","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function toonMaterial","glob":"**/API.md"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":949,"output_tokens":599,"cache_read_input_tokens":106752,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"6a44f429-5ed6-4778-a032-4fe8ada00e32"}
