{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-9b25d253-3b31-473b-8da2-45786442beef-60","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"1365→color, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n1370→```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n1380→### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n1390→\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\\n1400→- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\\n- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\\n- `broken: boolean`\\n\\n### interface BreakableOptions\",\"content_concise\":\"1365→color, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n1370→```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n1380→### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n1390→\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\\n1400→- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\\n- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\\n- `broken: boolean`\\n\\n### interface BreakableOptions\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/API.md\",\"offset\":1365,\"limit\":40,\"raw_output\":\"color, keeping its base color texture (`map`, nearest-filtered) and vertex colors. Makes\\nany GLB (or hand-built mesh) match the engine's look without per-asset work.\\n\\n### toonMaterial()\\n\\n```ts\\nfunction toonMaterial(color: ColorRepresentation, options: ToonMaterialOptions = {}): MeshToonNodeMaterial\\n```\\n\\nShared 3-band toon node material for a palette color, optionally textured and/or\\nvertex-colored (color × map × vertex color), cached per combination. Untextured ones\\n(and ones whose texture is itself shared, e.g. from a cached GLB) are marked\\n`userData.shared`, so level unloads keep them; a material with a level's own texture is\\ndisposed with the level, and disposing it drops it from the cache.\\n\\n### interface ToonMaterialOptions\\n\\n- `map?: Texture | null`: Base color texture. Switched to nearest filtering (crisp texels, no mip blur).\\n- `vertexColors?: boolean`: Multiply by the geometry's `color` attribute (vertex colors).\\n- `rim?: number`: A hard-banded rim light in this colour (hex) on grazing, upward-facing surfaces: a silhouette that reads against dark floors (monsters in dark levels). Added to the emissive, so `material.emissive` (hit flashes) still works on top. Same shader for every rim c…\\n- `dissolve?: boolean`: Pixel dissolve: the material reads its own `dissolve` property (0 = solid, 1 = gone) and discards a per-art-pixel noise pattern below it, with a 1-pixel glowing front in the rim colour (or white). Set it on per-body clones (`material.dissolve = 0.4`), not on…\\n\\n## 5. Physics\\n\\n### interface BoxOptions\\n\\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\\n- `halfExtents: [number, number, number]`\\n- `rotationY?: number`\\n- `friction?: number`\\n- `density?: number`\\n\\n### interface Breakable\\n\\n- `readonly o: BreakableOptions`\\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\\n- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\\n- `broken: boolean`\\n\\n### interface BreakableOptions\\n\",\"total_lines\":5143}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"68c695f3-97c4-4c5c-9292-81b0c800b32f"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_503","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The material map should be the texture.\n\nMeshToonNodeMaterial might store the map differently. The plan is to set material.map explicitly after creating the toon material, then run tests.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e18d4141-f98e-4a14-bae0-f0cb2d573627-61","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.js\").read_text()\ni = text.find(\"function toonMaterial\")\nprint(\"fn\", i)\n# maybe minified export\ni = text.find(\"toonMaterial\")\nprint(\"first\", i)\n# search unique comment\ni = text.find(\"3-band\")\nprint(\"3-band\", i)\ni = text.find(\"userData.shared\")\nprint(\"shared\", i)\nidx = 0\nc = 0\nwhile c < 5:\n    i = text.find(\"MeshToonNodeMaterial\", idx)\n    if i < 0: break\n    print(\"\\n\", i, text[max(0,i-80):i+200].replace(\"\\n\",\" \")[:280])\n    idx = i+20\n    c += 1\nPY","description":"Find toonMaterial implementation"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":694,"output_tokens":614,"cache_read_input_tokens":108544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"337b2427-5e87-478a-b983-e5b3915a37f2"}
