{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_517","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The click focused on 0 instead of 4.\n\nThe new hover code should have set focus to 4. It remained at 0, so either the old code is still running or something reset focus during the click.\n\nThe menu window top is computed from focus before the click, so a focus change during the event would be ignored. The pointer y calculation is unlikely to be the cause, since missing a row would leave focus at 10. setButtons(1) also triggers a MouseLeft press.\n\nmenuInput ignores MouseLeft outside hover button events. The dev screen opens via Enter before focus is set to 10, then the click happens. Focus may reset to 0 because the slider at items[10] calls activate when clicked.\n\nThe slider activate function does not handle slider IDs, so it cannot be resetting focus. The menu window top may have been zero when hover ran, or focus was not yet set to ten during the hover event.\n\nThe click is processed in two steps. The first step sets focus to 10, then hover should set it to 4. If focus becomes 0 during the first step, the second step cannot restore it. This confirms the bug occurs during hover itself. Either the menu window top was zero when hover began, or the hover logic is not actually running inside menuWindow.\n\nThe Enter key press is ruled out as the cause. It releases on the second step and endFrame clears wasPressed, so it cannot trigger focus reset on the next step. The investigation is now shifting to the order of click and menuInput, or to another input such as Arrow.\n\nThe HUD height may not be 270 in headless mode. If the engine uses a different height, the pointer y calculation would be wrong and hover would miss the window. That would leave focus at 10, but the result was 0 instead. The pointer coordinate might also need to be in pixels rather than NDC.\n\nThe same pointer formula works for the settings touch test, so the coordinate math is likely correct. The click happens during pause with timeScale at zero, but frameStep still calls advance and should run update. The next step is to inspect game.update when the mode is dev.\n\nI am re-reading the hover code on disk to confirm the edit is correct. I suspect menuWindow may use a stale top value when focus is 10. I also re-examined the tap function and confirmed that Enter releases on the second step, so it cannot be the cause.\n\nThe `true` argument to `setPointer` might reset or overwrite the pointer coordinates. The touch test succeeds with the same call while timeScale is 1, but dev mode freezes time at 0. Since `setPointer` runs before `step`, the pointer should remain set during the frame.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-6335cf21-b26b-4560-8347-8ab6f9bb8cac-82","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.js\").read_text()\ni = text.find(\"setPointer(\")\nprint(text[i:i+600])\nprint(\"--- step ---\")\nj = text.find(\"step(e=1\")\nif j < 0: j = text.find(\"step(e=\")\nprint(\"j\", j)\n# search method step\nk = text.find(\"step(e,t){\")\nprint(\"k\", k)\nprint(text[k:k+500] if k>0 else \"no\")\nPY","description":"Read setPointer and headless step"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":742,"output_tokens":1847,"cache_read_input_tokens":122240,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"f0c949f4-17bb-4296-b860-3189b6887301"}
