{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_518","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The third argument of `setPointer` is not \"over\".\n\nThe third argument of `setPointer` is a boolean that presses the mouse button. The touch test passes `true`, which already triggers the button press before `setButtons(1)`. Button events persist across frames, so the click should still work.\n\nThe click logic seems sound. The focus issue remains unclear. I will add a temporary debug log to inspect the HUD height and pointer position.\n\nI will add a temporary debug log to inspect focus, screen, mode, pointer position, HUD dimensions, and menuWindow state. I also ruled out the slider activation logic as the cause of the focus reset.\n\nThe dev mode activation logic was ruled out as the cause of the focus reset. The investigation is now focusing on whether `timeScale` 0 prevents the current frame's input from being processed, or if a previous frame's state is interfering.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-2c64f0b5-e0a1-4662-8b4f-e41dba193d67-83","name":"run_terminal_command","input":{"command":"python3 - << 'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ntext = Path(\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/pixel-engine.js\").read_text()\ni = text.find(\"step(e=1,t=1/60)\")\nprint(\"i\", i)\nif i < 0:\n    i = text.rfind(\"manual=!0\")\nprint(text[i-200:i+800])\nPY","description":"Read Engine.step manual frame path"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2361,"output_tokens":795,"cache_read_input_tokens":122880,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"fbe2002b-88cd-4038-82ba-97e06322ea49"}
