ver the viewport at an…\"},{\"line_number\":219,\"content\":\"- `debugKeys?: DebugKeysOption`: Engine hotkeys (P Pixel/Raw, R resolution, ` debug panel, [ ] looks, M mute): developer tools. Default: on with the debug panel (dev, ?debug=1), off in a shipped game, whose players have the same options in the settings. `true` / `false`: always on / off; an…\"},{\"line_number\":245,\"content\":\"function frameView(viewport: Viewport, base: Resolution, aspect: AspectMode, current: Resolution): { framing: Framing; resolution: Resolution }\"},{\"line_number\":248,\"content\":\"The framing and art resolution of a view (PixelRenderer's canvas, or a HeadlessView's viewport):\"},{\"line_number\":249,\"content\":\"`computeFraming`, and the art size as a resolution. Identity is kept where nothing changed: the\"},{\"line_number\":255,\"content\":\"- `readonly artWidth: number`: Art (internal) resolution actually rendered. Equals `internal` in fixed mode.\"},{\"line_number\":309,\"content\":\"- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\"},{\"line_number\":367,\"content\":\"- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\"},{\"line_number\":402,\"content\":\"the art resolution), so quality trades the shadow map size and the number of dynamic\"},{\"line_number\":426,\"content\":\"resolution: 'F7' })`), so a shipped game, which has no hotkeys, gets none back.\"},{\"line_number\":433,\"content\":\"`scale`, and the scene renders at exactly the art resolution (pixelSize = scale). Every\"},{\"line_number\":439,\"content\":\"- `fixed`: the art resolution is exactly `internal` (16:9); other screen shapes letterbox.\"},{\"line_number\":449,\"content\":\"const RESOLUTIONS: { readonly default: { readonly width: 480; readonly height: 270; }; readonly compare: { readonly width: 320; readonly height: 180; }; }\"},{\"line_number\":485,\"content\":\"- `readonly renderer: { readonly mode: RenderMode; readonly baseResolution: Resolution; readonly lookVersion: number; setMode(mode: RenderMode): void; setResolution(resolution: Reso…`\"},{\"line_number\":494,\"content\":\"The settings panel (DOM, like the debug panel: it stays legible at any art resolution) and the\"}]}]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"cdec2fdf-5476-4441-9146-1c2dd23cb299"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_524","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The default viewport for headless mode is 960×540.\n\nThe default resolution is 480×270. The 960×540 viewport matches this aspect ratio. The HUD should be 480×270. Pointer calculations for a height of 540 place the cursor at row 5. The focus would become 9 instead of 0.\n\nAt 1080 height the cursor misses all rows, so focus stays 10. Width checks out. The draw function does not change focus. I am checking if a button event or item activation resets focus to zero.\n\nThe dev screen's BACK button sets focus to 0. The assertion only checks focus, not the screen state, so the click on BACK passed the test. Focus was likely on item 23.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-e5147f1e-e3ed-4583-9d8e-800a17812eb6-91","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","old_string":"  game.focus = 10;\n  const windowTop = Math.max(0, game.focus - 6);\n  clickHud(86);\n  assert(game.focus === windowTop, 'scrolled click focused ' + game.focus + ' wanted ' + windowTop);","new_string":"  game.focus = 10;\n  const windowTop = Math.max(0, game.focus - 6);\n  const hud = game.ctx.hud;\n  console.log('dev before', game.focus, game.screen, game.mode, 'hud', hud && hud.width, hud && hud.height, 'items', game.items().length);\n  clickHud(86);\n  console.log('dev after', game.focus, game.screen, 'ptr', engine.input.pointer);\n  assert(game.focus === windowTop, 'scrolled click focused ' + game.focus + ' wanted ' + windowTop);"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2002,"output_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":131328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"a48d2b21-541b-442e-913f