uter link uses a BroadcastChannel.\\\",\\n    \\\"testing\\\": \\\"node tests/run.mjs --all. Headless Engine.step playthrough. Playwright Chromium with WebGPU flags. Hub harness, four scenarios.\\\",\\n    \\\"research\\\": \\\"Mechanics from the plan, not a port. No source maps, names, or plot.\\\",\\n    \\\"environment\\\": \\\"Grok CLI (headless); Linux\\\",\\n    \\\"model\\\": \\\"xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\\\",\\n    \\\"usage\\\": \\\"added on import\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"testingFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"13. Listed in tests/ISSUES.md.\\\",\\n    \\\"13. Each one stopped a required path.\\\",\\n    \\\"node tests/run.mjs --all. One shared engine showed the leaks.\\\",\\n    \\\"A blank WebGPU screenshot. The state read is the proof.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"engineFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels, and a vehicle that stays upright.\\\",\\n    \\\"First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z. The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z. Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.\\\",\\n    \\\"The fire grid, jams, fever, map, mission runner, and the hub round.\\\",\\n    \\\"Pointer lock, timeScale pause, and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.\\\",\\n    \\\"None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.\\\",\\n    \\\"A first-person rig that does not steal the use key or the pointer.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"promptFeedback\\\": [\\n    \\\"The plan names the traps and the order to cut whole features.\\\",\\n    \\\"File stem spaces, and which card the harness presses Enter on.\\\",\\n    \\\"One world that is a campaign, a 6 minute round, and a hub server.\\\",\\n    \\\"Ship the hub check before asking for every prop in the art list.\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"aiHub\\\": {\\n    \\\"name\\\": \\\"A Cry Too Far\\\",\\n\",\"total_lines\":51}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"9d1b5b26-380f-4d04-bf9a-22eb5e892dbb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_552","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Updating PROGRESS.md with the four fixes and verification results.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-77329834-7dfe-4d67-87a2-257019f7e7a4-143","name":"search_replace","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md","old_string":"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\n\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\n\n## Checks on this computer\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.","new_string":"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\n\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\n\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\n\n## Checks on this computer\n\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending."}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-77329834-7dfe-4d67-87a2-257019f7e7a4-144","name":"todo_write","input":{"todos":[{"id":"reverify","status":"completed"}],"merge":true}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1881,"output_tokens":1120,"cache_read_input_tokens":179328,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"9324de57-87e9-4f88-a926-57f014133b2c"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-77329834-7dfe-4d67-87a2-257019f7e7a4-143","content":"{\"type\":\"SearchReplace\",\"EditsApplied\":{\"old_string\":\"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\",\"new_string\":\"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated successfully.\",\"tool_output_for_prompt_concise\":\"The file /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md has been updated.\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"edits\":{\"details\":[{\"old_string\":\"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering are in the scratch shots folder. The frames show the basin, the title, night, the truck, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\",\"old_line\":22,\"new_string\":\"The story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\",\"new_line\":22,\"context_before\":\"\\nOne 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\n\",\"context_after\":\"\\n## Issues\\n\\n\",\"line_prefix\":\"\"}]}}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-77329834-7dfe-4d67-87a2-257019f7e7a4-144","content":"{\"type\":\"Todo\",\"TodosUpdated\":{\"summary_for_prompt\":\"- [completed] map-draw: Draw the held map from mapPx while walking and driving, and assert that path\\n- [completed] m6-syrette: Let knockBuddy offer syrette or finish-it, finish-it only with no syrette\\n- [completed] actor-mesh: Instance soldier rigs for soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians and move them with the actors\\n- [completed] dev-hit: Hit-test Dev Mode against the same 9-row window the HUD draws\\n- [completed] reverify: Rebuild HTML, rerun headless tests, file://, phone, hub, and refresh hand-in\\n\",\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Draw the held map from mapPx while walking and driving, and assert that path\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Let knockBuddy offer syrette or finish-it, finish-it only with no syrette\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Instance soldier rigs for soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians and move them with the actors\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Hit-test Dev Mode against the same 9-row window the HUD draws\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML, rerun headless tests, file://, phone, hub, and refresh hand-in\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}],\"state\":{\"todos\":{\"map-draw\":{\"content\":\"Draw the held map from mapPx while walking and driving, and assert that path\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"m6-syrette\":{\"content\":\"Let knockBuddy offer syrette or finish-it, finish-it only with no syrette\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"actor-mesh\":{\"content\":\"Instance soldier rigs for soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians and move them with the actors\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"dev-hit\":{\"content\":\"Hit-test Dev Mode against the same 9-row window the HUD draws\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"},\"reverify\":{\"content\":\"Rebuild HTML, rerun headless tests, file://, phone, hub, and refresh hand-in\",\"priority\":\"medium\",\"status\":\"completed\"}}}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e4311078-9275-4c94-a25d-34d4f69da0d6"}
