{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-03b93098-a966-47f9-a34b-004245ae764b-145","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"17→\\n## What plays\\n\\n20→One 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n30→- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\n40→Testing caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\",\"content_concise\":\"17→\\n## What plays\\n\\n20→One 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n30→- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\n40→Testing caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PROGRESS.md\",\"offset\":17,\"limit\":30,\"raw_output\":\"\\n## What plays\\n\\nOne 1280 m basin. Walk, run, sprint, crouch, jump, and wade, on foot and in the truck, first person. Guns wear, jam, and break. Locker guns start at condition 100. The 5 m fire grid spreads with wind, burnt ground stays burnt, and scars stay on the map. A tablet clears blackwater fever. Ignoring it collapses you and costs stones. Field surgery, buddy rescue, and finish-it are in. The map can be raised while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Music starts at 0.1 on clean storage. Voices and effects are code, with no audio files.\\n\\nThe story runs from the opening ride through the firebreak reveal, the choice of who gets the minefield sheet, and both ending cards. On the long-field down, a syrette picks the buddy up. Finish-it is the prompt only when no syrette is left, or the buddy is burning. The Ledger tracks hectares, people moved, men paid to kill, friends lost, and stones earned. Player bullets do not kill civilians.\\n\\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS square on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving, and the world does not pause. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode draws nine rows and hit-tests those same rows, including Reset.\\n\\nCash Run is about 6 minutes, solo against hired guns or 1–4 players. Dev mode sliders live under pause, with reset. Attract starts after 10 seconds on the title and main menu only. A touch-only device shows `Controller or keyboard required` and Settings.\\n\\n## Checks on this computer\\n\\n- `node tests/run.mjs --all`: passed 10, failed 0. The map, syrette, rig, and dev-click checks drive the shipped game.\\n- Two `file://` Chromium boots at 1920×1080: title `A Cry Too Far`, `AIHub.active` false, no page or console errors. The two runs agree. SHA-256 of that HTML is `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`, same as `tests/.site/game.html`.\\n- iPhone 14 profile under Chromium: the notice is exact, the menu is only Settings, attract starts once idle passes 10, and a tap opens Settings.\\n- WebKit on that phone profile has no WebGPU. The page reports that and stops. That failure is evidence only.\\n- Four hub scenarios on the shipped file: all passed (14, 14, 14, and 15 checks).\\n- Two `file://` pages shared one round: both carried case r1 to the same standings, and both saw the same grass fire.\\n- Screenshots after the page had been rendering show the basin and the title, the map sheet in the hands with the GPS mark, a soldier in the field, night, dialogue, surgery, the dev sliders, the hub card, and an ending.\\n\\n## Issues\\n\\nTesting caught 13 defects. All 13 were game-breaking. They are listed in `tests/ISSUES.md`.\\n\",\"total_lines\":40}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"9c5c77f6-a5fa-4a08-a452-07c1b20e995c"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_554","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The hand-in is complete. Progress looks good.\n\nThe final reply will list four fixes: held map drawing from mapPx during movement, knockBuddy using the real m6 path instead of forcing burning, actor rigs for soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians, and dev hover matching the 9-row window. It will repeat the source information block and testing feedback.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The four rejected paths are fixed in the shipped game, and the hand-in matches that file.\n\nThe held map is a sheet in the scene, textured from the painted map, with a GPS mark on it. It stays in the hands while walking and driving. The long-field down offers a syrette when one is left, and finish-it only when none is left or the buddy is burning. Soldiers, mercs, buddies, and civilians use the soldier rig and move with the actor. Dev mode hit-tests the same nine rows the HUD draws, including Reset.\n\n`node tests/run.mjs --all` passed 10 and failed 0. Two `file://` boots, the iPhone touch gate, four hub scenarios, and the same-computer link all passed on `A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html` (SHA-256 `253c66ea48fed19415b5989cdded0b140bdfe888299bf4eb2da0c6f7083c04fe`). Screenshots show the map in the hands and a soldier in the field. `exit-interview.json` and `PROGRESS.md` are beside that HTML. Fauna stays cut.\n\n## Source information\n\n- Date: 2026-11-05 01:39:17\n- Source: Far Cry 2\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: first-person shooter\n- Perspective: first person on foot, at the wheel, and in story scenes\n- Tech: Pixel Engine 0.46.0, three.js r186, Rapier 0.20, esbuild 0.28.2. Original sim, fire grid, weapons, and missions.\n- Art direction: Engine pixel-art toon at 480×270. Sand, orange, and red land. Slate for Concord, orange for the Harvest Front. Green only for water and regrowth.\n- Animation: Engine clips on the soldier rig. First-person hands on a small rig. Mixer poses for reload, the map, and surgery.\n- Audio: Code songs, code effects, and no audio files. Animalese voices. Music starts at 10 percent.\n- Online: AI Hub shared-world for 1–4 players. Cash Run lasts 6 minutes. Same-computer link uses a BroadcastChannel.\n- Testing: `node tests/run.mjs --all`. Headless Engine.step playthrough. Playwright Chromium with WebGPU flags. Hub harness, four scenarios.\n- Research: Mechanics from the plan, not a port. No source maps, names, or plot.\n- Environment: Grok CLI (headless); Linux\n- Model: xAI, grok-4.7, reasoning effort xhigh\n- Usage: added on import\n\n## Testing feedback\n\n- How many issues did testing catch? 13. Listed in tests/ISSUES.md.\n- How many would be game breaking? 13. Each one stopped a required path.\n- Most helpful test: `node tests/run.mjs --all`. One shared engine showed the leaks.\n- Least helpful test: A blank WebGPU screenshot. The state read is the proof.\n\n## Engine feedback\n\n- Liked most: Headless step, seeded RNG, HUD pixels, and a vehicle that stays upright.\n- Stuck or guessed: First-person yaw 0 looks down -Z. The car yaw 0 drives toward +Z. Speed is a writable field, as the plan said.\n- Built: The fire grid, jams, fever, map, mission runner, and the hub round.\n- Hardest engine part: Pointer lock, timeScale pause, and keeping Pad codes off the keyboard.\n- Changed in the engine: None. pixel-engine.js is the kit file.\n- One change: A first-person rig that does not steal the use key or the pointer.\n\n## Prompt feedback\n\n- Liked most: The plan names the traps and the order to cut whole features.\n- Confusing: File stem spaces, and which card the harness presses Enter on.\n- Hardest: One world that is a campaign, a 6 minute round, and a hub server.\n- Change the prompt: Ship the hub check before asking for every prop in the art list."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":988,"output_tokens":1149,"cache_read_input_tokens":182400,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"8cc9396e-538b-44ee-a95c-4505801552eb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_555","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Re-verifying the previous gaps.\n\nFour bugs need verification: held map/GPS not drawing, knockBuddy always burning, missing meshes for soldiers/mercs/buddies/civilians, and dev-mode hover hit-test mismatch. The agent's claims will be ignored. Current files must be re-read.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The four prior gaps are the bar. I’ll re-read the current map, buddy, soldier, and dev-menu code, then check the new tests against them."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc419a5f-0550-4243-b0b8-47b0eb96e256-78","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mapPx|mapSheet|map-sheet|DataTexture|knockBuddy|burning|spawnSoldier|syncActors|actorMesh|hover|menuWindow|visibleItems","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src","glob":"*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc419a5f-0550-4243-b0b8-47b0eb96e256-79","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"mapPx|mapSheet|knockBuddy|actorMesh|menuTop|visibleStart|mapShown|figure","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-bc419a5f-0550-4243-b0b8-47b0eb96e256-80","name":"list_dir","input":{"target_directory":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":180358,"output_tokens":603,"cache_read_input_tokens":1792,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"ffd03025-e0d2-4220-a6b8-cce3954a5ee8"}
