\n\\nawait grab('hub-card', () => {\\n  const g = window.__GAME__;\\n  g.mode = 'card';\\n  g.screen = 'card';\\n  g.attract = false;\\n  g.card = { ready: [0], left: 9000 };\\n  g.session = { players: [{ id: 0, name: 'HOST' }, { id: 1, name: 'JOIN' }], answer() {} };\\n  return { mode: g.mode, players: 2 };\\n});\\n\\nwriteFileSync(dir + '/notes.json', JSON.stringify({ errors, notes }, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify({ errors: errors.length, shots: Object.keys(notes) }, null, 2));\\nawait browser.close();\\n\",\"total_lines\":171}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89edcbb2-aaf1-4b4b-97cd-ac19dd6c2475-31","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-89edcbb2-aaf1-4b4b-97cd-ac19dd6c2475-32","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"ImageContent\":{\"data\":\"\",\"mime_type\":\"image/jpeg\"}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"9473d19c-fb80-4f6e-afce-0a54bb737a04"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_569","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Screenshots confirm the map is a large tan sheet in the lower view with a black GPS square and red dot.\n\nThe shot script forces map state directly rather than pressing the M key. The unit test instead exercises the real KeyM path during walking and driving. The screenshot confirms the mesh renders in the camera view, so the gap is fixed. Whether the tan sheet uses a real texture or is just solid toon color remains unclear.\n\nThe tan color matches the map texture's base fill exactly. A solid white material would appear pale under toon lighting, not this specific brown. The black GPS square and red dot also match the GPS texture. This confirms the map is properly sampled from its texture.\n\nThe fight scene now shows a humanoid soldier in the field. Gap C is fixed visually.\n\nSyrette is implemented and tested, but the test log only reports passed 10 failed 0. A real run of the updated tests would have failed if the new assertions were missing. The implementer likely fabricated this log.\n\nThe test log is fresh and green. A targeted spot-check of just the map, syrette, and rig tests could verify the captured run without a full suite.\n\nThe driving screenshot forces inVehicle and teleports the hero directly, so it does not prove the truck camera works. The unit test instead enters the truck with KeyE and holds M while driving, then asserts the map stays held. In headless mode the camera rig still matches the poseMap matrix, so assertHeldMap passes even if the camera never moved. The beige slab on the left is the town block at 12,55, not the vehicle.\n\nWalking and driving share the same poseMap mesh path, so the map should render identically in both modes. The dev mode screenshot hides the scrolled window because focus is set to zero. Hover and draw share menuWindow, which could be a source of bugs. I am re-examining the draw function.\n\nThe dev screen menu now uses the same top and count values for both hover and draw, so the shared menuWindow bug is fixed. The hit-test y-offset matches the text anchor exactly, resolving the prior index mismatch. The slider key list contains 24 entries, which prevents the old focus>6 overflow.\n\nThe knockBuddy subtitle still shows buddy:burn even when the buddy is not burning. This is flavor text, not a functional bug.\n\nSyrette places the buddy at feet+1.2. After one engine step, the player may move out of range before KeyE is pressed. The prompt logic finds any down buddy regardless of distance. tryUse requires distance under 2.5.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30f0ae52-cec8-45c0-b3b6-d6559ac69fe8-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"knockBuddy\\(\\)|downBuddy\\(b\\.id\\)|burning:\\s*true","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30f0ae52-cec8-45c0-b3b6-d6559ac69fe8-34","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"SLIDER_KEYS","glob":"**/tuning*.js"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-30f0ae52-cec8-45c0-b3b6-d6559ac69fe8-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917.html","offset":45180,"limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5525,"output_tokens":1617,"cache_read_input_tokens":81536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"b4a735e3-7b57-478c-9d20-70a1fdbc016d"}
