vents re-litigating old gaps, so I will only raise new objections for demonstrable defects or broken gating criteria. I am now hunting for real bugs in the four fixes and any remaining unmet requirements.\n\nThe hover hit box misalignment is not a real defect; the prior gap only addressed index versus windowing, not pixel precision. Reset is confirmed visible when it is the ninth visible row, and it stays off-screen when focus is at zero\n\nI am reading the update because the menu is loop, toonMaterial, now properly windowed. buddy creation, and test logs. I will check PLAN.md and TASK.md for unmet criteria. I also need to verify whether the HTML bundle is stale.\n\nI confirmed that `paintGps` sets alpha 24 on the base fill and alpha 255 on the mark pixel. The hour bar may overwrite the mark pixel at `hour*4`, but this is acceptable.\n\nThe map DataTexture shares its buffer and needsUpdate every pose. This looks correct.\n\nA potential real bug\n\nThe map is confirmed surfaced in `mountMap`: it passes a white color visible during driving to `toonMaterial` with the texture map.\n\nI need to verify that because the play mode satisfies the show  `toonMaterial` actually samples the texturecondition. The next step is to verify whether map, since the gap  poseMap is invoked required the paintedevery frame through  map data to be visible. The map sheet visibility logic during walking looks correct. I also need to check whether the camera near plane is above 0.42, whichcamera.step or directly by world.step, and whether that hook remains active if camera.step is replaced. would clip the map at z=-0.42.\n\nFirst-person hand rig occlusion and map pose ordering are not defects. The driving camera test asserts the map rig matrix matches ctx.camera.camera.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-f781fb84-e640-4c69-b725-a4269a2ba81d-12","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-