{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_582","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nspawnSoldier always attaches a rig regardless of faction. The test mutates kind to merc after spawning. Need to check if syncViews tracks these actors and whether round.js later changes the kind.\n\nChecking if keepCivilians strips soldier rigs. Tracing syncViews call sites in round.js and world step. Verifying the HTML bundle includes the new code. Also examining makeBuddy attachRig.All 10 tests passed.\n\nThe soldier mesh fix satisfies the gap requirement. The merc test mutates kind after spawning, but round.js uses spawnSoldier directly. A real bug was found: nearPrompt does not check distance for buddy prompts.\n\nThe nearPrompt distance issue is minor and not a prior gap. The knockBuddy subtitle bug is cosmetic. A real defect was found: handleUse melee finishes the buddy regardless of syrette.\n\nVerifying the HTML bundle contains the fixes and that the log is recent. Checking PLAN.md for overlooked bugs in map rendering and buddy mechanics.\n\nReconsidering the melee finish-it bug.\n\nThe test asserts zero Melee and syrette may syrettes remain after be intended as mutually the buddy-down campaign. exclusive actions.  I am checking whetherThe test only uses KeyE, the test setup accidentally so this may not be a real defect. pre-emptively consumes them.\n\nChecking whether melee finish-it violates \n\nThe syrette count the spec when a syretteis honest: the test  is available. Also passed, so the mission setup gives exactlyexamining map cursor one.\n\nFor rig following, versus GPS: paintGps uses wind direction I need to confirm that `engine.step` calls and hour, not player `game.update` and that position, while refreshMap actor positions update stamps the player as before `syncViews`. a white pixel. Need The test moved an actor and stepped; passed to verify if the waypoint cursor is drawn on  results mean the AI did not teleport themthe map texture. in that frame.\n\nThe prior gap only required drawing mapPx on a mesh in the hands. GPS is extra functionality, so its absence does not violate the original request. The dev mode\n\nThe rig test confirms click test needs a  placeRig executes. full read to verify The dev hover test isit is honest. Bundle honest because it monkeypatches staleness is flagged activate to observe as critical. the real hover path.\n\nI am now hunting for real bugs in the shipped game. I will inspect game.update and world fixedUpdate for map, actor, and HTML rebuild logic. I also need to verify toonMaterial map sampling and whether\n\nNeed to verify the the map is clipped behind the near plane. built HTML contains mapSheet, knockBuddy burning changes, and\n\nSoldiers may be invisible menuWindow. Tests passed, to aim at if they lack so syncViews must be colliders. The prior in the step path. Still gap only required visible need to check when  rigs, not hit detection, so I will not expandkeepCivilians drops views. scope. I am now hunting for why the map might fail to appear in the rendered view.\n\nSoldier yaw and animation are not required to be perfect. The map rig stays in view while driving because poseMap uses the camera world position, and the driving test confirms this works correctly. Calling poseMap from both rig.step and syncViews is safe. The hookCamera setup properly handles map updates during vehicle movement.\n\nThe toon shader might ignore the map texture. The map sheet visibility depends on game.mode. Camera hook ordering is critical: if poseMap runs in syncViews before the camera moves, the hookCamera wrapper should re-apply it afterward. However, if the engine stored the original\n\nDataTexture mutation step before wrapping, is safe because refreshMap the hook is bypassed reuses the same array and syncViews alone and sets needsUpdate. handles posing. The toonMaterial map property test passes if the material actually uses `.map`. Next I will check tests-all.log, the dev test, round merc kind handling, syncViews callers, and grep the HTML bundle for menuWindow and held-map. I also need to review PLAN.md criteria for map and buddy requirements.\n\nA one-frame camera lag is acceptable and does not hide the map.\n\nThe driving map test passed, so the toggle does not consume the key during vehicle mode.\n\nI am skipping the full map feature because the prior round only required the base map to be drawn.\n\nChecking if round.js overwrites the actor after spawnSoldier for mercs, which could strip the rig view. Verified soldier death hides the view and buddy down states keep it visible with rotation. Will inspect round.js near line 680 and confirm the HTML bundle matches current source.\n\nI will inspect the screenshots to confirm the map and soldier visuals are correct. I also need to verify the single HTML bundle contains the held-map, knockBuddy burning fix, menuWindow, and attachRig code.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4fcc259d-a611-447e-aa9e-0a63a4e58cf5-16","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs","offset":660,"limit":120}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4fcc259d-a611-447e-aa9e-0a63a4e58cf5-17","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/round.js","offset":40,"limit":80}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4fcc259d-a611-447e-aa9e-0a63a4e58cf5-18","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"syncViews\\(","glob":"**/*.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4fcc259d-a611-447e-aa9e-0a63a4e58cf5-19","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"held-map|menuWindow|SYRETTE OR FINISH|knockBud