{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_589","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"\n\nThe map is a uniform tan plane drawn from mapPx, with the GPS mark overlaid. A soldier appears in the field. The dev mode windowing shows nine rows correctly.Reviewing touch.log against the verification plan.\n\nThe player position stamp is a single white pixel, which may be hard to see. The map cursor still fails to draw.\n\nThe map cursor is missing from the texture.\n\nThe touch.log notice The player cannot see matches the required where the cursor is text exactly. The afterTap on the map. This is menu shows settings items, so I need to a functional hole in verify whether that map interaction. screen is actually the settings page. I will also check launch-2.log and examine screenshots for corroboration. I am now hunting for a real bug rather than relying on refuted bias.\n\nThe map drawing code sets `flipY = true` on a Three.js DataTexture. In Three.js r152+, DataTexture defaults\n\nThe plan specifies to `flipY = false`, the held map should display a cursor, waypoint, so the manual override sites, heading, and may be incorrect. notes. The prior fix only added the base texture, scars, player dot, and GPS wind arrow. The cursor, waypoint, sites, heading, and notes remain missing.\n\nThe missing cursor\n\nThe `flipY` override on the DataTexture should work correctly. The real issue may be that the toon shader ignores the map texture and renders a white plane instead of sampling `mapPx`. The current test only verifies the material reference, not whether the shader actually uses it. may be a valid refutation. The anti-ratchet rule allows new objections only when they are demonstrable defects in shipped behavior or unmet gating criteria. A visible cursor is required for the map to function as intended. Tests verify cursor movement and waypoint placement, which depends on the cursor position.","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a055e421-958d-48f3-b161-33f0aadf932b-33","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"function toonMaterial|export function toonMaterial|map:","glob":"**/pixel-engine.js","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917","head_limit":30}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a055e421-958d-48f3-b161-33f0aadf932b-34","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/shots/notes.json"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a055e421-958d-48f3-b161-33f0aadf932b-35","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/src/sim/world.js","offset":450,"limit":70}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a055e421-958d-48f3-b161-33f0aadf932b-36","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/launch-2.log","limit":20}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-a055e421-958d-48f3-b161-33f0aadf932b-37","name":"read_file","input":{"target_file":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/tmp/grok-goal-e16164d1c2de/implementer/link.log","limit":40}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4244,"output_tokens":871,"cache_read_input_tokens":73600,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"04d4dc99-1de0-4d09-9b39-f785d8be923e"}
