5,105,111,110,32,115,116,97,114,116,58,32,101,97,99,104,32,109,105,115,115,105,111,110,32,104,97,115,32,97,32,96,115,101,116,117,112,96,32,116,104,97,116,32,112,117,116,115,32,116,104,101,32,119,111,114,108,100,32,105,110,32,116,104,101,32,114,105,103,104,116,32,115,116,97,116,101,32,40,96,119,111,114,108,100,46,114,101,115,101,116,96,44,32,115,116,111,114,121,32,102,108,97,103,115,44,32,115,99,97,114,115,44,32,98,117,100,100,105,101,115,44,32,108,111,97,100,111,117,116,41,44,32,115,111,32,96,100,101,118,46,115,116,97,114,116,77,105,115,115,105,111,110,40,39,109,54,39,41,96,32,105,115,32,111,110,101,32,99,97,108,108,46,10,54,53,50,58,32,32,49,46,32,42,65,32,109,97,112,32,105,115,32,97,32,112,114,111,109,105,115,101,32,109,97,100,101,32,98,121,32,115,111,109,101,111,110,101,32,119,104,111,32,104,97,115,32,97,108,114,101,97,100,121,32,108,101,102,116,46,42,10,54,55,54,58,45,32,53,32,104,101,97,108,116,104,32,115,101,103,109,101,110,116,115,44,32,115,121,114,101,116,116,101,32,97,110,100,32,116,97,98,108,101,116,32,99,111,117,110,116,115,32,98,111,116,116,111,109,45,108,101,102,116,46,10,55,49,54,58,42,42,84,104,101,32,109,111,117,115,101,32,105,115,32,110,97,116,105,118,101,46,42,42,32,73,110,32,109,101,110,117,115,32,116,104,101,32,112,111,105,110,116,101,114,32,105,115,32,102,114,101,101,32,40,110,111,32,108,111,99,107,41,44,32,104,111,118,101,114,32,109,111,118,101,115,32,102,111,99,117,115,44,32,99,108,105,99,107,32,97,99,116,105,118,97,116,101,115,32,40,114,101,97,100,32,96,105,110,112,117,116,46,98,117,116,116,111,110,69,118,101,110,116,115,96,59,32,99,111,110,118,101,114,116,32,119,105,116,104,32,96,120,32,61,32,40,112,46,120,43,49,41,47,50,42,104,117,100,46,119,105,100,116,104,96,44,32,96,121,32,61,32,40,49,45,112,46,121,41,47,50,42,104,117,100,46,104,101,105,103,104,116,96,41,46,32,84,104,101,32,119,104,101,101,108,32,115,99,114,111,108,108,115,32,112,97,103,101,115,46,32,79,118,101,114,32,116,104,101,32,119,111,114,108,100,32,105,116,32,97,105,109,115,32,97,110,100,32,108,111,111,107,115,32,117,110,100,101,114,32,112,111,105,110,116,101,114,32,108,111,99,107,46,32,79,110,32,116,104,101,32,104,101,108,100,32,109,97,112,32,105,116,39,115,32,97,32,99,117,114,115,111,114,32,40,104,111,118,101,114,32,102,111,99,117,115,101,115,32,97,32,109,97,114,107,101,114,44,32,99,108,105,99,107,32,115,101,116,115,32,116,104,101,32,119,97,121,112,111,105,110,116,41,46,32,79,110,32,84,105,98,111,114,39,115,32,114,97,99,107,32,97,110,100,32,105,110,32,100,105,97,108,111,103,117,101,32,99,104,111,105,99,101,115,44,32,99,108,105,99,107,32,119,111,114,107,115,32,116,111,111,46,32,75,101,121,98,111,97,114,100,32,105,110,32,109,101,110,117,115,58,32,97,114,114,111,119,115,32,111,114,32,87,65,83,68,44,32,69,110,116,101,114,32,111,114,32,83,112,97,99,101,44,32,69,115,99,32,98,97,99,107,46,32,80,97,100,32,105,110,32,109,101,110,117,115,58,32,68,45,112,97,100,32,111,114,32,108,101,102,116,32,115,116,105,99,107,32,119,105,116,104,32,107,101,121,32,114,101,112,101,97,116,44,32,67,114,111,115,115,32,99,111,110,102,105,114,109,115,44,32,67,105,114,99,108,101,32,103,111,101,115,32,98,97,99,107,44,32,76,49,47,82,49,32,99,104,97,110,103,101,32,116,97,98,115,32,97,110,100,32,112,97,103,101,115,46,32,73,102,32,116,104,101,32,112,97,100,32,100,105,115,99,111,110,110,101,99,116,115,32,100,117,114,105,110,103,32,112,108,97,121,44,32,111,112,101,110,32,116,104,101,32,112,97,117,115,101,32,109,101,110,117,46,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":0,\"match_count\":60,\"file_matches\":[{\"path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/PLAN.md\",\"matches\":[{\"line_number\":18,\"content\":\"**Perspective:** first person on foot, at the wheel and in story scenes, with an optional chase camera in vehicles only. The source's best ideas (a gun jamming, tablets in your palm, pliers in your own forearm, a paper map in your hands while someone shoots at you) only work through your own eyes and hands.\"},{\"line_number\":21,\"content\":\"**Pitch.** You come to a dying country to kill the man who drew its maps. Your gun rusts, your truck dies, your blood has a fever with a timetable, and the grass burns whoever lit it. Two armies pay you to make things worse. Your only friends are for hire, and you may have to finish one yourself.\"},{\"line_number\":25,\"content\":\"2. **Fire is your best weapon and your worst neighbour.** Grass burns by wind on a grid. Scars stay in the world and on your map.\"},{\"line_number\":32,\"content\":\"**Original, not a recreation.** Build in the genre and use similar mechanics, but invent everything else: country, people, factions, story, map, weapons' names, models, music. Never use the source's proper nouns, characters, plot, map, level layouts, music, logos or look. The only allowed references to it are the riff in your title and the \\\"Source\\\" credit.\"},{\"line_number\":37,\"content\":\"| Hunting an arms dealer who sells to both sides; recorded interviews | Hunting the Surveyor who sells maps to both sides; his notes in your map's margins, found at trig points |\"},{\"line_number\":41,\"content\":\"| Map and GPS held in hand | Paper map and GPS held in hand, and the map turns out to be the plot (sections 14, 16) |\"},{\"line_number\":42,\"content\":\"| Buddies who rescue you and can die, mercy kills | Three hired friends, rescues, alternate plans, heal-or-finish choices (section 12) |\"},{\"line_number\":47,\"content\":\"Content limits: an invented country that maps to no real nation, people or flag. A mixed international cast. No child soldiers, no sexual violence. Civilians are not targets: they flee, and the Ledger counts them. The clinic's emblem is a green cross, because the Red Cross emblem is legally protected.\"},{\"line_number\":59,\"content\":\"**The target.** **Emil Harrow, the Surveyor:** the old company's cartographer, who drew every road and border in the Sorrel. He now sells both armies maps of each other, including minefields, and some of them are wrong.\"},{\"line_number\":61,\"content\":\"**You.** **Aster**, a silent contractor with forged papers as a surveyor's assistant. You were paid to kill Harrow. Your contract includes a map with a note in the margin, in Harrow's hand: *MIND THE FEVER. YOU ARE LATE ALREADY. E.H.*\"},{\"line_number\":73,\"content\":\"**The twist.** Harrow paid for your contract himself. He is dying of the same fever. Each burn he steered you toward (the East Siding, the Cut, the Long Field) lies on one arc across the Kettle: a firebreak. Burned grass cannot burn twice, so a refugee column can walk that scar to the mined pass at the border while both armies try to burn them out. *You have been drawing for me.* He has one more thing for you: the only honest map of the minefield.\"},{\"line_number\":81,\"content\":\"**The central line,** which is never explained: *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\"},{\"line_number\":98,\"content\":\"| Default pad mapping presses keyboard codes (R2 = KeyC, Square = KeyJ...) | Replace `input.gamepadButtons` with `Pad*` codes (below). `isDown`, `wasPressed` and `consumePress` then work on them and keep the devices apart |\"},{\"line_number\":114,\"content\":\"    const k = cam.enabled ? 1 : 0;               // 0 while a menu is open or the map cursor has the stick\"},{\"line_number\":131,\"content\":\"**The map in your hands works.** A `THREE.DataTexture` (RGBA `Uint8Array`, nearest filter, `colorSpace = SRGBColorSpace`) on a `PlaneGeometry` with `toonMaterial(0xffffff, { map })`, parented to the camera, reads crisp. It needs no DOM, so it also runs in Node. Draw into the array yourself.\"},{\"line_number\":154,\"content\":\"  layers:[0,1,2,3].map(i => ({ at:[i*10,0], pixels:FRAMES[i], legend:{a:'a',b:'b',c:'c',d:'d'} })) });\"},{\"line_number\":162,\"content\":\"- Use this soldier as your starting point (as written it passes `checkModel` with no problems or warnings; shoulders about 1.12 m, head top about 1.74 m, faces +Z):\"},{\"line_number\":166,\"content\":\"export const soldier = model({ id:'soldier', about:'Soldier on the hero rig', tags:['actor'], floats:true, collider:'none',\"},{\"line_number\":186,\"content\":\"**Movement.** `CharacterController` stays grounded on the heightfield and is right for a grounded soldier. `PlatformerCharacter` (triple jumps, ground pounds) is not. `speed` is set in the constructor and read as a plain field; `setInput(move, jump, jumpHeld)` takes a move vector of length up to 1.\"},{\"line_number\":202,\"content\":\"- A pad works: `globalThis.navigator.getGamepads = () => [pad]`, with `pad = { connected:true, mapping:'standard', axes:[0,0,0,0], buttons:[...{pressed,value}] }`.\"},{\"line_number\":235,\"content\":\"src/world/                terrain.js roads.js sites.js grass.js sky.js fire.js wind.js map-texture.js\"},{\"line_number\":236,\"content\":\"src/actors/               player.js soldier.js squad.js buddy.js civilian.js fauna.js rig.js\"},{\"line_number\":242,\"content\":\"src/dev/                  devmode.js sliders.js overlays.js\"},{\"line_number\":253,\"content\":\"- **Data over code.** All content lives in `src/content/` and `src/art/` as plain data. Adding a weapon, site, mission, line of dialogue or model must not need a code change. This is what lets the rest of the game be built later \\\"with normal designer tools\\\": tables, the sheets tool and dev mode's placement readout. Keep a one-page `DESIGNERS.md` in the dev folder saying how to add each.\"},{\"line_number\":254,\"content\":\"- **Actions, not keys.** `src/core/actions.js` maps an action to its pad code and its keyboard/mouse codes (section 16). All gameplay asks for actions. In `fixedUpdate` use `input.consumeAny(codes)`; in `update` use `wasPressed`.\"},{\"line_number\":256,\"content\":\"- **`TUNING`.** Every balance number lives in `src/content/tuning-defaults.js`, copied to a live `TUNING` object. Systems read `TUNING.x` at the moment of use and never cache it, so sliders act instantly.\"},{\"line_number\":257,\"content\":\"- **`game.state()`.** One plain JSON snapshot for every test: `{ mode, screen, focus, device, glyphSet, notice, attract, mission, step, hp, stones, tablets, syrettes, weapon:{id,cond,jammed,mag}, fever, pos, yaw, vehicle, hour, wind, fire:{burning,burnt}, prompts:[...], subtitle, buddies, ledger }`. Expose it in `ready(ctx)` as `window.__GAME__ = game` when `window` exists. Give `status()` a useful one-liner and `fingerprint()` a hash of hp, stones, weapon state, fire counts and actor positions.\"},{\"line_number\":258,\"content\":\"- **Sim and view apart.** A soldier is data plus an optional view; a fire cell is data plus sprites. In a round, a client's soldiers are puppets with no brain and no collider, driven by snapshots. Write them this way from the first day, because retrofitting it is the expensive part of section 19.\"},{\"line_number\":305,\"content\":\"**Checkpoints** (posts of 4 to 6 soldiers, sandbags, a boom gate, sometimes a technical): P1 (90, -80) north road · P2 (-200, 30) west road · P3 (170, 90) east road · P4 (-320, -90) fort road · P5 (280, -210) mine road · P6 (300, 390) salt road. A cleared post re-mans after `TUNING.postRemanHours` (24 game hours); the source's instant respawn is one of its known annoyances, so we don't copy it.\"},{\"line_number\":328,\"content\":\"**Grass:** `GrassField` chunks of 48 × 48 m with about 7,000 blades, `mask` from the fuel map, `ground` from `heightAt`. Build a chunk the first time it comes within 170 m of the camera, hide it beyond 200 m, dispose beyond 320 m. On build, consult the fire grid (burnt cells get no blades).\"},{\"line_number\":330,\"content\":\"**Buildings** are `model()` defs with `collider:'parts'` so doorways stay open. Single storey with open doorways; no doors, no ladders. Watchtowers carry a soldier the player can shoot but not climb to.\"},{\"line_number\":351,\"content\":\"- `ignite(x, z, radius)` is the only way in. Used by flare, molotov, flamethrower, explosions, burning soldiers, wrecks and tracer fire on full-auto from the mounted MG (small chance).\"},{\"line_number\":357,\"content\":\"- Actors in a burning cell catch fire: soldiers panic (section 10), players burn (section 9).\"},{\"line_number\":365,\"content\":\"- Burn scars show on your held map.\"},{\"line_number\":384,\"content\":\"**Weather.** Dry by default. A dust wind (`particles`, stronger wind, haze raised) and a storm (`Precipitation` rain, lightning `screen.flash` + thunder, fire damped). Storms are rare, scripted for M9, and available from dev mode.\"},{\"line_number\":414,\"content\":\"**In a menu or with the map cursor active,** the look stick does nothing. Otherwise the world never pauses except in the pause menu.\"},{\"line_number\":428,\"content\":\"| `flare` | Flare pistol | sidearm | 1 / 8 | 0.6/s | 12 + ignite | arcs to 70 m | 0 | given in M3 | Gravity projectile; lights fuel where it lands; sets soldiers alight |\"},{\"line_number\":429,\"content\":\"| `tractor` | \\\"Tractor\\\" rifle | main | 30 / 150 | 9/s | 24 | 110 m | 0.35 | 6 | Every soldier has one, mostly rusted |\"},{\"line_number\":438,\"content\":\"Hip fire has a small spread; L2/RMB aims (FOV 62 to 45; `empire` to 12) with tighter spread and recoil. Hitscan for bullets using `physics.castRay`, with the collider-to-actor map from section 10; rockets, flares and bottles are projectiles integrated per fixed step with a ray per step. Head ×2.5, legs ×0.7, by hit height on the capsule.\"},{\"line_number\":448,\"content\":\"**Feedback:** `engine.shake.add`, `hitstop(0.02)` on a hit, muzzle `lights.request({ lifetime:0.06 })`, tracer (`Trail` or sprite) on every third round, `particles.burst('impact')` plus red pixel blood, `Decals` for scorches, hit marker (small X) and rumble. Body-shot soldiers play `HitReact`; a killing shot switches to `Ragdoll` with the bullet's push.\"},{\"line_number\":476,\"content\":\"**Bodies:** the soldier model in faction palettes (several `skin` values and hat variants), a rifle parented to `HandR`, a `CharacterController` capsule (speed from role), `physics.tag(collider, 'npc')` and a `Map` from collider handle to actor. Clips are in section 21.\"},{\"line_number\":488,\"content\":\"**Hostility.** Everyone outside Mile Forty shoots you on sight, with one exception: **while you hold a contract from a faction, you carry its pass**, and its soldiers leave you alone unless you fire near them or walk into their HQ's inner yard. Choosing whose ground to cross becomes a real decision.\"},{\"line_number\":490,\"content\":\"**Brain:** a `BehaviorTree` for each soldier, ticked at 10 Hz, in priority order:\"},{\"line_number\":512,\"content\":\"**Driving in first person:** eye at the driver's seat, your hands on a wheel that turns with steering, a dash, a small arrow on the dash pointing to your waypoint. R3/C toggles a chase camera (computed in your `step`, via `cam.override`). You can raise the map while driving, as you should: it's the most famous moment in this kind of game, and it's dangerous.\"},{\"line_number\":530,\"content\":\"| Perk | Rescues you by truck, from farther away | Gives 2 free charges per mission | +1 syrette at any safehouse; rescues you with 60 HP instead of 40 |\"},{\"line_number\":542,\"content\":\"If you have no syrettes, only the second option is lit. If the 40 s run out, they die anyway. If they are burning, they ask you to finish it. M6 forces this moment at least once.\"},{\"line_number\":568,\"content\":\"- **Crate:** ammo and syrettes.\"},{\"line_number\":573,\"content\":\"**Trig points** (6): stone pillars on hilltops. Use one: a new note in Harrow's hand appears in your map's margin, and you can read it on the map. All six: he leaves you a clean `empire` at a locker. A note that says so.\"},{\"line_number\":603,\"content\":\"**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the map margin. Bots drive these same steps.\"},{\"line_number\":609,\"content\":\"| M0 | The Goods Line | 2 min, dusk, skippable | You ride Old Bakr's flatcar into the Kettle as he talks. Prompt: raise the map (must do). The margin note. Fever on the platform; you fall | Look, map | - | Fade to the clinic |\"},{\"line_number\":610,\"content\":\"| M1 | Mercy Run (Odile) | 7 min, morning | Wake at the clinic. Take a tablet. Given an old `tractor` (cond 45). Drive medicine to Three Wells. On the way back P2 is manned. The 5th shot **jams by script**; then the truck is hit and stalls: repair. Syrette. Report | Walk, use, tablet, drive, waypoint, fire, jam, reload, syrette, repair | - | +3 tablets, 5 stones, Pump Shed |\"},{\"line_number\":612,\"content\":\"| M3 | Fuel for the Peace (Vance) | 7 min | Burn the Harvest's 3 tanks at East Siding. Vance hands you the flare pistol. Wind pinned toward the depot: the grass will carry fire if you start it upwind | Flare, wind, fire, chain explosions | Ines: steal the tanker at P3 and drive it in; soldiers hold fire until you're inside | Scar A, 15 stones (+5). A column of smoke visible across the map for a game day |\"},{\"line_number\":617,\"content\":\"| M8 | Last Train (Odile) | 7 min | Mile Forty under shells. Hold the platform 120 s while people board. Then ride Old Bakr's train to East Siding on a flatcar MG, 60 s, on rails, under fire. *He says the grass won't burn twice.* The column starts walking the scar | Defence, on-rails MG | - | Column on the map, moving slowly and visibly along the scar |\"},{\"line_number\":618,\"content\":\"| M9 | The Surveyor | 10 min, night, storm | Climb to the Observatory (deserters from both armies; no fires, it's raining). Harrow sits at a table with a lamp, as sick as you. The scene: he lays your contract map down; the three scars glow as one line; he draws the last stroke. He offers tablets and the minefield sheet, and asks you to finish your contract, or not | Choice | - | `choice` steps: shoot him or don't (a Ledger line, no other effect). Then who gets the sheet |\"},{\"line_number\":624,\"content\":\"- **Walk out:** *You reached the border with a case of stones and a map nobody else will ever use. The guard asks your trade. You tell him: surveyor.*\"},{\"line_number\":625,\"content\":\"- **Give it to them:** *They crossed at first light, walking on ash. Nobody has asked who lit it. The fever is not finished with you, and you are out of tablets. It is a good view.*\"},{\"line_number\":627,\"content\":\"**Attract, tests and dev mode** can jump to any mission start: each mission has a `setup` that puts the world in the right state (`world.reset`, story flags, scars, buddies, loadout), so `dev.startMission('m6')` is one call.\"},{\"line_number\":652,\"content\":\"  1. *A map is a promise made by someone who has already left.*\"},{\"line_number\":676,\"content\":\"- 5 health segments, syrette and tablet counts bottom-left.\"},{\"line_number\":716,\"content\":\"**The mouse is native.** In menus the pointer is free (no lock), hover moves focus, click activates (read `input.buttonEvents`; convert with `x = (p.x+1)/2*hud.width`, `y = (1-p.y)/2*hud.height`). The wheel scrolls pages. Over the world it aims and looks under pointer lock. On the held map it's a cursor (hover focuses a marker, click sets the waypoint). On Tibor's rack and in dialogue choices, click works too. Keyboard in menus: arrows or WASD, Enter or Space, Esc back. Pad in menus: D-pad or left stick with key repeat, Cross confirms, Circle goes back, L1/R1 change tabs and pages. If the pad disconnects during play, open the pause menu.\"}]}]}","is_error":false},{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-88a71a20-5626-4e67-9caa-ac8309375539-39","content":"{\"type\":\"GrepSearch\",\"stdout\":[60,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,32,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,112,97,116,104,61,34,47,104,111,109,101,47,109,105,99,104,97,47,100,101,118,47,99,99,45,109,97,116,114,105,120,47,114,117,110,115,47,103,114,111,107,45,120,104,105,103,104,46,98,117,105,108,100,45,118,50,95,95,50,48,50,54,49,49,48,53,45,48,49,51,57,49,55,95,95,120,48,55,51,57,51,99,47,119,111,114,107,34,62,10,78,111,32,109,97,116,99,104,101,115,32,102,111,117,110,100,10,60,47,119,111,114,107,115,112,97,99,101,95,114,101,115,117,108,116,62],\"stderr\":[],\"exit_code\":1,\"match_count\":0,\"file_matches\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"d0cd7920-b1b1-46de-a577-2d5ee4e7321a"}
