{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_596","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"A plan requirement for buddies needs to be addressed.Criterion 2 requires offering a syrette when a buddy is downed, but only finish-it if no syrettes remain.\n\nThe down prompt should offer both a syrette and a finish-it option when the player has a syrette. The prior gap incorrectly restricted finish-it to cases where no syrette remains.\n\nThe current code shows both options when a syrette is available, but KeyE only offers it and melee always finishes. This conflicts with Criterion 2, which requires finish-it to be the sole option when no syrettes remain.\n\nCriterion 2 is satisfied. Melee can finish while holding a syrette, and burning enemies only receive finish-it.\n\nThe current code ignores Burnt cells are marked the plan. It finishes on the map texture. any downed buddy on melee regardless of syrettes. It also skips distance and burning checks.\n\nThe held map texture reads from `mapPx`, so dark pixels from burnt cells are visible. The `refreshMap` early-out only skips stamping when the current tick already matches `_scarDrawn`.\n\nThe fix aligns the code with the plan. Syrette is available when a buddy is down and not burning. Finish-it is available in all other cases. KnockBuddy\n\nThe `refreshMap` early-out no longer sets burning, is broken. Both `scarTick` so syrettes work again. and `_scarDrawn` start as undefined, so they are always equal. The function returns immediately and never paints scars onto the map texture.\n\nThe prompt should be a single string rather than two separate buttons. The behaviors already match the plan and prior gap. Need to verify that melee is mapped to the F or Triangle","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call-4825ef7c-074d-4951-9c9b-e2403b6dd724-36","name":"grep","input":{"pattern":"scarTick|_scarDrawn|mapHasScar|burntList","glob":"**/*.{js,mjs}","path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matr