{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call-da5711e5-bf5a-4cc6-9302-387dbdb3dc56-39","content":"{\"type\":\"ReadFile\",\"FileContent\":{\"content\":\"330→  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n340→  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n350→  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n360→    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n370→  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n380→    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n390→  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n400→  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\",\"content_concise\":\"330→  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n340→  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n350→  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n360→    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n370→  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n380→    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n390→  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n400→  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\",\"absolute_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/grok-xhigh.build-v2__20261105-013917__x07393c/work/A Cry Too Far-Far Cry 2-grok-4.7-xhigh-20261105-013917/tests/run.mjs\",\"offset\":330,\"limit\":80,\"raw_output\":\"  for (const line of shown) {\\n    for (const ch of String(line).toUpperCase()) {\\n      if (!allowed.has(ch)) throw new Error('font glyph ' + JSON.stringify(ch) + ' in ' + line);\\n    }\\n  }\\n});\\n\\ntest('title music and basin', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const state = game.state();\\n  assert(state.screen === 'title', 'screen ' + state.screen);\\n  assert(state.title === 'A Cry Too Far', state.title);\\n  assert(game.ctx.audio.volume.music === 0.1, 'music ' + game.ctx.audio.volume.music);\\n  assert(game.world.land.nx === 512 && game.world.land.sizeX === 1280, 'basin');\\n  engine.step(30, DT);\\n  const heard = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('gun-m38');\\n  game.ctx.audio.play('explosion');\\n  engine.step(5, DT);\\n  const heardAfter = Object.values(game.ctx.audio.counts).reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n  assert(heardAfter > heard, 'sounds silent');\\n  assert(engine.errors.length === 0, 'boot errors');\\n});\\n\\ntest('fire spread scars and reburn', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const fire = game.world.fire;\\n  game.world.windPin = { dir: 0, speed: 5 };\\n  let column = null;\\n  for (let ix = 30; ix < 220 && !column; ix++) {\\n    let ok = 0;\\n    for (let iz = 70; iz < 100; iz++) if (fire.fuel[ix + iz * 256] > 0) ok++;\\n    if (ok >= 24) column = ix;\\n  }\\n  assert(column != null, 'no grass column');\\n  const iz0 = 70;\\n  const iz1 = 99;\\n  for (let iz = iz0; iz <= iz1; iz++) fire.lightIndex(fire.idx(column, iz));\\n  engine.step(16 * 60, DT);\\n  let maxX = column;\\n  let minZ = iz1;\\n  let maxZ = iz0;\\n  let burnt = null;\\n  for (let i = 0; i < fire.state.length; i++) {\\n    if (fire.state[i] !== 1 && fire.state[i] !== 2) continue;\\n    const ix = i % 256;\\n    const iz = (i / 256) | 0;\\n    if (ix > maxX) maxX = ix;\\n    if (iz < minZ) minZ = iz;\\n    if (iz > maxZ) maxZ = iz;\\n    if (fire.state[i] === 2 && !burnt) burnt = i;\\n  }\\n  const head = ((maxX - column) * 5) / 16;\\n  const flank = ((Math.max(iz1, maxZ) - Math.min(iz0, minZ) - (iz1 - iz0)) / 2 * 5) / 16;\\n  assert(head >= 2 && head <= 5, 'head speed ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(flank < head, 'flank ' + flank.toFixed(2) + ' head ' + head.toFixed(2));\\n  assert(burnt != null, 'nothing burnt');\\n  const before = fire.state[burnt];\\n  const [bx, bz] = fire.center(burnt % 256, (burnt / 256) | 0);\\n  fire.ignite(bx, bz, 0);\\n  assert(fire.state[burnt] === before, 'burnt cell relit');\\n  game.world.refreshMap();\\n  assert(game.world.mapHasScar(), 'map has no scar');\\n  game.world.windPin = null;\\n});\\n\\ntest('locomotion', async () => {\\n  await boot();\\n  const w = game.world;\\n  w.startMission('m7');\\n  w.lines = [];\\n  release();\\n  game.ctx.camera.yaw = 0;\\n  const z0 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n  const run = z0 - w.feet().z;\\n  assert(run > 4 && run < 7, 'run ' + run.toFixed(2));\\n  tap('KeyC');\\n  const z1 = w.feet().z;\\n  holdKey('KeyW', 60);\\n\",\"total_lines\":775}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"01a1aadc-c537-7073-8756-0b078a9e97df","uuid":"e873f13b-ef90-4a18-a37e-56339a840078"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_599","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"grok-4.7","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":" expand scope to distance checks unless they are clearly part of the broken behavior being fixed. The test does not assert that finish-it is blocked when syrettes remain.\n\nThe prompt wording \"SYRETTE OR FINISH IT\" confirms both actions are available when a syrette is held. The prior gap's parenthetical describes the campaign's forced moment, not a strict rule that finish-it must be blocked while a syrette remains. The implementation already satisfies this by gating the Use key on inventory.\n\nMelee finish-it is a valid extra path that works alongsideA potential bug in refreshMap syrettes, matching  was identified. WhenPLAN section 12 and the gap's intent. The scarTick increments knockBuddy flow through but paintMapBase is the mission is correct. called later, the map\n\nNow checking world.js line 30 for scarTick gets wiped. If scarTick updates. The early  does not change again,return is acceptable scars fail to redraw. if scarTick changes. Tests assert mapHasScar after refreshMap.\n\nSoldier AI movement is a large cut under PLAN section 26. The soldier mesh remains\n\nDuring play, refreshMap visible and correctly correctly stamps burnt placed by placeRig. cells and updates _scarDrawn. No underground or size bug is present. Dev mode items() is also However, applySetup calls paintMapBase to wipe the map before noted. laying scars. If burnStrip sets cells directly without invoking onBurnt, scarTick never increments and refreshMap early-outs.\n\nTests confirm scars render correctly on the held map texture.\n\nThe dev mode items() The burnStrip path triggers onBurnt, so list is being checked scarTick increments for an off-by-one bug. and refreshMap redraws Reset-to-defaults sits the scars properly. after 22 sliders and back, so it should remain visible within the 9-row window when focused.\n\nA minor map trail bug was found. refreshMap stamps the player position every frame without clearing old white dots, so a trail of white pixels accumulates. Full redraws do not clear the base first,\n\nThe pointer-to-pixel and the position remains visible. mapping in clickHud is mathematically correct. When height equals 270, pixelY maps directly to py, so the hit test passes for the Reset button at y = 86. The setPointer call with its third argument does not generate an extra click activation.\n\nDev mode correctly routes to menuInput, so hover works. Engine.step still processes input when timeScale is zero. All four gaps are fixed and tests are honest.\n\nI will not re-audit the entire game unless a defect appears. I am checking the hand-in requirements and file timestamps to confirm nothing is missing. I also spotted a potential bug: gpsPx.fill(24) overwrites the alpha channel completely.\n\nA search for a cheap, demonstrable core defect is underway. The GPS alpha fill and map transform appear acceptable. The soldier rig now has a visual mesh, but it may still lack an aim target or collider.\n\nThe GPS alpha overwrite is harmless. The mark pixel stays fully opaque while the rest of the square remains visible.\n\nThe map copies the\n\nThe soldier rig is camera matrix each  now visible and positioned in the world. However,poseMap cycle. This can lag one frame behind if it lacks physics the camera, but it is not a defect.\n\nThe hookCamera wrapper around rig.step risks being lost if step is replaced later. The colliders, bullets will pass straight through the mesh. This would leave the original aiming complaint unresolved. The fix requested both instancing the rig and asserting that path. code stores the hook in _mapHook.\n\nThe map hook is redundant because syncViews already updates the pose each frame. The map visibility check correctly uses game.mode during campaign driving. Tests confirm the world pauses while the map is open. A potential bug was noted: spawn sets the kind to soldier, but round 